- text: "I’ll focus on Track 2 (algorithm improvements) and keep the best baseline architecture (CNN+LSTM) unchanged. I’m submitting a clipped PPO training step with advantage normalization and optional value clipping while preserving the CNN-LSTM network and default optimizer.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Clipped PPO on CNN-LSTM for Sokoban\"\ntags: \"ppo, policy gradient, rnn, lstm, distributed training\"\nabstract: \"We keep the CNN-LSTM architecture from the RNN baseline and replace the default policy gradient loss with a clipped PPO objective, including advantage normalization and optional value function clipping. Hyperparameters are searched via Ray for clip_epsilon and value loss weight, with architecture fixed to isolate the algorithmic effect.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  Clipped PPO training step with CNN-LSTM architecture (unchanged from baseline).\n  Track: Algorithm (keep architecture fixed; modify learning objective only).\n  \"\"\"\n\n  from typing import\
    \ Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  # Reuse system GAE for consistency\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  # Fixed base seed for reproducibility across runs\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      \"\"\"\n      Define Ray Tune search space for algorithmic PPO settings.\n      Keep architecture fixed to isolate algorithm effects.\n      \"\"\"\n      return {\n          # Keep architecture fixed (same as baseline best settings)\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          # Optimization / losses\n          'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(3e-4, 8e-4),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.005, 0.02),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.3, 0.7),\n          # PPO-specific\n          'clip_epsilon':\
    \ tune.uniform(0.1, 0.3),\n          'vf_clip': tune.uniform(0.1, 0.4),\n          'normalize_advantages': tune.choice([True, False]),\n      }\n\n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN baseline + LSTM for Sokoban (matches system RNN baseline).\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(\n          self, \n          x: jnp.ndarray, \n          done: jnp.ndarray, \n          rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None\n      ) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size,\
    \ 1).astype(jnp.float32)\n              keep = 1.0 - done_mask\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * keep,\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * keep,\n              }\n          \n          # CNN backbone (same as DefaultResidualCNN)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv2_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dims\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM on top\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (c, h), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'c': c, 'h': h}\n          \n          # Small MLP head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n\
    \  def create_network(hparams):\n      \"\"\"Use CNN-LSTM architecture; keep features fixed via hparams.\"\"\"\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      \"\"\"Default Adam optimizer (same as system default).\"\"\"\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n\n  def _gather_log_probs(log_probs_all, actions):\n      \"\"\"Gather log-prob for taken actions; shapes: (B,T,4) and (B,T)->(B,T).\"\"\"\n      B, T = actions.shape\n      b_idx = jnp.arange(B)[:, None]\n      t_idx = jnp.arange(T)[None, :]\n      return log_probs_all[b_idx, t_idx, actions]\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n \
    \ ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Clipped PPO objective with optional value clipping and advantage normalization.\n      \"\"\"\n      observations = batch['observations']       # (B, T, 8, 8, 8)\n      actions = batch['actions']                 # (B, T)\n      rewards = batch['rewards']                 # (B, T)\n      dones = batch['dones']                     # (B, T)\n      old_values = batch['values']               # (B, T)\n      old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']         # (B, T)\n      final_values = batch['final_values']       # (B,)\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      # GAE advantages and returns\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      # Optionally normalize advantages (per-batch)\n      if hparams.get('normalize_advantages', True):\n          adv_mean = jnp.mean(advantages)\n          adv_std = jnp.std(advantages) + 1e-8\n\
    \          advantages = (advantages - adv_mean) / adv_std\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def forward_all(params):\n          # Compute new logits and values over the full (B,T) batch\n          if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n              # Process each env trajectory sequentially to update RNN state\n              def process_env(env_idx):\n                  env_init_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rnn_state = carry\n                      obs_t = observations[env_idx, t]\n                      prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n\n                      obs_b = obs_t[None, ...]\n                      done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                      rnn_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n\n                      logits_b, value_b, new_state_b = network.apply(params, obs_b,\
    \ done_b, rnn_b)\n                      logits = logits_b[0]\n                      value = value_b[0]\n                      new_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_state_b) if new_state_b is not None else None\n                      return new_state, (logits, value)\n\n                  _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_init_state, jnp.arange(T))\n                  return env_logits, env_values\n\n              all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n          else:\n              obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n              dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n              logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_flat, dones_flat)\n              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n              all_values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n\n          return all_logits, all_values\n\n      def loss_fn(params):\n          all_logits, all_values = forward_all(params)\n\n          # New log-probs\n\
    \          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)   # (B,T,4)\n          new_log_probs = _gather_log_probs(log_probs_all, actions) # (B,T)\n\n          # Probability ratio\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n\n          # Clipped policy objective\n          eps = hparams['clip_epsilon']\n          unclipped = ratio * advantages\n          clipped = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - eps, 1.0 + eps) * advantages\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(unclipped, clipped))\n\n          # Value loss (with optional clipping)\n          if 'vf_clip' in hparams and hparams['vf_clip'] > 0:\n              v_clip = hparams['vf_clip']\n              v_pred_clipped = old_values + jnp.clip(all_values - old_values, -v_clip, v_clip)\n              v_loss_unclipped = (all_values - returns) ** 2\n              v_loss_clipped = (v_pred_clipped - returns) ** 2\n              value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(v_loss_unclipped, v_loss_clipped))\n          else:\n\
    \              value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns) ** 2)\n\n          # Entropy bonus\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n\n          # Total loss\n          entropy_coef = hparams['entropy_coef']\n          value_loss_coef = hparams['value_loss_coef']\n          total_loss = policy_loss + value_loss_coef * value_loss - entropy_coef * entropy\n          return total_loss\n\n      loss_and_grad = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n      loss, grads = loss_and_grad(params)\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: "**Proposing a research approach**\n\nI'm thinking about our research approach and the need to submit code. I've gone through the defaults and baseline reviews, noting the tools we're using: JAX, Flax, optax, and Ray. The training step utilizes default_training_step with simple policy gradient (PG) methods. I see a couple of tracks for improvement—architecture or algorithm. The baseline highlights memory's significance, with CNN+PG solving 25% and RNN+PG achieving 40.8%. I wonder if we can innovate within architecture while respecting model-based RL restrictions.**Exploring reinforcement learning ideas**\n\nI'm considering the possibility of incorporating Gated Transformer-XL style gating into attention to enhance stability in reinforcement learning (RL). However, since model-based RL isn't permitted, I'm thinking a Transformer policy network is an allowable model-free architecture. Another idea is value decomposition through dueling heads. For RL enhancements, we might\
  \ explore a PPO-style clipped loss, but the current setup uses old log_probs stored in trajectories. I'd need to modify the training step to implement a PPO surrogate, which means ensuring that we calculate new log_probs correctly.**Investigating potential bugs**\n\nI’m noticing a possible bug with action_indices, which uses jnp.arange for both batch and trajectory dimensions. The actions shape is (B, T), so when indexing multi-dimensional arrays, flattening or advanced indexing might be necessary. Given JAX's advanced indexing semantics, it could work, but since it’s part of the baseline, we might be okay.\n\nFor implementing PPO, we'll need to store old log_probs and the entropy coefficient. This means calculating the ratio using exp(new_log_prob - old_log_probs) and normalizing advantages, all while considering value clipping. Just noting that trials have a 30-minute runtime limit after 50 million steps!**Deciding on PPO and architecture**\n\nI’m thinking that PPO typically requires\
  \ multiple epochs per batch, but to meet constraints, we could just implement one epoch update per rollout. For architecture, I'm considering a residual CNN combined with ConvGRU memory and spatial attention. However, I noticed that mixing architecture and algorithm improvements isn't encouraged, so I should stick to one track.\n\nI’m likely going to choose Track 2, focusing on algorithm improvements with a PPO-style clipped objective while keeping the baseline RNN. I need to stick with the default network, but I could create a new network to define the LSTM baseline if necessary.**Finalizing the optimizer setup**\n\nI’m thinking about the 'create_optimizer' function now, and we'll set it to return the default 'optax.adam' with a learning rate and eps of 1e-5. I've also noted that 'BASE_SEED' should be set to 42. \n\nWhen handling YAML, I need to ensure the 'content' section has proper indentation, using a code block format without extra backticks. After submitting, it seems we can create\
  \ a second submission, but we should first evaluate performance. I'll prepare the final answer with the tags \"ppo, policy gradient, rnn, lstm, distributed training\" and mention that we chose Track 2 as well."
