tick: 9
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO with grad clipping and GAE tuning (CNN-LSTM)\"\ntags: \"ppo, rnn, lstm, gae, gradient clipping, distributed training\"\nabstract: \"We keep the CNN-LSTM architecture fixed and improve the algorithm with clipped PPO, global gradient clipping, and Ray-tuned gamma/lambda for GAE. We also support advantage normalization and optional value clipping. This isolates algorithmic effects while keeping the architecture constant.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  PPO variant with gradient clipping and GAE hyperparameter tuning.\n  Track: Algorithm (architecture fixed to CNN-LSTM).\n  \"\"\"\n\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  # Reuse default GAE\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 43  # distinct from previous submission\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fix\
    \ architecture; tune algorithmic knobs\n      return {\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(3e-4, 8e-4),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.005, 0.02),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.3, 0.7),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.uniform(0.1, 0.3),\n          'vf_clip': tune.uniform(0.1, 0.4),\n          'normalize_advantages': tune.choice([True, False]),\n          'gamma': tune.uniform(0.970, 0.995),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.uniform(0.90, 0.99),\n          'grad_clip_norm': tune.choice([0.5, 1.0]),\n      }\n\n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"CNN baseline + LSTM for Sokoban (matches system RNN baseline).\"\"\"\n      lstm_features: int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(\n          self, \n          x: jnp.ndarray, \n          done: jnp.ndarray,\
    \ \n          rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None\n      ) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          batch_size = x.shape[0]\n          \n          # Initialize RNN state if not provided\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((batch_size, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          \n          # Reset states for episodes that are done\n          if done is not None:\n              done_mask = done.reshape(batch_size, 1).astype(jnp.float32)\n              keep = 1.0 - done_mask\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': rnn_state['h'] * keep,\n                  'c': rnn_state['c'] * keep,\n              }\n          \n          # CNN backbone (same as DefaultResidualCNN)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv2_in = x\n          x =\
    \ nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_1, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv2_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          conv4_in = x\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(features=self.cnn_features_2, kernel_size=(3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = x + conv4_in\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Flatten spatial dims\n          x = x.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n          \n          # Shared MLP\n          x = nn.Dense(features=256)(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # LSTM on top\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(\n              features=self.lstm_features,\n      \
    \        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n              recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )\n          (c, h), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'c': c, 'h': h}\n          \n          # Small MLP head\n          x = nn.Dense(features=128)(lstm_out)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # Policy and value heads\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(features=4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(features=1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4, grad_clip_norm: float = 1.0) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      # Gradient clipping + Adam\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(grad_clip_norm),\n\
    \          optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n      )\n\n  def _gather_log_probs(log_probs_all, actions):\n      \"\"\"Gather log-prob for taken actions; shapes: (B,T,4) and (B,T)->(B,T).\"\"\"\n      B, T = actions.shape\n      b_idx = jnp.arange(B)[:, None]\n      t_idx = jnp.arange(T)[None, :]\n      return log_probs_all[b_idx, t_idx, actions]\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      \"\"\"\n      Clipped PPO objective with:\n      - GAE using tuned gamma/lambda\n      - Optional advantage normalization\n      - Optional value clipping\n      - Global gradient clipping via optimizer\n      \"\"\"\n      observations = batch['observations']       # (B, T, 8, 8, 8)\n      actions = batch['actions']                 # (B, T)\n      rewards = batch['rewards']                 # (B, T)\n      dones = batch['dones']\
    \                     # (B, T)\n      old_values = batch['values']               # (B, T)\n      old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']         # (B, T)\n      final_values = batch['final_values']       # (B,)\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      gamma = float(hparams.get('gamma', 0.97))\n      gae_lambda = float(hparams.get('gae_lambda', 0.97))\n\n      # GAE advantages and returns\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(\n          rewards, old_values, dones, gamma=gamma, gae_lambda=gae_lambda, next_values=final_values\n      )\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n\n      # Optionally normalize advantages (per-batch)\n      if hparams.get('normalize_advantages', True):\n          adv_mean = jnp.mean(advantages)\n          adv_std = jnp.std(advantages) + 1e-8\n          advantages = (advantages - adv_mean) / adv_std\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def forward_all(p):\n          # Compute new logits and values over the full (B,T)\
    \ batch\n          if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n              def process_env(env_idx):\n                  env_init_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rnn_state = carry\n                      obs_t = observations[env_idx, t]\n                      prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n\n                      obs_b = obs_t[None, ...]\n                      done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                      rnn_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n\n                      logits_b, value_b, new_state_b = network.apply(p, obs_b, done_b, rnn_b)\n                      logits = logits_b[0]\n                      value = value_b[0]\n                      new_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_state_b) if new_state_b is not None else None\n                      return new_state, (logits, value)\n\
    \n                  _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_init_state, jnp.arange(T))\n                  return env_logits, env_values\n\n              all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n          else:\n              obs_flat = observations.reshape(B * T, *observations.shape[2:])\n              dones_flat = dones.reshape(B * T)\n              logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat)\n              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n              all_values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n\n          return all_logits, all_values\n\n      def loss_fn(p):\n          all_logits, all_values = forward_all(p)\n\n          # New log-probs\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)   # (B,T,4)\n          new_log_probs = _gather_log_probs(log_probs_all, actions) # (B,T)\n\n          # Probability ratio\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n\n          # Clipped policy objective\n\
    \          eps = hparams['clip_epsilon']\n          unclipped = ratio * advantages\n          clipped = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - eps, 1.0 + eps) * advantages\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(unclipped, clipped))\n\n          # Value loss (with optional clipping)\n          if 'vf_clip' in hparams and hparams['vf_clip'] > 0:\n              v_clip = hparams['vf_clip']\n              v_pred_clipped = old_values + jnp.clip(all_values - old_values, -v_clip, v_clip)\n              v_loss_unclipped = (all_values - returns) ** 2\n              v_loss_clipped = (v_pred_clipped - returns) ** 2\n              value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(v_loss_unclipped, v_loss_clipped))\n          else:\n              value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns) ** 2)\n\n          # Entropy bonus\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n\n          # Total loss\n          total = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef']\
    \ * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n          return total\n\n      loss_and_grad = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)\n      loss, grads = loss_and_grad(params)\n\n      # Optimizer with grad clipping\n      grad_clip_norm = float(hparams.get('grad_clip_norm', 1.0))\n      # Rebuild optimizer if needed to honor per-trial grad_clip_norm\n      # Note: optimizer passed in is constructed by create_optimizer; ensure it matches hparams\n      if hasattr(optimizer, \"inner_state_maker\"):  # no reliable way; keep simple and rely on create_optimizer using hparams\n          pass\n\n      updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n      params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating GAE improvements**\n\nIt seems like I need to make some adjustments regarding GAE parameters like gamma and lambda. I could define them in hyperparameters and supply them to the default_calculate_gae function, which currently uses default values of 0.97. I'll also think about normalizing advantages per environment instead of globally, and consider generalized advantage normalization with per-timestep whitening. Lastly, I might explore bootstrapping from a target network for value stability, but that will require managing extra parameters across steps.**Considering optimizer design**\n\nIt’s clear that redesigning the optimizer to include a state with target parameters isn’t straightforward. While create_optimizer returns an optax transformation, the training loop primarily uses opt_state for updates. Embedding target parameters in opt_state feels unnatural, but maybe I should consider soft value clipping similar to PPO.\n\nFor another improvement, I could\
  \ suggest using GAE advantage with truncated returns on solved episodes, although it's not strictly necessary. I could also propose a second experiment involving PPO with a clipped objective, gradient clipping, and KL penalty.**Planning PPO implementation**\n\nI know that PPO is generally more stable and could improve the solve rate. Given that we can run only two experiments at a time and one is already in progress, I'll prepare to submit a second experiment.\n\nFirst, I’ll need to provide code for create_optimizer with clip_by_global_norm for better implementation. My proposal will focus on \"PPO with KL penalty and gradient clipping,\" possibly including GAE gamma/lambda tuning. I’ll ensure to reuse our previous CNN-LSTM and provide all functions like _define_hyperparameters, create_network, and training_step, while also noting that we'll compute the KL divergence between old and new policies.**Assessing KL penalty limitations**\n\nI realize that we only have log_probs for the actions\
  \ taken, not the old policy logits or probabilities, which makes it tricky to compute the KL divergence properly. We can't add a well-defined KL penalty without the full old distribution, but I could approximate it using the sample-based KL for the actions taken. This would mean relying on the difference in log-probs for the sample, which is commonly referred to as \"policy KL.\"\n\nAdditionally, I could consider other improvements like implementing momentum-target advantage normalization across rollouts or even an A2C approach with advantage normalization and multi-head value for time channels, but persistence can be an issue here.**Reviewing intrinsic rewards and PPO enhancements**\n\nI think intrinsic rewards might be viewed as domain-specific, but \"curiosity\" seems like a valid algorithmic improvement. We should not use external resources, though complexity might be high.\n\nOne improvement could be implementing \"PPO with generalized advantage mixing, gradient norm clipping, and\
  \ per-batch whitening.\" I should also inspect how 'log_probs' are stored and used in system/train_single.py. Additionally, proposing V-trace for off-policy corrections is interesting, but since we’re on-policy, I’ll focus on other enhancements.\n\nUltimately, I’ll submit the second experiment titled \"PPO with Grad Clip + Gamma/Lambda tuning (CNN-LSTM)\" and ensure all required functions are included.**Finalizing submission for PPO experiment**\n\nI'm processing a submission for \"PPO with Grad Clip + GAE tuning (CNN-LSTM).\" Since each submission is independent, I must carefully replicate the required code and ensure everything is organized properly. \n\nI need to make sure the import path for 'defaults' is correct and handle log-probabilities properly. Setting hyperparameters like learning rate and entropy coefficient is crucial, as is the grad clipping range. \n\nNow, I'll prepare the YAML code for submission and include minimal commentary, ensuring clarity and compliance with format\
  \ rules. Let's get this submitted!**Preparing final submission**\n\nI’m considering the training loop which involves 'rnn_states' in transitions, and for RNN networks, my forward passes will update these states for each step. The edge cases look good, as ‘prev_done’ uses past states to ensure resets. \n\nNow, I’m crafting the final content for submission. Although there's a suggestion to go to Private Memory to write a research plan, I think it’s not necessary. I’ll keep commentary minimal and finalize the YAML code for submission. Let’s get this action executed!"
