role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PPO (multi-epoch full-batch) on CNN-LSTM\"\ntags: \"ppo, multi-epoch, rnn, lstm, policy optimization\"\nabstract: \"We keep the CNN-LSTM architecture fixed and implement PPO with multiple full-batch epochs per rollout (no minibatching) plus value clipping and advantage normalization. This isolates the algorithmic effect of PPO with iterative policy improvement while keeping architecture and other settings constant.\"\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  PPO with multi-epoch full-batch updates on top of the CNN-LSTM baseline.\n  Track: Algorithm (architecture fixed).\n\n  Key differences vs. default PG:\n  - Clipped PPO surrogate with K epochs per rollout (no minibatching).\n  - Optional value clipping and advantage normalization.\n  - Optional KL penalty toward a small target.\n  \"\"\"\n\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import lax, vmap\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n\n  from defaults import default_calculate_gae\n\n  BASE_SEED = 45\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          # Architecture fixed to isolate algorithmic effect\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'lstm_features': tune.choice([256]),\n          # Optimizer/loss\n          'learning_rate': tune.loguniform(3e-4, 8e-4),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.uniform(0.005, 0.02),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.uniform(0.3, 0.7),\n          # PPO specifics\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.uniform(0.1, 0.3),\n          'vf_clip': tune.uniform(0.1, 0.4),\n          'normalize_advantages': tune.choice([True, False]),\n          'ppo_epochs': tune.choice([2, 3, 4, 5, 6]),\n          # Optional small KL penalty toward target\n          'kl_coef': tune.choice([0.0, 0.01, 0.02]),\n          'kl_target': tune.choice([0.01, 0.02]),\n      }\n\n  class CNNLSTM(nn.Module):\n      lstm_features:\
    \ int\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      \n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None) -> Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray, Dict]:\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # Init RNN state if missing\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = {\n                  'h': jnp.zeros((B, self.lstm_features)),\n                  'c': jnp.zeros((B, self.lstm_features)),\n              }\n          # Reset on episode boundaries\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # CNN backbone (matches DefaultResidualCNN capacity)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          s = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x + s)\n\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          s = x\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME')(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x + s)\n\n          x = x.reshape((B, -1))\n          x = nn.Dense(256)(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\n          lstm_cell = nn.LSTMCell(features=self.lstm_features,\n                                  kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n                                  recurrent_kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())\n          (c, h), lstm_out = lstm_cell((rnn_state['c'], rnn_state['h']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'c': c, 'h': h}\n\n          x = nn.Dense(128)(lstm_out); x = nn.relu(x)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(x)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(x).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\
    \n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNLSTM(\n          lstm_features=hparams['lstm_features'],\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2']\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4) -> optax.GradientTransformation:\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=1e-5)\n\n  def _gather_log_probs(log_probs_all, actions):\n      B, T = actions.shape\n      b_idx = jnp.arange(B)[:, None]\n      t_idx = jnp.arange(T)[None, :]\n      return log_probs_all[b_idx, t_idx, actions]\n\n  def training_step(\n      network: Any,\n      optimizer: Any,\n      params: Any,\n      opt_state: Any,\n      batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n      hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n  ) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n      observations = batch['observations']    # (B, T, 8, 8, 8)\n      actions = batch['actions']              # (B, T)\n      rewards = batch['rewards']              # (B, T)\n      dones = batch['dones']     \
    \             # (B, T)\n      old_values = batch['values']            # (B, T)\n      old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']      # (B, T)\n      final_values = batch['final_values']    # (B,)\n      initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n\n      # GAE and returns (use defaults' gamma/lambda to match baseline behavior)\n      advantages = default_calculate_gae(rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n      returns = advantages + old_values\n      if hparams.get('normalize_advantages', True):\n          adv_mean = jnp.mean(advantages)\n          adv_std = jnp.std(advantages) + 1e-8\n          advantages = (advantages - adv_mean) / adv_std\n\n      B, T = observations.shape[:2]\n\n      def forward_all(p):\n          # Compute logits and values across (B,T). Handle RNN via per-env scan.\n          if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n              def process_env(env_idx):\n                  init_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]),\
    \ initial_rnn_states)\n                  def step_fn(carry, t):\n                      rnn_state = carry\n                      obs_t = observations[env_idx, t]\n                      prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                      obs_b = obs_t[None, ...]\n                      done_b = prev_done[None, ...]\n                      rnn_b = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state) if rnn_state is not None else None\n                      logits_b, value_b, new_state_b = network.apply(p, obs_b, done_b, rnn_b)\n                      logits = logits_b[0]\n                      value = value_b[0]\n                      new_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_state_b) if new_state_b is not None else None\n                      return new_state, (logits, value)\n                  _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, init_state, jnp.arange(T))\n                  return env_logits, env_values\n              all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env)(jnp.arange(B))\n\
    \          else:\n              obs_flat = observations.reshape(B*T, *observations.shape[2:])\n              dones_flat = dones.reshape(B*T)\n              logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(p, obs_flat, dones_flat)\n              all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(B, T, -1)\n              all_values = values_flat.reshape(B, T)\n          return all_logits, all_values\n\n      eps = hparams['clip_epsilon']\n      vf_clip = hparams.get('vf_clip', 0.0)\n      ent_coef = hparams['entropy_coef']\n      vf_coef = hparams['value_loss_coef']\n      kl_coef = hparams.get('kl_coef', 0.0)\n      kl_target = hparams.get('kl_target', 0.01)\n      num_epochs = int(hparams.get('ppo_epochs', 4))\n\n      def loss_once(p):\n          all_logits, all_values = forward_all(p)\n          log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          new_log_probs = _gather_log_probs(log_probs_all, actions)\n\n          ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n          unclipped = ratio\
    \ * advantages\n          clipped = jnp.clip(ratio, 1.0 - eps, 1.0 + eps) * advantages\n          policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(unclipped, clipped))\n\n          if vf_clip and vf_clip > 0:\n              v_pred_clipped = old_values + jnp.clip(all_values - old_values, -vf_clip, vf_clip)\n              v_loss_unclipped = (all_values - returns) ** 2\n              v_loss_clipped = (v_pred_clipped - returns) ** 2\n              value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean(jnp.maximum(v_loss_unclipped, v_loss_clipped))\n          else:\n              value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns) ** 2)\n\n          probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n          entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n\n          # Approximate KL using sampled actions\n          approx_kl = jnp.mean(old_log_probs - new_log_probs)\n          kl_penalty = kl_coef * jnp.maximum(0.0, approx_kl - kl_target)\n\n          total = policy_loss + vf_coef * value_loss - ent_coef * entropy + kl_penalty\n\
    \          return total\n\n      def epoch_update(carry, _):\n          p, o = carry\n          loss_val, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_once)(p)\n          updates, o = optimizer.update(grads, o, p)\n          p = optax.apply_updates(p, updates)\n          return (p, o), None\n\n      (params, opt_state), _ = lax.scan(epoch_update, (params, opt_state), xs=None, length=num_epochs)\n      return params, opt_state\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating compute constraints**\n\nI'm considering compute constraints and the 30-minute limit for trials. Adding more compute during updates could limit the number of updates per seed. The training loop runs a single training_step per update, maintaining time constraints, but can compile heavy functions. If updates are fewer before the limit, it might reduce the covered timesteps. However, the training environment collects trajectories separately, ensuring 50 million environment steps remain intact. I need to consider how the number of updates impacts the overall results.**Assessing update limits**\n\nI'm analyzing the number of updates allowed, but the time limit might be reached earlier due to timeout checks. In the code, timeouts are checked every config['timeout_check_interval'] updates. The training_step_jit function remains constant, but increasing its complexity could lead to hitting the timeout sooner. Past data indicates they completed 39062 updates in about\
  \ 680-850 seconds, suggesting there's room for more compute per update. I think implementing clipped PPO with multiple epochs and mini-batches could work well within the time constraints.**Analyzing training step advantages**\n\nI’m looking into how the default training_step performs. It benefits from old_log_probs in batch data, filled from collect_trajectory’s vmap of select_action returns. The PPO ratio usage seems correct, but we didn't utilize multiple epochs. Considering improvements, we could explore V-trace or advantage normalization over time. Customizing gamma/gae_lambda might produce lower scores, like 36.2 or 32.2 compared to the baseline of 40.8. Additionally, entropy scheduling could help; using a higher entropy coefficient might encourage exploration. Implementing dynamic entropy annealing could make a difference, but I need to find a way to track the iteration number.**Exploring improvement strategies**\n\nI'm considering approximating by using the magnitude of advantages\
  \ or the time channel in observations, but that seems unusual. A better approach might be using the A2C algorithm with value normalization, specifically PopArt value normalization to stabilize targets. We could also apply reward scaling or value standardization, though reward shaping isn't allowed. Another potential improvement is to use separate optimizers for policy and value with different learning rates. While this isn't straightforward due to how create_optimizer works, I can implement a multi-transform that uses masks for policy and value parts with Flax and optax.**Designing training strategies**\n\nI'm exploring how to name networks without explicit parameter names by labeling them based on dictionary keys. I’ll create a function to distinguish policy from value for the CNN+LSTM architecture. A potential improvement is implementing clipped PPO with GAE and a KL adaptive penalty. I’ll also consider using TD-lambda returns while avoiding LSTM changes. Additionally, I can reset RNN\
  \ states properly during training. For reward clipping, using a range of [-1, 1] could reduce signal. My plan includes submitting a PPO with multiple epochs and mini-batches, ensuring proper adjustments for training_step.**Structuring PPO updates**\n\nI'm designing the training step for our PPO algorithm with several important components. First, I'll pre-calculate the advantages and returns, and if initial RNN states are present, I'll define a function for scanning data. The `compute_losses()` function will get new log probabilities and calculate policy loss with clipping, possibly using a clipped surrogate approach. I'll loop through the number of epochs specified in hyperparameters, applying updates accordingly. \n\nAdditionally, I plan to include a KL penalty for adjusting policy behavior, but I can't adaptively change the coefficient. I also need to ensure proper handling of log probabilities and the architecture will remain fixed to the CNN-LSTM structure we began with. Finally, I'll\
  \ make sure to tag the submission appropriately for future reference.**Preparing submission code**\n\nI’m working with the `network.apply` function inside a JAX jitted context, and it’s functioning as expected. Now, I want to craft the submission code clearly, including necessary imports and hyperparameters for the CNN-LSTM class to maintain consistent shapes. It's crucial to remember that the default `training_step` in the configuration uses `jax.value_and_grad`, not just `jax.grad`.\n\nI’ll also consider including a `create_optimizer` function with gradient clipping, but I’ll keep the default `optax.adam` for now to avoid complicating the results. Once everything is set, I plan to submit the action."
