role: model
parts:
- text: "Great progress. Two ablations are running. I’ll prep normalized ConvLSTM variants to queue next and log a brief notebook update.\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update:\n  - Baseline re-run (ID 10): 23.6 mean—consistent with system CNN baseline.\n  - PPO multi-epoch (ID 8): 6.3 mean; frequent timeouts at ~30 min. Multi-epoch compute per update reduces total environment steps, harming performance under fixed wall-clock. PPO likely needs stronger KL control and/or fewer epochs to fit the time budget.\n  Plan:\n  - Queue ConvLSTM+GroupNorm gates (width=64) and stacked x2 + GroupNorm next.\n  - Await width/depth ablations (IDs 12, 13) before further changes.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_norm.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellGN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      kernel_size:\
    \ Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(\n              features=4 * self.features, kernel_size=self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMGN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              h = jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              c = jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n    \
    \          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM with GroupNorm on gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellGN(self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Heads\n          z = h_out.reshape((B, -1))\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM2GN(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset stacked states\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h1': zeros(), 'c1':\
    \ zeros(), 'h2': zeros(), 'c2': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {k: v * m for k, v in rnn_state.items()}\n\n          # Layer 1\n          (h1, c1), y1 = ConvLSTMCellGN(self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups)((rnn_state['h1'], rnn_state['c1']), x)\n          # Layer 2\n          (h2, c2), y2 = ConvLSTMCellGN(self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups)((rnn_state['h2'], rnn_state['c2']), y1)\n          rnn_state = {'h1': h1, 'c1': c1, 'h2': h2, 'c2': c2}\n\n          # Heads from top layer\n          z = y2.reshape((B, -1))\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ConvLSTMCellGN\", \"CNNConvLSTMGN\", \"CNNConvLSTM2GN\"]\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM + GroupNorm gates (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, groupnorm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Introduce GroupNorm on ConvLSTM gating preactivations to stabilize recurrent updates while keeping the default PG algorithm and fixed hyperparameters. Architecture-only change.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_norm import CNNConvLSTMGN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fix all defaults to isolate normalization effect (features=64)\n      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMGN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          num_groups=8,\n      )\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Stacked ConvLSTM x2 + GroupNorm (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, depth, groupnorm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Two-layer ConvLSTM with GroupNorm on each layer’s gates atop a residual CNN. Default PG and fixed hyperparameters isolate the impact of deeper normalized spatial memory.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_norm import CNNConvLSTM2GN\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      from ray import tune\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM2GN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          num_groups=8,\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to figure out what to do next. I have two running experiments (12, 13), and we’ve made progress — our ConvLSTM default PG score is 52.7, which beats the RNN PG baseline of 40.8, so that's great! However, there's a restriction on the Archive Room until we reach maturity. It seems we can't publish anything until we hit tick 50, but I can still prepare content in private memory while we wait.**Planning next experiments**\n\nI’m thinking about additional experiments, specifically involving normalization methods in ConvLSTM like layer norm and group norm. I want to try two-layer depth and adjust the capacity width while exploring gating modifications. But I'm limited to two concurrent experiments, which are already filled, so I can’t submit just yet. I could focus on writing reusable storage code modules and prepare a submission for scheduling once a slot is available. Also, there's a critical comment in train_single.py about updating RNN states,\
  \ but the actual code doesn’t seem to do that.**Examining the code for bugs**\n\nI’m taking a closer look at the provided code in the run_single_seed_training function, especially the training loop. I notice that the final RNN states should be carried from the previous trajectory to the next rollout, which is marked as critical for RNN networks. But there seems to be a bug! The final_rnn_states are already being assigned to rnn_states, which are then used as an argument in the next collect_trajectory_jit call. So, the comment about updating RNN states is unnecessary.**Analyzing PPO multi-epoch failure**\n\nI’m looking into why the PPO multi-epoch training is failing. It seems like the environment is using an on-policy PG, while the training step JIT is using entire trajectories once; this could create issues due to stale data. We've implemented a small KL penalty, but it might not be enough, so I’m thinking a bigger penalty or early stopping could help. Also, repeated epochs work with\
  \ importance sampling vs. old policies, but it’s clear that our approach isn't finishing the 50 million steps in the expected time, so I need to jot this down in the notebook.**Considering ConvLSTM and PPO adjustments**\n\nI’m pondering the idea of combining the ConvLSTM architecture with PPO, but past algorithmic changes have underperformed. Perhaps we can make minor improvements, like implementing advantage normalization, an entropy schedule, or tweaking the value loss coefficient schedule. However, I think we should keep it simple for now and proceed with the architecture track. I want to add spatial attention pooling after ConvLSTM while also testing layer normalization in the gating mechanism. \n\nI have to be careful with shared storage and code-sharing rules. While it seems like we can share code in storage, there's a strict prohibition against sharing raw code with other agents. So, I’ll continue ensuring that I adhere to all the collaboration rules while preparing for future submissions!**Planning\
  \ GroupNorm submissions**\n\nI’m thinking about submitting a third experiment, but it might queue until a slot opens. The system allows additional submissions, which can keep the GPU busy, but I want to follow best practices by performing one step at a time. For now, I can prepare to submit variants like \"ConvLSTM + LayerNorm on gates\" and \"ConvLSTM with residual connections.\"\n\nI also want to implement GroupNorm on ConvLSTM gating outputs for stabilization. My plan is to write a file with the necessary code and prepare for two submissions while making sure not to exceed the concurrent limit. I’ll keep things concise to manage tokens effectively, and I’ll rely on existing storage utilities to streamline the process!**Preparing submission commands**\n\nI’m focusing on creating minimal submission wrappers, including adding a path for imports and defining a network that reads hyperparameters. I’ll keep features fixed at 64 to isolate the effect of normalization and create relevant YAML\
  \ content. \n\nFor our command lines, I’ll ensure each /execute_action is on a new line. I’m also considering replying to the Private Memory Notebook with results and documenting failures from the multi-epoch PPO timeouts, although that isn’t immediate. Let’s implement this carefully!"
