tick: 16
role: model
parts:
- text: "I'll prepare improved ConvLSTM variants (GroupNorm + forget-gate bias, and an attention readout head) in lineage storage so we can submit them as soon as the current runs finish.\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_variants.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # --------------------------\n  # Core building blocks\n  # --------------------------\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellGNFB(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"ConvLSTM cell with GroupNorm on gates\
    \ and positive forget-gate bias.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      f_bias: float = 1.0\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          # carry: (h, c) with shapes (B, H, W, C)\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(\n              features=4 * self.features,\n              kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n              padding='SAME',\n              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n          )(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          # Normalize gate preactivations to stabilize recurrent dynamics\n          gates = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          # Forget bias encourages memory retention early in training\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f + self.f_bias)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n\
    \          return (h, c), h\n\n  # --------------------------\n  # Networks\n  # --------------------------\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMGNFB(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + 1x ConvLSTM (GN + forget-bias) with MLP heads.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      f_bias: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n\n          # CNN backbone (capacity parity with defaults)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n        \
    \  # Init/reset ConvLSTM state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellGNFB(\n              self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups, f_bias=self.f_bias\n          )((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Heads\n          z = h_out.reshape((B, -1))\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n\
    \          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM2GNFB(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + 2x ConvLSTM (GN + forget-bias) with MLP heads.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      f_bias: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset stacked states\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h1': zeros(), 'c1': zeros(), 'h2': zeros(), 'c2': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {k: v * m for k, v in rnn_state.items()}\n\n          # Layer 1\n          (h1, c1), y1 = ConvLSTMCellGNFB(\n              self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups, f_bias=self.f_bias\n          )((rnn_state['h1'], rnn_state['c1']), x)\n\n          # Layer 2\n          (h2, c2), y2 = ConvLSTMCellGNFB(\n              self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups, f_bias=self.f_bias\n          )((rnn_state['h2'], rnn_state['c2']), y1)\n\n          rnn_state = {'h1': h1, 'c1': c1, 'h2': h2, 'c2': c2}\n\n          # Heads from top\
    \ layer\n          z = y2.reshape((B, -1))\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMGNFB_Attn(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Residual CNN + 1x ConvLSTM (GN+FB), with spatial attention pooling\n      instead of flattening. Attention is general (no Sokoban-specific logic).\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      f_bias: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x:\
    \ jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset ConvLSTM state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out\
    \ = ConvLSTMCellGNFB(\n              self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups, f_bias=self.f_bias\n          )((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Spatial attention pooling\n          # attn logits: (B, H, W, 1)\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn_logits = attn_logits.reshape((B, -1))  # (B, H*W)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)     # (B, H*W)\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))  # (B, HW, C)\n          # Weighted sum over spatial positions\n          z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)  # (B, C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n\
    \          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\n      \"ResidualBlock\",\n      \"ConvLSTMCellGNFB\",\n      \"CNNConvLSTMGNFB\",\n      \"CNNConvLSTM2GNFB\",\n      \"CNNConvLSTMGNFB_Attn\",\n  ]\n```\n\nOnce the current runs (IDs 16, 17) finish, I will submit:\n- ConvLSTM + GroupNorm + ForgetBias (single-layer)\n- ConvLSTM + GroupNorm + Attention pooling (single-layer)\n\nI’ll wait for the two running evaluations to complete before queuing these."
thinking_content: "**Planning module development**\n\nI’m thinking of writing a module to create a unified building for convlstm, including optional group normalization and forget bias. We recently updated the memory capsule, but I'll also want to consider changing the ranking to a scoring system to capture the top values. While we know about scores already, it’ll be worthwhile to read evaluation logs for versions 16 and 17 once everything is completed. For coding, I need to ensure proper YAML formatting for values and blocks.**Implementing Conv layer details**\n\nI need to implement the bias in the Conv layer, which might be easier to handle by adding it after I compute the gates. So, after calculating gates from the convolution, I'll split them and add the bias to the forget gate. I’ll set the bias as a hyperparameter to +1.0. Additionally, I’m thinking of including an attention readout with multi-head global average and softmax spatial attention, while keeping the architecture straightforward.\
  \ Once I save the functions for CNNConvLSTM_Attn and finish my ongoing experiments, I can queue the new configurations for submission later.**Planning memory and scoring adjustments**\n\nI’m thinking about adjusting the Private Memory to include a record of my plan. It might also be good to go to the Research Counter and change the ranking to a score, so I can track leaders by score, but this might not be essential. I also need to keep an eye on the token budget since I'm at 62k out of 270k used, which is plenty. \n\nNext, I’ll write the code for `zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_variants.py`, focusing on the various classes, including `ConvLSTMCellGNFB` for group normalization and forget bias, along with several CNNConvLSTM variants.**Ensuring code implementation**\n\nI need to make sure that the code uses JAX's `jnp` and `flax`, following the import path 'storage/zephyr' for the networks. I also plan to implement an attention pooling function that provides a vector output. This will involve\
  \ calculating alpha with softmax over a flattened representation from a 1x1 convolution on `h_out`, resulting in a weighted sum across spatial dimensions. \n\nI want to keep the code length moderate and create a training step variant with small enhancements, like advantage normalization. We don’t need major algorithm changes, just some architectural adjustments will suffice. Implementing “conv_lstm_forget_bias_init” to add 1 is on my mind too.**Summarizing the action plan**\n\nI’m considering writing a private memory reply to summarize my plan. Earlier, I encountered a failure when trying to 'reply' in the Research Counter, but I did manage to execute 'reply 1' in Private Memory successfully. Now, in this Private Memory Room, I can create additional updates after writing the code but might skip that to reduce noise. \n\nI plan to set up submission templates in storage, but since I can’t submit right now due to ongoing experiments, I’ll focus on writing the code for `zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_variants.py`.\
  \ I'll implement the required classes, taking care to use `jnp` and `flax` throughout. Also, I'll make sure to adhere to GroupNorm specifications within the design. Once the code is ready, I'll hold off on submissions until the current experiments are finished."
