tick: 19
role: model
parts:
- text: "Great: attention pooling on ConvLSTM+GN set a new high score (54.4). I’ll submit two focused follow-ups: a ConvGRU baseline and an attention-temperature/forget-bias ablation on the ConvLSTM+GN+Attn variant.\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvGRU (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convgru, rnn, cnn, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Replace ConvLSTM with ConvGRU on top of the residual CNN to compare gated spatial memory variants under default policy-gradient training. Architecture-only change; hyperparameters fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convgru import CNNConvGRU\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fix to defaults; only introduce conv_gru_features to match prior capacity\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_gru_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvGRU(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_gru_features=hparams['conv_gru_features'],\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM+GN+Attn: temp and forget-bias ablation (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, attention, temperature, groupnorm, forget bias, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Ablate attention temperature and forget-gate bias on ConvLSTM+GroupNorm with attention pooling under default PG. Capacity and other hparams fixed to isolate effects.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  from ray import tune\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y =\
    \ nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellGNFB(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      f_bias: float = 1.0\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.GroupNorm(num_groups=self.num_groups)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f + self.f_bias)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c =\
    \ f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMGNFB_AttnTemp(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_groups: int = 8\n      f_bias: float = 1.0\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          # Init/reset RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features),\
    \ dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellGNFB(\n              self.conv_lstm_features, num_groups=self.num_groups, f_bias=self.f_bias\n          )((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          # Attention pooling with temperature\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn_logits = attn_logits.reshape((B, -1))\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n          # Heads\n   \
    \       z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fix training hparams; tune attention temperature and forget bias only\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([0.7,\
    \ 1.0]),\n          'f_bias': tune.choice([0.5, 1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMGNFB_AttnTemp(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          num_groups=8,\n          f_bias=hparams['f_bias'],\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to outline the next actions based on our strong results of 54.4 with ConvLSTM + GN + FB + Attention pooling. This looks promising compared to other numbers. I’m thinking about refining further—maybe testing attention pooling with temperature or multihead options. I have to be cautious about complexity though, keeping it simple. It might be interesting to add value head regularization like V-trace, but we should maintain the default PG settings. We could also experiment with GroupNorm and consider gating detach options. Writing an Archive paper could be a goal as well!**Navigating Archive Room access**\n\nThe Archive Room is marked as \"Unavailable - Requires Maturity,\" which seems to apply to guest access, but recursive access might still work. Earlier, I noticed a message stating that after 50 ticks, maturity would be reached, granting full access to collaborative features. Until then, I can't publish anything. However, I can prepare\
  \ a capsule with structured sections and results. I’ll also write code to store the attention variant in storage and push for more experiments—like multihead attention pooling and contextual gating options.**Analyzing gate bias effects**\n\nI’ve noticed the reset is happening. I forgot the gate bias, which decreased performance compared to GroupNorm alone (50 vs. 53.6). However, by adding attention, we boosted performance to 54.4, showing that FB alone may harm results. I might experiment with FB values like 0.5 or 2.0, since we used 1.0. While we didn’t expose f_bias as a hyperparameter, we can still test values like 0.0, 0.5, and 1.5. I should ensure to parse 'f_bias' from hyperparameters and consider tuning 'GroupNorm num_groups' too. Additionally, I want to test adjusting the \"attention pooling temperature\" with an 'attn_temp' parameter and replace attention pooling with global max pooling for comparison.**Submitting new experiments**\n\nIt seems we're limited to running two experiments\
  \ at a time. Currently, there are no running experiments, and after tick 19, experiments 20 and 21 finished. So, I can submit two new proposals now. \n\nFirst, I’m thinking of ConvLSTM + GroupNorm + Attention pooling with tuned f_bias values (0, 0.5, 1.0, 1.5) and possibly num_groups set to 4 or 8, along with conv_lstm_features of 64 or maybe 96. I should change one variable at a time while keeping minor hyperparameter tweaks within our architectural parameters. The system is set to sample four hyperparameter configurations from our search space.**Planning submissions and adjustments**\n\nI need to be careful not to dilute coverage by including too many degrees of freedom. I think keeping 2-3 options is best. Based on a pattern, I'll fix conv_lstm_features to 64 while tuning f_bias and attn_temp. For my new network design, I’ll modify CNNConvLSTMGNFB_Attn to include those parameters and num_groups. Although the current class allows f_bias, it doesn't have attn_temp yet. I can implement\
  \ attn_temp by dividing attn_logits by temperature before softmax, but that requires some editing in the storage code.\n\nTo avoid unnecessary complexity, I’ll duplicate the model within the submission code for the attn_temp adjustment. Alternatively, creating a new class in the storage file could work, updating it to include the new parameter while keeping previous classes unchanged. Then, I can propose two submissions: \n\n1) \"ConvLSTM + GN + Attn: temperature and group count tuning,\" which includes f_bias. \n2) \"ConvGRU (default PG)\" for comparison purposes.\n\nI'll ensure the code for both submissions is accurate and update my Private Memory with results. I'll follow through with these actions one step at a time, keeping an eye on token management to stay within limits.**Setting up AttnTemp variant**\n\nFor the AttnTemp variant, I’m embedding the module with the attn_temp parameter. I’ll define a class called CNNConvLSTMGNFB_AttnTemp with specific attributes like cnn_features_1,\
  \ cnn_features_2, conv_lstm_features, num_groups (set to 8), f_bias (1.0), and attn_temp (1.0). In the call, I’ll compute attn_logits and apply softmax on them divided by attn_temp to tune focus—potential values for attn_temp could be {0.7, 1.0, 1.3}, keeping f_bias tuned at {0.5, 1.0}. \n\nI’ll submit two actions: one for \"ConvGRU (default PG)\" and another for \"Attn temperature and forget-bias ablation.\" I might leave any updates to Private Memory for next time to keep things minimal. I'll also ensure proper YAML formatting for the titles and keep my message straightforward with a summary on the SOTA improvement to 54.4."
