tick: 20
role: model
parts:
- text: "SOTA updated: 54.4 with ConvLSTM + GroupNorm + Attention pooling. Two runs in flight (ConvGRU baseline, temp/forget-bias ablation). I’ll record findings, then stage LayerNorm and dilated CNN variants in storage for next submissions.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 20):\n  - New best: ConvLSTM + GroupNorm + Attention pooling = 54.4 (ID 21).\n  - GroupNorm single-layer (no attn): 53.6 (ID 16).\n  - Forget-bias on GN alone regressed to 50.0 (ID 20).\n  - Stacked GN hurt (38.4, ID 17). Single layer ≈ 2-layer (IDs 12,13 ~53).\n  Interpretation:\n  - Spatially structured memory is key; attention pooling over ConvLSTM features adds a steady +0.8 to +1.7 points.\n  - Extra normalization depth (stacked GN) likely over-regularizes and/or slows optimization under fixed time.\n  - Forget-bias without attention doesn’t help; retention is better leveraged when paired with attention.\n  Running:\n  - ConvGRU baseline (ID 23).\n\
    \  - ConvLSTM+GN+Attn temp/forget-bias ablation (ID 24).\n  Next (queued after results):\n  - LayerNorm-on-gates variant (LN vs GN).\n  - Dilated CNN backbone to widen spatial receptive field.\n  Notes-to-self: Quote YAML titles that contain colons to avoid parser issues.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n\
    \      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm on gates) + attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n\
    \          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h':\
    \ h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          # Attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bij,bi->bj', h_flat, attn)\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__\
    \ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_dilated.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int = 2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(1,1),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry,\
    \ x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_Dilated(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN with dilated blocks + ConvLSTM + MLP heads.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # Dilated CNN backbone to enlarge spatial RF\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          # ConvLSTM update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          # Heads\n          z = h_out.reshape((B, -1))\n          z = nn.Dense(256,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualDilatedBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCell\", \"CNNConvLSTM_Dilated\"]\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating architectures and normalization**\n\nI'm focusing on the ablation study and need to evaluate conv_gru vs conv_lstm, which we’ve already submitted.\n\nNext, I want to look into gating normalization types, specifically LayerNorm vs. GroupNorm. I could implement a LayerNorm variant soon, but we might also queue this for later.\n\nI'm also considering a value head architecture that adds value bootstrap with extra features while keeping the default PG minimal. Evaluating multi-head attention could be substantial, but I want to avoid domain-specific heuristics. I'll keep refining my approach!**Planning next iterations**\n\nI’m aiming for a succinct verbosity level of 3, and I’ll note that our current state-of-the-art (SOTA) is 54.4. For the upcoming runs, I'm considering testing the GN+FB LSTM without attention, since we've already tested it.\n\nI could look into adjusting the temperature to 0.5 versus 1.5. I’ve already tried 0.7 and 1.0, so maybe later I’ll check\
  \ 0.5 and 1.2. I’m also wondering about adding residual gating across time steps, but that could complicate things. \n\nUsing dropout on attention might be an option, but I think the RL training should remain stable. It's worth exploring the conv depth; a deeper ResNet could increase compute time, but our fixed compute means more parameters won’t change step counts. I noticed conv LSTM training times improved to around 1100 seconds, so we should stay of course. Adding \"coordconv\" for coordinate channels could also be interesting, but let’s avoid customizing the environment preprocessing.**Planning memory and architecture updates**\n\nI’m thinking about adding a convolution layer that uses 1x1 for gating, but I'm reconsidering that. A \"dilated conv\" could also help enlarge the receptive field, which is allowed in general.\n\nHowever, it seems like we shouldn't submit anything while two processes are still running. I don’t need to check previous pages at this point, and creating a public\
  \ memory isn't an option until maturity is reached. \n\nSo, I'll focus on updating my private memory with the SOTA update and my plans. I might also prepare a LayerNorm variant for storage and \n\nthe dilated conv variant. The goal is to produce code files to save tokens for future use. I’ll write to \"zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py,\" defining ConvLSTM with LayerNorm and including a Dilation parameter.**Organizing command structure and YAML rules**\n\nI need to make sure commands are placed properly, each on a new line. It’s also important to keep the 'rank score' updated, but it's already sorted. I might want to note that the 'tags truncated from 7 to 6' message means we should keep tags under 6 moving forward.\n\nI need to ensure that if I use a colon in titles, it must be quoted in YAML. For instance, I didn’t quote \"ConvLSTM+GN+Attn: temp and forget-bias ablation (default PG),\" which included a colon. \n\nWhile it still passed, I forgot the quoting rule, so I'll remember\
  \ that next time. For now, I'm going to hold off on submitting and prepare the code instead.**Planning actions for memory and code**\n\nI’m considering calling 'review evaluation id' to fetch logs for 21, but since I've already seen some system messages, I might skip that to save tokens. Instead, I'll focus on storage writes and creating or replying to private memory.\n\nI'll use commands like /execute_action{create} to add a new entry, replying to capsule #1 for updates. Then, I’ll go to private_memory to record the new SOTA, 54.4, and detail the effects of GN and GN+FB. After that, I can head to research for storage writes for both the LN and dilated files.\n\nFor the LN variant, I’ll define the ConvLSTMCellLN, incorporating LayerNorm on gates, and for the dilated conv network, I'll create a ResidualDilatedBlock using dilation. My focus is on keeping the code minimal and concise, avoiding unnecessary details, while developing the structure for future work.\n\nFinally, I’ll ensure to\
  \ quote YAML correctly in future titles but will limit the current action to replying rather than submitting anything now. Let's wrap up with the action commands!"
