tick: 23
role: model
parts:
- text: "Incredible jump—LayerNorm on ConvLSTM gates with attention pooling set a new SOTA: 63.5. I’ll now (1) test multi-head attention pooling with LayerNorm and (2) add a modest forget-gate bias to the LayerNorm model, each as a single-variable change.\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_ln_mha.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"ConvLSTM with LayerNorm on gate preactivations (per-pixel over channels).\"\
    \"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n      f_bias: float = 0.0  # default 0.0 to isolate MHA effect\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f + self.f_bias)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_MHAttn(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm gates) + multi-head spatial attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      num_heads: int = 4\n \
    \     attn_temp: float = 1.0\n      f_bias: float = 0.0  # keep 0.0 here to isolate MHA from forget-bias\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n\
    \              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM with LayerNorm gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features, f_bias=self.f_bias)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Multi-head attention pooling\n          Hd = self.num_heads\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(Hd, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)  # (B,H,W,Hd)\n          attn_logits = attn_logits.reshape((B, 8*8, Hd)).transpose((0,2,1))  # (B,Hd,HW)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)            # (B,Hd,HW)\n\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, 8*8, self.conv_lstm_features))           # (B,HW,C)\n          context = jnp.einsum('bhw,bwc->bhc', attn, h_flat)                  # (B,Hd,C)\n          z = context.reshape((B, Hd * self.conv_lstm_features))              # (B,Hd*C)\n\n  \
    \        # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTMLN_MHAttn\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_fb.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3),\
    \ padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLNFB(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"ConvLSTM with LayerNorm on gates and configurable forget-gate bias.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n      f_bias: float = 0.5\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f + self.f_bias)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n\
    \          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnFB(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LayerNorm gates + forget bias) + single-head attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      f_bias: float = 0.5\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset state\n\
    \          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM update (LN + forget-bias)\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLNFB(self.conv_lstm_features, f_bias=self.f_bias)(\n              (rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x\n          )\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, 8*8, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bij->bj',\
    \ attn, h_flat)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLNFB\", \"CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnFB\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM + LayerNorm gates + Multi-head attention pooling (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, multi-head attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Extend the SOTA LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM with multi-head spatial attention pooling (4 heads) to test whether\
    \ distributing attention improves planning signal aggregation. Training and capacity fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_mha import CNNConvLSTMLN_MHAttn\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_MHAttn(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          num_heads=4,\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n          f_bias=0.0,  # keep 0.0 to isolate MHA effect vs prior single-head LN model\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM + LayerNorm gates + Attention + ForgetBias (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, forget bias, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Ablate a modest forget-gate bias (+0.5) on the SOTA LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM with attention pooling. Tests whether encouraging memory retention improves performance under default PG.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_fb import CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnFB\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnFB(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          f_bias=0.5,   # isolate forget bias effect vs. prior LN model (f_bias=0.0)\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments for LN and GN**\n\nAlright, I want to run some ablation tests comparing GN and LN. It seems that LN improved performance. Next, I'm considering testing LN with forget bias toggling. The LN variant reached 63.5 without an explicit forget bias, which is interesting. I might want to investigate adding forget bias to the LSTM cell with LN, testing LN with and without it. I need to implement LN with attention and consider multi-head attention pooling as well. Let's keep things incremental to avoid too many variables at once!**Adapting LN for experiments**\n\nI'm thinking about how to adapt to LN since it significantly outperforms GN. We previously created the \"cnn_convlstm_coord_mha.py\" with GN and FB, but maybe I should consider an LN version with FB, MHA, and CoordConv. However, that feels like too many changes at once. It might be better to test MHA and CoordConv separately.\n\nI plan to run two experiments: one with LN using MHA pooling and another\
  \ with LN and attention plus forget bias. That should help keep things more focused!**Clarifying hyperparameter sampling**\n\nI need to isolate the effect of f_bias, and I think setting it to 0.5 might help. Ideally, I'd like to perform an ablation that tests both 0 and 0.5. However, I can't use loops here, so I should consider using Ray Tune for this. From what I understand, it samples four hyperparameters from defined ranges. If I define f_bias as [0.0, 0.5], it’ll explore those options across different configurations. It seems that the system actually runs multiple trials, but I need to clarify how parallel trials and seeds work together. It feels a bit ambiguous!**Understanding hyperparameter sampling**\n\nThe logs indicate that the training starts with four seeds, not separate trials, which raises a question about how hyperparameter sampling is utilized. It looks like they sample a hyperparameter set for each seed, leading to a \"best trial\" representing the best seed and hyperparameter\
  \ combination. If I include different choices for f_bias, each seed might use a different value. The final score reported is the mean across all seeds, but if the seeds have different hyperparameters, that could confound the results. It seems like this was a concern in the baseline too!**Setting up experiments with hyperparameters**\n\nI need to keep hyperparameters constant across seeds to avoid messy comparisons, especially for f_bias. I plan to run two experiments with f_bias fixed at either 0 or 0.5. Unfortunately, the submission interface only allows sampling; however, I can manually set f_bias in the network creation. \n\nI'll create two new scripts for LN with MHA and one for LN with f_bias. I also want to submit two experiments: one with LN and MHA pooling, and the other with LN, attention, and forget bias. I'll ensure the code and titles are formatted properly before proceeding!"
