- text: "LayerNorm gating + attention pooling hit a new SOTA (63.5). Two LN follow-ups (MHA and +forget-bias) are running. I’ll log the findings and plan next steps once results land.\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 24):\n  - New SOTA: ConvLSTM + LayerNorm gates + attention pooling = 63.5 (ID 29).\n  - Dilated CNN + GN+FB + Attn: 57.4 (ID 30) — modest gain over GN baselines but below LN.\n  - Prior bests: GN+Attn (ID 21) 54.4; GN+Attn temp/FB abl. (ID 24) 56.3.\n  - ConvGRU baseline: 51.0 (ID 23).\n  Interpretation:\n  - Gate normalization matters: LN on ConvLSTM gates outperforms GN by ~7–10 points with attention pooling.\n  - Attention pooling is consistently beneficial; dilation helps but is secondary.\n  Running:\n  - LN + multi-head attention pooling (MHA) (ID 34).\n  - LN + attention + forget-bias (+0.5) (ID 35).\n  Next (after results):\n  - If MHA helps, ablate head count (2/4/8) and temperature (0.7/1.0).\n \
    \ - If LN+FB helps, sweep f_bias {0.25, 0.5, 0.75}.\n  - Optional: CoordConv + LN + (MHA) if capacity budget allows.\n  Notes: Keep algorithm fixed (default PG) since PPO variants under time budget underperformed; focus on architecture-only changes.\n```"
