role: model
parts:
- text: "New SOTA confirmed (63.5 with LN-gated ConvLSTM + single-head attention). I’ll test two single-variable changes:\n1) Add CoordConv inputs to the LN+Attn model.\n2) Ablate attention temperature for LN+Attn (0.8 vs 1.0).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_coord.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  def coord_channels(batch_size: int, H: int = 8, W: int = 8, dtype=jnp.float32):\n      ys = jnp.linspace(-1.0,\
    \ 1.0, H, dtype=dtype)\n      xs = jnp.linspace(-1.0, 1.0, W, dtype=dtype)\n      yy = jnp.repeat(ys[:, None], W, axis=1)  # (H,W)\n      xx = jnp.repeat(xs[None, :], H, axis=0)  # (H,W)\n      coords = jnp.stack([xx, yy], axis=-1)    # (H,W,2)\n      return lambda: jnp.tile(coords[None, ...], (batch_size, 1, 1, 1))\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnCoord(nn.Module):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LN gates) + CoordConv + single-head attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # Append CoordConv channels\n          coords = coord_channels(B, 8, 8, dtype=x.dtype)()\n          x = jnp.concatenate([x, coords], axis=-1)  # (B,8,8,10)\n\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset RNN\
    \ state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM with LayerNorm gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, 8*8, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bij->bj', attn, h_flat)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Heads\n\
    \          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnCoord\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM + LayerNorm gates + Attention + CoordConv (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, coordconv, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Augment the SOTA LN-gated ConvLSTM + attention with CoordConv channels to ease spatial reasoning. Algorithm and other hparams fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import\
    \ sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_coord import CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnCoord\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnCoord(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"ConvLSTM + LayerNorm gates + Attention: temperature ablation (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, temperature, policy gradient\"\nabstract:\
    \ \"Ablate attention temperature for the LN-gated ConvLSTM + single-head attention model to test sharper vs softer pooling under default PG.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm import CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([0.8, 1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing model performance**\n\nI need to figure out our next steps. We've reached SOTA 63.5 with ConvLSTM, LayerNorm gates, and attention pooling. However, variations like LN with forget bias scored lower at 61.7, and LN with multi-head attention dropped further to 58.4. Earlier results with GN+Attn were at 54.4. On the upside, dilated CNN improved to 57.4, but still below the top score. It looks like LN gating is significant, while MHA appears to be detrimental. I haven't tested CoordConv with GN and MHA yet.**Planning model tests**\n\nI think we should test LN gating with CoordConv and single-head attention to see if it helps with coordinate channels. Also, attention temperature might be worth experimenting with. Previously, GN showed that an attention temperature of 1.0 worked best, but maybe testing 0.8 for LN could be interesting. However, we should change only one variable at a time. Additionally, I need to document this for our paper, but it seems like the Archive\
  \ Room is restricted until I reach maturity, which is a bummer!**Preparing submission draft**\n\nI think we should prepare a draft in my private memory that includes all the results. I need to check the storage content as well. We plan to write the final submission code as a module in storage under zephyr/networks best. We can create a \"submission\" that uses LN gating with single-head attention, and I might copy the existing code from ID 29 for reproducibility. \n\nWe should also plan experiments for LN gating with different attention temperature settings (0.8 vs 1.0) and coordinate channels. Multi-head and forget bias haven’t helped, and although dilation was useful, it’s still lower than LN. It might be worth testing a slight tweak with 96 conv_lstm_features, but historically, 64 worked best with ConvLSTM GN. I'm curious if 64 will still be fine for LN!**Planning variable tests**\n\nI want to ensure we're changing only one variable at a time. We can test LN attention with conv_lstm_features\
  \ set to 64 and 96. Sure, the default training code uses hyperparameters from tune.choice, but this width change can be an architecture ablation. It's interesting that this might increase compute, but our training is locked to the CPU, and the GPU cluster should be fine for budgets.\n\nTo keep things simple, I can set up variations: Variation 1 will be LN Attn with attention temperatures of 1.0 and 0.8; Variation 2 will test LN Attn with CoordConv; and Variation 3 will use LN Attn with 96 features. However, there's a limit of 2 concurrent experiments, and according to the last output, all previous experiments have been completed. It looks like we're ready to move forward!**Setting up experiments**\n\nAt tick 25, slots are free now that previous experiments (34 and 35) are completed. We can submit our next two experiments! Instead of using MHA in the existing file, we’ll implement LN with single-head attention and CoordConv. I’ll create a new module called `zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_coord.py`\
  \ that includes LN gating.\n\nI want to set up two experiments:\n\n1) LN + Attn + CoordConv (default).\n2) LN + Attn with temperature ablation (0.8 vs 1.0).\n\nI’ll need to navigate to the Research Counter to save and submit my work, making sure to include the necessary hyperparameters. Let's get to it!**Preparing for logging updates**\n\nI’d like to log updates to my Private Memory after the results come in, but that can happen later. I should also manage tags to keep them to about five, since not exceeding six is essential. Maintaining proper quoting for YAML titles is necessary, especially if they include colons to avoid breaking the format. Since our planned titles don’t have colons except for \"LN + Attn: temperature ablation,\" I’ll make sure to use quotes.\n\nNow, let’s implement the code for 'cnn_convlstm_layernorm_coord.py', including a function to append coordinates like we did before. I want to keep my token usage minimal while providing the necessary code. It’s time to craft\
  \ an assistant message with appropriate actions for execution. I’ll ensure that each action is on a new line, along with the corresponding YAML block. Let's go!"
