parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fixed-seed replicate: LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (64ch, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"replication, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Replicate the SOTA configuration with a fixed BASE_SEED=42 to standardize the 4 evaluation seeds and quantify stability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm import CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42  # fixed for replicability across runs\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(\n\
    \          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_pergate.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"ConvLSTM with LayerNorm applied separately to each gate preactivation.\"\"\"\n      features:\
    \ int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(i)\n          f = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(f)\n          g = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(g)\n          o = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(o)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n          f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n          o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + ConvLSTM (LN per gate) + single-head attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp:\
    \ float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n   \
    \       # ConvLSTM with LN per gate\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, 8*8, self.conv_lstm_features))\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bij->bj', attn, h_flat)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLNPerGate\", \"CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN per-gate normalization: ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, per-gate, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test LayerNorm applied separately to each gate preactivation in ConvLSTM (vs a single LN over all gates) with single-head attention pooling. Capacity and training fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_pergate import CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn\n  from ray import tune\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLNPerGate_Attn(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Assessing next steps**\n\nI’m thinking about running another replicate to confirm the mean, or perhaps making some additional minor adjustments like tweaking layer normalization parameters. However, I need to follow the guideline of changing one variable at a time. I also need to remember that the Archive Room is currently unavailable due to maturity restrictions, so I should continue experimenting while being mindful of memory and token budget management. I’ve used 139k of my 270k tokens, which is still okay!**Exploring BASE_SEED for replicability**\n\nI’m considering defining the constant BASE_SEED as 42 to unify my submissions across replicates. Previously, we sometimes set the seed differently, but I want to standardize this now. By using BASE_SEED = 42, I can generate seeds like 42 + {0,1,2,3} for comparisons with earlier submissions. Setting it to a fixed number like 123456 might help in achieving better replicability. I could also explore different gating locations\
  \ or variations with GroupNorm, but I’ll need to tread carefully with modifications in this environment.**Finalizing SOTA plan**\n\nI'm considering that we've matured to about 63.5 as a top score, and given the limited time, it might be best to finalize the “SOTA” around 61-64. I could run a \"median-of-2 replicates\" aggregator, but the system's leaderboard is based on the highest score. The user is expecting us to take further actions. I could suggest a meta update with the latest SOTA info, queue a fixed-seed replication of LN+Attn, and explore a minor ablation with LN epsilon. There's also the idea of gating \"pre-activation LN separately,\" but that might add complexity.**Planning next steps for SOTA**\n\nI'm reflecting on the strong SOTA and thinking we should craft a plan to use the \"Research Counter filter tag\" for ‘layernorm’ to assist with paper prep. This could help create a relevant results table, but I need to be cautious as it might consume a lot of tokens. We can preview\
  \ all before compiling. Updating Private Memory is necessary, and I might need to write \"train_config\" to shared storage, ensuring I do this from the correct room — Research Counter. \n\nI could queue actions like moving to research, submitting replication with BASE_SEED set to 42, and maybe experimenting with “LN epsilon” settings too.**Proposing experiments within architecture**\n\nGiven the two concurrent limit, I think we should set up two experiments. First, I want to try the \"LN-gated ConvLSTM\" with single-head attention, using BASE_SEED=42 to ensure consistent performance. The second experiment could involve small tweaks, like adding residual pre-activation around Conv features or regularizing the value head to prevent overestimation. \n\nNow, I should focus on designing an architecture-based plan that involves “LayerNorm per gate” and possibly gating with \"tanh-sigmoid normalization.\" I’ll avoid algorithm changes for now. I'll submit the fixed seed replicate and the per-gate\
  \ LN. Finally, I’ll ensure everything is written to the correct Research Counter room and stay cautious with token usage while crafting the content."
