parts:
- text: "Per-gate LN regressed (57.8). Fixed-seed replicate of SOTA is strong at 62.5, confirming the LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) + 1-head attention baseline is robust (~62–64). I’ll save the SOTA network helper to storage and run a second fixed-seed replicate (different BASE_SEED) to finalize stability.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/sota_ln_attn.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  SOTA network helper: LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) + single-head attention pooling.\n  Default CNN widths: 32/64. Attention temperature = 1.0.\n  \"\"\"\n  from typing import Any\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm import CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\n\n  def make_sota_network(\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32,\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64,\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64,\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0,\n  ) -> Any:\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(\n          cnn_features_1=cnn_features_1,\n          cnn_features_2=cnn_features_2,\n          conv_lstm_features=conv_lstm_features,\n\
    \          attn_temp=attn_temp,\n      )\n\n  __all__ = [\"make_sota_network\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Fixed-seed replicate #2: LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (64ch, BASE_SEED=7)\"\ntags: \"replication, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Second fixed-seed replicate of the SOTA configuration using BASE_SEED=7 to quantify stability across a different standardized seed set.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm import CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7  # second fixed seed set\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 36)\n  Results:\n  - SOTA: 63.5 (LN(shared)-gated ConvLSTM 64ch + 1-head attn, temp=1.0).\n  - Fixed-seed replicate #1 (BASE_SEED=42): 62.5 (stable).\n  - Per-gate LN: 57.8 (regresses) → reject.\n  Plan:\n  - Run fixed-seed replicate #2 (BASE_SEED=7). If mean in 62–64 range, lock baseline and proceed to paper drafting.\n  - No further architecture tweaks unless a simple knob clearly promises >63.5 (unlikely given ablations).\n  Paper:\n  - Emphasize LN>GN, attention pooling benefit, capacity sweet spot (64ch), temp=1.0, negative results (FB, MHA>1, PPO).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 36 update:\n  -\
    \ Per-gate LN scored 57.8 (ID 63) — below baseline; discard.\n  - Fixed-seed SOTA replicate (BASE_SEED=42) scored 62.5 (ID 62), consistent with earlier 63.5 run; baseline is robust (~62–64).\n  - Submitted second fixed-seed replicate (BASE_SEED=7) to finalize stability.\n  Next:\n  - If replicate #2 lands in 62–64, lock baseline and start turning the private outline into the Archive draft once matured (tables with mean±std and all IDs).\n  - Otherwise, if significant drop, revisit small knobs (e.g., CNN 32/64 vs 40/80), but current evidence suggests 64ch ConvLSTM + 1-head attn is optimal under the budget.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering replication strategies**\n\nI'm thinking about the Archive requiring maturity over 50 ticks, meaning publishing isn't possible yet. However, I can continue experiments and prepare local notes. There’s mention of running another replicate for stability, building on what we've already done with fixed seeds. I wonder if changing the BASE_SEED could help us get independent replicates and better estimate distribution. It’s all about balancing standardization with randomness, ensuring the results are as accurate as possible!**Planning architecture and replication**\n\nI'm realizing there's no need to chase more architecture since per-gate LN regressed. My plan is to submit the second fixed-seed replicate using BASE_SEED=7 and provide a meta update, documenting everything in Private Memory. I'm considering small attentional temperature adjustments, maybe sticking with 1.0 and contemplating 0.9 as an option, but it seems unnecessary. Additionally, I could explore\
  \ minor training algorithm adjustments, staying within allowed changes. Focusing on architecture now seems key while also summarizing results in a storage table. Lastly, I should reset the page size to 10 if it was changed!**Planning next steps**\n\nI think we should be careful when quoting YAML values with colons since our titles often include them. It’s good we’ve used quotes for those. Here’s my proposed action plan:  \nFirst, we should submit the second fixed-seed replicate with BASE_SEED=7 for LN+Attn 64 channels. We might also consider changing the CNN features, testing widths like 40/80 or possibly even 24/48. But honestly, it might not be necessary. After the replicates, I can draft the \"Archive Outline\" in private memory and store the SOTA network code properly, making sure to follow our process for Research Counter!**Correcting storage steps**\n\nI noticed that our last attempt to write the file \"sota_ln_attn.py\" in Private Memory didn't go through. So, the plan is to move\
  \ to the research area and properly execute the storage write for that file. Here are my next steps:  \n\n1. Move to research.  \n2. Write the file to zephyr/networks/sota_ln_attn.py with the previous content.  \n3. Submit the second fixed-seed replicate using BASE_SEED=7.  \n4. Set a meta update.  \n5. Summarize final steps in private memory, planning the \"Archive Table.\"  \n\nI just need to ensure we keep concurrent experiments to two. Since \"Running Experiments\" shows none, it's a good time to submit the second replicate and potentially replicate with the original time-based seed as well!**Planning for replication**\n\nI’m considering that we’re allowed two experiments. So, I can run the second replicate and maybe do an \"Attn Temp 1.0 replicate\" over fixed seeds, but I have to be cautious since more replicates can impact tokens. I think we should focus on one new replicate and possibly create a summary. Here’s how I’ll proceed:  \n\nFirst, I’ll write the content for the SOTA network\
  \ in storage, confirming the path exists since we saved 'zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm.py' earlier. Next, I need to implement the second replicate, update meta data, and check private memory. A \"rank score\" run could help sort the scoreboard, but I'll be mindful of token usage.  \n\nI’ll provide a commentary on results noting the per-gate LN underperformance, where the fixed seed replicate yielded 62.5, so I endorse the baseline. Lastly, my actions will involve going to research, writing storage, submitting the replicate, performing the meta update, and finally responding in private memory. I’ll make sure to mention we'll use BASE_SEED pinned replicates for clarity!"
