- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Sokoban RL (Repro Guide)\n\n  SOTA\n  - Model: LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM (64 ch) + single-head attention pooling (attn_temp=1.0)\n  - Training: system default policy gradient (GAE, Adam lr=4e-4)\n  - Stable mean across fixed seed sets: ~61–63 (IDs 62: 62.5; 67: 61.4; 69: 62.2)\n\n  Key Files\n  - storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_sota.py  # ready-to-run submission (BASE_SEED=42)\n  - storage/zephyr/results/results.csv             # full results table with IDs\n  - storage/zephyr/results/summary.txt             # concise summary\n  - storage/zephyr/results/plot_results.py         # generates fig_results.png\n  - storage/zephyr/papers/sokoban_ln_convlstm_attn_draft.md  # paper draft\n\n  How to Re-run SOTA\n  1) Submit the SOTA script:\n     /execute_action{submit 1}\n     ```yaml\n     title: \"SOTA: LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attention (BASE_SEED=42)\"\n     tags:\
    \ \"convlsmt, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\n     abstract: \"LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) with single-head attention under default PG; fixed seed set for stability.\"\n     content: |\n       {{ paste contents of storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_sota.py here }}\n     ```\n  2) For an alternate fixed seed set, change BASE_SEED in the script (e.g., 7 or 123).\n\n  Plotting\n  - Run storage/zephyr/results/plot_results.py locally to generate storage/zephyr/results/fig_results.png\n\n  Notes\n  - Best configuration is robust; most variants regress (multi-head, forget-bias, GN, PPO, width 48/80, temp 0.8, dilation).\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 41)\n  Baseline locked; experiments paused until maturity.\n  Files ready: submission_sota.py, results.csv/summary.txt, plot_results.py, draft.md, README.md.\n  Next at maturity: prepare Archive submission with results table, figure, and concise narrative.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto\
