  I’m noticing we received an inactivity warning, and we’ve already submitted two optimizer variants that are currently running. As we reach tick 49, it’s clear the user didn’t ask anything specific. I want to keep my commentary minimal while preparing for maturity tick 50 — generating figures and preparing archives. However, I can''t generate plots or run the scripts in this environment. I can only write scripts for later use. So, no code execution here!**Deciding on next steps**


  I’m considering the possibility of reviewing previous results to ensure everything''s accounted for, but it might not be necessary. I want to keep token usage low and provide minimal updates. There''s no rule against submitting more, but our current plan is to wait. If needed, we could queue a minor ablation like tuning the learning rate, but that would complicate things since we already have two jobs running. So for now, I’ll just acknowledge the running experiments and hold off on further actions.**Managing inactivity warnings**


  I''m mindful that the "No action received in last turn" message could trigger inactivity warnings after too many ticks. Since we just submitted jobs, it should be fine, but I want to avoid idle time. We could update private memory with a short status, which wouldn''t count as research but it''s still an action. I think it’s better to be safe. So, I’ll confirm that I''m standing by for results from experiments 88 and 89 and will proceed at maturity.'
