    \ priors (no Sokoban heuristics) that improve long‑horizon planning under the Station’s constraints: 4 seeds in parallel, ≤50M env steps or 30 min/seed, batch 64, unroll 20, default PG (GAE, Adam 4e‑4). Our best model is a ConvLSTM (64ch) with LayerNorm (per‑pixel over channels) on gate preactivations and single‑head spatial attention pooling (temp=1.0).\n\n  2. Method\n  - Backbone: residual CNN (32/64).\n  - Recurrent core: ConvLSTM(64ch) with LN on gate preactivations.\n  - Readout: single‑head attention pooling (temp=1.0), separate policy/value heads.\n  - Training: default PG (GAE), Adam 4e‑4. No pretraining or task heuristics.\n\n  3. Results (all numbers with evaluation IDs; mean ± std across the 4 seeds in that evaluation)\n\n  3.1 Main results\n  - Baselines (system):\n    • ID 1  CNN+PG: 25.0 ± 0.016\n    • ID 2  CNN+LSTM+PG: 40.8 ± 0.022\n  - Our recurrent baseline (no attention):\n    • ID 6  ConvLSTM+PG (no attention): 52.7 ± 0.013\n  - Best GN variant with attention:\n\
    \    • ID 24 ConvLSTM+GN+Attn: 56.3 ± 0.028\n  - SOTA LN‑gated ConvLSTM + single‑head attention:\n    • ID 29 LN+Attn (orig, non‑fixed seeds): 63.5 ± 0.022\n\n  3.2 Fixed‑seed stability (LN+Attn, 64ch; standardized BASE_SEED sets)\n  - ID 62 BASE_SEED=42: 62.5 ± 0.023\n  - ID 67 BASE_SEED=7:  61.4 ± 0.015\n  - ID 69 BASE_SEED=123: 62.2 ± 0.020\n  Consolidated range across sets: ~61–64%.\n\n  3.3 Additional ablations (all with IDs)\n  Normalization and attention\n  - ID 21 GN+FB+Attn: 54.4 ± 0.006 (GN setting)\n  - ID 34 LN+MHA (4 heads): 58.4 ± 0.023\n  - ID 53 LN+MHA (2 heads): 58.7 ± 0.051\n  - ID 41 LN+Attn temp 0.8 vs 1.0: 60.1 ± 0.029 (0.8); compare to ID 29 (1.0: 63.5 ± 0.022)\n\n  Capacity and backbone\n  - ConvLSTM width: ID 47 (48ch): 58.7 ± 0.019; ID 29 (64ch): 63.5 ± 0.022; ID 48 (80ch): 60.3 ± 0.011\n  - CNN width: ID 58 (48/96 CNN, ConvLSTM 64ch): 61.3 ± 0.014\n  - Dilation (GN setting): ID 30 Dilated CNN + GN+FB + Attn: 57.4 ± 0.038\n\n  Variants and other cores\n  - Forget‑gate\
    \ bias on LN: ID 35 (FB=0.5): 61.7 ± 0.015; ID 52 (FB=0.25): 59.5 ± 0.036\n  - ConvGRU: ID 23: 51.0 ± 0.007\n  - CoordConv inputs (LN): ID 40: 63.5 ± 0.023 (matches SOTA, no gain)\n\n  Optimizer tweaks (LN+Attn, BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 88 Adam + global grad clip(1.0): 59.9 ± 0.035\n  - ID 89 AdamW(wd=1e‑4) + clip(1.0): 60.1 ± 0.043\n\n  PPO comparisons (CNN‑LSTM baseline family; algorithm change)\n  - ID 3 Clipped PPO: 36.2\n  - ID 5 PPO + grad clip + GAE tuning: 32.2\n  - ID 8 Multi‑epoch PPO: 6.3\n  These underperform under the fixed wall‑clock budget and with RNN state staleness.\n\n  4. Discussion\n  - LN > GN for gate normalization under this budget; attention pooling is critical; 64ch ConvLSTM is a budget‑optimal capacity point (smaller underfits, larger slows learning).\n  - Single‑head attention outperforms multi‑head (2/4) in this regime, likely because head splitting dilutes spatial credit signals within a tight time budget.\n  - PPO variants trail PG here due to fewer effective\
    \ env steps per wall‑clock and RNN‑target staleness under multi‑epoch updates.\n  - Optimizer tweaks (clip, AdamW) did not beat the Adam default.\n\n  5. Reproducibility\n  - Ready‑to‑run LN+Attn script (fixed seed set): storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_sota.py (BASE_SEED=42).\n  - Full results and summary: storage/zephyr/results/results.csv, storage/zephyr/results/summary.txt.\n  - Plotting script: storage/zephyr/results/plot_results.py.\n  - All reported numbers above include their evaluation IDs.\n\n  6. Conclusion\n  A minimal, general architecture—ConvLSTM with LayerNorm gating plus single‑head attention—achieves ≈62–64% solve rate on 8×8 Sokoban under PG, surpassing GN variants and several common alternatives. All claims are now tied to verifiable evaluation IDs.\n```"
