parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_ln_mha_grouped.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          # carry: (h, c) each (B,H,W,C)\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                       \
    \   kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_Concat(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) + grouped 2-head attention over channel halves, concat+MLP aggregation.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n\
    \          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM update with LN gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Grouped 2-head attention: split channels and attend each half separately\n          C = self.conv_lstm_features\n          assert C % 2 == 0, \"conv_lstm_features must be even for\
    \ grouped heads\"\n          h1, h2 = jnp.split(h_out, 2, axis=-1)  # (B,8,8,C/2) each\n\n          # Per-head 1x1 conv logits\n          logits1 = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h1).reshape((B, -1))\n          logits2 = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h2).reshape((B, -1))\n\n          attn1 = nn.softmax(logits1 / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)  # (B,64)\n          attn2 = nn.softmax(logits2 / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)  # (B,64)\n\n          h1_flat = h1.reshape((B, 64, C//2))\n          h2_flat = h2.reshape((B, 64, C//2))\n\n          ctx1 = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn1, h1_flat)  # (B,C/2)\n          ctx2 = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn2, h2_flat)  # (B,C/2)\n\n          # Concat contexts -> (B,C)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([ctx1, ctx2], axis=-1)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_GatedSum(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"LN-gated ConvLSTM + grouped 2-head attention with learned per-head gates (gated sum).\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n               \
    \       kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          C = self.conv_lstm_features\n          assert C % 2 == 0, \"conv_lstm_features must be even for grouped heads\"\n          h1, h2 =\
    \ jnp.split(h_out, 2, axis=-1)\n\n          logits1 = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h1).reshape((B, -1))\n          logits2 = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h2).reshape((B, -1))\n          attn1 = nn.softmax(logits1 / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          attn2 = nn.softmax(logits2 / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n\n          h1_flat = h1.reshape((B, 64, C//2))\n          h2_flat = h2.reshape((B, 64, C//2))\n          ctx1 = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn1, h1_flat)  # (B,C/2)\n          ctx2 = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn2, h2_flat)  # (B,C/2)\n\n          # Learned scalar gates per head from concatenated contexts\n          gates_raw = nn.Dense(2, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([ctx1, ctx2], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.sigmoid(gates_raw)  # (B,2)\n          # Weighted sum; project ctx1/ctx2 to same size\
    \ and sum\n          ctx = jnp.concatenate([ctx1, ctx2], axis=-1)  # (B,C)\n          # For stability, compute weighted sum at the split level\n          ctx_sum = gates[:, :1] * ctx1 + gates[:, 1:] * ctx2  # (B,C/2)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([ctx_sum, ctx_sum], axis=-1)  # (B,C) simple expansion\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\n      \"ResidualBlock\",\n      \"ConvLSTMCellLN\",\n      \"CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_Concat\",\n      \"CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_GatedSum\"\
    ,\n  ]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Grouped 2-head attention (concat+MLP) on LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, multi-head, grouped\"\nabstract: \"Test a 2-head attention variant that attends over disjoint channel halves with per-head 1x1-logits and concatenates per-head contexts with an MLP aggregator. Keeps LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch), default PG, and budget.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_mha_grouped import CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_Concat\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_Concat(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Grouped 2-head attention (gated-sum) on LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, multi-head, grouped, gating\"\nabstract: \"Test a 2-head attention variant with grouped channel halves and learned per-head gates to aggregate contexts (gated sum). Keeps LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch), default PG, and budget.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_mha_grouped import CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_GatedSum\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n \
    \         'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn_GatedSum(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Meta Protocol (Post-acceptance)\n  - Published paper with full IDs. Reviewer suggested exploring multi-head attention with specialization/aggregation.\n  - Submitted two grouped 2-head variants (concat+MLP, gated-sum) with BASE_SEED=42 to test if structured MHA can surpass 63.5.\n  - Keep algorithm and budget fixed; report IDs and update Archive capsule if improvements are observed.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next actions**\n\nI need to decide what to do next since the agent is in the Archive Room and the paper has been accepted. The previous inactivity warning got resolved, so we can move forward with our research. There’s no direct question from the user, but it seems we should either go to the Public Memory Room and announce or head to the Common Room. I can store files and summarize results with IDs for broader communication, but generating an image may not be feasible. Let's update the meta prompt to show the matured status.**Proposing next experiments**\n\nI might suggest experiments focused on improving MHA, particularly with the recent addendum. Since I've already added it, I can start scheduling these experiments. The previous idea was to use grouped channel heads and entmax, so I plan to implement and submit a 2-head grouped MHA variant, while being cautious about token coupling. I have a token budget of 188k, which is sufficient. I’ll create a storage\
  \ file to implement CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn with minimal architecture, using per-head gating for attention logits.**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI need to submit two experiments: one with grouped 2-head attention pooling combined with a concat and MLP aggregator, and the other with a gated sum aggregator that uses per-head temperature parameters. Fixed seeds aren’t necessary since the system uses a time-based default unless I set BASE_SEED. I can standardize it at 42 if needed. I’ll also implement a temperature of 1.0, even if 0.8 was an option. Finally, I might notify Public Memory with a high-level summary, but the priority is to proceed with the action of writing the new module and then submitting the experiments.**Writing code for attention model**\n\nI’m setting out to write some code now. I'll start by importing jax and flax.linen, and defining a class called ResidualBlock — I might reuse some existing code for this. For simplicity, I’ll replicate only the necessary pieces,\
  \ keeping it concise. Next, I’ll define the Grouped2HAttention pooling class, inputting a shape of (B, 8, 8, C). \n\nI’ll perform operations like splitting channels, computing attention logits, and applying softmax on the features. The aggregator could either concatenate context vectors from two heads or use a 256 Dense layer with ReLU. It's essential to incorporate the aggregator before generating policy/value while maintaining LayerNorm gating throughout.  I’ll also ensure to reuse pre-existing code from storage for efficiency.**Preparing submissions for MHA**\n\nI need to ensure the submission references the new network module. For the MHA, I could implement a new one using LN gating cells from scratch, or I could try importing and modifying CNNConvLSTMLN_Attn, but I’ve decided to define CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2HAttn and copy its structure instead. Once I complete the code, I'll go ahead with two submissions: one with the Grouped2HAttn and a concat MLP aggregator, and another with a gated\
  \ sum aggregator using learned gates. I'll set BASE_SEED to 42 and update the meta to reflect these planned experiments. I'll aim to produce this in one response with all actions included."
