tick: 54
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_ln_mha_grouped_learned.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2H_LearnedTemp(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) + grouped 2-head attention with learned per-head temperatures.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      init_temp: float = 1.0  # initial temperature per head\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x =\
    \ nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM update with LN gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Grouped 2-head attention over channel halves\n          C = self.conv_lstm_features\n          assert C % 2 == 0, \"conv_lstm_features must be even for grouped heads\"\n          h1, h2 = jnp.split(h_out,\
    \ 2, axis=-1)  # (B,8,8,C/2)\n\n          # Per-head temps (learned positive scalars)\n          log_temp1 = self.param('log_temp1', lambda rng: jnp.log(jnp.array(self.init_temp)))\n          log_temp2 = self.param('log_temp2', lambda rng: jnp.log(jnp.array(self.init_temp)))\n          temp1 = jnp.maximum(jnp.exp(log_temp1), 1e-3)\n          temp2 = jnp.maximum(jnp.exp(log_temp2), 1e-3)\n\n          # Per-head 1x1 conv logits\n          logits1 = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h1).reshape((B, -1))\n          logits2 = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h2).reshape((B, -1))\n\n          attn1 = nn.softmax(logits1 / temp1, axis=-1)\n          attn2 = nn.softmax(logits2 / temp2, axis=-1)\n\n          h1_flat = h1.reshape((B, 64, C//2))\n          h2_flat = h2.reshape((B, 64, C//2))\n          ctx1 = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn1, h1_flat)\
    \  # (B,C/2)\n          ctx2 = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn2, h2_flat)  # (B,C/2)\n\n          # Concatenate contexts and MLP aggregation\n          z = jnp.concatenate([ctx1, ctx2], axis=-1)  # (B,C)\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n\n          # Heads\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Grouped 2-head attention with learned per-head temperatures (LN-gated ConvLSTM 64ch)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, multi-head, temperature\"\nabstract: \"\
    Extend grouped 2-head attention by learning per-head temperatures to avoid credit dilution (head-specific sharpness). Keep LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch), default PG, budget, and BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_mha_grouped_learned import CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2H_LearnedTemp\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_Grouped2H_LearnedTemp(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n\
    \          init_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum (new experiments with IDs):\n  - ID 92: Grouped 2-head attention (concat+MLP agg) on LN-gated ConvLSTM(64ch) scored 63.2 ± 0.029 with BASE_SEED=42 — close to single-head 63.5 but not surpassing.\n  - ID 93: Grouped 2-head attention (gated-sum agg) scored 53.7 ± 0.030 — underperforms; naive gating unstable under budget.\n  Next submitted (pending IDs):\n  - Grouped 2-head with learned per-head temperatures (head-specific sharpness) to mitigate credit dilution while keeping budget and algorithm fixed.\n  We will report the new evaluation ID and result in a subsequent update.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning model adjustments**\n\nI need to respond since the user hasn't specified anything. The system shows results for a grouped 2-head attention model with an accuracy of 63.2, which is close to the state-of-the-art score of 63.5 but slightly lower. Gated-sum performed poorly at 53.7. I should probably log these findings and consider small tweaks like per-head temperatures, sparsity, and head dropout. We might want to prepare an archive update with our new results and possibly run additional tests with different temperature parameters.**Exploring model adjustments**\n\nI'm considering proposing a \"per-head learned temperature\" adjustment, but it might be tricky since the training framework requires a pure Flax module. I can implement a variable to scale the logits per head. Also, there's potential for sparse attention using entmax or sparsemax, which is complex but manageable in JAX. Alternatively, we could use a 2-head grouped configuration with head dropout and\
  \ gating, but that may not perform well. I should keep minor variable changes and consider generating plots later. An archive update could be beneficial too!**Planning new experimental variants**\n\nThe latest suggestions mention we’ve matured enough to proceed with a few actions. First, I’ll reply to the archive with new result IDs (92 and 93) and note that the grouped 2-head (concat) achieved 63.2, which falls short of 63.5. That means the structured MHA hypothesis holds partially.\n\nNext, I’ll implement a variant for \"Grouped 2-head with per-head learned temp,\" using a network module variant file. We'll also explore \"Sparse attention using entmax15,\" considering it might be complex but can be managed with a sharp softmax instead.**Designing new variants**\n\nI believe keeping the 2-head grouping to halves is sufficient. Since we’ve completed job IDs 92 and 93, it's time to submit two new ones. I'll remember to consider inactivity warnings, although we just submitted recently. I’ll\
  \ create a code file named \"cnn_convlstm_ln_mha_grouped_learnedtemp.py\" that incorporates per-head learned temperature parameters. This will use a softplus function for scaling.\n\nAdditionally, I’m thinking of a second variant, \"Hybrid single+two-head residual,\" which could be complex, so perhaps I’ll test the learned temperature approach first. Alternatively, I might explore a simpler \"sparsemax\" to streamline the definition.**Implementing sparsemax and new variants**\n\nI think a robust implementation of sparsemax is doable. The plan is to compute \\( z = \\text{logits} - \\text{mean} \\), sort them, and find \\( k \\) such that \\( z_i - \\frac{\\sum z_j}{k} > 0 \\) to compute \\( \\tau \\) and produce \\( p = \\max(z - \\tau, 0) \\). I’ll also consider combining per-head learned gates with a single-head residual. \n\nThe steps include updating the archive with results, submitting two new experiments—one for grouped 2-head attention and another for the mixed residual variant.\
  \ I'll ensure we carefully format the YAML values as well while crafting the code!"
