tick: 59
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_ln_attn_variants.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnLearnTempNorm(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      LN-gated ConvLSTM with single-head attention pooling.\n      Differences vs baseline: learned positive temperature (exp(param)) and optional\n      LayerNorm on features before attention to stabilize attention logits.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      use_feat_ln: bool = True\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n           \
    \           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          if self.use_feat_ln:\n              h_out = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(h_out)\n\
    \n          # Learned attention temperature (init ~1.0)\n          log_temp = self.param('attn_log_temp', lambda k: jnp.array(0.0))\n          temp = jnp.exp(log_temp)\n\n          # Single-head spatial attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)  # (B,8,8,1)\n          logits = logits.reshape((B, -1))  # (B,64)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits / temp, axis=-1)  # (B,64)\n\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))  # (B,64,C)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, h_flat)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  class CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnStandardized(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      LN-gated ConvLSTM with single-head attention where attention logits are standardized\n      per-sample across spatial positions before softmax. Intuition: stabilize and sharpen\n      attention without changing capacity.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Single-head attention with standardized logits\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)  # (B,8,8,1)\n          logits = logits.reshape((B, -1))  # (B,64)\n          mu = logits.mean(axis=-1,\
    \ keepdims=True)\n          sigma = logits.std(axis=-1, keepdims=True) + 1e-5\n          logits_std = (logits - mu) / sigma\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits_std, axis=-1)\n\n          H = W = 8\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features))  # (B,64,C)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, h_flat)  # (B,C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\n      \"ResidualBlock\",\n      \"ConvLSTMCellLN\",\n      \"CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnLearnTempNorm\"\
    ,\n      \"CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnStandardized\",\n  ]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (learned temp + feature LN)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, learned temperature\"\nabstract: \"SOTA LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) with single-head attention, adding a learned attention temperature and LayerNorm on features before attention to stabilize/sharpen pooling. Default PG and fixed hyperparameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_attn_variants import CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnLearnTempNorm\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnLearnTempNorm(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          use_feat_ln=True,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (standardized logits)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, normalization\"\nabstract: \"SOTA LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) with single-head attention where spatial attention logits are standardized per-sample before softmax to stabilize gradients and encourage peaky credit. Default PG; fixed hyperparameters.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_attn_variants import CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnStandardized\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n\
    \          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnStandardized(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 59)\n  Token load pruned to ~30%. Continuing targeted, low-risk architectural tests while preserving SOTA baseline:\n  - Submitted single-head variants: (a) learned attention temperature + feature LN; (b) standardized attention logits.\n  - BASE_SEED=42; default PG; one variable at a time.\n  - If neither >63.5, we retain 1-head baseline and focus on qualitative analysis + documentation.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Exploring temperature and algorithms**\n\nI've been experimenting with temperature settings, comparing 0.8 and 1.0, though 0.8 didn't yield good results. I’m considering trying 1.2, but it's not looking promising so far. Adding LayerNorm to pre-attention conv features or adjusting attention logits might help without too much complexity. Maybe exploring temperature annealing could be viable too, although my training setup is fixed. There are other adjustments we could make, like trying out learned temperature parameters for single-head attention.**Considering memory and experimentation**\n\nI noticed I can now read the full document with \"read 2,\" but I'm cautious about token usage since I have 81k tokens left. It's important to prune wisely and update my private memory to reflect that. I'm also thinking about accessing the Common Room, which was previously unavailable but now seems matured—though it isn't critical. For my next steps, I should focus on proposing a minimal\
  \ new experiment involving single-head LayerNorm gating and \"sparse attention via top-k softmax.\" This could be interesting!**Addressing implementation complexity**\n\nI'm considering adding a function to compute a top-k distribution by picking the top m positions using logits. I’ve found that JAX has ops for top_k with 'jax.lax.top_k', but I'm not sure if it's available. Writing 'entmax15' softmax from scratch would be heavy, so I wonder if a simpler approach like temperature-scheduled attention would work—though training returns can’t pass timesteps. We have a time channel that could help compute temperature as a function of time. I could also explore using a learned scalar temperature parameter clipped between [0.5, 1.5].**Planning concurrent experiments**\n\nI'm proposing to test two small variants in concurrent experiments: the first is a single-head learned temperature LayerNorm gating baseline with feature normalization before attention, and the second includes attention logits\
  \ being normalized by subtracting the mean and dividing by the standard deviation to sharpen them while keeping stability. I should craft two submissions and update the archive about the pruning plan, although it might not be essential.  \n\nI’ll create the code in 'cnn_convlstm_ln_attn_variants.py' within storage/zephyr/networks. I want to make sure the CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnLearnTempNorm module incorporates attn_temp as a learned positive scalar parameter and applies LayerNorm either across channels or using GroupNorm at each pixel.**Implementing normalized attention variants**\n\nI’ll implement a function where if we use feature LayerNorm, we'll apply it to h_out. The module CNNConvLSTMLN_AttnStandardized will compute attention logits through a 1x1 convolution, standardizing them per sample across all 64 positions. After that, I’ll apply softmax.\n\nI'll submit two fixed hyperparameter experiments, making sure to include \"from ray import tune\" and setting BASE_SEED to 42 to maintain consistency.\
  \ I’ll also write the file for both variants and ensure the correct LayerNorms are applied while checking memory tokens. Keeping track of disclaimers is important too!"
