thinking_content: "**Considering output options**\n\nI didn't read the instructions thoroughly earlier, but it seems like saving isn't provided. Maybe I could modify the submission to save ephemeral outputs in some form. I recall that we persisted files before, but writing to a storage path during remote tasks could be tricky. The only function we can run is 'test()', which limits our options. I’m wondering about logging in training for attention maps, but that might be too risky. Alternatively, I could ask to preview Aether I's paper, but I've already done that and only saw the abstract. Thus, I need to plan my next steps more carefully!**Managing tokens and experiments**\n\nI need to focus on token management since we have seven ticks left before the next prune. Scheduling that will help keep future tokens lower. As I run experiments, a baseline with some Y/N checks could be useful. It would be great to log results to keep track. I’m thinking of going to Archive to preview Aether #2 fully,\
  \ but reading the whole capsule could take a lot of tokens. The tip suggests previewing is cheaper, so I should prioritize that! We’ve already done a preview, so that’s good. Now with two experiments running, I could draft a qualitative analysis plan in my private memory.**Planning experiments and updates**\n\nI’m considering proposing an additional small ablation, like comparing attention logit standardization versus not. We already have that, so another possibility could be head dropout. However, I want to stick to the principle of changing only one variable at a time, and since we’re already testing, it might be better to wait. The \"Research Inactivity detected\" message suggests I should maintain activity, so I’ll send a minimal acknowledgment about awaiting results. \n\nSince the UI encourages using station actions, I’ll update my private memory summary but it’s not strictly necessary. The multi-agent environment expects commands with /execute_action, and I’ve been using them quite\
  \ a bit. I'll go ahead and add a brief note about my next prune ticks and the overall status. I could also set the meta to reflect that experiments are running, but I’ve already done that. Alternatively, I could prepare the token management prune schedule, though we’re currently on cooldown.**Analyzing attention weights**\n\nAlright, I’m considering staging analysis scripts to compute attention entropy and gating stats from network forward passes using random sequences. However, to do this for environment rollouts, I need the environment files, which might exist in storage. I could write a CPU analysis script using the test() function in a submission to instantiate the environment, run episodes, and record attention weights. \n\nBut, the current network code doesn’t return these weights since we didn’t expose them. We could modify the network to return extra outputs like the last attention weights, but the 'create_network' signature expects only specific outputs. So, if I change it, that\
  \ could break things. Thus, for now, I’ll need to compute attention weights outside of training using the network modules.**Planning analysis and actions**\n\nI’m thinking about how to simulate calling the module forward and hooking into internal convolution or attention logits. In our LN+Attn architecture, I would need to restructure things or create a separate 'analysis_network' that returns both outputs and attention. The test() function can instantiate our network class, but since attention is computed inside that call, I could either replicate that computation or modify the module to optionally return attention. However, altering the network signature could impact training.\n\nAnother idea is to create a wrapper module that calls the baseline network while computing attention, but the weights would differ from actual training weights. Without saved checkpoints, it seems like there’s limited value there. So, it might be best to pause and wait for experiment results. \n\nFor now, I\
  \ should acknowledge the experiments running and maintain activity. I can update my private memory and plan for the next prune after cooldown ticks, so I’ll craft a note for that. I'll make sure to add that to the consolidated summary as well."
