- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_dilated.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int = 2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(1,1),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,\
    \ self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          # LayerNorm over channels (per-pixel)\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_LN_Dilated(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Dilated residual CNN + LN-gated ConvLSTM + single-head attention pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 2\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # Dilated CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n   \
    \                   kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM with LN gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\
    \n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, h_out.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualDilatedBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTM_LN_Dilated\"\
    ]\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_twostream.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_LN_TwoStream(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Residual CNN + LN-gated ConvLSTM, with two pooling streams: attention and GAP.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # ConvLSTM with LN gates\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Stream A: single-head attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp,\
    \ axis=-1)\n          ctx_attn = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, h_out.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n          # Stream B: global average pooling\n          ctx_gap = h_out.mean(axis=(1,2))  # (B, C)\n\n          # Fuse streams (concat + MLP)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([ctx_attn, ctx_gap], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n\n          # Heads\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTM_LN_TwoStream\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit\
    \ 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Dilated CNN (d=2) + LN-gated ConvLSTM + 1-head Attn (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilation, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test dilated residual CNN (d=2) feeding an LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) with single-head attention pooling, under default PG. Goal: enlarge receptive field without heavy compute to improve long-horizon planning.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_dilated import CNNConvLSTM_LN_Dilated\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_Dilated(\n\
    \          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=2,\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-stream pooling: LN-gated ConvLSTM + (Attn ⊕ GAP) (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, pooling, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Augment single-head attention with a parallel global-average-pooling stream (concat + MLP) on top of an LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch). Tests whether combining focused and holistic spatial summaries improves solve rate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_twostream import CNNConvLSTM_LN_TwoStream\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n \
    \         'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_TwoStream(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"On Sokoban feature engineering and station rules\"\ntags: \"discussion, research-policy, sokoban\"\nabstract: \"High-level note on domain-specific feature engineering vs. general architectures under Research Task 1 constraints.\"\ncontent: |\n  Friendly reminder for Task 1: the spec disallows Sokoban-specific heuristics (e.g., hand-crafted push/box heuristics or explicitly engineered “push destination” maps). General architectures\
    \ that learn from the provided observation channels are allowed; adding derived channels that encode task-specific logic may violate the “no domain-specific shortcuts” clause. When in doubt, please clarify with reviewers or provide justification in Archive submissions. This is a high-level policy note; not a judgment on any specific work.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering model improvements**


  I see that Nomos I scored 69.7, but we probably shouldn’t replicate certain features to stay within policy. Instead, we can focus on broader enhancements like dropout, gating-style attention, and advantage normalization. There''s also a competitor showing better results (69.7 vs. 63.5), which we need to evaluate. Their methods may involve domain-specific features, which we can''t use, but we should explore alternative general improvements, like multi-step lookahead with shallow transformers.**Planning experiments while monitoring budget**


  I need to keep an eye on our token budget, which is at 94k (35% used), so that''s good. I should carefully choose our next experiments to improve performance using allowed methods. We’ve already tested LN gating, attention, width ablations, MHA, temperature, optimizer adjustments, and dilations. The competitor achieved 69.7 through feature engineering, which isn’t possible for us. Next, I might explore self-attention across time or gating at timesteps using attentional pooling from our last k ConvLSTM outputs.**Exploring network signature API**


  The API for the network signature function `create_network(x, done, rnn_state)` returns a new `rnn_state` but doesn''t pass the entire history. However, I can maintain memory within `rnn_state` by storing an Exponential Moving Average (EMA) of previous outputs or using a small buffer. I could even include additional fields in `rnn_state` to capture the last K frames. We have to ensure that `rnn_state` retains the proper array shapes. If we need an alternative, we could try implementing Residual Squeeze-and-Excitation or a "Gated Spatial Bias" method with Fourier positional encoding.**Considering generalization techniques**


  I’m thinking about trying DropBlock or Spatial dropout for better generalization, but I wonder what their actual effect will be. Another plan is to gate attention with the advantage, but since we can''t use advantage directly in the training step, maybe we could implement an alternative training step algorithm, like Track 2. For improved stability and performance, we could explore methods like V-trace or GAE-lambda adjustment. Implementing value normalization for returns, advantage normalization per mini-batch, and gradient clipping could also be beneficial. A KL penalty might help prevent policy explosion, but it’s crucial that we’re careful about MHA impacts.**Evaluating training strategies**


  I’m exploring the idea of implementing a general policy gradient with a baseline and advantage normalization, even though I’m not sure if it’s already in use. Checking defaults and previous system logs might help clarify. An alternative could be incorporating architectural changes like ConvLSTM with slot attention, although that may be resource-intensive. We could also consider using a Spatial Transformer for soft attention instead. Given our competitor''s performance of 69.7, we need to pursue general methods to improve, like utilizing auxiliary losses for prediction. Implementing various strategies could optimize our training steps. I also need to manage tokens effectively while experimenting with these options.**Implementing new experiments**


  I see that our `training_step` signature is set, making it tricky to incorporate a schedule directly. We could manage schedules using parameters or the optimizer''s state, although I need to double-check how the environment code works. Since the competitor improved to 69.7 using domain-specific features, we can’t replicate that. I’m proposing two experiments: one adding LN-gated residual dilated CNN with a ConvLSTM, and the other using a two-stream model with average pooling and attention. I’ll ensure all code is minimal and correct before implementing.'
