- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Residual CNN + ConvLSTM with LayerNorm-gated gates.\n      Double-step recurrence per env step (shared weights): apply the same ConvLSTM cell twice\n      on the same input x to increase effective temporal computation without adding new layers.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              h, c = zeros(), zeros()\n          else:\n              h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              h, c = h * m, c * m\n\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          # Step 1\n          (h1, c1), y1 = cell((h, c), x)\n          # Step 2 (shared weights, same input x)\n          (h2, c2), y2 = cell((h1, c1), x)\n\n          rnn_state =\
    \ {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y2)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, y2.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\"\
    ]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) + 1-head Attn with double-step recurrence (default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, attention, recurrence, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Increase effective temporal computation by applying the same LayerNorm-gated ConvLSTM cell twice per env step (shared weights), keeping the CNN and attention pooling unchanged. Tests whether deeper recurrence helps planning under the fixed budget.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 66:\n  - Results: Two-stream pooling regressed (57.5); dilated CNN + LN scored 61.7; micro-sweep peaked at 61.8. Baseline remains ~62–64.\n  - Running: slot-style pooling (ID 112).\n  - Submitted: double-step recurrence (shared-weights ConvLSTM applied twice per step) to test deeper temporal computation without extra layers.\n  - Next: If both new variants ≤63.5, pause tweaks and focus on qualitative analysis and maintenance of the published baseline.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering architectural improvements**\n\nI should log the results and think about my next steps, like starting a qualitative analysis or planning some architecture improvements. One idea is adding depth to the recurrence of ConvLSTM over time. I could run two sequential ConvLSTM steps per environment step, but this might break the network's original design. However, implementing two ConvLSTM steps using the same input could work. It seems like an architecture change that might enhance planning depth!**Revisiting ConvLSTM configurations**\n\nI remember we previously experimented with stacked ConvLSTM layers using GroupNorm but not LayerNorm. The earlier attempts with per-gate LayerNorm didn't work well, regressing in performance. Now, I'm thinking about testing two ConvLSTM layers with LayerNorm gating, but we noted that stacking with GroupNorm regressed to 38.4. Interestingly, stacking ConvLSTM layers scored 52.9 before without LayerNorm. This suggests that stacking\
  \ under budget might not be the best approach. I’m also considering shallow self-attention or residual attention glimpses across multi-step memory.**Considering analysis and experiments**\n\nThere's a bit of complexity here! For qualitative analysis, I need to gather attention maps and gating stats, which means I should add some debug prints or a test() function for lightweight validation. Unfortunately, if we're missing training logs, we might be limited, but I can implement a test() to load the network and print aggregator shapes.\n\nRegarding token management, it seems unnecessary right now as we’re only using about 44% of our tokens. Currently, the slot pooling experiment is running, and there's one slot left for concurrent experiments. I could submit another test, possibly for the LN-gated ConvLSTM with single-head attention.**Exploring architectural variants**\n\nIt seems the time channel is key in the observation specification, and while I can't change the environment input, the\
  \ network could potentially ignore it. That's something to consider.\n\nNext, I might try an additive residual connection from CNN features after pooling, but we previously attempted two-stream pooling by concatenating GAP, which didn't perform well.\n\nLayerNorm could be added to the slot pooling architecture; we've already integrated it within slots, which should be fine.\n\nAnother thought is to use gating for attention pooling, combining attention and baseline. We've done two-stream gating with attention and GAP, but it underperformed.\n\nI’m also curious about implementing value bootstrap regularization or altering advantage normalization.**Formulating next steps**\n\nI'm considering various algorithmic adjustments. The default training step could be customized, but we previously saw regression with PPO. I could modify advantage normalization, think about a dynamic entropy schedule, and adjust the training step for that. \n\nI want to propose testing an \"object-centric architecture\"\
  \ with slot attention and increase iterations, even just one or two, to minimize compute costs. Also, incorporating multi-scale CNN features and residual memory gating could enhance performance, and I might test a stronger value head capacity. \n\nNow, I'm ready to detail actions: write the new double-step network, submit experiments, update memory, and ensure appropriate formatting for titles. Let's get started!"
