role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 67\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 59)\nToken load pruned to ~30%. Continuing targeted, low-risk architectural tests while preserving SOTA baseline:\n- Submitted single-head variants: (a) learned attention temperature + feature LN; (b) standardized attention logits.\n- BASE_SEED=42; default PG; one variable at a time.\n- If neither >63.5, we retain 1-head baseline and focus on qualitative analysis + documentation.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,505 / 270,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 67 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research\
    \ submission 'LN-gated ConvLSTM + Slot-style pooling (4 slots, default PG)' (ID: 112) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 46.3\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.499, 0.471, 0.441, 0.442]\nMean: 0.463, Std: 0.024\nBest trial: 1 (0.499)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 112\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the AttributeError in SlotPooling class that was preventing the network from initializing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in `storage/zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_ln_slots.py` had a bug in the `SlotPooling` class at line 47:\n\n```python\nscale = 1.0 / jnp.sqrt(C.astype(tokens.dtype))\n```\n\nThe variable `C` comes from `B, T, C = tokens.shape` and is a Python integer (not a JAX array). Python integers don't have an `.astype()`\
    \ method, causing an `AttributeError: 'int' object has no attribute 'astype'`.\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Copied the buggy SlotPooling class** from the lineage file into `submission_v2.py`\n2. **Fixed the type conversion issue** by changing line 47 to:\n   ```python\n   scale = 1.0 / jnp.sqrt(jnp.array(C).astype(tokens.dtype))\n   ```\n   This converts the Python integer `C` to a JAX array before calling `.astype()`.\n3. **Created a fixed version of the main network class** (`CNNConvLSTM_LN_SlotPool_Fixed`) that uses the corrected `SlotPooling`\n4. **Updated the create_network function** to use the fixed class\n\nThe fix preserves all the original functionality while resolving the type error. The evaluation is now running successfully without crashes, as confirmed by the \"pending\" status in the evaluation file.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code\
    \ (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom networks.cnn_convlstm_ln_slots import CNNConvLSTM_LN_SlotPool, ResidualBlock, ConvLSTMCellLN\nfrom ray import tune\n\nclass SlotPooling(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Single-step slot-style pooling (general, no domain heuristics).\"\"\"\n    num_slots: int\n    feat_dim: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, tokens):  # tokens: (B, T, C)\n        B, T, C = tokens.shape\n        # Learned initial slots (shared across batch)\n        slots = self.param('slots_init', nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), (self.num_slots, C))\n        slots = jnp.tile(slots[None, ...], (B, 1, 1))  # (B, S, C)\n\n        # Projections\n        k = nn.Dense(C, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(tokens)   # (B,T,C)\n        v = nn.Dense(C, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(tokens)   # (B,T,C)\n        q = nn.Dense(C, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(slots)\
    \    # (B,S,C)\n\n        # Fix: Convert C to JAX array before calling astype\n        scale = 1.0 / jnp.sqrt(jnp.array(C).astype(tokens.dtype))\n        attn_logits = jnp.einsum('bsc,btc->bst', q, k) * scale  # (B,S,T)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)                 # (B,S,T)\n\n        # Slot updates\n        slot_context = jnp.einsum('bst,btc->bsc', attn, v)      # (B,S,C)\n        # Lightweight MLP on slots\n        slot_context = nn.relu(nn.Dense(C, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(slot_context))\n        return slot_context.reshape(B, -1)  # (B, S*C)\n\nclass CNNConvLSTM_LN_SlotPool_Fixed(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Residual CNN + LN-gated ConvLSTM + slot-style pooling (S=4) - with fixed SlotPooling.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    num_slots: int = 4\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN backbone\n \
    \       x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n        # Init/reset state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # ConvLSTM\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n        # Flatten spatial tokens and apply\
    \ slot pooling\n        tokens = h_out.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features))  # (B,T=64,C)\n        z = SlotPooling(self.num_slots, self.conv_lstm_features)(tokens)  # (B, S*C)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return CNNConvLSTM_LN_SlotPool_Fixed(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        num_slots=4,\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n\
