    \ archive}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — Double-step recurrence result and recent ablations (all claims tied to evaluation IDs)\n\n  New main result (general, no domain-specific features):\n  - ID 116: LN-gated ConvLSTM (64ch) + single-head attention with double-step recurrence — 66.2 ± 0.028\n\n  Recent ablations and variants:\n  - ID 110: Two-stream pooling (Attn ⊕ GAP) — 57.5 ± 0.017\n  - ID 109: Dilated CNN backbone (d=2) + LN-ConvLSTM — 61.7 ± 0.012\n  - ID 113: Micro hyperparameter sweep around baseline — 61.8 ± 0.028\n  - ID 112: Slot-style pooling (4 slots) — 46.3 ± 0.024\n  - ID 99: Learned attention temperature + feature LN — 55.9 ± 0.024\n  - ID 100: Standardized attention logits — 61.9 ± 0.025\n\n  Notes:\n  - Double-step recurrence increases effective temporal computation under the same wall-clock budget and outperforms single-step (≈63.5) on the same fixed seed set.\n  - Replication and compute-conscious ablation are running and not included\
    \ in claims:\n    • Pending: ID 118 (double-step, BASE_SEED=7), ID 119 (double-step width 48, BASE_SEED=42).\n  - Reproducibility: ready-to-run script added at storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_double_step.py (BASE_SEED=42). Existing scripts for earlier SOTA remain unchanged.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 69)\n  Status:\n  - New SOTA (no domain-specific features): double-step LN-ConvLSTM 66.2 (ID 116).\n  - Replication (ID 118) and width-48 ablation (ID 119) running.\n  Plan:\n  - If stable ≥66 across seeds, finalize Archive revision with updated results table (IDs for all numbers), reproducibility script paths, and discussion on temporal compute vs env steps.\n  - Otherwise, retain 1-head LN-ConvLSTM baseline and consolidate qualitative analysis.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Continuing actions on Zephyr I**\n\nI need to respond as Zephyr I and continue with the next steps while we wait for runs 118 and 119. I should keep in mind the station rules about domain-specific feature engineering since we previously wrote a public note. With improvements in our research, we achieved 66.2 with the double-step LN ConvLSTM, which is a strong result. Now, I need to publish the updated Archive, ensuring it includes all evaluation IDs and our new results.**Proposing Archive updates**\n\nI should propose updating the Archive with the results indicating that double-step recurrence improves the LN-gated ConvLSTM to 66.2. It’s important that all numbers have evaluation IDs, and we already have many, like the 116 for double-step. We're waiting on results from runs 118 and 119. While we wait, I can draft a revision for the Archive, making sure to reference existing IDs and mark any pending experiments, as the Archive requires these IDs for clarity.**Updating\
