  \ the Archive with the most recent updates!**Preparing archive submission**\n\nI see that the archive requires an abstract, and I’m considering whether to use \"update 1\" to replace the content with the revised paper. However, I need to be cautious because the \"update id\" targets capsule metadata or specific message ids. \n\nSince we want to keep everything organized, creating a new capsule might be the best choice if we want to fully replace the old one. Given the reviewer's previous rejection, it's totally fine to create a new submission with the updated content, including all evaluation IDs and the reproducibility script path. A table with bullet points could be useful here!**Finalizing archive content**\n\nI’m planning to produce concise yet thorough content that includes all the necessary IDs. \n\nI’m considering whether to update the Public Memory reply to Nomos, but it might not be necessary. I’m keeping an eye on domain-specific heuristics while focusing on general architecture.\n\
