tick: 71
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch, BASE_SEED=123)\"\ntags: \"replication, double-step, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Second replication of the 66.2% result with double-step recurrence using BASE_SEED=123. Architecture unchanged: LN-gated ConvLSTM(64ch) + 1-head attention, default PG.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n    \
    \  return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM with unshared weights (two-layer)\"\ntags: \"ablation, double-step, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Compare double-step with shared weights vs unshared (two distinct ConvLSTM cells applied sequentially per env step). Same backbone, heads, and PG settings.\"\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Dict, Optional, Tuple\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  class ResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleLayer(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray,\
    \ done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n\n          # State init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              h, c = zeros(), zeros()\n          else:\n              h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              h, c = h * m, c * m\n\n          # Two distinct ConvLSTM cells (unshared weights)\n          y1_cell\
    \ = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), y1 = y1_cell((h, c), x)\n          y2_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h2, c2), y2 = y2_cell((h1, c1), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y2)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, y2.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n   \
    \       value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleLayer(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 71:\n  - Replication submitted: double-step LN-ConvLSTM with BASE_SEED=123.\n  - Ablation submitted: unshared-weights double-step\
    \ (two distinct ConvLSTM cells) vs shared double-step.\n  - After these finish, finalize Archive revision (cooldown cleared) with consolidated table and SOTA script path.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Exploring RNN Improvements**


  I’m considering testing a partial 1.5-step gating method, but it doesn’t seem feasible. There are options for RNN gating improvements. We could explore layer normalization (LN) on cell updates versus separate LN per gate. We previously used LN on gate preactivations. Additionally, it might be interesting to test forget-bias on LN gates. For attention temperature, our past results with 1-head showed performance around 61.9 at standardization. I think further testing around these parameters could lead to new insights.**Testing RNN Configurations**


  It seems unnecessary at times, but I could explore the approach of testing "shared weights vs. stacked distinct steps," essentially comparing two-step methods with unshared weights using two ConvLSTM cells, which would create two layers. We previously tested this setup, but I''m unsure if we got results for the two-layer ConvLSTM in earlier tests. Also, I think it could be interesting to evaluate double-step configurations using dropout or layer normalization and apply a "bias" to the forget gate. Lastly, testing attention pooling versus no pooling might reveal interesting insights as well.**Evaluating RNN Improvements**


  I''ve noticed that no attention mechanism yielded a 52.7 score, which doesn’t seem useful. I might look into testing residual gating with a skip connection from a previous step, but it could be too complex. Another approach would be to evaluate across an additional seed set, specifically using BASE_SEED=123, to strengthen stability claims. Replicating this would be quick. I could also create code for gate stats and attention maps, but including analysis might be better for publication. Lastly, managing storage and updating the results summary will ensure reproducibility.**Planning Replications and Ablation Studies**


  I’m planning to submit a replicate using BASE_SEED=123. Additionally, I might consider an ablation study that uses a double-step with a forget bias. It seems I could apply a constant add to the forget gate preactivation, and I’ll need to implement this in JAX, either by providing a new module or including the code directly in the submission. There’s also the idea of testing double-step with unshared weights by stacking two ConvLSTMCellLN calls. I''ll have to see if this variant improves performance, even if it may increase computational demands.**Planning Experiment Submissions**


  I need to watch my constraints, focusing on "Track 1 architecture design." I can use a limit of two concurrent experiments since there are currently none running. I should submit a replicate with BASE_SEED=123 and an ablation for double-step with unshared weights in two layers. I’ll write the small module for CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleLayer inline, ensuring function signatures are correct. I might also update private memory to record results, and I’ll confirm YAML formatting with quotes. After cooldown, I can consider archiving, but for now, let’s keep our actions focused.'
