tick: 77
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int = 2\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(1,1),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates\
    \ = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Dilated(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Dilated residual CNN (parameterized dilation) + LN-gated ConvLSTM with\n      shared-weights double-step recurrence and single-head attention pooling.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 2\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n\
    \          # Dilated CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              h, c = zeros(), zeros()\n          else:\n              h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              h, c = h * m, c * m\n\n          # Double-step shared ConvLSTM\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n\
    \          (h1, c1), y1 = cell((h, c), x)\n          (h2, c2), y2 = cell((h1, c1), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y2)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, y2.reshape((B, 64, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n      \
    \    return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualDilatedBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Dilated\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM + Dilated CNN (d=4, default PG)\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilation, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Synergy test: combine dilated residual CNN (d=4) with shared-weights double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64ch) and single-head attention. Default PG; BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Dilated\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Dilated(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM + Dilated CNN (d=3, default PG)\"\ntags: \"ablation, dilation, convlstm, layernorm, attention, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Control ablation matching prior d=3 backbones: double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64ch) with dilated residual CNN (d=3). Default PG; BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Dilated\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n\
    \      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([3]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Dilated(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 77:\n  - Results: shared double-step + learned mix gate hits 67.8 (ID 130); unshared + FB + mix gate regresses to 59.2 (ID 129) — added params hurt stability.\n  - Submitted synergy with dilated CNN:\n    • d=4\
    \ (BASE_SEED=42) — direct challenge to current 69.9 SOTA but without feature engineering.\n    • d=3 (BASE_SEED=42) — controlled ablation.\n  - Next: If d=4 double-step ≥70, replicate across seeds and update Archive addendum; else keep 66–69 double-step as robust baseline and pivot to qualitative analyses.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Implementing network parameters**


  I think it’s better to use a new parameterizable network that keeps both setups in the same file but with different parameter values. Ray uses four trials with hyperparameters, so I can set ‘dilation’ to tune.choice. I’ll ensure that we follow the principle of changing one variable at a time while testing across dilation values. I also need to check that ‘kernel_dilation’ is accepted in Flax nn.Conv, which seems to have shifted from ‘dilation’ in earlier code. Time to craft the code!**Logging final actions**


