parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch) + AdamW+clip — micro-sweep\"\ntags: \"optimizer, adamw, gradient clipping, convlstm, layernorm, double-step\"\nabstract: \"Test optimizer parity with dilated-CNN SOTA: apply AdamW + global grad clipping to double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64ch) with a small hyperparameter micro-sweep around entropy and value loss coefficients.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3e-4, 4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01, 0.012]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5, 0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (64ch) + AdamW+clip — BASE_SEED=60608\"\ntags: \"replication, optimizer, adamw, gradient clipping, convlstm, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Replication with AdamW + global grad clipping using BASE_SEED=60608 (to match strong dilated-CNN runs). Architecture unchanged: double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64ch), single-head attention, default PG.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step\
    \ import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 60608\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply\
    \ 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 79:\n  - Reading shows dilated CNN (d=4) SOTA 69.9 (Krono). Our double-step + dilated synergy under fixed 30min budget underperforms (63–65), likely due to slower updates from dilation.\n  - New experiments submitted:\n    • Double-step + AdamW+clip micro-sweep (entropy/value_coef, lr) — optimizer parity with dilated-CNN papers.\n    • Double-step + AdamW+clip replicate with BASE_SEED=60608 to compare directly to dilated runs.\n  - Hypothesis: optimizer/clip parity can lift double-step from 66–69 to ≥70 without domain-specific features; if confirmed, replicate across seeds and update Archive addendum.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Proposing new experiments**\n\nI'm working on some new experiments. First, we might propose a \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM with AdamW + clip,\" replicating base 64 channels. I’m thinking of trying slight entropy of 0.012 if micro-sweep suggests it’s best. We'll also consider a small hyperparameter space including learning rate and value loss coefficient, keeping base seed 42.\n\nAdditionally, another idea is reducing CNN features to speed updates, but we need to remember that this would be deviating from the original plan.**Exploring ablation strategies**\n\nI’m considering some ablation strategies right now. One idea is to lighten the conv_lstm_features to 56 or 48, but double-stepping at 48 only got us 63.3, which might not be worth it.\n\nI also think about using a \"shared double-step with a 1.5 step\" and learned mix gating on step 2, which has shown to improve results. There’s the idea of adding AdamW to the shared gating architecture, aiming for stronger results.\n\
  \nLastly, I wonder about implementing KL regularization between step outputs, but that might add unnecessary complexity to the process.**Implementing new submissions**\n\nI’m thinking of two new submissions here. First, I want to implement a double-step LN-ConvLSTM with AdamW and gradient clipping set to 1.0. We can replicate the base and use the existing architecture module we’ve created. I’ll import the double-step network from 'cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step.py' and customize the optimizer with AdamW plus clipping. \n\nFor the second submission, I’m considering a double-step LN-ConvLSTM with a downsample pre-conv stride of 2, which might not degrade performance significantly. Alternatively, we could test a different configuration, but it seems some options may not yield meaningful improvements.**Planning experiment runs**\n\nI’m planning to keep the micro-sweep for our runs while adhering to the 2-run limit. The first run will focus on using AdamW with clipping for a micro-sweep\
  \ of entropy, value, and learning rate for the double-step.\n\nFor the second run, I'm considering a double-step with a decayed entropy schedule, but that requires customizing the training_step function. Instead, I might keep it simpler by adjusting the optimizer. Also, I’ll test the impact of varying conv_lstm_features while ensuring we don’t compromise on feature quality. Let's implement the AdamW+clip micro-sweep for the first run!**Planning second run submissions**\n\nFor the second run, I’m considering a \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM 64 channels\" with baseseed=60608 to mirror the Krono base seed for fairness. I think replicating this might yield valuable insights, although we've previously tested across seeds. \n\nA better approach could involve limiting updates by reducing the conv LSTM width to 56 while striving to maintain performance. To push beyond 69.9, adopting AdamW with clipping might help. \n\nI’ll create two submissions: the first will utilize AdamW+clip micro-sweep with base\
  \ seed 42, while the second will replicate with base seed 60608 for comparison. I'll make sure to code the optimizer appropriately, including the required imports!"
