- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class ResidualDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(1,1),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n   \
    \       h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class CNNConvLSTM_LN_SingleStep_Dilated(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Dilated residual CNN backbone (configurable dilation) + LN-gated ConvLSTM (single-step)\n      + single-head spatial attention pooling, policy/value heads.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 4\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n       \
    \   B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          # Dilated CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = ResidualDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              h, c = zeros(), zeros()\n          else:\n              h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              h, c = h * m, c * m\n\n          # Single-step LN-gated ConvLSTM\n      \
    \    (h_new, c_new), y = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Single-head spatial attention pooling\n          logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits.reshape((B, -1)) / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bi,bic->bc', attn, y.reshape((B, H*W, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n   \
    \       return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"ResidualDilatedBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"CNNConvLSTM_LN_SingleStep_Dilated\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Single-step LN-ConvLSTM + Dilated CNN (d=4) + AdamW+clip — BASE_SEED=60608\"\ntags: \"replication, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm, adamw+clip\"\nabstract: \"Replicate strong dilated-CNN results with our LN-gated ConvLSTM single-step agent: d=4 backbone, AdamW+clip optimizer. Matches compute budget and settings; BASE_SEED=60608 for direct comparability.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated import CNNConvLSTM_LN_SingleStep_Dilated\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 60608\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        \
    \  'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_SingleStep_Dilated(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Single-step LN-ConvLSTM + Dilated CNN (d ∈ {3,4}) + AdamW+clip — micro-sweep\"\ntags: \"ablation, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm, adamw+clip\"\nabstract: \"Micro-sweep over dilation {3,4} and small hparam grid (lr∈{3e-4,4e-4},\
    \ entropy∈{0.01,0.012}, vcoef∈{0.5,0.55}) for single-step LN-ConvLSTM with dilated CNN and AdamW+clip.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated import CNNConvLSTM_LN_SingleStep_Dilated\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3e-4, 4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01, 0.012]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5, 0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([3, 4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_SingleStep_Dilated(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n\
    \          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 81:\n  - AdamW+clip on double-step: 66.5 (ID 140) at best; replicate with BASE_SEED=60608 underperformed (60.2, ID 141). Optimizer parity alone doesn't beat dilated-CNN SOTA.\n  - New submissions:\n    • Single-step LN-ConvLSTM + dilated CNN (d=4) + AdamW+clip, BASE_SEED=60608 (direct comparability).\n    • Micro-sweep: single-step + dilation {3,4} with small lr/entropy/value grids under AdamW+clip.\n  - Rationale: double-step may hurt update throughput under 30-min cap; switching to single-step with larger receptive field aligns with recent SOTA trend while staying task-agnostic.\n  - If ≥70 achieved,\
    \ replicate across seed sets and add to Archive as an addendum; else consolidate guidance on when to prefer temporal compute (double-step) vs spatial receptive field (dilations).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering synergy testing options**\n\nI'm thinking about whether to escalate and test synergy further. One option is to combine a double-step recurrence with a dilated CNN at dilation=4. We've previously tried dilated CNNs with d=3 and d=4, but our results were underwhelming. \n\nKrono's synergy experiment with d=3 and double-step outperformed ours but was still below the top results. There's a significant gap with the latest state-of-the-art, so I’m wondering if we should focus on algorithm improvements or architectural changes.**Exploring dilated CNN and ConvLSTM**\n\nGiven the strong performance of dilated CNNs, I'm considering whether to combine a single-step LN-gated ConvLSTM with dilations of d=4 or d=3 and apply AdamW with clipping. However, I can't share code, so we’ll implement our architecture using our existing functions. \n\nOur earlier tests with double-step didn’t perform well, so I wonder if single-step might provide a better compute ratio. I'll also\
  \ conduct a micro-sweep on dilution rates and evaluate performance. Additionally, I think about adding layer normalization gating on ConvLSTM and testing coordinate channels again.**Proposing temporal gating schedule**\n\nI'm considering a \"Temporal gating schedule,\" using double-step only after some initial warm-up. We’ve previously explored training curriculums to manage compute and time, so I wonder if testing \"1-step for the first X updates, then switching to 2-step\" might help reduce early costs, especially within a 30-minute budget.\n\nAlso, we’ve seen that shared gating produced better results, so I want to stick with that. My action plan includes submitting our new designs and updating the archive addendum with fresh results while keeping an eye on our token budget.**Examining training steps and implementation**\n\nI see that the network call receives only x, done, and rnn_state, without a global step. I’m realizing there's no option to customize the default training_step,\
  \ but I can override it since I've done so before with PPO. \n\nHowever, implementing this can be risky. To align with our time budgets, I could focus on the \"single-step LN-ConvLSTM with d=4 and AdamW+clip\" approach, while also considering a micro-sweep of hyperparameters. I’ll check if we can adapt our existing code for dilated double-step to single-step easily.**Outlining network implementation steps**\n\nI'm planning to create a network file called 'cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated.py', including d as a hyperparameter and an LN-gated LSTM. I’ll submit two runs: \n\nThe first run will be 'Single-step LN-ConvLSTM with dilated CNN (d=4) and AdamW+clip,' comparing it to BASE_SEED 60608. The second run will involve a micro-sweep of entropy, value, and learning rate combinations. \n\nI need to ensure proper quoting for tags lengths in the YAML, implement the optimizer, and prepare action submissions. Let’s get started!"
