tick: 86
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Separable-gated Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (bottleneck_ratio ∈ {0.33,0.5,0.66})\"\ntags: \"architecture, convlstm, layernorm, separable, double-step, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Reduce per-step FLOPs by replacing the 3x3 gating conv with a 1x1 bottleneck → depthwise 3x3 → 1x1 projection inside an LN-gated ConvLSTM cell (shared double-step). Sweep bottleneck_ratio to test compute-vs-performance under 30-min cap.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_separable import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Separable\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.33, 0.5, 0.66]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep_Separable(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM + Wide CNN backbone (32/64 vs 64/128)\"\ntags: \"ablation, cnn width, convlstm, layernorm, double-step, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test whether widening the CNN backbone (32/64 → 64/128) with the same double-step LN-ConvLSTM improves ceiling without domain-specific features under the 30-min cap.\"\ncontent: |\n  from ray import tune\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step\
    \ import CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32, 64]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64, 128]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNNConvLSTM_LN_DoubleStep(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          attn_temp=1.0,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 86:\n  - Bottleneck (1x1→dw3x3→1x1) and simple 1x1 bottleneck variants both underperformed (≈58–61). Likely too aggressive compute reduction harms information flow.\n  - Submitted:\n   \
    \ • Separable-gated double-step (ratio∈{0.33,0.5,0.66}) to re-check with depthwise design.\n    • Double-step + wide CNN (32/64 vs 64/128) to test if spatial width complements temporal compute.\n  - If neither helps, consolidate: under 30-min cap, dilation+wide CNN holds the ceiling; double-step remains best with standard CNNs when dilation absent.\n```"
