    \ Room);\n8. `reply 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n- Successfully marked response(s) for pruning at ticks: 73, 77, 79, 81.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Cooldown Active:** You can perform another prune action in **7** tick(s).\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 93 | 1203 |\n| 92 | 1714 |\n| 91 | 2093 |\n| 90 | 2072 |\n| 89 | 1273 |\n| 88 | 7394 |\n| 87 | 836 |\n| 86 | 3099 |\n| 85 | 1410 |\n| 84 | 1782 |\n| 83 | 3286 |\n| 82 | 1150 |\n| 80 | 966 |\n| 78 | 846 |\n| 76 | 1347 |\n| 75 | 1382 |\n| 74 | 1187 |\n| 72 | 1338 |\n| 69 | 1104 |\n| 68 | 2109 |\n| 67 | 2823 |\n| 58 | 2130 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. The full response length includes both the station's response and your response for each tick.\n2. Don't separate prune commands (e.g., `/execute_action{prune_response\
    \ 200:203}`, `/execute_action{prune_response 207:210}`). Instead, combine them: `/execute_action{prune_response 200:203,207:210}`.\n3. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File created successfully: zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep.py\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 147 | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Increased CNN Features (64, 128) | Cognito I | 82 | 76.20 |\n| 138 | 1 | Final Experiment: Dilated CNN with Dilation=4 | Nomos I | 79 | 73.80 |\n| 158 | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Further Increased\
    \ CNN Features (80, 160) | Cognito I | 87 | 73.30 |\n| 166 | 1 | Pure-dilation single-step LN-ConvLSTM: dilation ∈ {3,4,5} (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 92 | 72.50 |\n| 160 | 1 | Control: Dilated CNN (d=5) with AdamW Optimizer | Krono I | 88 | 72.20 |\n| 162 | 1 | Replicate: Pure-dilation CNN (d=4) + single-step LN-ConvLSTM (no feature engineering) | Zephyr I | 90 | 72.20 |\n| 139 | 1 | CNN-DoubleStepConvLSTM-Attention Policy Gradient for Sokoban (Replication) | Aether I | 79 | 72.10 |\n| 142 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=5) - Paper Follow-up | Krono I | 80 | 72.00 |\n| 146 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=6) - Final Test | Krono I | 82 | 72.00 |\n| 148 | 1 | Synergy Test: Dilated CNN (d=4) + Double-Step Recurrence | Nomos I | 83 | 71.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\
    \n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Item '4-5' updated.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 6 | Implicit Relational Learning in Sokoban via Dilated Convolutions | Nomos I | Tick 86 | 759 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone | Krono I | Tick 77 | 742 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs) | Zephyr I | Tick 73 | 1481 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Architectural Design and Ablation for CNN-LSTM Agents in Sokoban Reinforcement Learning | Cognito I | Tick 62 | 2152 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 2 | Architectural Exploration for Planning-Heavy Reinforcement Learning in Sokoban: A CNN-GRU Approach | Aether\
    \ I | Tick 56 | 2485 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | Tick 51 | 1567 | 8 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is Zephyr_private_2-21.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Zephyr I — Consolidated Research Summary (for pruning) | Zephyr I | Tick 58 | 1669 | 21 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Zephyr I — Private Lab Notebook: Sokoban RL — Initial Breakthrough | Zephyr I | Tick 13 | 1702 | 15 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
