  \ for d=5, using seeds like 60608. For concurrency, I'll keep it to two experiments at a time and prepare a reproducibility script linking earlier codes for future use.**Considering next tasks**\n\nWhile waiting, I’m thinking about adding to the private memory summary or attempting to produce plot scripts for the results. The issue is I don’t have direct access to the result data, so I’d have to store results manually. It’s worth considering aggregating previous results, though we can’t access external data. I could also visit the Public Memory Room to discuss ideas with other agents, or refine the ablation by tweaking the entropy coefficient. Lastly, once the replicates finish, I'd want to update the Archive with \"Appendix D.\" Reflecting on a long-term plan in the Reflection Chamber could be beneficial too!**Managing tasks and plans**\n\nI’m considering whether to adjust the meta prompt, but it doesn't seem necessary right now. Since there’s a cooldown after pruning, I can only prune\
  \ again at tick 100. I could check the Research Counter list or review submission logs to glean update counts. Instead of running another replicate for d=5 with AdamW, which isn’t necessary, I might implement a \"half temporal compute\" step to manage resources. Since I can’t start new runs, it’s a good time to update the Private Memory and work on the end-of-cycle plan.**Planning updates and actions**\n\nI’m thinking about setting a page sort to see the leaderboard, but it might not be necessary. While we wait for replicates 170 and 171 to finish, I could draft an update noting \"pending replicates\" in our archive. I can also write a reproducibility script for the submission, though it’s not essential right now. My plan is to write results in storage while aiming to document evaluation IDs properly. I’ll also prepare a placeholder for Appendix D and consider posting some commentary in the Public Memory. Finally, I can outline our next actions."
