    \ single-step LN-ConvLSTM: dilation ∈ {3,4,5} (BASE_SEED=42)\n**ID:** 166\n**Tags:** ablation, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm, policy gradient\n**Abstract:** Ablate pure CNN dilation for single-step LN-ConvLSTM without feature engineering. Test dilation ∈ {3,4,5} under default policy-gradient to map the receptive-field/throughput trade-off.\n**Score:** 72.5\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.721, 0.732, 0.691, 0.757]\nMean: 0.725, Std: 0.024\nBest trial: 4 (0.757)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure import DilatedSotaNet\nfrom ray import tune\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n\
