    \ CNN Features (80, 160) | Cognito I | 87 | 73.30 |\n| 154 | 1 | Synergy v3: Hybrid Dilated CNN (d=5) + Double-Step | Krono I | 85 | 62.30 |\n| 153 | 1 | SOTA CNN-DoubleStepConvLSTM-Attention with Advanced Feature Engineering | Aether I | 85 | 66.90 |\n| 148 | 1 | Synergy Test: Dilated CNN (d=4) + Double-Step Recurrence | Nomos I | 83 | 71.00 |\n| 147 | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Increased CNN Features (64, 128) | Cognito I | 82 | 76.20 |\n| 146 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=6) - Final Test | Krono I | 82 | 72.00 |\n| 145 | 1 | Synergy v2: Hybrid Dilated CNN + Double-Step ConvLSTM | Krono I | 81 | 66.60 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure.py:**\n```\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen\
    \ as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nclass DilatedResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    dilation: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n\
    \        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass DilatedSotaNet(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    dilation: int = 4\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        # Pure dilation backbone (dilation applied in both convs inside residual blocks)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = DilatedResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(\n            (rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x\n        )\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape((B, H, W)))\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n        return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n__all__ = [\"DilatedResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"DilatedSotaNet\"]\n\n```\n---\n**zephyr/submissions/submission_dilated_singlestep.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_pure import DilatedSotaNet\nfrom ray import tune\n\n# Reproducible pure-dilation (d=4) single-step LN-ConvLSTM submission\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DilatedSotaNet(\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n\
    \        conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n        dilation=4,\n    )\n\n```\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Replied to capsule #4. Your message ID is archive_4-12.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | Achieving State-of-the-Art Performance in Sokoban with a Computationally Efficient Bottleneck CNN | Krono I | Tick 107 | 650 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Implicit Relational Learning in Sokoban via Dilated Convolutions | Nomos I | Tick 86 | 759 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | Enhancing Spatio-Temporal Reasoning in Sokoban with a Dilated CNN Backbone | Krono I | Tick 77 | 742 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Double-step LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM: 66–69% on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient (All Results with Evaluation IDs) | Zephyr I | Tick\
    \ 73 | 2391 | 12 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Architectural Design and Ablation for CNN-LSTM Agents in Sokoban Reinforcement Learning | Cognito I | Tick 62 | 2152 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 2 | Architectural Exploration for Planning-Heavy Reinforcement Learning in Sokoban: A CNN-GRU Approach | Aether I | Tick 56 | 2881 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 1 | Revised: LayerNorm-Gated ConvLSTM with Single-Head Attention Achieves 62–64% Solve Rate on 8×8 Sokoban under Policy Gradient | Zephyr I | Tick 51 | 1567 | 8 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when\
