parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the improved non-FE baseline: d=5 bottleneck-dilated CNN + single-step LN-ConvLSTM with bottleneck_ratio=0.5 and ReLU. Fixed hparams to verify stability under BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=32,\n          cnn_features_2=64,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.5,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123\"\ntags: \"replication, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Second replication of the improved non-FE baseline: d=5 bottleneck-dilated CNN + single-step LN-ConvLSTM with bottleneck_ratio=0.5 and ReLU. Fixed hparams to verify stability under BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return\
    \ {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=32,\n          cnn_features_2=64,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.5,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 4}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Addendum — Bottleneck-dilated CNN (non-FE) improves d=5 track\n\n  New results (non-FE, single-step LN-ConvLSTM, default PG):\n  - ID 190 (stored-module d=5 sanity): 72.9\n  - ID 191 (bottleneck-dilated residuals, ratio sweep): 73.6 (best ratio=0.5)\n\
    \  - ID 192 (activation ablation on bottleneck-dilated): 73.3 (ReLU > SiLU)\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - Replacing pure dilated residuals with 1×1→3×3(d=5)→1×1 bottleneck-dilated residuals yields a consistent ~+0.7–1.0 improvement over the non-FE d=5 baseline.\n  - ReLU remains slightly better than SiLU in this regime.\n\n  Replications (pending):\n  - Submitted fixed-hparam replications of best config (ratio=0.5, ReLU) at BASE_SEED=7 and 123 to confirm stability beyond ID 191 (BASE_SEED=42).\n  - If both confirm ≥73, we will freeze the non‑FE recipe and update the consolidated table with all IDs.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 111:\n  - Strong non-FE improvement: bottleneck-dilated residuals (ID 191) 73.6; activation ablation (ID 192) 73.3 with ReLU best.\n  - Sanity (ID 190) reconfirmed stored-module d=5 at 72.9.\n  - Submitted replications for bottleneck ratio=0.5, ReLU at BASE_SEED=7 and 123 to validate stability.\
    \ Next: run fine sweep (submission_d5_bottleneck_fine.py) if a slot frees, then finalize archive update with full results + IDs.\n```"
