parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck_depth.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n\n  class BottleneckResidualBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      dilation: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.5\n      use_silu: bool = False\n\n      def _act(self, x):\n          return nn.silu(x) if self.use_silu else nn.relu(x)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(8, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1, 1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = self._act(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = self._act(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1, 1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return self._act(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class DilatedBottleneckDepthNet(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio:\
    \ float = 0.5\n      use_silu: bool = False\n      num_blocks1: int = 1\n      num_blocks2: int = 1\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          # Stage 1\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks1):\n              x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_1, dilation=self.dilation,\n                                          bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                          use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n          # Stage 2\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          x = nn.relu(x)\n          for _ in range(self.num_blocks2):\n              x = BottleneckResidualBlock(self.cnn_features_2, dilation=self.dilation,\n\
    \                                          bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                          use_silu=self.use_silu)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)(\n              (rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x\n          )\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1, 1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape((B, -1)), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn.reshape((B, H, W)))\n\
    \n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckResidualBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"DilatedBottleneckDepthNet\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Depth ablation: stack bottleneck residuals per stage (1 vs 2), d=5 (single-step LN-ConvLSTM)\"\ntags: \"ablation, depth, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Test scaling via depth: compare 1 vs 2 bottleneck-dilated residual blocks per CNN stage on the non-FE d=5 single-step LN-ConvLSTM baseline under default PG. Fixed compute-friendly settings; BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck_depth\
    \ import DilatedBottleneckDepthNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n          'num_blocks': tune.choice([1, 2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      nb = int(hparams['num_blocks'])\n      return DilatedBottleneckDepthNet(\n          cnn_features_1=32,\n          cnn_features_2=64,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.5,\n          use_silu=False,\n          num_blocks1=nb,\n          num_blocks2=nb,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Width ablation\
    \ on bottleneck-dilated d=5: 32/64 vs 48/96 (single-step LN-ConvLSTM)\"\ntags: \"ablation, width, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Evaluate modest width scaling with compute-efficient bottleneck-dilated residuals: compare CNN widths 32/64 vs 48/96 on the non-FE d=5 single-step LN-ConvLSTM baseline under default PG; BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32, 48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64, 96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n\
    \      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.5,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Author Update (Tick 114) — Scaling plan per reviewer suggestion\n\n  Following acceptance, we began systematic scaling tests while preserving the 30‑min/seed cap:\n  - Depth scaling (ID pending): stack 2 bottleneck‑dilated residuals per stage vs 1 (constant widths 32/64).\n  - Width scaling (ID pending): modest CNN widening to 48/96 with bottleneck‑dilated residuals (baseline 32/64).\n  Rationale: the bottleneck improves compute‑efficiency; these tests probe whether extra spatial capacity maintains ≥34–35k updates/seed and converts to higher solve rate. Results and evaluation IDs\
    \ will be added upon completion.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 114:\n  - Accepted archive (10/10) — added scaling plan reply to capsule #8.\n  - Launched depth ablation (1 vs 2 bottleneck blocks per stage) and width ablation (32/64 vs 48/96) for the non‑FE d=5 + LN‑ConvLSTM baseline. Fixed ratio=0.5, ReLU.\n  - Success criteria: ≥75 with stable updates/seed (no throughput collapse). If positive, replicate across seeds; if negative, freeze 0.5 bottleneck (32/64) as the recommended non‑FE baseline and move to minimal recurrent/readout tweaks.\n```"
