- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (ratio=0.60, SiLU) — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Replication of fine-sweep best config: d=5 bottleneck-dilated CNN + single-step LN-ConvLSTM with bottleneck_ratio=0.60 and SiLU activation. Fixed hparams to verify stability under BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.60]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([True]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=32,\n          cnn_features_2=64,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.60,\n          use_silu=True,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/summary_bottleneck.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Non-FE Dilated CNN + Single-step LN-ConvLSTM (d=5) — Results Summary (updated Tick 116)\n\n  Baseline (stored module):\n  - ID 166: 72.5 (BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 170: 73.4 (BASE_SEED=7)\n  - ID 171: 72.8 (BASE_SEED=123)\n  - ID 174: 73.0 (micro-sweep, BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 190: 72.9 (sanity replicate, BASE_SEED=42)\n\n  Bottleneck-dilated residuals (1x1 → 3x3(d=5) → 1x1), single-step LN-ConvLSTM(64):\n  - ID 191: 73.6 (best ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 192: 73.3 (activation ablation; ReLU > SiLU at ratio=0.66; BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 194: 74.5 (replicate\
    \ ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=7)\n  - ID 195: 74.8 (replicate ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=123)\n  - ID 198: 74.6 (fine sweep; best ratio=0.60 + SiLU; BASE_SEED=42)\n\n  Scaling/ablations:\n  - ID 201: 67.0 (depth: 2 bottleneck blocks/stage vs 1; throughput loss; mixed seeds)\n  - ID 203: running (width: 32/64 vs 48/96; ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=42)\n\n  Negative/neutral:\n  - ID 189: 69.1 (pre-LSTM 1×1 bottleneck; best 0.75; hurts credit assignment)\n  - ID 182: 62.5 (LR/entropy/vcoef micro-sweep on d=5; regresses)\n  - ID 186: 62.5 (inline attn-temp sweep; slower updates/seed)\n\n  Pending:\n  - Replicate 0.60 + SiLU at BASE_SEED=7 (submitted) and at 123 (next slot) to confirm stability.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 116):\n  - Fine sweep (ID 198) identified a slightly stronger config: bottleneck_ratio=0.60 with SiLU achieves 74.6 (BASE_SEED=42), comparable to 0.5/ReLU reps (IDs 194=74.5, 195=74.8).\n  - Depth scaling\
    \ to 2 bottleneck blocks/stage under the 30‑min cap reduced throughput and hurt performance (ID 201: 67.0), so we recommend 1 block/stage.\n  - Width ablation (32/64 vs 48/96) is running (ID 203). We also submitted a replication of the 0.60+SiLU config at BASE_SEED=7; 123 will follow when a slot frees. We will report IDs and finalize recommended defaults accordingly.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 116:\n  - Depth ablation (ID 201) dropped to 67.0; seed with ~31.5k updates underperformed, confirming depth hurts throughput/returns under 30-min cap. Keep 1 block/stage.\n  - Fine sweep best (ID 198): 0.60 + SiLU at 74.6; submitted replication at BASE_SEED=7. Next: replicate at 123.\n  - Width ablation (ID 203) running (32/64 vs 48/96). Success criteria unchanged: ≥34–35k updates/seed and ≥75 mean without FE.\n  - If 0.60+SiLU replicates ≥75 on both seeds, adopt as default; else retain 0.5/ReLU as recommended non-FE baseline.\n\
    ```"
