- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, width, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm, layernorm\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the improved non-FE configuration: bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5) with widths 48/96, single-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), bottleneck_ratio=0.5, ReLU. Fixed settings to verify stability under BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=48,\n          cnn_features_2=96,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.5,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/summary_bottleneck.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Non-FE Dilated CNN + Single-step LN-ConvLSTM (d=5) — Results Summary (updated Tick 117)\n\n  Baseline (stored module):\n  - ID 166: 72.5 (BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 170: 73.4 (BASE_SEED=7)\n  - ID 171: 72.8 (BASE_SEED=123)\n  - ID 174: 73.0 (micro-sweep, BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 190: 72.9 (sanity replicate, BASE_SEED=42)\n\n  Bottleneck-dilated residuals (1x1 → 3x3(d=5) → 1x1), single-step LN-ConvLSTM(64):\n  - ID 191: 73.6 (ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 192: 73.3 (activation ablation; ReLU > SiLU at ratio=0.66; BASE_SEED=42)\n\
    \  - ID 194: 74.5 (ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=7)\n  - ID 195: 74.8 (ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=123)\n  - ID 198: 74.6 (fine sweep; best ratio=0.60 + SiLU; BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 203: 76.0 (width 48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU; BASE_SEED=42)\n\n  Scaling/ablations:\n  - ID 201: 67.0 (depth: 2 bottleneck blocks/stage vs 1; throughput loss; mixed seeds)\n  - ID 203: 76.0 (width scaling 32/64 → 48/96 maintained throughput; improved mean)\n\n  Negative/neutral:\n  - ID 189: 69.1 (pre-LSTM 1×1 bottleneck; best 0.75; hurts credit assignment)\n  - ID 182: 62.5 (LR/entropy/vcoef micro-sweep on d=5; regresses)\n  - ID 186: 62.5 (inline attn-temp sweep; slower updates/seed)\n\n  Pending:\n  - ID 206: replicate ratio=0.60 + SiLU at BASE_SEED=7 — running\n  - (new) replicate width 48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU at BASE_SEED=7 — submitted now\n  - Next slot: replicate both promising configs at BASE_SEED=123 if not already covered\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n\
    \  Update (Tick 117):\n  - Width scaling result: ID 203 (48/96 widths, ratio=0.5, ReLU) reaches 76.0 (BASE_SEED=42), surpassing our previous non‑FE bests. Throughput held at full update count.\n  - Replications in progress:\n    • ID 206: ratio=0.60 + SiLU (BASE_SEED=7)\n    • Submitted: 48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU replication (BASE_SEED=7)\n  - Plan: run BASE_SEED=123 replications for both configs when a slot frees. If both stabilize ≥75, we will recommend 48/96 + bottleneck(0.5, ReLU) as default non‑FE, with 0.60 + SiLU as a close variant.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 117:\n  - New non‑FE high: 48/96 widths with bottleneck(0.5, ReLU) hit 76.0 (ID 203).\n  - Submitted replication of 48/96@0.5 ReLU at BASE_SEED=7; also running 0.60+SiLU replicate (ID 206).\n  - Next: replicate both at seed 123; compare mean±std across 42/7/123. If consistent ≥75, finalize recommended non‑FE default and close this thread with an updated\
    \ summary + pointers to stored modules and scripts.\n```"
