- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123\"\ntags: \"replication, width, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Second replication of the improved non-FE configuration: bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=5) with widths 48/96, single-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), bottleneck_ratio=0.5, ReLU. Fixed settings to verify stability under BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=48,\n          cnn_features_2=96,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.5,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 118):\n  - Width scaling (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU) achieved 76.0 at BASE_SEED=42 (ID 203).\n  - Replications: 48/96@0.5 ReLU is running at BASE_SEED=7 (ID 208) and now launched at BASE_SEED=123; 0.60+SiLU replicated at BASE_SEED=7 with 73.4 (ID 206).\n  - Plan: finalize recommended non‑FE default after width config stabilizes across {42,7,123}; if ≥75 consistently, we will recommend 48/96 + bottleneck(0.5, ReLU) with stored-module paths.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 118:\n  - Launched 48/96@0.5 ReLU replication at BASE_SEED=123. With ID 203=76.0 (seed 42) and ID 208 running (seed 7), we’ll have the full {42,7,123} set soon.\n  - 0.60+SiLU (ID 206) replicated at 73.4 on seed 7, below 0.5/ReLU reps; leaning toward 0.5/ReLU as default.\n  - Next: if 48/96@0.5 ReLU ≥75 on seeds 7 and 123, freeze as recommended non‑FE default; otherwise report both configs with full IDs and adopt the more stable one.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning research steps**\n\nI'm working on a plan here. First, I’ll research and submit a new replication for the 48/96 ratio of 0.5 using the stored network 'DilatedBottleneckSotaNet' at BASE_SEED=123. I'll update the summary file to reflect this plan too. \n\nEven though we posted updates recently, I could add a small reply to Archive capsule #8 about planned replicates. It seems our focus should be on continuing proactive experiments rather than just commenting on status updates. So, I’ll submit that replicate for 48/96. No need to prepare a script path for reproducibility just yet.**Crafting submission actions**\n\nI’m planning to submit the replication now and maybe set the rank by author for viewing, but that feels unnecessary. I’ll execute the research action first, then submit with the YAML to instantiate the network, including parameters like 'cnn_features_1 48' and 'cnn_features_2 96', along with a ratio of 0.5 and BASE_SEED 123.\n\nAfter submission, I might\
  \ update the archive with a note about the 48/96 replication running and the width improvements. Plus, I need to ensure I update the private memory setup. Oh, and remember to keep the tags at six!"
