- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"48/96 bottleneck ratio ablation at d=5: 0.5 vs 0.6 (ReLU, single-step LN-ConvLSTM)\"\ntags: \"ablation, bottleneck, width, dilation, cnn, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"At the improved non-FE setting (CNN 48/96, d=5), we ablate bottleneck_ratio ∈ {0.5, 0.6} with ReLU while keeping the ConvLSTM(64) unchanged. BASE_SEED=42 to isolate the ratio effect.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.5, 0.6]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=48,\n          cnn_features_2=96,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/summary_bottleneck.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Non-FE Dilated CNN + Single-step LN-ConvLSTM (d=5) — Results Summary (updated Tick 119)\n\n  Baseline (stored module):\n  - ID 166: 72.5 (BASE_SEED=42)\n  - ID 170: 73.4 (BASE_SEED=7)\n  - ID 171: 72.8 (BASE_SEED=123)\n  - ID 174: 73.0 (micro-sweep, 42)\n  - ID 190: 72.9 (sanity, 42)\n\n  Bottleneck-dilated residuals (1x1 → 3x3(d=5) → 1x1), single-step LN-ConvLSTM(64):\n  - ID 191: 73.6 (ratio=0.5, ReLU; 32/64; 42)\n  - ID 192: 73.3 (activation ablation; ratio=0.66; 32/64; ReLU > SiLU; 42)\n  - ID 194: 74.5 (ratio=0.5,\
    \ ReLU; 32/64; 7)\n  - ID 195: 74.8 (ratio=0.5, ReLU; 32/64; 123)\n  - ID 198: 74.6 (fine sweep; best ratio=0.60 + SiLU; 32/64; 42)\n\n  Width scaling (48/96), ratio=0.5, ReLU:\n  - ID 203: 76.0 (42)\n  - ID 208: 74.5 (7)\n  - ID 210: running (123)\n\n  Other notes:\n  - ID 201: 67.0 (depth: 2 bottleneck blocks/stage hurts under 30-min cap)\n  - ID 206: 73.4 (ratio=0.60 + SiLU replicate; 32/64; 7)\n\n  Pending/new:\n  - Submitted 48/96 ratio ablation (0.5 vs 0.6, ReLU) at 42 to test if 0.6 helps at wider CNN.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 119):\n  - New replication result for width scaling: ID 208 (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU, BASE_SEED=7) = 74.5. Together with ID 203 (76.0 at seed 42), this suggests strong performance with modest seed variability; seed 123 replicate is running (ID 210).\n  - Submitted targeted ablation at the 48/96 setting: bottleneck_ratio ∈ {0.5, 0.6} with ReLU (BASE_SEED=42) to check whether 0.6 improves\
    \ the wider model.\n  - Summary file updated at storage/zephyr/results/summary_bottleneck.txt.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 119:\n  - Replicate 48/96@0.5 ReLU on seed 7 = 74.5 (ID 208); seed 123 running (ID 210).\n  - Submitted 48/96 ratio ablation (0.5 vs 0.6, ReLU) at seed 42 to probe if 0.6 helps at the wider setting.\n  - Current recommendation trajectory (pending seed 123): adopt 48/96 + bottleneck(0.5, ReLU) as non‑FE default if {42,7,123} average ≥75; otherwise report both 0.5/ReLU and 0.60/SiLU variants with IDs and stability notes.\n```"
