parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: 48/96 d=5 bottleneck ratio=0.6 (ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, width, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the improved non-FE config at wider CNN: 48/96, dilation=5, bottleneck_ratio=0.6, ReLU, ConvLSTM(64), single-step LN, default PG. Fixed hparams under BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.6]),\n\
    \          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=48,\n          cnn_features_2=96,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.6,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate: 48/96 d=5 bottleneck ratio=0.6 (ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123\"\ntags: \"replication, width, bottleneck, dilation, cnn, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Second replication of the wider non-FE config: 48/96, dilation=5, bottleneck_ratio=0.6, ReLU, ConvLSTM(64), single-step LN, default PG. Fixed hparams under BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_single_step_dilated_bottleneck import DilatedBottleneckSotaNet\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n\
    \          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.6]),\n          'use_silu': tune.choice([False]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DilatedBottleneckSotaNet(\n          cnn_features_1=48,\n          cnn_features_2=96,\n          conv_lstm_features=64,\n          dilation=5,\n          bottleneck_ratio=0.6,\n          use_silu=False,\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 8}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 121):\n  - Ratio ablation at 48/96 (ReLU) indicates 0.6 > 0.5 at seed 42: ID 211 = 76.3 (vs. ID 203 = 76.0 at 0.5).\n  - Replications launched for 48/96 @ 0.6 (ReLU) at seeds 7 and 123 to test stability. If {42,7,123} mean ≥ the 0.5 config (current mean ≈75.6), we will update the recommended\
    \ default accordingly.\n  - Token budget nearing 75% threshold; proceeding to prune dialogue context while preserving results summaries and archive records.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{help token_management}"
thinking_content: '**Managing experiment submissions**


  I think it''s time to submit a new experiment if necessary, but it seems the evaluations are finished. The queue should be free now. I’ll submit replicates on seeds 7 and 123 with a ratio of 0.6 at 48/96. We need to keep the two concurrent submission limit in mind, but we can proceed with both right now. After that, I’ll update the summarization file and manage the token budget appropriately, making sure to prune effectively.**Planning token management**


  I’m looking at the token management room, which will show tick lengths for pruning. Here’s my plan: I’ll submit replicates for 48/96 with a ratio of 0.6, using ReLU at BASE_SEED 7 and 123. Then, I’ll update the summary file accordingly. I''ll archive the response about seed 42, which yielded 76.3. After that, I’ll check the dialogue history to choose tick ranges to prune based on the heavy ticks, even though it uses some tokens. Then I can select the appropriate ranges!**Strategizing token management**


  I realize that we can''t anticipate the tick numbers until we access the "Dialogue History." It’s okay to proceed by issuing multiple actions in one turn, but we need that list to choose accurately. While we can prune a larger range, like 80:120, the system may expect valid tick numbers. It might prune existing ones and ignore the rest. To be safe, I think I’ll go ahead and wait for the list before making any pruning decisions. So, I''ll issue the goto token_management first!**Implementing submissions and research actions**


  I can proceed with research actions in the same turn since the interface allows for executing multiple actions sequentially. Although the pre-warning indicates it’s a good time for pruning, I’ll still head to token_management to get the list. For submissions, I’ll use the code from before to import the network module and fix the hyperparameters. I’ll reuse the ratio of 0.6 and ReLU with BASE_SEED 7 and 123. Then I''ll submit replicates and update the summary file before returning to manage the token details.**Preparing submissions and token management**


  I need to generate commands for the Room Output, including a "preview" of token management. Since we haven’t pruned since tick 102, we should be fine regarding cooldown. I want to craft the code for the submissions, ensuring that the titles conform to YAML rules, especially since they''ll have colons. I’ll quote any single-line text that contains special characters. I’ll also include six tags related to replication and CNN features. After compiling the actions, I’ll update the results summary and check token management to display the list. Let’s finalize everything!'
