parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import jax.lax as lax\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  def xavier():\n    return nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n\n  class BottleneckDilated(nn.Module):\n    out_features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.6\n    dilation: int = 5\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n      in_ch = x.shape[-1]\n      hid = max(1, int(self.out_features * self.ratio))\n      y = nn.Conv(hid, (1, 1), kernel_init=xavier())(x)\n      y = nn.relu(y)\n      # Use kernel_dilation (Flax API) instead of dilation\n      y = nn.Conv(hid, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier(),\n                  kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n      y = nn.relu(y)\n      y = nn.Conv(self.out_features, (1, 1), kernel_init=xavier())(y)\n      if in_ch != self.out_features:\n\
    \        x = nn.Conv(self.out_features, (1, 1), kernel_init=xavier())(x)\n      return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n      h, c = carry\n      gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=xavier())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n      gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN across channels\n      i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n      i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n      c = f * c + i * g\n      h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n      return (h, c), h\n\n  class DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Residual dilated CNN (bottleneck) + double-step LN-ConvLSTM (shared weights).\n    step2 reuses input x and starts from (h1,c1); output is learned mix of h1/h2.\n    \"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n   \
    \ conv_lstm_features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.6\n    dilation: int = 5\n    stop_grad_first: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n      B = x.shape[0]\n      # Backbone\n      x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n      x = BottleneckDilated(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n      x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3, 3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n      x = BottleneckDilated(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n      # Init/reset recurrent state\n      if rnn_state is None:\n        zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n        rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n      if done is not None:\n        m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B, 1, 1, 1).astype(x.dtype))\n        rnn_state\
    \ = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n      cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n      # Step 1\n      (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n      # Optional stop-grad from step1 -> step2\n      h1s = lax.stop_gradient(h1) if self.stop_grad_first else h1\n      c1s = lax.stop_gradient(c1) if self.stop_grad_first else c1\n      # Step 2\n      (h2, c2), _ = cell((h1s, c1s), x)\n      # Learned mix\n      mix_logit = self.param('mix_logit', nn.initializers.zeros, (1,))\n      mix = nn.sigmoid(mix_logit)[0]\n      h_out = mix * h2 + (1.0 - mix) * h1\n      rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n      # Heads\n      z = h_out.reshape((B, -1))\n      z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=xavier())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n      pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=xavier())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n      policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=xavier())(pol_h)\n      val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=xavier())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n      value = nn.Dense(1,\
    \ kernel_init=xavier())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n      return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckDilated\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\", \"DoubleStepLNConvLSTM\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM + stop-grad (shared) + 48/96 d=5 bottleneck (ratio=0.6, ReLU) — retry (BASE_SEED=123)\"\ntags: \"double-step, stop-gradient, convlstm, layernorm, bottleneck, dilation\"\nabstract: \"Fix Flax API (kernel_dilation) and proper stop_gradient; re-run the stop-grad double-step on the improved 48/96 d=5 bottleneck (ratio=0.6) backbone. Default PG; BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck import DoubleStepLNConvLSTM\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.6]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          stop_grad_first=True,\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating evaluation modules**\n\nI want to make sure I write the updated module file correctly, using `import jax.lax as lax` and `lax.stop_gradient` where needed. I'll fix the code and plan to resubmit the failed evaluations, specifically 218, and also consider 217 since it's still running. It's okay to resubmit just the failed variant while ensuring to disable the auto debugger. So, I’ll update the file to include 'kernel_dilation' and adjust references for `lax.stop_gradient`.**Clarifying LayerNorm and Conv in Flax**\n\nI’m looking into the LayerNorm in Flax, where the default axis is -1 for normalizing across channels. For 4D inputs, to apply per-pixel layer normalization, I can use `axis = (-1,)`, but the default should work too. I see that LayerNorm has parameters like `dtype`, `epsilon`, and `axis` which is fine. \n\nI’ll also correct the Conv settings, ensuring to use `kernel_dilation` to accommodate dilation and update the file content accordingly with the right\
  \ Flax API.**Updating DoubleStep network module**\n\nIn the DoubleStep network, we utilize the `BottleneckDilated` module where we can pass the `dilation` parameter and set `kernel_dilation` within the call, which is good. I need to use `jax.lax.stop_gradient(h1)` or just return `h1` directly. \n\nThe validation passed during network creation, but it failed on the forward pass due to a dilation argument being instantiated. So, I’ll write a corrected module and resubmit evaluation 218 with the same 'stop-grad' variant, while maybe submitting a non-stop-grad variant across a different seed too.**Managing runs and updates**\n\nCurrently, we have evaluation 217 running with `BASE_SEED=42`, and I want to keep only one run active at a time. Since there's a concurrency limit of two, I can run 218 again, which will give us the maximum allowed.\n\nI'll also update my private memory notes and maintain minimal formatting to save tokens, as per the directions. I’ll implement a storage write with the\
  \ updated code, including adding `import jax.lax as lax` at the top and changing references to `nn.stop_gradient` in the DoubleStep LN conv class to `lax.stop_gradient`.**Finalizing actions for submission**\n\nI need to update the module code, ensuring I use `kernel_dilation` in `BottleneckDilated` and switch to `lax.stop_gradient`. Everything else will remain unchanged. \n\nNext, I’ll proceed with the following actions:  \n1. Move to research.  \n2. Write the updated storage path for the file.  \n3. Submit the stop-grad variant for evaluation 218.   \n\nThe submission will include the appropriate YAML content with settings like `stop_grad_first=True` and `BASE_SEED=123`. I probably won't set `no_debugger: true`, but I'll keep the message concise. Let’s do this!"
