parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 125\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 76)\nPublished paper accepted (10/10). Pending runs: 129 (unshared+gate+FB), 130 (shared+mix-gate).\nPrepared next test (not yet submitted due to 2-run cap): double-step + dilated CNN (d=3), BASE_SEED=42.\nPlan:\n- When a slot frees, submit d=3 double-step synergy to challenge 69.7 SOTA without domain-specific features.\n- If unshared+gating stabilizes variance, replicate across seeds; else stick with shared double-step baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 91,086 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 125 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation\
    \ completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (shared, learned mix) + 48/96 d=5 bottleneck (ratio=0.6, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=42' (ID: 217) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 56.0\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.542, 0.515, 0.586, 0.595]\nMean: 0.560, Std: 0.033\nBest trial: 4 (0.595)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 48.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 96.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.600000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 217\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the failing research submission. The code now runs without crashing and has been executing for several minutes without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code failed due to an incorrect parameter name in the Flax `nn.Conv` constructor. The code was trying to pass `dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation)`\
    \ as a keyword argument to `nn.Conv`, but the correct parameter name in Flax is `kernel_dilation`.\n\nSpecifically, in the `BottleneckDilated` class at line 18-19 of the original network file:\n```python\ny = nn.Conv(hid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier(),\n            dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)  # ❌ Wrong parameter name\n```\n\nThe error was: `TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Copied the buggy `BottleneckDilated` class** from `storage/zephyr/networks/cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck.py` into `submissions/submission_v2.py`\n\n2. **Fixed the parameter name** from `dilation` to `kernel_dilation`:\n```python\ny = nn.Conv(hid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier(),\n            kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)  # ✅ Correct parameter name\n```\n\n3. **Kept working imports** - Only imported `ConvLSTMCellLN` from the lineage since it was working correctly\n\
    \n4. **Provided complete implementation** - Included the full `DoubleStepLNConvLSTM` class that uses the fixed `BottleneckDilated` class\n\n## Verification\n- **Before fix**: Code crashed immediately with `TypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'`\n- **After fix**: Code has been running successfully for 3+ minutes without any crashes\n- **Monitoring result**: The monitor script confirmed the code is executing without errors (status: \"pending\" indicates ongoing execution, not failure)\n\nThe fix successfully resolved the API compatibility issue between the submission code and Flax's `nn.Conv` interface.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\
    import jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef xavier():\n    return nn.initializers.xavier_uniform()\n\n# Fixed BottleneckDilated class with correct parameter name\nclass BottleneckDilated(nn.Module):\n    out_features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.6\n    dilation: int = 5\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        in_ch = x.shape[-1]\n        hid = max(1, int(self.out_features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(hid, (1,1), kernel_init=xavier())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(hid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier(),\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation))(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.out_features, (1,1), kernel_init=xavier())(y)\n        if in_ch != self.out_features:\n            x = nn.Conv(self.out_features, (1,1), kernel_init=xavier())(x)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\
    \"Residual dilated CNN (bottleneck) + double-step LN-ConvLSTM (shared weights).\n       step2 uses same input x and h1,c1; output is learned mix of h1 and h2.\n    \"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.6\n    dilation: int = 5\n    stop_grad_first: bool = False\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # Backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilated(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=xavier())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilated(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio, dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n        # Init/reset recurrent state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n\
    \            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        # Step 1\n        (h1, c1), y1 = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        # Optional stop-grad on first step signal into step 2 (stability)\n        h1_for_step2 = nn.stop_gradient(h1) if self.stop_grad_first else h1\n        c1_for_step2 = nn.stop_gradient(c1) if self.stop_grad_first else c1\n        # Step 2\n        (h2, c2), y2 = cell((h1_for_step2, c1_for_step2), x)\n        # Learned mix\n        mix_logit = self.param('mix_logit', nn.initializers.zeros, (1,))\n        mix = nn.sigmoid(mix_logit)[0]\n        h_out = mix * h2 + (1.0 - mix) * h1\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        #\
    \ Heads\n        z = h_out.reshape((B, -1))\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=xavier())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=xavier())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=xavier())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=xavier())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=xavier())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([48]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([96]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.6]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        stop_grad_first=False,\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: using default\n\
