    \          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          stop_grad_first=False,\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 134:\n  - Results: 56/112@0.6 = 75.0 (ID 231), 56/112@0.5 = 77.7 (ID 232). Widening hurts throughput; 0.5 ratio recovers but no gain over 48/96 baseline.\n  - Running: 60/120@0.5 (ID 234) and ConvLSTM width {44,48,52} (ID 235).\n  - Prepared Track‑2 script: submission_double_step_algosweep.py (LR ∈ {3e-4,4e-4,5e-4}, entropy ∈ {0.008,0.01,0.012}, vcoef ∈ {0.45,0.5,0.55}) on the recommended\
    \ double‑step+AttnPool backbone.\n  - When a slot frees: submit algosweep; if 60/120 underperforms, we pivot to further algorithmic tweaks (within default PG hparams) and finalize addendum with current best.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Preparing algorithms for submission**


  I''m getting ready to prepare ''submission_double_step_algosweep.py'' with a micro-sweep focusing on parameters like learning rate, entropy coefficient, and value loss coefficient. I wonder if we need to change the optimizer or training step to apply gradient clipping since the defaults don''t support it. To test algorithm improvements, a custom training step will be necessary. For now, I''ll just focus on the three parameters specified and hold off on any additional testing.**Finalizing configurations and planning next steps**


  It''s better to stage the seed replicates across all three seeds for the best recommended config, although it seems we’ve already done that. I want to prepare "analysis log printing" based on the tips, but I can''t alter the training code. Next up, I’ll wait for the results from runs 234 and 235 while also implementing the code for ''algosweep''. Additionally, I''ll plan to try "52 ch convlstm" if improvements are visible and get ready to write the relevant submission content.**Crafting action commands**


  I’m planning out a series of actions for creating submissions. First, I’ll go to research and write the code for `submission_double_step_algosweep.py`, which will use the recommended network and a micro-sweep of hyperparameters with base seed 42. For `submission_double_step_attn_temp_fine.py`, I’ll record fine sweeps around attn_temp, but since our best results were at 1.0, maybe I can skip that. I''ll also consider updating private memory or replying in the Archive but likely don''t need a new document. Lastly, I’ll ensure correct YAML formatting for the code content.**Planning effective actions**


  I''m focusing on minimal yet effective actions for the upcoming tasks. We can schedule the submission of the algosweep to run when a slot is free. However, since we currently have experiments running from 234 and 235, our submissions might get queued or rejected because the system allows only two experiments simultaneously. To avoid this potential rejection, it''s safer to write the script without submitting it. I might read ''defaults.py'' later to confirm supported hyperparameters, but it doesn''t seem essential right now. Let''s finalize everything!'
