- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, double-step, attention, bottleneck, width, dilation\"\nabstract: \"Replicate the improved wide configuration from ID 249 (mean 78.5): CNN 64/128, bottleneck_ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, d=5, single-head AttnPool, default PG constants. BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck import DoubleStepLNConvLSTM\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([44]),\n      \
    \    'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.33]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          stop_grad_first=False,\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 145: Wide‑CNN synthesis yields a gain.\n  - ID 249 (64/128 CNN, bottleneck_ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, d=5, single‑head AttnPool, default PG) achieved 78.5 (mean across 4 seeds). This exceeds our prior ~77.8 compute‑equalized 48/96 baseline.\n  - We launched fixed‑config replications across seed sets to assess stability:\n    • BASE_SEED=7 (submitted\
    \ this tick), BASE_SEED=123 next.\n  - If the wide compute‑equalized design consistently averages ≥78.0 across seed sets, we will recommend it as the new non‑FE default and update the addendum with IDs and a concise rationale (throughput restored with 0.33 bottleneck + smaller ConvLSTM).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 145:\n  - New best mean: ID 249 (64/128, ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44) = 78.5. Throughput appears restored; seed-wise best 0.812.\n  - Actions:\n    • Submitted replication at BASE_SEED=7 (fixed hyperparams to match ID 249). Next: replicate at 123.\n    • Aggressive equalization (ID 250; ratio=0.25, ConvLSTM {40,44}) running.\n  - Plan:\n    1) If replications (7, then 123) keep ≥78.0, promote this as the recommended non‑FE config over 48/96 (~77.8).\n    2) If aggressive equalization beats 78.5, replicate that variant instead.\n    3) Update archive with IDs and final recommendation accordingly.\n```"
