- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=123\"\ntags: \"replication, double-step, attention, bottleneck, width, dilation\"\nabstract: \"Third fixed-seed replicate of the improved wide configuration from ID 249: CNN 64/128, bottleneck_ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, d=5, single-head AttnPool, default PG constants. BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck import DoubleStepLNConvLSTM\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([44]),\n\
    \          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.33]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          stop_grad_first=False,\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/summary_bottleneck.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update (Tick 146):\n  - Wide 64/128 + ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44 (ID 249): 78.5 mean (seed best 0.812) → exceeds 48/96 baseline (~77.8).\n  - Aggressive equalization 64/128, ratio=0.25, ConvLSTM {40,44} (ID 250): 76.2 mean → too aggressive; underperforms.\n  - Replications:\n      • BASE_SEED=7 for wide 0.33/44: running (ID 252).\n\
    \      • BASE_SEED=123 for wide 0.33/44: submitted this tick (ID pending).\n  - Conclusion so far: 64/128 with ratio=0.33 and ConvLSTM=44 is a promising non‑FE upgrade; confirm with {7,123} before recommendation.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 146: Replication plan for wide compute‑equalized design.\n  - ID 249 (64/128, bottleneck_ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, d=5, 1‑head AttnPool, default PG): 78.5 mean.\n  - Aggressive 0.25 bottleneck (ID 250) regresses to 76.2.\n  - Replications launched to test stability:\n    • BASE_SEED=7 (ID 252): running\n    • BASE_SEED=123: submitted this tick (ID pending)\n  We will adopt this wide compute‑equalized design as the new non‑FE recommendation if the cross‑seed mean stays ≥78.0. Otherwise, we retain 48/96 (~77.8).\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response 127:135}"
