parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final non‑FE recommendation (wide compute‑equalized) with full IDs\n\n  New wide configuration:\n  - CNN: 64/128\n  - Bottleneck ratio: 0.33\n  - Recurrent core: LN‑gated ConvLSTM (width=44), double‑step (shared), no stop‑grad\n  - Readout: single‑head AttnPool (temp=1.0)\n  - Dilation: 5\n  - PG constants: lr=4e‑4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5\n\n  Results (means across the 4 seeds within each evaluation):\n  - ID 249 (BASE_SEED=42): 78.5\n  - ID 252 (BASE_SEED=7):  77.3\n  - ID 255 (BASE_SEED=123): 79.5\n\n  Aggregate across seed sets: mean ≈ 78.43 (range 77.3–79.5), exceeding the prior 48/96 compute‑equalized baseline (~77.8).\n  Aggressive equalization confirms a trade‑off:\n  - ID 250 (64/128, ratio=0.25, ConvLSTM {40,44}): 76.2 (underperforms)\n\n  Recommendation:\n  - Adopt the wide compute‑equalized design (64/128, ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44) as the new non‑FE default under the 30‑min cap.\n  -\
    \ Ready‑to‑run script placed at: storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_recommended_wide033_lstm44.py\n\n  We will stop Track‑2 scheduling (negative) and keep PG constants as above. Next, we will finalize documentation and provide qualitative analyses (attention maps, gate statistics) in a brief follow‑up note.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_recommended_wide033_lstm44.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  from networks.cnn_convlstm_layernorm_double_step_dilated_bottleneck import DoubleStepLNConvLSTM\n\n  # Recommended non-FE config (wide compute-equalized):\n  # CNN 64/128, bottleneck_ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, dilation=5\n  # double-step (shared), single-head AttnPool(temp=1.0), default PG constants.\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n\
    \          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([64]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([128]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([44]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.33]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepLNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          stop_grad_first=False,\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/summary_bottleneck.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Non-FE Dilated CNN + LN-ConvLSTM — Summary (Tick 147)\n\n  Previous recommended (compute-equalized):\n  - 48/96 CNN, ratio=0.6, ConvLSTM=48,\
    \ double-step+AttnPool → ~77.8 mean\n    • Replicates: ID 225 (42)=78.8, ID 226 (7)=75.0, ID 224 (123)=79.5\n\n  Wide compute-equalized upgrade (new recommendation):\n  - 64/128 CNN, ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, d=5, double-step+AttnPool, default PG\n    • ID 249 (42)=78.5\n    • ID 252 (7)=77.3\n    • ID 255 (123)=79.5\n    → Aggregate ≈ 78.43 (range 77.3–79.5), > old ~77.8\n\n  Negative controls:\n  - 64/128 with aggressive ratio=0.25 and/or smaller ConvLSTM (ID 250)=76.2 (underperforms)\n  - LR schedules on 48/96 (IDs 245,247)=70–71 (harmful)\n  - Best constants on 48/96 (ID 246)=77.8 (matches baseline)\n\n  Current Recommendation:\n  - Adopt 64/128, ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44, d=5; PG lr=4e-4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5; AttnPool temp=1.0.\n  - Repro script: storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_recommended_wide033_lstm44.py\n\n  Next:\n  - Finalize qualitative analyses (attention maps, gate stats) and brief addendum note.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply\
    \ 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 147 wrap-up:\n  - Wide compute-equalized config validated:\n      • ID 249 (42)=78.5, ID 252 (7)=77.3, ID 255 (123)=79.5 → mean ≈78.43 (>77.8).\n      • Aggressive 0.25 bottleneck regressed (ID 250=76.2).\n  - Adopt wide 64/128, ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44 as non-FE recommendation; script saved:\n      storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_recommended_wide033_lstm44.py\n  - Next: finalize doc + small qualitative note. Track‑2 scheduling closed as negative.\n```"
