parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, sota-synthesis, bottleneck, dilation, double-step, attention\"\nabstract: \"Replicate our std-width synthesis (ID 270, 83.2) with BASE_SEED=7 to assess stability. Architecture: 32/64 CNN, main-conv dilation d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), single-head AttnPool, default PG with AdamW+clip, no FE.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStd\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStd(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: Std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool — BASE_SEED=123\"\ntags: \"replication, sota-synthesis, bottleneck, dilation, double-step, attention\"\nabstract: \"Second replication of our std-width synthesis (ID 270, 83.2) with BASE_SEED=123. Same architecture/hparams: 32/64 CNN, main-conv dilation d=5, double-step\
    \ LN-ConvLSTM(64), single-head AttnPool, default PG with AdamW+clip, no FE.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStd\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStd(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 156 — Std-width synthesis result and plan\n  - New result: ID 270 (std-width 32/64, main-conv dilation d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), single-head AttnPool, AdamW+clip, no FE) = 83.2. This aligns with the 82.6–84.4 SOTA range reported in recent station runs.\n  - Replications launched for stability: BASE_SEED=7 and 123 (matching ID 270 config). We will append their IDs and means upon completion.\n  - Single-variable follow-up (ID 273 running): keep bottleneck 3×3 undilated (dilation only on main convs), matching high-scoring practice seen in reviewed code; this isolates dilation placement as the factor.\n  - If replications hold ≥82 consistently, we will summarize this synthesis as a validated SOTA-competitive non-FE configuration,\
    \ with code pointers and training constants.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 156:\n  - ID 270 = 83.2 on std-width synthesis (32/64, main-conv d=5, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), AttnPool, AdamW+clip, no FE). This matches station SOTA range.\n  - Submitted fixed-seed replications (BASE_SEED=7, 123) for ID 270 config. Also running the undilated-bottleneck variant (ID 273) to test dilation placement.\n  - If replications sustain ≥82, write a short archive addendum with IDs and finalize std-width synthesis as SOTA-competitive. Otherwise, document negatives and retain wide compute-equalized non-FE (mean ≈78.43) as practical recommendation.\n  - Next housekeeping: prune early high-token ticks after results return to keep token load < 60%.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response 136:145}"
