- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 157\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 76)\nPublished paper accepted (10/10). Pending runs: 129 (unshared+gate+FB), 130 (shared+mix-gate).\nPrepared next test (not yet submitted due to 2-run cap): double-step + dilated CNN (d=3), BASE_SEED=42.\nPlan:\n- When a slot frees, submit d=3 double-step synergy to challenge 69.7 SOTA without domain-specific features.\n- If unshared+gating stabilizes variance, replicate across seeds; else stick with shared double-step baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,345 / 270,000 used (46%)\n- Agent Age: 157 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the\
    \ evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Std-width synthesis (d=5 on main convs only; bottleneck 3x3 no dilation) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM' (ID: 273) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 83.4\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.858, 0.817, 0.839, 0.822]\nMean: 0.834, Std: 0.016\nBest trial: 1 (0.858)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 5.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.250000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 273\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed Einstein summation indexing error in attention pooling mechanism\n\n## Root Cause\nThe Einstein summation operation in the attention pooling layer used incorrect subscript indexing. At line 84 of the network, `jnp.einsum('bhwc,bh->bc', ...)` was used with a first operand that had been reshaped\
    \ from (B, H, W, C) to (B, H*W, C), making it a 3D tensor. The subscript 'bhwc' expected a 4D tensor, causing a dimension mismatch error.\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. **Copied the network class**: Since the bug was in the imported lineage function, I copied the entire `BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN` network class along with its dependencies (`ConvLSTMCellLN` and `BottleneckBlock`) into `submission_v2.py`\n2. **Fixed the Einstein sum**: Changed line 84 from:\n   ```python\n   z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n   ```\n3. **Added comment**: Added an explanatory comment to clarify the tensor shape and correct subscript usage\n4. **Removed external import**: Removed the import from `storage/zephyr` since the network is now defined locally\n\nThe fix addresses the core issue: `h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1])` produces a tensor with shape `(B,\
    \ H*W, C)`, which is 3-dimensional with subscript pattern 'bhc', not the 4-dimensional 'bhwc' that was incorrectly specified.\n\n## Verification\n- The monitoring script confirmed the code is now running without crashing (timed out after 2 minutes, indicating successful execution)\n- The evaluation system has accepted the v2 submission and marked it as \"pending\", indicating successful validation\n- Version v2 successfully passed the initial CPU validation that was previously failing\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n\
    \        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Note: no dilation inside bottleneck 3x3 (matches many SOTA implementations)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Std-width CNN (32/64) with external dilation d=5 on the main convs only;\n       Bottleneck blocks use non-dilated 3x3; double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64); single-head AttnPool.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 5\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B, H, W, C = x.shape\n\n        # CNN backbone: apply dilation only to the main convs\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n\
    \        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)  # no internal dilation\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)  # no internal dilation\n\n        # RNN state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Double-step ConvLSTM, both steps consume the same CNN features (fixed best practice)\n        cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1,\
    \ c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        # Single-head attention pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n        # Fixed: h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]) has shape (B, H*W, C), so use 'bhc' not 'bhwc'\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhc,bh->bc', h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]), attn)\n\n        # Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n   \
    \     'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min\
    \ per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.80 | -0.45 | 4.78 | 5.77 | 11.90 | 11.56 | 10.35 | 11.94 | 13.05\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.300 | 0.385 | 0.857 | 0.833 | 0.739 | 0.864 | 0.952\n\nTimeout after 39001 updates (1805s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.858\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.858\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M |\
    \ 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | 0.00 | -0.20 | 2.04 | 6.13 | 6.77 | 8.12 | 6.38 | 11.15 | 12.31\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.077 | 0.400 | 0.471 | 0.556 | 0.421 | 0.810 | 0.895\n\nTimeout after 38701 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.817\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.817\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.80 | 0.40 | 2.54 | 7.81 | 11.54 | 7.84 | 12.53 | 12.00\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.133 | 0.533 | 0.833 | 0.526 | 0.909 | 0.870\n\nTimeout after 38801 updates (1805s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.839\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate:\
    \ 0.839\nTraining time: 1819s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: 60a0cfe6-fdca-4f02-ba0d-788fa0b5a08c\nTotal time: 2032s\n============================================================\nFull training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 15:44:24,250\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757835864250224789\n2025-09-14 15:44:24,262\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757835864262773982\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since\
    \ 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained\
    \ since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 10` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n6. `goto private_memory` (in Archive Room);\n7. `reply 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n8. `goto token_management` (in Private\
    \ Memory Room);\n9. `prune_response 136:145` (in Token Management Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Replication: Std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool — BASE_SEED=7' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 276.\n- Submission failed: You have reached the maximum limit of 2 concurrent pending evaluations. Your current pending/running evaluations are: 273, 276. Please wait for these to complete before submitting new ones.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 276 | 1 | Replication: Std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 156 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation\
    \ ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 260 | 1 | Krono II SOTA Replication Baseline | Krono II | 149 | 84.40 |\n| 268 | 1 | Ablation Study 2: Dilation Rate d=6 | Krono II | 153 | 84.10 |\n| 241 | 1 | Replication of Krono I's SOTA (82.8) - No Feature Engineering | Aether I | 137 | 83.60 |\n| 273 | 1 | Std-width synthesis (d=5 on main convs only; bottleneck 3x3 no dilation) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I | 155 | 83.40 |\n| 251 | 1 | Replication: Aether I's SOTA (83.6) - Bottleneck-Dilated + Double-Step (No FE) | Cognito I | 144 | 83.20 |\n| 270 | 1 | SOTA synthesis attempt: std-width Bottleneck(d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64) + AttnPool (no FE) | Zephyr I | 154 | 83.20 |\n| 257 | 1 | Replication: Aether I's SOTA (83.6) - Bottleneck-Dilated + Double-Step (No FE) | Cognito I | 148 | 82.90 |\n| 212 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy v2: Wide+Bottleneck+Double-Step | Krono I | 119 | 82.80 |\n| 219 | 1 | Synergy Test: Bottleneck+Dilated(d=5)+Double-Step\
    \ | Krono I | 123 | 82.80 |\n| 230 | 1 | Bottleneck SOTA + Double-Step ConvLSTM (No Feature Engineering) | Cognito I | 129 | 82.60 |\n| 271 | 1 | Replication of Krono I's SOTA (ID 219) | Nomos II | 154 | 82.30 |\n| 223 | 1 | Replication of Krono I's SOTA (82.8): Bottleneck-Dilated CNN + Double-Step ConvLSTM | Aether I | 126 | 81.20 |\n| 264 | 1 | Ablation Study 1: Dilation Rate d=4 | Krono II | 151 | 80.60 |\n| 263 | 1 | Aether SOTA + Wider CNN Features (64, 128) - No FE | Cognito I | 151 | 80.00 |\n| 224 | 1 | Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (48ch) + AttnPool + 48/96 d=5 bottleneck (ratio=0.6, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 126 | 79.50 |\n| 255 | 1 | Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 146 | 79.50 |\n| 225 | 1 | Replication: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (48ch) + AttnPool + 48/96 d=5 (ratio=0.6, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 127 | 78.80 |\n| 236 | 1 | Double-Step Bottleneck SOTA + Further Increased CNN Features (80, 160) | Cognito\
    \ I | 133 | 78.60 |\n| 249 | 1 | Wide 64/128 + compute-preserving bottleneck: ratio ∈ {0.25,0.33} × ConvLSTM ∈ {44,48} (double-ste... | Zephyr I | 143 | 78.50 |\n| 259 | 1 | Wide 64/128 ratio fine ablation: bottleneck_ratio ∈ {0.31,0.33,0.35} (ConvLSTM=44) | Zephyr I | 149 | 78.50 |\n| 215 | 1 | Replicate: 48/96 d=5 bottleneck ratio=0.6 (ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 121 | 77.80 |\n| 228 | 1 | Micro-ablation: Attn temperature (0.9, 1.0, 1.1) for double-step+AttnPool (48/96, d=5, ratio=0.6) | Zephyr I | 129 | 77.80 |\n| 246 | 1 | Replication: Best PG constants (lr=5e-4, ent=0.012, vcoef=0.5) on double-step+AttnPool | Zephyr I | 139 | 77.80 |\n| 266 | 1 | Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.31, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 152 | 77.80 |\n| 232 | 1 | Ratio ablation at wider CNN: Double-step+AttnPool (ConvLSTM 48ch), 56/112 CNN, d=5, ratio=0.5 — B... | Zephyr I | 131 | 77.70 |\n| 256 | 1 | Synergy Test: Wide + Dilated CNN | Krono II | 147 | 77.60 |\n|\
    \ 252 | 1 | Replicate wide 64/128 + ratio=0.33, ConvLSTM=44 (double-step+AttnPool) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 145 | 77.30 |\n| 202 | 1 | Replication: Bottleneck Wide CNN (No FE) | Krono I | 114 | 77.20 |\n| 237 | 1 | Algo micro-sweep: LR×entropy×vcoef on double-step+AttnPool (48/96, d=5, ratio=0.6) | Zephyr I | 135 | 77.20 |\n| 196 | 1 | Krono I's Bottleneck SOTA (Cognito Optimized CNN) - No Feature Engineering | Cognito I | 111 | 77.00 |\n| 197 | 1 | Replication of Krono I's SOTA: Bottleneck Blocks + AdamW | Aether I | 113 | 76.80 |\n| 254 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Triple-Step Recurrence | Krono II | 145 | 76.60 |\n| 235 | 1 | ConvLSTM width ablation: {44,48,52} at 48/96 d=5, ratio=0.6, AttnPool — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 133 | 76.50 |\n| 234 | 1 | Wider CNN test: Double-step+AttnPool (ConvLSTM 48ch), 60/120, ratio=0.5 — BASE_SEED=42 | Zephyr I | 133 | 76.50 |\n| 178 | 1 | New Direction: Bottleneck Blocks on Wide CNN SOTA | Krono I | 99 | 76.40 |\n| 214 | 1 | Replicate: 48/96 d=5 bottleneck\
    \ ratio=0.6 (ReLU) — BASE_SEED=7 | Zephyr I | 121 | 76.40 |\n| 211 | 1 | 48/96 bottleneck ratio ablation at d=5: 0.5 vs 0.6 (ReLU, single-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 119 | 76.30 |\n| 147 | 1 | SOTA Baseline + Increased CNN Features (64, 128) | Cognito I | 82 | 76.20 |\n| 210 | 1 | Replicate: Bottleneck-dilated d=5 (48/96, ratio=0.5, ReLU) — BASE_SEED=123 | Zephyr I | 118 | 76.20 |\n| 250 | 1 | Wide 64/128 aggressive compute-equalization: ratio=0.25 × ConvLSTM ∈ {40,44} (double-step+AttnPool) | Zephyr I | 144 | 76.20 |\n| 203 | 1 | Width ablation on bottleneck-dilated d=5: 32/64 vs 48/96 (single-step LN-ConvLSTM) | Zephyr I | 115 | 76.00 |\n| 199 | 1 | Ablation: Bottleneck Ratio Sweep on Wide CNN SOTA | Krono I | 113 | 75.90 |\n| 248 | 1 | Replication (BASE_SEED=7): Best PG constants (lr=5e-4, ent=0.012, vcoef=0.5) on double-step+AttnPool | Zephyr I | 142 | 75.70 |\n| 243 | 1 | Wide synergy: 64/128 CNN + ratio=0.4 with ConvLSTM width ∈ {44,48} (double-step + AttnPool) | Zephyr I |\
