- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_std_sota_nodil_seed7.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN\n\n  # Std-width SOTA-competitive (no-FE), bottleneck 3x3 undilated; main convs d=5\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate nodil-bottleneck variant (std-width d=5) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM — BASE_SEED=7\"\ntags: \"replication, std-width, bottleneck, dilation, double-step, attention\"\nabstract: \"Replication of the 83.4 nodil-bottleneck variant (ID 273): std-width 32/64 CNN, main-conv dilation d=5, bottleneck 3×3 undilated, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), single-head AttnPool, AdamW+clip; no feature engineering. BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from zephyr.submissions.submission_std_sota_nodil_seed7\
    \ import _define_hyperparameters as _dh, create_network as _cn, create_optimizer as _co, BASE_SEED as BASE_SEED\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return _dh()\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _cn(hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return _co(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 158 — Std-width synthesis: replication plan (nodil bottleneck)\n  - Current results:\n    • ID 270 (std-width, d=5, double-step, AttnPool): 83.2\n    • ID 273 (same but bottleneck 3×3 undilated and pooling einsum fixed): 83.4\n    • ID 276 (replicate std-width, BASE_SEED=7): 82.5\n  - Action this tick:\n    • Submitted replication of the nodil-bottleneck variant with BASE_SEED=7 (ID pending) to directly test dilation placement across seeds.\n  - Pending:\n    • BASE_SEED=123 replication for the std-width config is running (ID 278). After both 278 and nodil-7 complete, we will report cross-seed\
    \ means and finalize the SOTA-competitive configuration with precise IDs and constants.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 158:\n  - Results: std-width synthesis holds ~83.2–83.4 (IDs 270, 273); std replicate seed=7 is 82.5 (ID 276).\n  - Submitted nodil-bottleneck replicate (seed=7) to isolate dilation placement effect across seeds; std replicate seed=123 (ID 278) running.\n  - When both complete: compute cross-seed mean for (a) std, (b) nodil; publish concise addendum with IDs and final recommended std-width config if ≥82 across seeds.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Summarizing the SOTA configuration**\n\nI need to create an archive addendum summarizing the SOTA-competitive configuration, including evaluation IDs and the final cross-seed mean. The major scoreboard lists Krono II replication at 84.4, while we're at 83.4, so our goal is to publish a well-documented addendum with at least five experiments. \n\nI'm also thinking about proposing a minimal micro-ablation to potentially boost our score and considering various adjustments, like changing LayerNorm inside the bottleneck.**Planning documentation and actions**\n\nSince I'm aiming to finalize the documentation, it makes sense to wait for replication results. My immediate next steps include conducting research and monitoring 278 once I finish that. I need to archive my reply and update the results summary as well. \n\nI'm also patching our stored nodil class to fix the einsum bug, and I've already made corrections in storage. Regarding tokens, we pruned previously and are at\
  \ 51%, with a cooldown that means no additional pruning. I’ll also consider adding code for the reproducible script in storage.**Deciding on replication strategy**\n\nI notice we have one slot free, which means I can choose to submit another ablation or replicate the nodil variant using seeds 7 or 123. Since 273 already used seed 42 with our nodil-bottleneck variant, 270 used dilation for both main convolutions and the BottleneckBlock.\n\nTo test dilation placement, it sounds like replicating the nodil variant is the way to go rather than the original. However, I see that 276 already replicated the original, so I need to clarify that in my logs.**Planning for nodil variant replication**\n\nI see that for 157, we changed the nodil file and submitted replicates using BottleneckD5DoubleStepStd, which isn’t nodil. In 156, I submitted replicates of the standard network, aligning with the 270 configuration. Now, I need to replicate the nodil variant from 273 across seeds 7 and 123, especially\
  \ since we have a running replicate of the standard network at seed 123.\n\nOnce a slot is freed, I'll schedule the nodil variant for submission and prepare the code in the meantime. I also need to update the results summary and compose a new storage submission script while considering a public memory update.**Implementing actions for nodil variant**\n\nI’m outlining the actions we need to take. First, I’ll go to research. Next, I need to write to the storage directory with the necessary code to load the nodil network and set BASE_SEED to the default of 42. Since we have one free slot from our two-run cap with 278 running, I can queue the nodil variant replication using seed 7.\n\nOnce that’s done, I’ll update the archive addendum with current results and ensure the proper YAML formatting while crafting the necessary scripts and commands. Let's keep everything organized as we proceed!"
