- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_std_sota_nodil_seed123.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN\n\n  # Std-width SOTA-competitive (no-FE), bottleneck 3x3 undilated; main convs d=5\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replication: nodil-bottleneck std-width d=5 + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM — BASE_SEED=123\"\ntags: \"replication, std-width, bottleneck, dilation, double-step, attention\"\nabstract: \"Replicate the nodil-bottleneck variant (ID 273=83.4) with BASE_SEED=123: 32/64 CNN, main-conv dilation d=5, bottleneck 3×3 undilated, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), 1-head AttnPool, AdamW+clip; no FE.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from zephyr.submissions.submission_std_sota_nodil_seed123 import _define_hyperparameters\
    \ as _dh, create_network as _cn, create_optimizer as _co, BASE_SEED as BASE_SEED\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return _dh()\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return _cn(hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return _co(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 159 — Std-width synthesis reaches 85.6; cross-seed update\n\n  New results (std-width 32/64, main-conv d=5, double-step LN‑ConvLSTM(64), 1‑head AttnPool, AdamW+clip, no FE):\n  - ID 278 (BASE_SEED=123): 85.6\n  - Prior: ID 270 (42)=83.2, ID 276 (7)=82.5\n  Cross-seed aggregate (42,7,123): ~83.8 mean (range 82.5–85.6), SOTA-competitive.\n\n  NodIl bottleneck placement:\n  - ID 273 (42, bottleneck 3×3 undilated): 83.4\n  - Replication submitted: seed=7 (ID 281 running), seed=123 submitted this tick (ID pending).\n\n  Takeaways:\n  - Using the same CNN features for both LSTM steps and keeping bottleneck 3×3 undilated are\
    \ consistent with high-scoring implementations.\n  - The std-width synthesis (no FE) is validated across seed sets and is a strong SOTA-competitive baseline.\n\n  Next:\n  - Append nodil replications (IDs 281, pending 123). If nodil ≥ std across seeds, we’ll recommend nodil as default; otherwise the standard std-width config stands.\n  - Prepare a concise figure/table addendum with all IDs and constants once the pending runs finish.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 159 notes:\n  - Big jump: std-width replicate ID 278 (seed=123) = 85.6. With ID 270=83.2 (seed=42) and ID 276=82.5 (seed=7), cross-seed mean ≈83.8 (range 82.5–85.6).\n  - NodIl bottleneck: ID 273 (seed=42)=83.4; seed=7 (ID 281) running; seed=123 replication submitted this tick.\n  - Plan: finalize std-width SOTA-competitive config after nodil replications, then publish the short addendum (IDs, constants, cross-seed stability).\n```"
