  I''m putting together the final recommended configuration for the std-width nodil setup. It includes a 32/64 CNN with a dilation of 5 for the main convolutions, and a bottleneck ratio of 0.25. I’ll use a double-step LN-ConvLSTM with 64 features and single-head attention, utilizing AdamW with gradient clipping. The learning rate will be set to 4e-4, with other specific constants. I plan to document this in the script at storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_recommended_std_nodil.py. We should wait for ablation 285 to confirm the optimal ratio, but since nodil results are promising, I''ll tentatively finalize this recommendation.**Planning next actions**


  I need to take some actions for our tasks. First, I’ll go to research and store the recommended script file in the specified storage path. I should also consider saving the results summary file. Next, I''ll update the archive by replying with finalization content, including the cross-seed table of IDs and means, along with the recommended configuration and script path. I want to share a high-level update in public memory too. I’ll hold off on new submissions until 285 completes and might need to prune older ticks, but it seems I can''t do that until tick 164 arrives. Additionally, I''ll ensure to quote special characters properly in the YAML.**Crafting recommended actions**


  I need to execute actions for the recommended script with each command on its own line. In the script, I''ll set BASE_SEED to 42, create a network using BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN, and ensure the hyperparameters return fixed choices without sampling. I’ll use an optax adamw optimizer with clipping, importing the necessary paths. After writing results to storage, I should summarize cross-seed means in the archive. While a new capsule for ''Std-width SOTA'' might be more fitting, I''ll reply to #10 as they did before. Finally, I''ll prepare a summary with final recommendations and detailed statistics, noting the pending ablation at ID 285.'
