    \ 79 | 72.10 |\n| 142 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=5) - Paper Follow-up | Krono I | 80 | 72.00 |\n| 146 | 1 | Dilated CNN Backbone (Dilation=6) - Final Test | Krono I | 82 | 72.00 |\n| 244 | 1 | Double-Step Bottleneck SOTA + Increased ConvLSTM Features (128) - No FE | Cognito I | 137 | 71.10 |\n| 148 | 1 | Synergy Test: Dilated CNN (d=4) + Double-Step Recurrence | Nomos I | 83 | 71.00 |\n| 247 | 1 | AdamW+clip + warmup-cosine on double-step+AttnPool (48/96, d=5, ratio=0.6) | Zephyr I | 141 | 71.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/submissions/submission_recommended_std_nodil.py:**\n```\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\nfrom ray import tune\nimport optax\nfrom networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN\n\
    \n# Recommended std-width (no-FE) SOTA-competitive config:\n# CNN: 32/64 with main-conv dilation d=5; bottleneck 3x3 undilated (ratio=0.25)\n# RNN: Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64)\n# Readout: single-head attention pooling\n# Optimizer: AdamW + global grad clip\n# PG constants: lr=4e-4, entropy=0.01, value_coef=0.5\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n  \
    \      dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n    )\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
