parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_std_nodil_wd0.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42  # 4 parallel seeds from this base\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Keep architecture and PG constants fixed\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n\
    \          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Test AdamW with zero weight decay (effectively Adam + clip)\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Std-width nodil — AdamW weight decay = 0.0 (BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"std-width, nodil, optimizer, adamw, weight-decay, policy-gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test optimizer regularization strength: AdamW with zero weight decay on the std-width nodil baseline. All other constants fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from zephyr.submissions.submission_std_nodil_wd0 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters as _dh, create_network\
    \ as _cn,\n      create_optimizer as _co, BASE_SEED as BASE_SEED\n  )\n  def _define_hyperparameters(): return _dh()\n  def create_network(hparams): return _cn(hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4): return _co(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_std_nodil_wd2e4.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42  # 4 parallel seeds from this base\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Keep architecture and PG constants fixed\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Test stronger AdamW regularization\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=2e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Std-width nodil — AdamW weight decay = 2e-4 (BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"std-width, nodil, optimizer, adamw, weight-decay, policy-gradient\"\nabstract: \"Test increased AdamW weight decay (2e-4) on the std-width nodil baseline. All other constants\
    \ fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from zephyr.submissions.submission_std_nodil_wd2e4 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters as _dh, create_network as _cn,\n      create_optimizer as _co, BASE_SEED as BASE_SEED\n  )\n  def _define_hyperparameters(): return _dh()\n  def create_network(hparams): return _cn(hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4): return _co(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 174 — Micro-sweeps (lr, vcoef) negative; testing AdamW regularization\n\n  New results (BASE_SEED=42):\n  - ID 307 (value_loss_coef ∈ {0.45, 0.50, 0.55}): 84.9 → best at 0.50 (baseline).\n  - ID 308 (learning_rate ∈ {3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4}): 84.2 → best at 5e-4 but still below our 86.4–87.0 range.\n\n  Action:\n  - Launching two fixed-constant tests on optimizer regularization for std-width nodil:\n    • AdamW weight_decay = 0.0\n    • AdamW weight_decay = 2e-4\n  - Goal: verify\
    \ whether slightly weaker/stronger decoupled L2 improves cross-seed mean beyond the 86.4–87.0 band. If either helps at seed 42, we will replicate across {7,123} and update the recommended script.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 174 notes:\n  - lr and vcoef sweeps did not improve (IDs 308=84.2, 307=84.9 at seed 42).\n  - Submitted optimizer regularization tests on std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42): AdamW weight_decay {0.0, 2e-4}. If either >86.4, replicate across {7,123}; otherwise, close out std-width tuning.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating risk and adjustments**\n\nThere’s a small risk involved. The vcoef and lr sweeps didn’t seem to help much. I remember testing entropy values of 0.008, 0.01, and 0.012, and 0.01 was the best, so I might skip that. As for the gradient clip value, it’s currently at 1.0, but perhaps trying 0.5 or 2.0 could be worth it. I’ll keep in mind our two-run cap for resources, but it looks like there are currently no running experiments.**Planning new runs**\n\nAlright, it looks like we can go ahead and submit two new runs. Since we want to finalize our baseline and aim to surpass an 87.0 score, I’m considering a weight decay sweep and a gradient clip sweep. The gradient clip is part of the optimizer, so I’ll vary the clip threshold in the chain. We’ll need to reference the recommended network with the weight decay parameter and clip_by_global_norm value in our submission file. \n\nI’m noting combinations: weight_decay values (0.0, 1e-4, 2e-4) and clip_norm values (0.5,\
  \ 1.0, 2.0), totaling nine combinations. However, Ray will only evaluate four trials, so we might not cover all combos. I think restricting to three combinations for each parameter could be a good approach.**Adjusting sweeps**\n\nI’m thinking about fixing the weight_decay at the best value of 1e-4 and only sweeping the clip_norm with three values; that way, I can observe the clip effect better. Given that we have four trials, I’ll choose to sweep clip_norm at {0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0} while keeping weight_decay fixed. Alternatively, I could sweep weight_decay at {0.0, 1e-4, 2e-4} while keeping clip fixed at 1.0. \n\nI plan to make two submissions for these sweeps and update our archive with results from previous runs.**Ensuring YAML formatting**\n\nI need to make sure that the YAML format is correct, especially concerning titles that contain colons and parentheses. Since titles might have special characters like colons, they should be enclosed in quotes to avoid parsing errors. I've used quotes\
  \ in the past, but I’ll stick to quoting the title lines consistently this time.\n\nAlso, I need to ensure that the create_optimizer function includes the weight_decay parameter, which I’ll define in the hyperparameters. The clip_norm parameter should be included there too. I’m set to import the optax chain and keep the network import as before, with BASE_SEED set to 42. Time to craft the code!**Clarifying optimizer parameters**\n\nI’m grappling with how to set up the optimizer since the main harness only passes the learning rate and won’t pass clip_norm or weight_decay. It looks like I need to embed these parameters in \"hparams\" or accept that I can’t vary them in create_optimizer since the signature is fixed. \n\nSo, I can only run two submissions, testing weight_decay at 0 and 2e-4. I'll also look at testing clip_norm with separate runs. It seems the overall score consistency isn’t clear, but I’ll move forward with creating new submission files for each case. Let's implement the code!**Implementing\
  \ optimizer tests**\n\nI’m considering whether to test clipnorm instead of weight decay, but I think weight decay tests should be the priority. The current node indicates that both micro-sweeps didn’t beat the baseline, and additional sweeps might stall. However, the system suggests that tweaking hyperparameters could still help, so let’s move forward.\n\nI’ll write submission files for wd0 and wd2e4, using AdamW with weight decay set to 0.0 and ensuring everything is properly referenced. I’ll also make a note to update the archive with results from prior tests. Let's get started!"
