- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 176\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 76)\nPublished paper accepted (10/10). Pending runs: 129 (unshared+gate+FB), 130 (shared+mix-gate).\nPrepared next test (not yet submitted due to 2-run cap): double-step + dilated CNN (d=3), BASE_SEED=42.\nPlan:\n- When a slot frees, submit d=3 double-step synergy to challenge 69.7 SOTA without domain-specific features.\n- If unshared+gating stabilizes variance, replicate across seeds; else stick with shared double-step baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 163,594 / 270,000 used (61%)\n- Agent Age: 176 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 306**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hypothesis:\
    \ Late Time Feature Injection\n**ID:** 306\n**Tags:** hypothesis, architecture, time feature, input processing\n**Abstract:** This experiment tests a fundamental change to input processing. Instead of feeding the time feature through the CNN, I will inject it into the network after the pooling layer. The hypothesis is that this prevents the non-spatial time information from being distorted by convolutions and allows the final MLP to use it more effectively.\n**Score:** 85.6\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.817, 0.858, 0.876, 0.871]\nMean: 0.856, Std: 0.023\nBest trial: 3 (0.876)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys; from ray import tune; import optax\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\nfrom time_injection_net\
    \ import TimeInjectionNet\nfrom ppo_training_fixed import ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n    }\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return TimeInjectionNet(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n    )\n\ntraining_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n\
    \    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 10126\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 10126 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL\
    \ RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 30.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 1 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.87 | -0.41 | 4.15 | 8.72 | 11.66 | 7.73 | 11.90 | 11.27 | 12.12 | 10.87 | 10.56\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.250 | 0.615 | 0.833 | 0.526 | 0.857 | 0.811 | 0.882 | 0.778 | 0.750\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1804s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.817\n\nSeed 1 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.817\nTraining time: 1820s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 3 with timeout 30.0min\n\
    Performing initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.20 | -0.13 | 5.23 | 3.82 | 10.21 | 9.43 | 8.45 | 11.71 | 11.26 | 11.19 | 12.68\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.333 | 0.231 | 0.733 | 0.667 | 0.583 | 0.852 | 0.818 | 0.800 | 0.920\n\nCompleted 39062 updates (1804s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.876\n\nSeed 3 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.876\nTraining time: 1821s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | -0.57 | 2.61 |\
    \ 5.74 | 7.50 | 10.29 | 11.11 | 10.20 | 11.09\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.143 | 0.357 | 0.520 | 0.737 | 0.800 | 0.727 | 0.792\n\nTimeout after 38701 updates (1806s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.858\n\nSeed 2 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.858\nTraining time: 1823s\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 4 with timeout 30.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -1.20 | -0.37 | 5.01 | 6.13 | 8.71 | 10.94 | 10.01 | 9.85 | 12.29\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.333 | 0.400 | 0.607 | 0.789 | 0.714 | 0.692 | 0.895\n\nTimeout after 38701 updates (1808s)\nFinal test solve rate: 0.871\n\nSeed 4 completed:\nSolve rate: 0.871\nTraining time: 1825s\nSUBMISSION_UUID: f331e238-eecd-4b22-9dde-b03a4aadca6c\nTotal time: 1833s\n============================================================\n\
    Full training completed!\n\n\nSTDERR:\n2025-09-14 20:37:24,579\tINFO worker.py:1747 -- Connecting to existing Ray cluster at address: 10.60.151.21:6379... timestamp_ns=1757853444580010380\n2025-09-14 20:37:24,592\tINFO worker.py:1927 -- Connected to Ray cluster. timestamp_ns=1757853444592872802\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors\
    \ of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\nGym has been unmaintained since 2022 and does not support NumPy 2.0 amongst other critical functionality.\nPlease upgrade to Gymnasium, the maintained drop-in replacement of Gym, or contact\
    \ the authors of your software and request that they upgrade.\nUsers of this version of Gym should be able to simply replace 'import gym' with 'import gymnasium as gym' in the vast majority of cases.\nSee the migration guide at https://gymnasium.farama.org/introduction/migration_guide/ for additional information.\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Evaluation Review: 305**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Debug: Double-Step Synergy Architecture + Default PG (No FE)\n**ID:** 305\n**Tags:** debug, sota, architecture, bottleneck, dilated-cnn, double-step\n**Abstract:** This experiment is a debugging step following the failure of Eval ID 302 (Krono II PPO SOTA replication) due to \"No trial files found.\" The objective is to verify the stability of the `DoubleStepSynergyNetAdapted` architecture by running it with the system's **default Policy Gradient training step**, explicitly removing the custom PPO training step. It utilizes the architectural parameters (`cnn_features_1=32`, `cnn_features_2=64`,\
    \ `conv_lstm_features=64`, `dilation_rate=5`), no explicit feature engineering, AdamW optimizer, and Xavier initialization, aiming to confirm the architecture's foundational integrity before re-attempting PPO.\n**Score:** 81.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.832, 0.808, 0.827, 0.805]\nMean: 0.818, Std: 0.012\nBest trial: 1 (0.832)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n# Define a base seed for reproducibility.\nBASE_SEED = 10122 # Matching Krono II's PPO SOTA submission\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    \"\"\"\n    Define hyperparameters for this debug experiment, matching Krono II's Eval ID 288\
    \ architecture.\n    \"\"\"\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]), # Dilation applied only to initial CNN layers\n    }\n\n# engineer_features is not used in this architecture.\n@jax.jit\ndef engineer_features(obs):\n    \"\"\"\n    (Not used in this specific experiment)\n    Implements advanced feature engineering ('push destination' channels).\n    \"\"\"\n    agent_ch = obs[..., 3] + obs[..., 5]\n    box_ch = obs[..., 4] + obs[..., 6]\n    empty_ch = obs[..., 0] + obs[..., 2]\n    \n    agent_left = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    box_mid_lr = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=1)\n    empty_right = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    push_right_pattern = agent_left\
    \ * box_mid_lr * empty_right\n    push_right_ch = jnp.pad(push_right_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_right = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=1)\n    empty_left = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=1)\n    push_left_pattern = agent_right * box_mid_lr * empty_left\n    push_left_ch = jnp.pad(push_left_pattern, ((0,0), (1,1)))\n\n    agent_below = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    box_mid_ud = lax.slice_in_dim(box_ch, 1, 7, axis=0)\n    empty_above = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    push_up_pattern = agent_below * box_mid_ud * empty_above\n    push_up_ch = jnp.pad(push_up_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n\n    agent_above = lax.slice_in_dim(agent_ch, 0, 6, axis=0)\n    empty_below = lax.slice_in_dim(empty_ch, 2, 8, axis=0)\n    push_down_pattern = agent_above * box_mid_ud * empty_below\n    push_down_ch = jnp.pad(push_down_pattern, ((1,1), (0,0)))\n    \n    return jnp.concatenate([obs, push_up_ch[...,None], push_right_ch[...,None], push_down_ch[...,None],\
    \ push_left_ch[...,None]], axis=-1)\n\n# --- ConvLSTM Cell with LayerNorm (from Aether I's Eval ID 241, for robustness) ---\nclass LayerNormConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int, int] = (3, 3)\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, inputs):\n        c, h = carry\n        \n        inputs_h = jnp.concatenate([inputs, h], axis=-1)\n        \n        gates = nn.Conv(\n            features=4 * self.features,\n            kernel_size=self.kernel_size,\n            padding='SAME',\n            kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(),\n            name=\"gates_conv\"\n        )(inputs_h)\n\n        i, f, o, g = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n\n        i = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"i_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(i)\n        f = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"f_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(f)\n        o = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"o_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(o)\n        g = nn.LayerNorm(name=\"g_ln\", epsilon=1e-5)(g)\n        \n        i = nn.sigmoid(i)\n        f = nn.sigmoid(f)\n       \
    \ o = nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = nn.tanh(g)\n\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * nn.tanh(new_c)\n        \n        return (new_c, new_h), new_h\n\n# --- Bottleneck Block (from Krono I's bottleneck_sota.py - NO internal dilation) ---\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module): \n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features // 4, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y) # NO DILATION HERE\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Single-Head Attention Pooling (from Aether I's Eval ID 241) ---\nclass SingleHeadAttentionPooling(nn.Module):\n    temperature: float = 1.0 \n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray) -> jnp.ndarray:\n     \
    \   batch_size, H, W, C = x.shape\n        \n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(features=1, kernel_size=(1,1), kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=\"attn_logits\")(x)\n        attn_logits_flat = attn_logits.reshape((batch_size, -1))\n        attn_weights_flat = nn.softmax(attn_logits_flat / self.temperature, axis=-1)\n        attn_weights = attn_weights_flat.reshape((batch_size, H, W, 1))\n\n        weighted_features = x * attn_weights\n        pooled_features = jnp.sum(weighted_features, axis=(1, 2))\n        \n        return pooled_features\n\nclass DoubleStepSynergyNetAdapted(nn.Module): # Adapted from Krono II's DoubleStepSynergyNet\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n        # NO FEATURE ENGINEERING: directly use raw 8-channel observation\n\
    \        x_input_cnn = x \n        \n        # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks (Xavier init for all convs)\n        # Dilation applied ONLY to initial Conv layers, not inside BottleneckBlock's 3x3\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_input_cnn); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(x)\n        \n        # 2. Double-Step ConvLSTM (using Aether I's LayerNormConvLSTMCell for robustness)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype));\
    \ rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n        \n        lstm_cell = LayerNormConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        rnn_state_1, _ = lstm_cell(rnn_state, x)\n        rnn_state_2, h_out_2 = lstm_cell(rnn_state_1, x)\n        new_rnn_state = rnn_state_2\n\n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME', kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out_2)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out_2, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n        \n        # 4. Final MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        \n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return DoubleStepSynergyNetAdapted(\n\
    \        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n    )\n\n# Using default Policy Gradient training step for this debug run.\n# training_step = ppo_training_step_fixed_rnn # Removed for this debug run\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n    )\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING\
