    \ AdamW (wd=1e-4) on the std-width nodil baseline. Architecture and PG constants fixed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage')\n  from zephyr.submissions.submission_std_nodil_clip20 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters as _dh, create_network as _cn,\n      create_optimizer as _co, BASE_SEED as BASE_SEED\n  )\n  def _define_hyperparameters(): return _dh()\n  def create_network(hparams): return _cn(hparams)\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4): return _co(learning_rate)\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 176 — Optimizer regularization results and next tests\n\n  Results (BASE_SEED=42):\n  - AdamW weight decay=0.0: ID 313 → 85.0\n  - AdamW weight decay=2e-4: ID 314 → 85.2\n  Both below the 86.4–87.0 range; wd adjustments do not help.\n\n  Next (single-variable tests running):\n  - Gradient clipping norm sweep:\n    • clip=0.5 (tight)\n    • clip=2.0 (loose)\n  Constants held fixed; if either\
    \ exceeds 86.4 at seed 42, we will replicate across {7,123} and update the recommended script. Otherwise, we will try Adam (no WD) next, then close out std-width tuning.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 176 notes:\n  - WD tests: wd=0.0 → 85.0 (ID 313), wd=2e-4 → 85.2 (ID 314). Neither helps vs 86.4–87.0 baseline.\n  - Submitted grad-clip sweep at seed 42: clip ∈ {0.5, 2.0}. If neither helps, test Adam (no WD). If still negative, conclude std-width nodil tuning and document final constants.\n```"
