parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_timeinject.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_TimeInject(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Std-width CNN (32/64) with main-conv dilation d=5; bottleneck 3x3 undilated.\n         Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64); single-head AttnPool; inject time feature after pooling.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n  \
    \    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, C = x.shape\n          # Separate time channel (last channel); feed only spatial semantics (first 7) to CNN\n          x_spatial = x[..., :7]\n          t_map = x[..., 7:8]  # (B,H,W,1); constant over H,W in this env\n          t_scalar = jnp.mean(t_map, axis=(1,2,3), keepdims=False)  # (B,)\n\n          # CNN backbone: dilation only on main convs; bottleneck undilated 3x3\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spatial)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=y.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(y.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (both steps read same CNN features)\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), y)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), y)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape(B, -1)\n          attn\
    \ = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bn,bnc->bc', attn, h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1]))  # (B, C)\n\n          # Late time injection: concatenate scalar time to pooled features\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z, t_scalar[:, None]], axis=-1)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_TimeInject\", \"BottleneckBlock\", \"ConvLSTMCellLN\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_std_nodil_timeinject.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_timeinject\
    \ import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_TimeInject\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_TimeInject(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 177 prep:\n  - Two runs active (grad-clip 0.5 and 2.0). No new submissions to respect the 2-run cap.\n  - Prepared next PG baseline variant: late time injection (remove time channel from CNN; concatenate scalar time to pooled z). Files:\n      • networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_timeinject.py\n      • submissions/submission_std_nodil_timeinject.py\n  - When a slot frees:\n      • If clip sweep fails to exceed 86.4 at seed 42, submit the time-injection PG variant.\n      • If still no gain, conclude std-width tuning and finalize the recommendation + negative results summary.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating token management and updates**


  I’m considering that we can go to Token Management to prune some earlier ticks since we’re at 69% of our token budget, which is getting close. We had a cooldown period since the last prune, but it’s at 7 ticks now. I see that we might need to prune again soon, but it’s not urgent yet. Also, I could look at submitted SOTA by Krono and the improvements in PPO for ideas to apply to our PG baseline.**Considering architecture adjustments**


  In the PG baseline, I’m thinking about injecting time into the MLP heads. There are constraints since the time feature is part of observation channel 7, and it can be processed without being domain-specific. I could create an architecture variant that drops time from the CNN channels and concatenates a scalar (average time) to z. While I’m considering potential risks, I want to propose using small MLP gating or FiLM with minimal changes. I can prepare a new network file for future submission as well.**Planning CNN input adjustments**


  I''m planning to modify the input to the CNN by removing channel 7, which represents time, by either zeroing or slicing it out. The observation shape is (8,8,8), so I’ll pass the first seven channels into the CNN. After pooling to z, I need to compute a time scalar \( t \), which I could determine by taking the mean of the time channel or using the last channel as a constant across the grid. I''ll then concatenate \( z \) with \( t \) and proceed with testing. Additionally, I''ll prepare the necessary files for storage and submission.**Planning actions for time injection**


  I need to take several actions now. First, I’ll go to research and write a new network file for time injection, as well as a submission file referencing that. However, I shouldn’t submit it just yet since there are currently two runs active. The system might accept the submit command, but to avoid any concurrency violations, it’s best not to submit until one experiment is finished. I''ll also add a Public Memory message summarizing current results. Finally, I’ll ensure the code is correct before moving on to the next test when a slot frees up.**Creating the TimeInject module**


  I''m set to create a new module similar to BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN, but this one will include time injection after pooling. I’ll define a "TimeInject" network class while ensuring that create_network uses the correct hyperparameters. It’s crucial to keep late time injection domain-agnostic and follow the existing code style. I''ll extract the last channel to calculate a time scalar and reshape it before concatenating with z. I’ll preserve the baseline constants and craft the necessary files without submitting, ensuring I adhere to concurrency rules!'
