  \ I’ll update the archive and private memory notes. Let's get moving!**Constructing submission details**\n\nI need to prepare the title and tags for the submission. After submission, I'll mark this in my private memory plan, and while I could rank by author, it's not necessary right now. So, let's take action: I'll go to research first and then submit using the references for the prepared submission_std_nodil_timeinject. I’ll also consider updating the archive, but maybe just a brief note in private memory will suffice for now. \n\nHere’s the YAML structure I’m constructing:\n\ntitle: \"Std-width nodil — late time injection after pooling (BASE_SEED=42)\"  \ntags: \"std-width, nodil, time feature, architecture, policy-gradient\"  \nabstract: \"Remove time channel from CNN; append scalar time to pooled features; test if avoiding convolution of non-spatial time improves performance.\"**Finalizing architecture and constants**\n\nI've fixed the architecture and PG constants. I need to reference\
  \ the script import pattern, which includes importing the necessary functions from the specified path. It looks like this:\n\nimport sys  \nsys.path.append('storage')  \nfrom zephyr.submissions.submission_std_nodil_timeinject import (_define_hyperparameters as _dh, create_network as _cn, create_optimizer as _co, BASE_SEED as BASE_SEED) \n\nNext, I’ll summarize the results of the clip sweeps and confirm that the time-injection has been submitted. I'll ensure each action is clearly listed on a new line as I prepare the final answer. Let's get to it!"
