role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_earlyinj.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Undilated 3x3 inside bottleneck to preserve locality/compute\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_EarlyTime(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Early time injection: feed all 8 channels (including time) through the CNN and ConvLSTM.\n      Std-width CNN (32/64) with dilation d=5 on main convs only; bottleneck 3x3s undilated;\n      Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64); single-head AttnPool.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1:\
    \ int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n          # CNN backbone: dilation on main convs only\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\
    \n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=y.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(y.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM (shared cell)\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), y)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), y)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1])          # (B, H*W, C)\n   \
    \       z = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)              # (B, C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_EarlyTime\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 181 — Prepared early-vs-late ablation\n  - Stored early time injection counterpart at storage/zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_earlyinj.py (same settings as late-injection\
    \ variant; only difference is time channel enters at input).\n  - Waiting for reps (IDs 327, 328) to finish. As soon as a slot frees, I will submit the early-injection run with BASE_SEED=42 for a clean A/B comparison against ID 322.\n  - If early<late consistently across seeds, I’ll finalize an Archive addendum with the ablation table (IDs, mean±std).\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning the code submission**\n\nI’m preparing to store the code as a file for future submission, though I'm concerned about potential concurrency limits. It looks like I won’t be able to submit a third time without the system rejecting it. Instead, I’ll just save it. I also think it’s a good idea to visit the Archive Room and mention results or plans for a new paper, but I’ll keep it short. I can outline an 'early time injection' variant by including time as an eighth channel into the CNN input.**Exploring injection variants**\n\nI'm analyzing the current variant that uses late injection after pooling, while the original architecture most likely utilized the time channel as an input. The specifications indicate the environment includes a time channel at index 7, and older networks likely accepted eight channels. The LN gating LSTM recognizes these channels but does not use late injection. For an 'early injection' comparison, I think we should feed all eight channels\
  \ to CNN and LSTM, contrasting this with zeroing out and appending time after pooling.**Standardizing network features**\n\nI'm thinking about how earlier setups used a nodil-bottleneck-lateinj approach. To properly compare injection locations, I believe we should keep all other factors constant: same network features, only using the main convolution with undilated 3x3 inside the bottleneck, employing double-step LN ConvLSTM(64), and AdamW with clipping. The only variation would be the time channel injection point. I can create a network file like bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_earlyinj.py to reflect this, submitting it later when there's availability. Additionally, I can store some code for evaluation analysis, but that might not be urgent right now.**Planning project tasks**\n\nI’m outlining my best plan for moving forward. First, I want to leave a short note in Private memory about the replicate requests and my plan for conducting early versus late ablation, plus preparing\
  \ an Archive addendum. Next, I’ll write the early injection network to storage in Research Counter. I might also prepare the submission content to run when a slot is available since we can’t queue jobs. Additionally, I’m considering adding a \"test()\" function for quick runs without GPUs, which could be optional to define for shape verification. I also plan to update 'results/summary.txt', even though there's no explicit storage for that. Lastly, I could consider using Token management again for further pruning.**Organizing future actions**\n\nIt seems the cooldown is still active, with six ticks remaining, so we can't prune anything just yet. I think it would be smart to review the top results to ensure replicates across seeds, but I can wait for those to come. I'll draft an Archive reply or capsule, keeping in mind any accepted papers, but I might postpone due to token limitations. It’s interesting to note that our time injection method could reduce the distribution shift of features.\
  \ \n\nI believe documenting our plan and preparing an early injection network file are next steps. I’ll ensure that the code treats time as part of the input in a full 8-channel manner. Also, I'll avoid submitting for now since we’re already at capacity for running experiments.**Finalizing steps for early injection**\n\nSince the next step involves comparing early versus late ablation, I might want to create a 'test()' function to confirm shapes, although it’s not strictly necessary. My token budget is at 21%, so I feel safe. \n\nI’m planning to execute several actions: first, I'll go to research and write the early injection file to storage. Next, I'll reply in private memory with an update about preparing the early injection variant and plans for submission once there's an open slot. Also, if replicates exceed 86, we'll consider adding an addendum. I want to set a BASE_SEED constant to ensure fairness. It’s important to keep my imports well-organized and make sure everything is fully\
  \ coded."
