role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_notime.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n  \
    \    @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Undilated 3x3 inside bottleneck to preserve locality/compute\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_NoTime(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Std-width CNN (32/64) with dilation d=5 on main convs only;\n      Bottleneck 3x3s undilated; Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64);\n      Single-head AttnPool; NO TIME INPUT (drop time channel entirely).\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n\
    \      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          # Use only spatial channels (first 7); drop time channel\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          # CNN backbone: dilation on main convs only\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\
    \ ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=y.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(y.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM (shared cell)\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), y)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), y)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)  # (B,H,W,1)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape(B, -1,\
    \ h_out.shape[-1])          # (B, H*W, C)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)              # (B, C)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_NoTime\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Ablation: remove time input (late-injection arch) — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"ablation, time, bottleneck, dilation, convlstm, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Quantify the contribution of time\
    \ by removing the time channel entirely in the late-injection SOTA architecture. Std-width CNN (32/64) with d=5 on main convs only, undilated bottleneck 3×3s, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), single-head AttnPool, AdamW+clip. BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_notime import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_NoTime\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_NoTime(\n\
    \          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 185 — Next ablation launched\n  - Early vs late time injection: late wins (IDs 322/327/328 at 86.6/86.1/86.6 vs early 331=82.4, 332=84.7). Seed 123 (early) is running (ID 335).\n  - New ablation submitted: remove time input entirely on the late-injection SOTA backbone (std-width, d=5, undilated bottlenecks, double-step LN-ConvLSTM). BASE_SEED=42.\n  - Next when a slot frees: policy-only time injection (append time\
    \ only to policy head, not value) to probe where time helps most.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Deciding next actions**\n\nI'm analyzing the current state in the Archive Room. We've submitted early injection for seed 123, updated the CSV, and posted a reply about the system state. The user hasn't posed a question. Given our external constraints, we need to manage experiments and document results. Notably, the current state-of-the-art is around 86.6 from late time injection, as we found early injections to be less effective. My next steps involve waiting for seed 335 to finish, and in the meantime, I can prepare an Addendum to the Archive with the final table structure.**Exploring token management and ablations**\n\nI’m considering how to use token management since we currently have 93k tokens. I think proposing further ablations could help question the fundamentals while adhering to our constraints, avoiding domain-specific heuristics. \n\nIt seems like late time injection improved performance. We could test variants, like time injection focused on the value head\
  \ or both policy and value. I’m also thinking about using gating influences with FiLM or exploring positional/time embeddings. I should ensure we can test without time input versus late injection to see how that impacts results.**Analyzing improvement strategies**\n\nI'm noticing that using a gradient clip of 0.5 improved results to 85.5, while an entropy sweep reached 86.4, pointing to small differences. Our current state-of-the-art with late injection is 86.6. \n\nI’m thinking about tuning the attention temperature around 1.0 since evaluations at 299 with different temps scored 85.6 without late injection. It seems wise to test the attention temperature again under late injection while keeping other variables constant. \n\nAnother idea is to explore different injection strategies, such as concatenating to the policy head only. We might also compute equalization with small modifications.**Preparing code and updates**\n\nI’m thinking about creating persistent code named \"submission_sota_lateinj.py\"\
  \ to store the network and default hyperparameters, which can help others replicate our work for the paper. I also need to update the CSV for early injections 331 and 332, which I've done, and I’ll update 335 once it’s finished.\n\nSince I'm in the Archive Room, I can also prepare the addendum template related to our CSV. Currently, we have no ongoing experiments, but we just submitted 335, and the limit is two concurrent experiments. I could also submit a controlled ablation experiment comparing \"time to policy-only vs both\" and explore additional ablations like \"no time input.\"**Planning network modifications**\n\nI’m weighing the possibility of running two concurrent experiments, but since 335 is currently active, I can only submit one more evaluation. I’m opting for the \"No time channel\" variant on the late injection architecture to assess the impact of removing time. The hypothesis is that without time, performance might drop slightly due to reliance on the step penalty.\n\n\
  To implement this, I’ll create a new file called \"bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_notime.py,\" which is based on the late injection architecture but without any time input. I’ll ensure to keep the hyperparameters consistent, using BASE_SEED 42. Once the code is ready, I’ll proceed with submitting it alongside a summary of our progress in private memory."
