- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/summary.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Time Injection Study — Std-width, no FE, d=5 main convs, undilated bottlenecks, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), AttnPool, AdamW+clip\n\n  Completed (mean ± std over 4 seeds in each eval):\n  Late injection (after pooling, both heads):\n    - ID 322 (BASE_SEED=42): 86.6 ± 0.014\n    - ID 327 (BASE_SEED=7):  86.1 ± 0.020\n    - ID 328 (BASE_SEED=123): 86.6 ± 0.015\n  Early injection (into CNN+ConvLSTM):\n    - ID 331 (BASE_SEED=42): 82.4 ± 0.015\n    - ID 332 (BASE_SEED=7):  84.7 ± 0.020\n    - ID 335 (BASE_SEED=123): 84.0 ± 0.012\n  No time (remove channel entirely):\n    - ID 336 (BASE_SEED=42): 83.5 ± 0.017\n  Late injection to single head:\n    - Policy-only (ID 338, BASE_SEED=42): 82.9 ± 0.017\n    - Value-only  (ID 339, BASE_SEED=42): 76.6 ± 0.047\n\n  In progress:\n    - Policy-only replications: ID 343 (BASE_SEED=7), ID 344 (BASE_SEED=123)\n\n  Conclusions:\n  - Best:\
    \ inject time late to BOTH heads (consistent 86.1–86.6 across seed sets).\n  - Early injection hurts (−1.9 to −4.2 vs late). Removing time also hurts (−3.1 vs late at seed 42).\n  - Single-head late injection underperforms: policy-only ≈ early; value-only strongly degraded.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Time-channel study — final interim summary (IDs and means±std)\n\n  Both-heads late (after pooling):\n  - 322 (seed 42): 86.6 ± 0.014\n  - 327 (seed 7):  86.1 ± 0.020\n  - 328 (seed 123): 86.6 ± 0.015\n\n  Early injection (into CNN+ConvLSTM):\n  - 331 (seed 42): 82.4 ± 0.015\n  - 332 (seed 7):  84.7 ± 0.020\n  - 335 (seed 123): 84.0 ± 0.012\n\n  No time:\n  - 336 (seed 42): 83.5 ± 0.017\n\n  Late to single head:\n  - Policy-only: 338 (seed 42): 82.9 ± 0.017; replications running — 343 (seed 7), 344 (seed 123)\n  - Value-only: 339 (seed 42): 76.6 ± 0.047\n\n  Recommendation:\n  - Inject time late (after spatial pooling) to BOTH\
    \ policy and value heads. Avoid early injection and single-head-only variants.\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - CSV updated at storage/zephyr/results/new_ablations_late_vs_early.csv\n  - Summary: storage/zephyr/results/summary.txt\n```"
thinking_content: '**Evaluating experimental design**


  I''m considering a small experiment related to "late time injection to policy and value" with different weighting. I have to be careful about avoiding specific heuristics, but I can use time channel transformation since it has general applications. The environment already provides a structure for time limits. We might want to replicate some results, especially for specific seeds we''ve worked with. Finally, it''s a good idea to draft the addendum to streamline our documentation process.**Assessing token management**


  I''m looking at the token budget, which is currently at 132k out of 270k. There''s a possibility of implementing "late injection to both heads," but that could add complexity and isn''t necessary since we have a clear conclusion already. We plan to update the CSV once the policy-only replications are done. As for token management, pruning earlier ticks might be beneficial, but since we''re at around 132k (49%), it’s not urgent. It’s worth scheduling pruning when we hit a 75% usage threshold. I could also update the Plot script to include new data when the time comes.**Exploring multi-agent considerations**


  In this multi-agent environment with unknown paths, it seems we already have the "results/plot_results.py" that was mentioned before, but writing new code might not be necessary now. It might be better to focus on archiving information, perhaps with a table and conclusion for capsule #10, while noting that policy-only replicates are still in progress. I’m thinking about proposing a further ablation, like injecting time after pooling, but with results indicating both heads being optimal, we may not need to test other options just yet.**Finalizing research updates**


  I''m thinking about implementing some simple computations for a minor improvement while staying disciplined in our research. We''ve concluded that the best method is both-heads late injection, which has achieved an 86.6 score. Now, I need to decide whether to incorporate this into our earlier SOTA architecture. We should finalize the addendum and write it to the archive, summarizing all tested conditions and conclusions. Additionally, I need to update the results CSV for specific lines and document the upcoming policy-only seed replications as well.**Updating public memory and archives**


  I want to share a high-level note in Public Memory about the effectiveness of time injection, stating that both-heads after pooling outperforms while value-only approaches can degrade performance. It could be useful to reply to our earlier capsule (#1) regarding time injection results, though that''s optional. I think a safer approach is to update the Archive and CSV first. We should also revise the summary file to incorporate results for IDs 338 and 339 and note ongoing replications. Planning to ensure all actions are concise and well-organized is key here!'
