parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Late dual-head time injection — Dilation=3 (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilation, convlstm, bottleneck, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Ablate spatial receptive field: switch dilation from 5 to 3 on the main CNN convs while keeping undilated bottlenecks, late dual-head time injection, and double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64). BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([3]),  # ablation: d=3\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Late dual-head time injection — Dilation=6 (std-width nodil, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"architecture, dilation, convlstm, bottleneck, policy gradient\"\nabstract: \"Upper-bound dilation ablation: set CNN main-conv dilation to 6 (vs 5 baseline),\
    \ with undilated bottlenecks, late dual-head time injection, and double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64). BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),  # ablation: d=6\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n\
    \          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 192 — Dilation ablation started on late dual-head SOTA\n  - Submitted d=3 and d=6 (BASE_SEED=42) with the best backbone (undilated bottlenecks, late time to both heads, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64)).\n  - Goal: bracket around d=5 to confirm optimum. If either matches 86.6, replicate across {7,123}; else keep d=5 as the recommended setting.\n  - All time-channel findings finalized and reproducible script stored at storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_sota_late_dual.py.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering experimental tests**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing some generalization tests or additional ablations. However, the current setup prohibits external resources, but I can work with code ablations. There’s mention of a test not yet submitted due to a run cap. While we currently have no running experiments, we could examine the effects of using a double-step with dilation at 3. \n\nSo, I’ll plan to submit the double-step synergy test with the necessary parameter adjustments. Let’s get started!**Clarifying experiment parameters**\n\nI'm noticing that the script named 'BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN' includes the parameter 'dilation,' which can be a bit confusing since it refers to D5. The earlier network file adjusted for 'd=5' is acceptable, and we can pass '3' instead. Rather than focusing solely on the D5 reference, I’ll keep that class name but also consider our architecture that uses late time injection. \n\nI’m thinking we should submit two experiments:\
  \ one with 'd=3' and base seed 42, and maybe another with 'd=4' as a further test. Let’s proceed!**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI’m considering producing a final figure, but since we don’t have any running experiments, we can submit two runs concurrently under our limit of two. I’m thinking about submitting \"Dilation=3\" using the SOTA architecture with BASE_SEED=42. \n\nThen we could also test \"Dilation=6\" since Krono II got 84.10 with that. So I'll go for submissions of d=3 and d=6 to explore adjustments. I'll make sure to set the hyperparameters accordingly, referencing our earlier network architecture. Let’s keep it organized!**Preparing submission details**\n\nI'm considering updating the CSV file to include new experiments once we have results, but for now, it's time to focus on the submission. I’ll prepare the YAML content and set BASE_SEED to 42, just like before. \n\nI also want to ensure we follow the submission guidelines, including adding a cooldown period if needed,\
  \ even though it seems we can submit concurrently. I’ll format the title properly and propose: \"Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (late dual-head) — Dilation=3 — BASE_SEED=42\". After getting results, we can plan to select the optimal dilation. Let's finalize the actions!**Setting up commands and submissions**\n\nI’m thinking we should keep our commands and commentary straightforward and permissible. My plan is to proceed with these actions:\n\n- First, I'll go to research.\n\n- Next, I'll submit the configuration with YAML for d=3.\n\n- After that, I’ll submit another configuration with YAML for d=6.\n\nI also want to go to private memory and provide a summary. I’ll reference the necessary lines of code, focusing on 'BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTime', tuning just the 'dilation' parameter to 3 and 6 while keeping everything else the same. Let’s finalize this!"
