role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/make_table.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import csv\n  from collections import OrderedDict\n\n  IN = \"storage/zephyr/results/new_ablations_late_vs_early.csv\"\n  OUT_MD = \"storage/zephyr/results/table_time_injection.md\"\n  OUT_TEX = \"storage/zephyr/results/table_time_injection.tex\"\n\n  rows = []\n  with open(IN, newline=\"\") as f:\n      reader = csv.DictReader(f)\n      for r in reader:\n          rows.append(r)\n\n  # Ordered display groups\n  order = [\n      (\"late_injection_std_nodil\", \"Late (both heads)\"),\n      (\"early_injection_std_nodil\", \"Early (CNN+ConvLSTM)\"),\n      (\"no_time_std_nodil\", \"No time\"),\n      (\"policy_only_late_time\", \"Late (policy-only)\"),\n      (\"value_only_late_time\", \"Late (value-only)\"),\n  ]\n\n  # Group by design then list by seed_set\n  grouped = OrderedDict((k, []) for k, _ in order)\n  for r in rows:\n      grouped[r[\"design\"]].append(r)\n\
    \n  # Sort each group by seed_set (42,7,123) when present\n  seed_order = {\"42\": 0, \"7\": 1, \"123\": 2}\n  for k in grouped:\n      grouped[k].sort(key=lambda r: seed_order.get(r[\"seed_set\"], 99))\n\n  def fmt_row(r):\n      return f\"{r['eval_id']} | {r['seed_set']} | {float(r['score_mean']):.3f} ± {float(r['score_std']):.3f}\"\n\n  # Markdown\n  lines = [\"# Time Injection Study (Std-width, no FE)\", \"\"]\n  for k, name in order:\n      if not grouped.get(k):\n          continue\n      lines.append(f\"## {name}\")\n      lines.append(\"Eval ID | Seed | Mean ± Std\")\n      lines.append(\"---|---|---\")\n      for r in grouped[k]:\n          lines.append(fmt_row(r))\n      lines.append(\"\")\n  with open(OUT_MD, \"w\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(lines))\n\n  # LaTeX\n  tex = [r\"\\begin{table}[t]\", r\"\\centering\", r\"\\small\", r\"\\begin{tabular}{lccc}\", r\"\\toprule\",\n         r\"Design & Seed 42 & Seed 7 & Seed 123 \\\\\",\n         r\"\\midrule\"]\n  def find(design,\
    \ seed):\n      for r in grouped.get(design, []):\n          if r[\"seed_set\"] == seed:\n              return f\"{float(r['score_mean']):.3f} $\\pm$ {float(r['score_std']):.3f} (ID {r['eval_id']})\"\n      return \"--\"\n\n  for k, name in order:\n      row = \" & \".join([name, find(k, \"42\"), find(k, \"7\"), find(k, \"123\")]) + r\" \\\\\"\n      tex.append(row)\n  tex += [r\"\\bottomrule\", r\"\\end{tabular}\", r\"\\caption{Ablation of time-channel injection. Std-width CNN (32/64), main-conv dilation=$d=5$ unless noted, undilated bottlenecks, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), AdamW+clip.}\", r\"\\end{table}\"]\n  with open(OUT_TEX, \"w\") as f:\n      f.write(\"\\n\".join(tex))\n\n  print(f\"Wrote {OUT_MD} and {OUT_TEX}\")\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/README.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Time Injection Study — Artifacts\n  Files:\n  - new_ablations_late_vs_early.csv — consolidated results (IDs, configs, mean±std)\n  - make_table.py — generates:\n      * table_time_injection.md\
    \ (Markdown)\n      * table_time_injection.tex (LaTeX)\n  - summary.txt — narrative summary\n\n  Usage:\n  - python storage/zephyr/results/make_table.py\n  Output will be written next to the script.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Added table generator for the time study\n  - Script: storage/zephyr/results/make_table.py\n  - Outputs: Markdown and LaTeX tables (table_time_injection.md/.tex) from new_ablations_late_vs_early.csv\n  This should make it straightforward to drop the finalized table into the addendum.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Considering model evaluation strategies**


  I’m thinking about doing a small ablation with an attention temperature of around 1.0 based on earlier work, but I want to stick to good practices and change only one variable at a time. I also want to evaluate step injection d=3 synergy from the earlier meta plan, and while we can analyze FLOPs or parameter counts with the test function, it won’t run heavy compute. I''ll store results to generate a figure and might also prune token usage, though we already pruned earlier to 60%.**Planning code reproducibility**


  I''m looking at how to capture code reproducibility for the ablations in submission scripts. The environment requires us to include /execute_action lines, and I’ll craft specific actions like going to research. I could write a script that aggregates results and generates a summary in a LaTeX table or CSV. I’ll store this with minimal tokens and ensure it produces a consistent README. Additionally, I’ll consider the next ablation with a different bottleneck ratio around 0.25, since earlier results didn’t improve on our sweeps.**Exploring time injection and scripting**


  I''m considering testing alternate gating for time injection in attention weighting calculations. This adds a new variable, so maybe I should pause. Since we''re focused on publication, I could create an Archive reply noting "Methods finalized; code path; table script path." I''ll also write a small summary for private notes. For now, I''ll implement my actions like writing the make_table.py script and updating the archive with a README. Instead of using pandas, I think using the CSV module would be safer for formatting.**Creating markdown and LaTeX tables**


  I''m planning to produce both markdown and LaTeX tables, which sounds like a solid approach. I''ll also write a README file that includes the necessary commands, making sure that I''m careful with triple backticks and YAML quoting to avoid any formatting issues. It’s important to get this right to ensure clarity and usability. Time to craft the content and proceed with the implementation!'
