- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/dilation_ablation.csv}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  eval_id,dilation,design,cnn_features,conv_lstm_features,bottleneck_ratio,entropy,lr,value_loss_coef,score_mean,score_std\n  322,5,late_dual_heads,32/64,64,0.25,0.01,4e-4,0.5,0.866,0.014\n  349,6,late_dual_heads,32/64,64,0.25,0.01,4e-4,0.5,0.859,0.023\n  348,3,late_dual_heads,32/64,64,0.25,0.01,4e-4,0.5,0.763,0.054\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/dilation_summary.txt}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Dilation Ablation — Std-width, no FE, late time to both heads, undilated bottlenecks, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), AdamW+clip\n\n  Results (mean ± std over 4 seeds per eval):\n  - d=5 (baseline): ID 322 — 86.6 ± 0.014\n  - d=6: ID 349 — 85.9 ± 0.023  (−0.7 vs d=5)\n  - d=3: ID 348 — 76.3 ± 0.054  (−10.3 vs d=5)\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - d=5 remains optimal under the fixed budget. Increasing to d=6 slightly degrades performance; reducing to d=3 sharply degrades\
    \ performance.\n  - Recommendation: keep main-conv dilation at 5 with undilated 3×3 bottlenecks.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Dilation ablation on the finalized backbone (std-width, undilated bottlenecks, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64), late time to BOTH heads):\n\n  - d=5 (baseline): ID 322 — 86.6 ± 0.014\n  - d=6: ID 349 — 85.9 ± 0.023 (−0.7 vs d=5)\n  - d=3: ID 348 — 76.3 ± 0.054 (−10.3 vs d=5)\n\n  Conclusion: main-conv dilation d=5 remains the recommended setting; d=6 is slightly worse and d=3 is strongly worse under the station’s budget.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - CSV: storage/zephyr/results/dilation_ablation.csv\n  - Text summary: storage/zephyr/results/dilation_summary.txt\n  - Repro script (best config): storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_sota_late_dual.py\n```"
