parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj_film.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n\
    \      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Undilated 3x3 inside bottleneck for locality/compute balance\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTimeFiLM(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Std-width CNN (32/64) with dilation d on main convs only; bottleneck 3x3s undilated.\n      Double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64). Single-head AttnPool.\n      Late time injection to BOTH heads using FiLM-style modulation (gamma,beta) on the 256-d head preact.\n      \"\"\"\
    \n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          # Split spatial vs time\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))  # (B,1)\n\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          # CNN backbone: dilation on main convs only\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    \
    \  kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=y.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(y.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM (shared cell)\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), y)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), y)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Single-head attention pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out) \
    \ # (B,H,W,1)\n          attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape(B, -1, h_out.shape[-1])          # (B, H*W, C)\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)         # (B, C)\n\n          # FiLM-style modulators (separate for policy/value), shape (B, 256)\n          def film(z, t, name_prefix):\n              z_lin = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=name_prefix+\"_in\")(z)\n              gamma = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=name_prefix+\"_gamma\")(t)\n              beta  = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform(), name=name_prefix+\"_beta\")(t)\n              z_mod = z_lin * (1.0 + gamma) + beta\n              z_mod = nn.relu(z_mod)\n              return z_mod\n\n          # Policy head\n          z_pol = film(z_spat, t, \"pol\")\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_pol); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n\
    \          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n\n          # Value head\n          z_val = film(z_spat, t, \"val\")\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_val); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTimeFiLM\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"FiLM-style late time modulation (both heads) — std-width nodil (BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"architecture, time, FiLM, bottleneck, dilation, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Replace concat-based late time injection with FiLM-style modulation (learned gamma/beta on 256-d preactivations) for both policy and value heads. Backbone unchanged (d=5 main convs, undilated bottlenecks, double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64)). BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n\
    \  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_d5_double_step_std_nodil_bottleneck_lateinj_film import BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTimeFiLM\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([5]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckD5DoubleStepStdNoDilBN_LateTimeFiLM(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n\
    \      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 196 — New idea: FiLM-style late time modulation\n  - Replications for d=6 are running (IDs 353, 354). Dilation ablation shows d=5 best; d=6 slightly worse; d=3 much worse.\n  - Submitted a clean single-variable change: replace late time concatenation with FiLM-style gamma/beta modulation on the 256-d preactivations for BOTH heads (BASE_SEED=42). Backbone stays identical.\n  - Rationale: time as a conditioner (scaling + shifting features) may guide action selection/value bootstrapping more effectively than concatenation while preserving spatial credit assignment.\n  - Next: if FiLM ≥ 86.6, replicate across {7,123} and update the addendum; otherwise record as a negative result.\n\
    ```"
