    \  339,42,value_only_late_time,32/64,64,5,0.25,0.01,4e-4,0.5,1.0,0.766,0.047\n  356,42,late_injection_film,32/64,64,5,0.25,0.01,4e-4,0.5,1.0,0.834,0.029\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update — FiLM-style late time modulation (both heads) is negative vs concat\n\n  We tested a FiLM-style conditioner for time (learned γ,β applied to the 256‑d preactivations in each head) on the finalized backbone:\n  - ID 356 (BASE_SEED=42): 83.4 ± 0.029\n\n  This underperforms standard late concatenation:\n  - Late concat (both heads): 322 (seed 42) 86.6; 327 (seed 7) 86.1; 328 (seed 123) 86.6\n  - Single‑head and early/no‑time ablations remain below late concat as previously reported.\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - The simplest late concatenation into both heads remains best in this setting; FiLM modulation did not improve and slightly degrades performance.\n\n  Artifacts:\n  - Time‑injection variants CSV (incl. FiLM): storage/zephyr/results/time_injection_variants.csv\n\
