- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/bottleneck_lateinj_temp.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Optional, Dict\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n          )\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n          g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          new_c = f * c + i * g\n          new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n          return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n  class BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      ratio: float = 0.25\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self,\
    \ x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class BottleneckLateTimeTemp(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Residual bottleneck CNN (32/64) with dilation on main 3x3 convs only,\n      undilated 3x3 inside bottlenecks; double-step LN-ConvLSTM(64).\n      Late time injection to BOTH heads via concatenation.\n      Temperature 'attn_temp' scales attention logits before softmax.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int\
    \ = 5\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n      attn_temp: float = 1.0\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          x_spat = x[..., :7]\n          t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2))  # (B,1)\n          B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n          # CNN backbone\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\n          y = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(y)\n\
    \n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=y.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(y.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM\n          cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          (h1, c1), _ = cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), y)\n          (h2, c2), h_out = cell((h1, c1), y)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n          # Attention pooling with temperature\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out)  # (B,H,W,1)\n          logits_flat = attn_logits.reshape(B, -1)\n          attn = nn.softmax(logits_flat / self.attn_temp, axis=-1)  # (B, H*W)\n          h_flat = h_out.reshape(B,\
    \ -1, h_out.shape[-1])\n          z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)  # (B, C)\n\n          # Late time concat to BOTH heads\n          z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)  # (B, C+1)\n          # Heads\n          z_pol = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z_pol = nn.relu(z_pol)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_pol); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n\n          z_val = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z_val = nn.relu(z_val)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z_val); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  __all__ = [\"BottleneckLateTimeTemp\"]\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Late dual-head\
    \ (concat) with attention temperature=0.95 — dilation=6 (std-width, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"architecture, attention, temperature, dilation, convlstm, bottleneck\"\nabstract: \"Test whether slight sharpening of attention (temp=0.95) helps the d=6 late dual-head model. Backbone unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_lateinj_temp import BottleneckLateTimeTemp\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([0.95]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n\
    \      return BottleneckLateTimeTemp(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Late dual-head (concat) with attention temperature=1.05 — dilation=6 (std-width, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"architecture, attention, temperature, dilation, convlstm, bottleneck\"\nabstract: \"Test whether slight smoothing of attention (temp=1.05) helps the d=6 late dual-head model. Backbone unchanged.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from ray import\
    \ tune\n  import optax\n  from networks.bottleneck_lateinj_temp import BottleneckLateTimeTemp\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]),\n          'attn_temp': tune.choice([1.05]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return BottleneckLateTimeTemp(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          attn_temp=hparams['attn_temp'],\n      )\n\
    \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```"
thinking_content: "**Updating on current actions**\n\nI need to update the user about the ongoing tasks regarding the current tick. There's no direct question, but I'm aware that our token usage is at 71%, which is something to keep in mind since we've pruned some ticks. The FiLM result isn't favorable, but we've updated artifacts and shared the latest updates. Looking ahead, we might plan for the next experiments, particularly focusing on double-step synergy with an interesting peak noted. I'll aim to ensure careful transitions in our protocols.**Reflecting on recent experiments**\n\nI’ve noticed that early injection inside the CNN/LSTM doesn’t seem effective, and adding time as a bias in LSTM gates via FiLM might not work well either. I’m considering normalization improvements, possibly exploring GroupNorm. Another thought is to include a residual connection within the double-step approach, something we tested before. However, managing our token usage is a priority since we’re already\
  \ at 71%. Given our cooldown period, it seems we can prune again at tick 204, so focusing on token management right now doesn't seem necessary.**Planning new experiments**\n\nI see that we can submit new experiments since there are no current ones running. The Running Experiments table is empty, which means we have concurrency available. We recently wrapped up the FiLM study, so it might be time to close the time injection study. For our next experiment, I'm considering a double-step with dilated CNN (d=3) to challenge the previous SOTA of 69.7, although our current scores are at 86+. To improve further, I could test d=6 with small attention temperature tuning, reflecting on our previous temperature sweeps.**Considering potential improvements**\n\nI’m thinking of exploring a two-step LN ConvLSTM with residual mixing of steps. However, previous tests with stop-grad variations and learned mixing didn't yield good results. I’m considering memory gating improvements, like applying dropout\
  \ on the gating mask to avoid overconfidence, but I’m hesitant. Since our token budget is nearly reached, it might be wise to halt new experiments and prepare a concise summary for the archive about the time study and dilation instead. We could submit a minimal test with d=6 and temperature adjustments, but it’s essential to keep our submissions efficient given recent evaluations.**Planning targeted replicates**\n\nI’m thinking about running two targeted replicates, testing d=6 with temperatures at 0.95 and 1.05. However, I realized we didn’t include the temperature variable in our code, so I need to add a parameter to adjust the attention logits before softmax. I can modify our network accordingly, keeping our stored networks in mind. My plan is to create a new module that takes the attention temperature parameter and implement the necessary modifications. \n\nGiven the current token limitations, I'll keep our modifications minimal and prepare to submit both tests concurrently."
