parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/sota_v2_core.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', dilation=self.dilation,\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x +\
    \ y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class LateDualHead_LNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict]\
    \ = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n\
    \          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # LN-gated ConvLSTM\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Late dual-head pooling (concat of AttnPool and GAP)\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)   # (B, C)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)                    # (B, C)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n          z = nn.Dense(256,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fixed micro-sweep-best config (ID 367): lr=4e-4, br=0.28, dilation=6\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return LateDualHead_LNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # Match ID 366/367 optimizer: AdamW + global grad clip\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Note on replicates 372/373: I initially packaged the core with Adam (no clip), while the micro-sweep winners (IDs 366/367) used AdamW + global grad clip(1.0). I have corrected the shared core (zephyr/submissions/sota_v2_core.py)\
    \ to match the winning optimizer. Once a slot frees, I will re-run BASE_SEED ∈ {7,123} with the corrected optimizer for clean, verifiable robustness numbers.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Preparing submission code**\n\nI'm noticing that the cooldown has advanced to 208 with 6 ticks left, which isn't particularly helpful. I think I should prepare the next submission code now, so we're ready to submit quickly when a slot opens. \n\nI see the system has changed our new architecture to a dual-head LN-ConvLSTM with a bottleneck ratio of .28. The focus now should be on replicating results across seeds for robustness, especially with previous runs using BASE_SEED=42. Let's consider testing different seed sets for further insights!**Preparing for submission**\n\nI see that we typically use seeds 42, 7, and 123. I’m thinking of preparing the code for \"double-step + dilated CNN (d=3),\" but it might be outdated for our current config. There's also a concurrency limit of 2, so I should wait a bit.\n\nIn the meantime, I can stage submission content in a storage file or set up a YAML to copy later. I feel like I should keep checking on running experiments while also\
  \ preparing an Archive update for \"SOTA v2 replicate results.\" I can write a script for \"sota_v2_submission.py\" and test it with BASE_SEED 42 once we’re ready!**Reviewing actions and experiments**\n\nI’m considering calling /execute_action{rank author} to display my submissions first, though calling /execute_action{preview 372,373} might not be necessary right now. When I try /execute_action{review 372}, it says the review is only for finished evaluations.\n\nI could propose next experiments, like ablation studies comparing grad clipping with Adam and AdamW, but micro-sweeps are already using AdamW with clipping. Interestingly, my earlier code for SOTA v2 just uses optax.adam without clipping. I need to check if the reviewed code aligns with this!**Addressing optimizer mismatches**\n\nI realize that in my \"sota_v2_core\" version, I used optax.adam instead of AdamW, which might degrade the effectiveness of replicates relative to the score of 86.6. I definitely need to ensure the replicates\
  \ use the same optimizer as the successful micro-sweep: AdamW with weight decay and clipping.\n\nThe scoreboard shows some inconsistencies with learning rates and performance. I can't modify the already submitted replicates 372 and 373, but I can prepare new corrected replicates for the next available slot!**Updating experiments and core file**\n\nI’m considering whether it’s better to cancel the running experiments, but there's no cancel command documented, so I'll have to wait and rerun them later. However, I can go ahead and update our \"core\" file now to fix the optimizer for future runs. I plan to modify \"zephyr/submissions/sota_v2_core.py\" to implement the AdamW chain.\n\nOnce a slot opens up, I’ll re-submit the replicates. In the meantime, I’ll create a note for Private Memory and reply in the archive about the optimizer mismatch. Let's get started on all these updates!"
