parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 209\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 76)\nPublished paper accepted (10/10). Pending runs: 129 (unshared+gate+FB), 130 (shared+mix-gate).\nPrepared next test (not yet submitted due to 2-run cap): double-step + dilated CNN (d=3), BASE_SEED=42.\nPlan:\n- When a slot frees, submit d=3 double-step synergy to challenge 69.7 SOTA without domain-specific features.\n- If unshared+gating stabilizes variance, replicate across seeds; else stick with shared double-step baseline.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 52,524 / 270,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 209 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Replicate (BASE_SEED=7): d=6 late dual-head (concat) LN-ConvLSTM,\
    \ br=0.28 (default PG)' (ID: 372) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 75.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.758, 0.737, 0.778, 0.757]\nMean: 0.758, Std: 0.015\nBest trial: 3 (0.778)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.280000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 372\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code so it runs without crashing. The evaluation has been running for over 3 minutes without errors, indicating successful network training.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code was importing neural network classes from `sota_v2_core.py` that contained a bug in the `BottleneckDilatedBlock` class. Specifically, the `nn.Conv` layer was using an invalid parameter name `dilation` when it should have been `kernel_dilation` for Flax's\
    \ Conv layer.\n\nThe error was:\n```\nTypeError: Conv.__init__() got an unexpected keyword argument 'dilation'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v3.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Fixed parameter name**: Changed `dilation=self.dilation` to `kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation)` in the `BottleneckDilatedBlock` class\n2. **Copied necessary classes**: Since the buggy classes were in the lineage files (read-only), I copied the complete neural network architecture (`BottleneckDilatedBlock`, `ConvLSTMCellLN`, `LateDualHead_LNConvLSTM`, and `create_network`) to the submission file\n3. **Selective imports**: Only imported the working functions (`_define_hyperparameters`, `create_optimizer`) from the original lineage code\n\nThe fix ensures that the dilated convolution uses the correct Flax API parameter format, allowing the network to initialize and train properly.\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashes and proceeds to the actual reinforcement\
    \ learning training phase, as evidenced by the evaluation running for over 3 minutes without errors.\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\nsys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n\n# Import only the working functions, not the buggy classes\nfrom sota_v2_core import _define_hyperparameters, create_optimizer\n\n# Fixed version of BottleneckDilatedBlock with correct parameter name\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n               \
    \     kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        # Fixed: Use kernel_dilation instead of dilation\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel over channels\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n \
    \       i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass LateDualHead_LNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int\n    cnn_features_2: int\n    conv_lstm_features: int\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN backbone\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\n                                   bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                   dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n\
    \        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\n                                   bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                   dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n        # Init/reset recurrent state\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # LN-gated ConvLSTM (single-step per env step, as per default training)\n        (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n        # Late dual-head pooling (concat of AttnPool and GAP)\n        H, W, C = h_out.shape[1], h_out.shape[2], h_out.shape[3]\n        # Attention pooling (single head)\n   \
    \     attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B, H*W))\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B, H*W, 1))\n        tokens = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, C))\n        attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)  # (B, C)\n        # Global average pooling\n        gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)  # (B, C)\n        # Concat and MLP trunk\n        z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        # Heads\n        pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n        val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n\
    \        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return LateDualHead_LNConvLSTM(\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n        conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n        dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n        bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n    )\n\nBASE_SEED = 7\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable\
