- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/double_step_time_core.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Correct Flax API: kernel_dilation is an (h, w) tuple\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class DoubleStepCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      def setup(self):\n          self.cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.features)\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          (h1, c1), _ = self.cell(carry, x)\n          (h2, c2), y2 = self.cell((h1, c1),\
    \ x)\n          return (h2, c2), y2\n\n  class LateDualHead_DoubleStep_LNConvLSTM(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.ds = DoubleStepCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # Late time scalar from channel 7 (steps/time feature)\n          t_map = x[..., 7:8] if x.shape[-1] >= 8 else jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, 1), dtype=x.dtype)\n          t_scalar = t_map.mean(axis=(1,2,3))  # (B,)\n\n          # CNN backbone with bottleneck-dilated blocks\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\n                                   \
    \  bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step ConvLSTM (shared params)\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = self.ds((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n \
    \         rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Late dual-head pooling (Attn ⊕ GAP) + late time concatenation\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)  # (B, C)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)                   # (B, C)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec, t_scalar[:, None]], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C+1)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n \
    \         val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return LateDualHead_DoubleStep_LNConvLSTM(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # AdamW + global grad clip, matching prior best configs\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BASE_SEED=42 — d=6 Double-Step\
    \ LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (exact match, AdamW+clip)\"\ntags: \"replicate, double-step, time-injection, dilated, bottleneck, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Direct comparison to no-time ablation (ID 384). Same config except we include late time injection. d=6, br=0.28, AdamW+clip, BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from double_step_time_core import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"BASE_SEED=42\
    \ — d=4 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (AdamW+clip)\"\ntags: \"ablation, dilation-4, double-step, time-injection, bottleneck, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Dilation sweep: test d=4 (vs d=3: ID 383=83.5 and d=6 expected ≈85–86) under matched Double-Step + late time inj. Fixed hparams; BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from double_step_time_core import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([4]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n```"
thinking_content: '**Analyzing time injection results**


  I''m considering whether late time injection will help replicate results with seed 42. Interestingly, an earlier test with ID 354 on seed 123 scored 88.0 with Dilation=6, suggesting variability in outcomes based on seeds or datasets. The title mentions "std-width nodil," which seems contradictory since it includes "Dilation=6." It''s tough to reconcile, but I''ll base my conclusions on careful empirical comparisons. I''ll monitor our current experiments and record the results for further manageable tests moving forward.**Planning next experiments**


  The Running Experiments table was empty earlier, but after submitting ablation 384, it''s still clear that no experiments are currently running. Previously, we submitted experiments 384 and 383, and both have finished. Moving forward, I can propose new experiments, including dilations with d=4, d=5, or d=7, or perform a micro-sweep on the bottleneck ratio with d=3. I also want to measure the effect of time injection across different seeds and configurations, like late time injection. However, I need to keep it simple and only run two experiments at a time.**Proposing new experiments**


  I''m suggesting two new experiments. First, let''s run a d=4 double-step with BASE_SEED=42 to check monotonicity. Second, I propose a d=6 double-step with late time injection, but we need to use corrected packaging for verification. Comparing this with previous runs at BASE_SEED=42 will help assess the impact of time injection versus no time injection, since we''ve previously noted 85.6 for no time. I’ll label it "d=6 Double-Step with late time inj (BASE_SEED=42)." We currently have no running experiments, so we can submit both!**Preparing code for experiments**


  I need to write code for our double-step with time injection. We previously had this in experiments 380 and 381, but to reuse it, I can either inline it or import from earlier storage. However, it seems we didn’t save the specific network module for double-step with time injection. We have d3_double_step.py available, and there’s also "sota_v2_core.py," but that’s for a single-step model. To ensure reproducibility, I should create ''zephyr/submissions/d6_double_step_time.py'' that includes the entire network. It''s essential to document results in the Private Memory or Archive as well.**Setting up new submissions**


  I’m estimating that seed 42 will give around 86, while the ''no time inj'' ablation scored 85.6. If ''with time inj'' also yields around 85.4, it might not make a significant difference. I propose running ''d=6 with time inj (BASE_SEED=42)'' and ''d=4 with time inj (BASE_SEED=42)'', using both slots. We’re at tick 215, and both past experiments have finished, so we’re ready to submit. Also, I need to ensure the code is correct and set the appropriate hyperparameters. Let’s craft that module code!'
