role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/double_step_notime_core.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          # Flax API: kernel_dilation is a (h, w) tuple\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class DoubleStepCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      def setup(self):\n          self.cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.features)\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          (h1, c1), _ = self.cell(carry, x)\n          (h2, c2), y2 = self.cell((h1, c1), x)\n          return (h2, c2), y2\n\n  class LateDualHead_DoubleStep_NoTime(nn.Module):\n\
    \      cnn_features_1: int\n      cnn_features_2: int\n      conv_lstm_features: int\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.ds = DoubleStepCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\n                     \
    \                bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step LN-ConvLSTM (shared params)\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = self.ds((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # Late dual-head pooling (Attn ⊕ GAP), no time concatenation\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights\
    \ = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          # Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return LateDualHead_DoubleStep_NoTime(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams.get('cnn_features_1', 32)),\n    \
    \      cnn_features_2=int(hparams.get('cnn_features_2', 64)),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams.get('conv_lstm_features', 64)),\n          dilation=int(hparams.get('dilation', 6)),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams.get('bottleneck_ratio', 0.28)),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  New results and interim conclusions (Tick 216):\n  - ID 383 — d=3 Double-Step + late dual-head + AdamW+clip (BASE_SEED=42): 83.5 ± 0.026. Smaller dilation underperforms vs. d=6.\n  - ID 384 — d=6 Double-Step NO time injection (BASE_SEED=42): 85.6 ± 0.019. This slightly exceeds our earlier time-injected fixed2 runs (IDs 380/381 ≈85.2–85.3), suggesting late time injection is neutral or mildly negative at seed 42 under this config.\n\
    \  - Running: ID 386 (d=6 Double-Step + late time inj., exact match), ID 387 (d=4 Double-Step + late time inj.). These will complete the clean d∈{4,6} comparison and re-check the time effect with exactly matched code.\n\n  Takeaways so far:\n  - Dilation: d=6 > d=4? (pending) > d=3 (83.5). The larger receptive field appears beneficial given 8×8 planning depth.\n  - Time: Removing late time inj. did not hurt and may slightly help on seed 42. We’ll A/B across seeds before recommending the default; code modules have been unified to avoid drift:\n      • storage/zephyr/submissions/double_step_time_core.py  (with time)\n      • storage/zephyr/submissions/double_step_notime_core.py (no time)\n\n  Next once slots free:\n  - A/B replicates at BASE_SEED ∈ {7, 123}: (time vs no-time) with d=6 Double-Step to quantify the time-injection delta robustly.\n  - If d=4 lands between 83.5 and 85.6, we’ll keep d=6 as default and document the sweep.\n\n  We’ll append IDs and stats as runs finish.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating time injection and experiments**\n\nI’m considering that time injection might not be effective or could have been implemented incorrectly before. Currently, I have 384, which specifically doesn't include time injection, scoring 85.6, and 386 and 387 are running with different parameters, but we have a cap on runs. \n\nFor this tick, I could document things in my notebook and think about follow-up experiments, like alternative time injection positions. I need to be mindful of my token usage too when previewing the archives.**Updating addendum with results**\n\nI should update the addendum with the latest experiment results: the d=3 double-step scored 83.5, and without time injection, the score is 85.6. It looks like time injection has a neutral or slightly negative impact when BASE_SEED=42, so I’m thinking we should keep it off for robust replicates. I’m considering different doping methods, like early injection and FiLM-style gating.\n\nHowever, previous tests\
  \ for late time modulation didn't prove beneficial. For now, I can schedule replicates with the \"no time injection d=6\" for seeds 7 and 123 once the current runs wrap up.**Considering code updates and future plans**\n\nI’m thinking about updating the core storage code to parameterize time injection, using a toggle flag. We already have the double_step_time_core.py for time injection and a separate ablation code without it. Creating a reusable module would help manage this better.\n\nWhile we can't change the running submissions now, it's something to keep in mind for future updates. After runs 386 and 387 are completed, I can schedule replicates to evaluate the time injection delta across various seed sets. Plus, I might want to do some token management to prune unused ticks later on.**Planning replicate submissions and code updates**\n\nSo, my next steps include documenting everything in Private Memory or the Archive. I want to prepare two replicate submission files: one for seed 7\
  \ without time injection and another with time injection. Currently, I can’t make submissions due to the run cap, but I can create a new module named double_step_core.py that includes a parameter for 'use_time.' \n\nI’ll define a core function, create_network, that accepts this parameter while embedding 'use_time' in hyperparameters. This setup should help keep everything consistent for future submissions.**Implementing core modules and updates**\n\nI’m planning to add the `_define_hyperparameters` function to include 'use_time' as a tune choice of 0 or 1. However, I may not want to modify the default training code's 'dilation' and 'bottleneck_ratio.'\n\nFor no time injection, I can create a new module called `double_step_core_notime.py` using the same structure as `double_step_time_core.py` but without time injection. I'll also write a note to the Archive summarizing the results of previous experiments. \n\nSince we can't submit new experiments due to the run cap, I'll prepare new submission\
  \ specs. My next steps involve writing the necessary code and managing token usage carefully."
