- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip)\"\ntags: \"replicate, double-step, no-time, dilated, bottleneck, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Robustness replicate without late time injection. d=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28, AdamW+clip; BASE_SEED=7. Direct A/B against time-injected runs (IDs 380≈85.3).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from double_step_notime_core import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio':\
    \ tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip)\"\ntags: \"replicate, double-step, no-time, dilated, bottleneck, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Robustness replicate without late time injection. d=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28, AdamW+clip; BASE_SEED=123. Direct A/B against time-injected run (ID 381≈85.2).\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  from double_step_notime_core import create_network, create_optimizer\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n      \
    \    'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Submitted A/B robustness (no-time) at d=6 Double-Step:\n  - BASE_SEED=7: \"Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip)\"\n  - BASE_SEED=123: \"Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip)\"\n  Comparison targets (time-injected): ID 380 (85.3), ID 381 (85.2).\n  If no-time ≥ time across seeds, we will set no-time as default and update the addendum with consolidated stats.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing research outcomes**\n\nI need to outline the next steps based on the current findings from Zephyr I's RL research on Sokoban. They've previously achieved state-of-the-art results around 86.6 to 88 with particular configurations. The latest trials show varying impacts of time injection: in some cases, it appears detrimental, particularly with seed 42. The d=6 configuration consistently performed best, but others weren’t as effective. I should summarize these insights and prepare for further testing based on these results.**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to plan the next experiments. Firstly, I’ll run replicates for no-time injection using BASE_SEED 7 and 123 to confirm earlier results. I've already prepared the necessary scripts: double_step_time_core.py and double_step_notime_core.py. New tests for seeds 7 and 123 can include both time and no-time variants. The previous runs yielded results of 85.2 and 85.3 for seeds 7 and 123, which had time injection. I\
  \ can set up two concurrent experiments to check if the no-time variants can exceed those scores.**Submitting new experiments**\n\nIt looks like the \"Running Experiments\" table doesn't show any active experiments right now, which is a bit strange since ticks 216 and 217 had results from 386 and 387. Since the evaluation is complete, I think I can go ahead and submit two new experiments. The submissions will focus on replicating no-time injection for BASE_SEED 7 and BASE_SEED 123, both with a d=6 double-step approach. I should save the code to reference double_step_notime_core and also consider including time injection comparisons for thoroughness.**Evaluating past results**\n\nI've noted the time injection results from experiments 380 and 381 yielding 85.3 and 85.2, as well as earlier seeds 366 and 367 at seed 42 giving results of 86.0 and 86.6. However, I wonder if those results are exact matches. Also, there were \"fixed2\" replicates that were double-step with LN-ConvLSTM, achieving\
  \ similar scores. So, it's important to focus now on running no-time replicates for seeds 7 and 123 and updating the Archive addendum with these findings. I'll also consider proposing a default to no-time injection, but running a d=3 variant isn't essential right now.**Preparing to submit experiments**\n\nI’m set to submit two replicates at the Research Counter using double_step_notime_core for BASE_SEED 7 and 123. First, I have to confirm that no experiments are currently running—tick 217 shows none, so it’s clear to proceed. I need to include the required YAML content and set up the parameters accordingly. Also, I can think about updating Private Memory but that’s optional. \n\nI should navigate to the Research Counter using the right command and ensure my titles are unique without unnecessary colons. Let's get this done!"
