thinking_content: '**Planning updates and constraints**


  I’m considering how to update the addendum once everything is finished. In the meantime, I might submit a micro-sweep for the learning rate, but need to note the time injection effect could overshadow results. However, we can only have two concurrent tasks running right now, and we already have two active. I can document everything in memory and update the archive later, while also preparing code storage for a new default config and versioning.**Organizing updates and archiving**


  I want to ensure the default response remains minimal, yet we have been outputting actions too. So, I''ll plan to reply with a summary and update the archive. I also need to log this in Private Memory. I should compare double_step_time_core with no-time; that’s already noted. I’ll summarize new results: For the d sweep, we have d=3 at 83.5, d=4 at 82.9, and d=6 time injection at 84.1 versus no-time at 85.6. I’ll plan for replicates across seeds, with updates to the addendum as needed.**Analyzing results and planning ahead**


  I’m considering the results and potential confusion here. The previous SOTA reached 86.6, but now the d=6 time injection on seed 42 gave only 84.1. The initial micro-sweep had results around 86.0-86.6. The discrepancy might stem from not using late dual-head or even code drift. While earlier replications gave fixed results of 85.3 and 85.2, seed 42 is lower. With no-time on seed 42, we managed 85.6, close to 86.6. Once runs finish, I’ll aim to combine means across sets for stronger insights, but proposing increased compute isn’t allowed. We may prepare for further operations later.**Organizing archives and planning**


  I can create an archive reply to maintain our lab records, which I think I’ve already done. I could log this in Private Memory, but it’s not essential. We might also consider pruning earlier ticks in Token Management, though our current token usage of 51% doesn’t make it necessary. I plan to prepare code for writing aggregated results, but that might not be urgent either. I’ll focus on updating Private Memory with a concise summary and next steps after results from 390/391, but keep it limited for now.**Updating archives and planning experiments**


  I realize the last tick already included an archive update, but I can still add one with a predicted plan. Alternatively, I could adjust rankings in Research to group our results, but I don’t think it’s necessary. I''ll focus on two actions: first, I’ll prepare an archive reply summarizing new results from IDs 386 and 387, highlighting the time injection effect and the plan to adopt no-time if confirmed. Next, I’ll note future experiments in Private Memory regarding early injection variants and gating, while keeping our focus on simplicity and value.'
