    \          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"LR sweep (4e-4 vs 5e-4): d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"learning-rate, double-step, no-time, dilated, bottleneck, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Micro-sweep learning_rate ∈ {4e-4, 5e-4} for the d=6 Double-Step without time injection under AdamW+clip to compare directly to the time-injected sweep.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from double_step_notime_core import create_network, create_optimizer\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4, 5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation':\
    \ tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 219—plan and status:\n  - Mixed time-injection effect across seeds: +1.5 on seed 42 (85.6 no-time vs 84.1 time), but −0.7 to −1.2 on seeds 7/123 (84.6/84.0 no-time vs 85.3/85.2 time). Net difference across 3 seeds is small (~0.13 in favor of time).\n  - Submitted optimizer micro-sweeps (lr ∈ {4e-4, 5e-4}) at d=6 for both variants (with and without time) at BASE_SEED=42 to check if 5e-4 recovers the gap for either side.\n  - If results remain within noise, we’ll keep d=6 + late time injection as default and document the small, seed-dependent deltas; otherwise, adopt no-time only if it wins consistently in A/B.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing time injection results**\n\nI need to respond with the next actions regarding our results in the Archive Room. For instance, the time injection removal showed no-time replicates on seeds 7 and 123 giving 84.6 and 84.0, while the base time-injected values were 85.3 and 85.2. Interestingly, on seed 42, no-time improved to 85.6 compared to 84.1 for time-injected. Overall, it seems time injection helps on seeds 7 and 123 but hurts on seed 42, indicating mixed results.**Proposing further analysis steps**\n\nI could run more replicates to estimate the significance of delta, but I already have evidence that suggests not changing the default settings and keeping late time injection. Alternatively, we could treat it as neutral with minimal effect, focusing on d=6 as the standard dilation since d=3 and d=4 underperform. We also have the option to do a minor hyperparameter check, micro-sweeping certain learning rates for optimal architecture on seed 42. Since both 390\
  \ and 391 finished, we can submit two micro sweeps and then plan an archive update. Additionally, pruning tokens could be considered, but it isn’t necessary just yet.**Planning token management**\n\nIt looks like Token Management is currently on cooldown, and we’ve previously pruned, which might affect things. I could summarize this in private memory for future pruning. I need to use the proper /execute_action commands, keeping commentary separate but succinct. My plan includes going to research and submitting two small experiments: first, a learning rate micro-sweep of 4e-4 vs. 5e-4 on d=6 Double-Step with late time injection; second, a weight decay ablation with AdamW+clip. I need to make sure our submission interface supports the required hyperparameters.**Working on hyperparameter submissions**\n\nThe training system currently passes hyperparameters to create_network but not to create_optimizer, which limits our ability to set weight_decay directly. The original create_optimizer only\
  \ accepts a learning_rate, which complicates things. I could potentially use a global variable or encode weight_decay within learning_rate, but that doesn’t feel ideal. Instead, I think I’ll proceed with a learning_rate micro-sweep. I’m planning to do a separate submission for lr 4e-4 vs. 5e-4 for both time and no-time variants, with two defined submissions ready to go.**Finalizing optimizer commands**\n\nThe create_optimizer uses the learning_rate parameter, which is great. I'm planning to implement an LR sweep for the d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time) using BASE_SEED=42 with double_step_notime_core. We might replicate across other seeds later. \n\nFirst, I’ll execute commands to go to research and then submit two actions with YAML blocks. I’ll summarize the effects of time injection across seeds in the Archive, indicating mixed outcomes but keeping the default at time injection since it shows slightly better results. After that, I’ll document everything clearly!"
