- text: "/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 220 — Consolidated A/B across seeds (d=6, Double-Step)\n\n  Time injection vs No-time (means):\n  - BASE_SEED=42: time 84.1 (ID 386) vs no-time 85.6 (ID 384) → no-time +1.5\n  - BASE_SEED=7:  time 85.3 (ID 380) vs no-time 84.6 (ID 390) → time +0.7\n  - BASE_SEED=123: time 85.2 (ID 381) vs no-time 84.0 (ID 391) → time +1.2\n\n  Aggregate over {42,7,123}:\n  - time: (84.1 + 85.3 + 85.2)/3 ≈ 84.87\n  - no-time: (85.6 + 84.6 + 84.0)/3 ≈ 84.73\n  - Δ (time – no-time) ≈ +0.13 in favor of time injection, with seed-dependent effects.\n\n  Dilation check at BASE_SEED=42 (with time):\n  - d=6: 84.1 (ID 386)\n  - d=4: 82.9 (ID 387)\n  - d=3: 83.5 (ID 383)\n  ⇒ d=6 > d=3 > d=4 under matched compute.\n\n  Pending:\n  - LR micro-sweeps at d=6 (BASE_SEED=42) for both variants (IDs 392 time, 393 no-time) to test whether 5e-4 shifts the A/B outcome.\n\n  Tentative stance:\n  - Keep d=6 as default.\n  - Time injection\
    \ remains the default pending LR results; current cross-seed average is marginally in its favor, but the effect is small and seed-dependent. Will finalize after 392/393 complete.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 220 — Notes and next steps\n\n  Results summary (d=6 Double-Step):\n  - Seed 42: no-time wins (85.6 vs 84.1 time).\n  - Seeds 7/123: time wins (85.3/85.2 vs 84.6/84.0).\n  - Cross-seed mean: time ≈ 84.87, no-time ≈ 84.73 (Δ ≈ +0.13).\n\n  Dilation sweep (seed 42, with time): d=6 (84.1) > d=3 (83.5) > d=4 (82.9).\n  Conclusion: stick with d=6 backbone.\n\n  Running:\n  - IDs 392 (time) and 393 (no-time): LR ∈ {4e-4, 5e-4} at seed 42.\n\n  Plan after 392/393:\n  1) If deltas remain small, standardize “time injected d=6 Double-Step” as default; document seed dependence.\n  2) Optional small WD sweep at seed 42: weight_decay ∈ {0, 1e-4} (AdamW) for time variant only.\n  3) Freeze default, update archive addendum with\
    \ the finalized table (IDs and means), and close out this line.\n  4) If we have slack, revisit head design (late dual-head vs simple MLP) under PG only (no algorithm changes), single-variable ablation.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering MLP head options**\n\nI'm thinking it might be useful to propose adding headless ablation to test the MLP head against late dual-head pooling. However, previous lineages suggest that a simple MLP head works synergistically with PPO, and we're currently using PG. We need to stay on our architecture track. I should consider actions like archiving replies to update with new results, computing aggregated results across seeds, and maybe submitting some additional ablation tests if there's available capacity.**Crafting next steps**\n\nI realize I can't add more, but I can prepare a script for a weight decay sweep in storage. I should use Private Memory to write a summary of the next steps, which is recommended. I can also take some conclusions and write them to a private memory capsule while pruning tokens if necessary, though we're not on Token Management status right now. \n\nCreating an update for results.csv could be useful but isn’t essential. My main actions\
  \ will be replying to archive #10 with computed results and discussing time injection findings.**Updating memory and planning tasks**\n\nI need to update my private memory with a concise summary and a task queue for the weight decay micro-sweep, focusing on one variable at a time, like weights. I'll plan to run the weight decay micro-sweep for both time and no-time at base seed 42 after the learning rate sweeps, but only if the time injection difference is small. \n\nI might update the results in the storage summary file—it’s optional. Since we’re capped at two runs, I can prepare a YAML content for weight decay but hold off on submission for now.**Finalizing tasks and computations**\n\nIt's time to finalize my actions. I’ll first go to the archive and reply to #10 with the updated stats and decisions. Then, I’ll go to the private memory and respond to #2 with concise notes, ensuring I quote YAML correctly since we're not creating a new capsule. \n\nNow, I need to compute aggregated values\
  \ for time injection across seeds, which shows a mean of around 84.87 and for no-time, approximately 84.73. This gives a delta of about +0.13 in favor of time injection, though it's not conclusive and could be within the noise across seeds.**Implementing evaluation actions**\n\nI'm noting that the standard deviations are around 0.02 on average, but with additional variability across seeds. Although the difference of 0.13 in means seems small, it could be significant, so I’ll phrase it as \"slight.\" The dilation results indicate that d=6 is the best option, achieving 84.1 with time injection at seed 42. \n\nAs a result, I’ll keep d=6 as the default with double-step and late time injection. Since both runs 392 and 393 are full, I won't submit new experiments. I’ll now go to the archive to reply with a summary and also update private memory with next steps."
