parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"WD ablation (wd=0) — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time, BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"ablation, weight-decay, double-step, no-time, dilated, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Test AdamW weight_decay=0.0 (vs 1e-4 default) for the d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM without time injection. Fixed best lr=4e-4 from ID 393. BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from double_step_notime_core import create_network as base_create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),  # best from ID 393\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation':\
    \ tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  # Use the same network as in the core (no-time variant)\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return base_create_network(hparams)\n\n  # WD=0.0 ablation\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"WD ablation (wd=0) — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (BASE_SEED=42)\"\ntags: \"ablation, weight-decay, double-step, time-injection, dilated, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Test AdamW weight_decay=0.0 (vs 1e-4 default) for the d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM with late time injection. Fix lr=5e-4 (best per ID 392). BASE_SEED=42.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from double_step_time_core import create_network as\
    \ base_create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]),  # best from ID 392\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return base_create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 5e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 221 — LR sweeps complete (BASE_SEED=42), launching WD ablations\n\n  Results:\n  - ID 392 (time, lr ∈ {4e-4,5e-4}):\
    \ 84.2 ± 0.019, best lr=5e-4.\n  - ID 393 (no-time, lr ∈ {4e-4,5e-4}): 85.6 ± 0.010, best lr=4e-4.\n\n  Interpretation:\n  - LR does not close the gap at seed 42; no-time remains +1.4 over time (85.6 vs 84.2).\n  - Cross-seed mean (42,7,123) still slightly favors time overall, but effect is small (~+0.13). The split likely reflects seed-dependent optimization dynamics.\n\n  Next:\n  - Submitted weight decay ablations at d=6 Double-Step (AdamW):\n    • WD=0.0 (no-time, lr=4e-4) — BASE_SEED=42\n    • WD=0.0 (time,   lr=5e-4) — BASE_SEED=42\n  - If WD=0 helps time-injected more than no-time, we may revert to time as default; else, recommend no-time for PG-only setting at seed 42 while noting cross-seed nuance.\n\n  Will report IDs and stats on completion and finalize the default accordingly.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Proposing a weight decay sweep**\n\nI'm considering running a weight decay sweep for both the no-time variant using seed 42, and the time variant as well. We have two slots, so scheduling both sweeps seems feasible. Each would need me to customize the `create_optimizer` to include a weight_decay parameter. Currently, it's fixed at 1e-4. I might need to override this with hyperparameters. However, `create_optimizer` only accepts learning_rate, leaving me pondering how to handle weight_decay effectively. I could either modify it or define a new version that accommodates my needs.**Exploring weight decay options**\n\nI’m examining the `create_optimizer` interface, which only accepts a learning rate without additional hyperparameters. I see that the default training code can't pass weight decay directly, but I could potentially work around this by customizing `_define_hyperparameters` to introduce weight_decay or by reading from an environment variable. However, since `create_optimizer`\
  \ doesn't accept weight decay, I’m exploring whether to define a new version referencing a constant. Alternatively, I could modify the training step or optimizer parameters, but changing weight decay might require copying the entire default training loop, which isn't ideal.**Examining weight decay adjustments**\n\nI'm looking at how the system changed weight decay using `create_optimizer`, which incorporated a weight_decay constant. However, for a sweep of weight decay values, we'd need to change the `create_optimizer` implementation across trials. The system samples hyperparameters, but I can choose weight_decay from `tune.choice` in `_define_hyperparameters` and then \"monkey patch\" a global variable used in `create_optimizer`. But since the training system only passes hyperparameters to `create_network` and `training_step`, this complicates things. It seems we can't easily implement weight decay sweeps.**Planning new submissions for weight decay**\n\nI've noticed that previous ablations\
  \ set a weight_decay constant inside `create_optimizer`, using only one value instead of sweeping. I can run two separate jobs by hardcoding weight decay values: one at 0 and the other at 1e-4. So the plan is to submit:\n\n- \"d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time) with AdamW weight_decay=0\" at BASE_SEED=42.\n- \"d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time with weight_decay=0\" at BASE_SEED=42.\n\nThe earlier experiment used 2e-4, but I want to test with 0 instead. With slots free now, let’s implement those new submissions, tweaking `create_optimizer` accordingly. I'll also document this in the archive.**Planning weight decay submissions**\n\nI’m considering exploring the \"simple MLP head\" versus \"late dual-head pooling\" approach under PG. The current scoreboard suggests synergy with a Simple MLP head, but I want to test alternatives for the no-time MLP head. Changing pooling might degrade performance, so I should focus on weight decay sweeps. \n\nI'll draft two submissions: one for no-time\
  \ with weight decay 0 using a learning rate of 4e-4, and another for the time variant, potentially using a learning rate of 5e-4. I also want to update the archive with our findings, summarizing results from different seeds accurately, and ensuring that YAML quoting is correct. Let's proceed with these actions!"
