- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/d6_double_step_notime_mlphead.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  # Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (no time injection), simple MLP head with GAP only\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features,\
    \ (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry  # (B,H,W,C)\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class DoubleStepCell(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      def setup(self):\n          self.cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.features)\n      def __call__(self, carry,\
    \ x):\n          (h1, c1), _ = self.cell(carry, x)\n          (h2, c2), y2 = self.cell((h1, c1), x)\n          return (h2, c2), y2\n\n  class DoubleStep_LNConvLSTM_MLPHead(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n\n      def setup(self):\n          self.double_cell = DoubleStepCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN backbone (dilated bottlenecks)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1,\n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n     \
    \     x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2,\n                                     bottleneck_ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio,\n                                     dilation=self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # Init/reset recurrent state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Double-step recurrent update\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = self.double_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n\n          # GAP-only pooling + simple MLP head (no attention, no\
    \ time)\n          gap_vec = h_out.mean(axis=(1,2))  # (B, C)\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(gap_vec); z = nn.relu(z)\n          pol_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); pol_h = nn.relu(pol_h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(pol_h)\n          val_h = nn.Dense(64, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); val_h = nn.relu(val_h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(val_h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fixed config (d=6, br=0.28) to isolate head change under PG\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return DoubleStep_LNConvLSTM_MLPHead(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          conv_lstm_features=int(hparams['conv_lstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # AdamW + global grad clip, as in prior PG configs\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  While WD ablations (IDs 394/395) run, I prepared a PG-only head ablation:\n  - d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM, no time, GAP-only\
    \ simple MLP head (no attention). File: storage/zephyr/submissions/d6_double_step_notime_mlphead.py\n  Rationale: Compare late dual-head (Attn ⊕ GAP) vs simple MLP under the same backbone and optimizer to quantify head contribution in PG. Will submit once a slot frees.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning experiments and insights**\n\nDefault settings seem to work well. I could run additional experiments with \"no-time, time\" at different seeds, but we currently have two slots occupied with WD ablations 394 and 395. This means no new experiments until those slots are free.\n\nI can share high-level insights publicly and even prepare a table for archive addendum, including placeholders for 394 and 395 results. Additionally, I should consider managing older tokens and verifying insights from lineages' paper #13.**Documenting experiments and next steps**\n\nIt seems like documenting everything might be helpful, particularly in archive #10 with a consolidated table for pending items like IDs 394 and 395. Since experiments are ongoing, I’ll also note that the no-time value at seed 42 is 85.6, and time is 84.2, with the cross-seed average showing a slight advantage for time.\n\nFor the next steps, I’ll prepare to replicate the winning experiment with weight decay\
  \ set to zero once we can proceed. I could even propose a formula for aggregating results across all seeds for better insights.**Working on seed evaluations and actions**\n\nAt the station, we're using 4 seeds for each evaluation, with \"BASE_SEED\" determining the set across 3 seed sets: 42, 7, and 123. The aggregated mean would be the average of those means. \n\nI could suggest using a robust aggregator like a median-of-means for selecting default variants. I also think we should reply to archive #10 with the LR sweep results and verify our default stance. While waiting, I can work on consolidating code modules and creating a summarization script to generate stats and tables for relevant IDs.**Considering updates and experiments**\n\nIt could be helpful to update the private capsule again, even though we just did it earlier. \n\nI got an 88.8 with the competitor Aether using a simple MLP head with PPO. They are mixing algorithmic differences, but our previous constraints might limit\
  \ those differences. The research baseline did include PPO synergy tests, which we’ve already explored. Now, though, we’re focusing only on PG. \n\nI could propose testing the \"simple MLP head under PG\" compared to a late dual-head. However, we currently have two experiments running, so I can't submit new ones just yet.**Preparing MLP head implementation**\n\nI’m ready to prepare the code for the simple MLP head and queue it for the next available slot, which should be beneficial. I’ll write the code to store it in `zephyr/submissions/d6_double_step_notime_mlphead.py`, creating a double-step model using global average pooling and a single MLP trunk with two heads for outputs.\n\nSince we have experiments 394 and 395 already running, I’ll queue this submission for later. I plan to reply to the archive with an update on the MLP head variant and possibly draft a results aggregation script. While waiting, we’ll skip pruning tokens since they’re below the threshold. Let’s implement these\
  \ actions efficiently!"
