thinking_content: '**Analyzing research findings**


  I need to respond with our actions based on recent evaluation results. We’ve found that the GAP-only MLP head got a significantly lower score (66.0) compared to the standard Attn⊕GAP head (85.6), indicating that attention pooling is crucial. I should log these findings and consider stopping further exploration of the GAP-only head. Once I have results from the time-injected head, I can decide on the next steps, like testing a lighter attention head variant.**Reviewing token management**


  I’m considering whether to submit the d=3 synergy that was planned earlier. We already ran d=3 Double-Step (ID 383) and found it was less effective than d=6. Since we’ve completed that task, I should evaluate our current token usage, which is at 70% of 270k. While the recommendations suggested pruning at 75%, I think it’s okay at 70%. Maybe I could compress preemptively, but it doesn’t seem necessary right now.**Planning next actions**


  I’m considering updating Archive (#10) with the head ablation results and might stop the GAP-only test. I want to finalize the recommended default, which looks like d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM with Attn⊕GAP pooling. There’s some uncertainty around time injection, but it seems to provide a slight net advantage across seeds. For our focus on PG-only and algorithm restrictions, I may maintain time injection as the default because of its previous cross-seed advantages and synergy with PPO. I''ll also submit the companion time head results once they''re available.**Determining next steps**


  I need to report that attention pooling is crucial since the MLP-only head drops to about 66%, which is significant. For the next experiments, I’m considering some “cheap” improvements like comparing group norm vs. layer norm gating, as it was tested before. It might be helpful to finalize our defaults and prepare a concise addendum. I could also run a GAP-only MLP with a larger capacity head to test if it can recover. However, I suspect that increasing capacity won’t resolve the issue since attention pooling focuses on relevant features. Adding “spatial min pooling” with GAP could be a thought, but I should keep things simple.**Planning token management actions**


  I’m thinking about pruning tokens since we''re at 70%. It might make sense to create a private summary and prune some older ticks, but there’s a cooldown on that since our last prune was at tick 207. My plan includes issuing /execute_action commands only, keeping commentary minimal. I’ll update Archive #10 with the head ablation results, concluding that Attn⊕GAP is critical, and I might log to Private Memory for notes. I’m not initiating new experiments now but will conclude the current findings and ensure any special characters in my YAML quotes are handled properly.'
