    \          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return base_create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG)\"\ntags: \"replicate, no-time, weight-decay-0, double-step, convlstm, dilated\"\nabstract: \"Cross-seed robustness: no-time variant with AdamW weight_decay=0.0 (lr=4e-4) on d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM. Matches ID 394 settings; BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from double_step_notime_core import create_network as base_create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return base_create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Head ablations complete:\n  - ID 397 (no-time, GAP-only MLP): 66.0 ± 0.052 vs Attn⊕GAP ≈ 85.6 → attention pooling is essential.\n  - ID 399 (time, GAP-only MLP): 71.8 ± 0.028 vs Attn⊕GAP ≈ 84.2 → same conclusion.\n\n  WD effects at BASE_SEED=42:\n  - No-time:\
    \ wd=0.0 (ID 394) 85.7 vs wd=1e-4 (ID 393) 85.6 → small +.\n  - Time:   wd=0.0 (ID 395) 84.9 vs wd=1e-4 (ID 392) 84.2 → moderate +.\n\n  Running now to complete cross-seed robustness:\n  - Replicates (no-time, wd=0.0, lr=4e-4) at BASE_SEED ∈ {7, 123} — IDs pending.\n\n  Tentative defaults (PG setting, subject to final cross-seed):\n  - Backbone: d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (64 ch), bottleneck CNN (br=0.28).\n  - Head: Attn⊕GAP (keep attention).\n  - Time: seed-dependent; both time and no-time viable. At seed 42, no-time stronger; across seeds 7/123, time slightly ahead. We will report consolidated stats across wd=0.0 once replicates finish.\n  - Optimizer: AdamW + clip(1.0); wd=0.0 appears preferable for both time/no-time (pending cross-seed confirmation). lr ≈ 4e-4 (no-time) and 5e-4 (time) at seed 42.\n\n  Next:\n  - If wd=0.0 lifts no-time at seeds 7/123 into parity, recommend wd=0.0 default and allow time/no-time as minor variant. Otherwise, prefer time+wd=0.0 as the cross-seed default,\
    \ noting seed-42 exception.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 226 — Consolidated decisions and token management note\n\n  Conclusions to date:\n  - Attn⊕GAP head is critical (−19 to −20 points when removed).\n  - d=6 > d=3 > d=4 under Double-Step (seed 42).\n  - Time vs No-time: small, seed-dependent deltas; wd=0.0 improves both; no-time wins seed 42, time slightly ahead on 7/123 (wd=1e-4 baseline). Running wd=0.0 replicates at 7/123 to finalize.\n  - Likely default (PG): d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (64), bottleneck ratio 0.28, Attn⊕GAP head, AdamW+clip; wd=0.0; lr ≈ 4e-4 (no-time) or 5e-4 (time).\n\n  Action items:\n  - Await IDs for wd=0.0 replicates at seeds 7/123 (no-time).\n  - If consistent, finalize addendum with a clean table and recommendations.\n  - Next ablation only if needed: time+wd=0.0 at seeds 7/123; otherwise, close loop.\n\n  Token note: approaching 75%. After posting final summary and table, plan to\
    \ prune recent verbose ticks while preserving addendum and this summary.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}"
thinking_content: "**Managing tokens and summaries**\n\nI realize that we haven't tested wd=0 for no-time versus time cross-seed yet, and we've only used base seed 42. I think we can finalize our approach with some nuances and plan improvements. We should continue our experiments for now, but with about 73% of tokens used, it's smart to manage them carefully. I'll create a summary in private memory and prune older ticks, ensuring we optimize our token usage efficiently before proceeding.**Pruning token usage**\n\nI need to provide prune ranges to lessen token usage, focusing on older ticks that aren’t critical, like those between 0-50 — though the instructions suggest not to prune early codex readings. Pruning mid to high-volume logs could be beneficial. I’ll check the Token Management Room for response lengths and prune accordingly. It’d be good to update the archive with head ablation results, and I also want to consider stopping heavy ablations in favor of documentation and possibly finalizing\
  \ a new paper.**Planning experiments**\n\nI see that there aren't any experiments running right now, just the completion of experiment 399. I can propose additional runs, particularly cross-seed replicates for wd=0, both for time and no-time conditions since tokens are above 70%, but still manageable. I’ll suggest running two experiments simultaneously since there’s a limit of two concurrent runs. I could go with no-time wd=0 seed 7 and time wd=0 seed 7 for the first tests. Let's refine this setup and start executing!**Setting up replicates**\n\nI’m deciding to start with no-time wd=0 replicates at seeds 7 and 123. First, I’ll create submissions that import double_step_notime_core and override the optimizer settings to wd=0, lr=4e-4, adjusting the BASE_SEED like in experiment 394. Once those finish, I’ll move on to the time wd=0 replicates. \n\nFrom the evidence, I’ve noted the importance of having a strong Attention⊕GAP head and the best dilation at d=6. Now, I’ll implement my actions,\
  \ including submitting the replicates and updating the archive.**Managing tokens and pruning**\n\nI need to go to token management first to identify the heavy ticks. The room should show a table that helps in deciding which ranges to prune. I need to be cautious not to degrade important information, especially regarding old ablation details. We might have an opportunity to prune ticks 206-220, but I must remember that those include significant results. \n\nWith tokens at 73%, I’ll follow the recommended cycle and create a summary before pruned logs. Then I'll implement the necessary changes. Let's get started!"
