parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG, lr=4e-4)\"\ntags: \"replicate, time-injection, weight-decay-0, double-step, convlstm, dilated\"\nabstract: \"Cross-seed robustness for time-injected variant with AdamW weight_decay=0.0 at fixed lr=4e-4 to isolate WD effect vs prior wd=1e-4 results. BASE_SEED=7.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from double_step_time_core import create_network as base_create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),  # match prior time-injected replicates (IDs 380/381)\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features':\
    \ tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return base_create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG, lr=4e-4)\"\ntags: \"replicate, time-injection, weight-decay-0, double-step, convlstm, dilated\"\nabstract: \"Cross-seed robustness for time-injected variant with AdamW weight_decay=0.0 at fixed lr=4e-4 to isolate WD effect vs prior wd=1e-4 results. BASE_SEED=123.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr/submissions')\n  from ray import tune\n  import optax\n  from double_step_time_core import create_network as base_create_network\n\n  BASE_SEED\
    \ = 123\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),  # match prior time-injected replicates (IDs 380/381)\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return base_create_network(hparams)\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=0.0),\n      )\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update — wd=0.0 no-time replicates done; launching time+wd=0.0 for fairness\n\n  Completed:\n  - ID 401 (no-time, wd=0.0,\
    \ BASE_SEED=7): 83.3 ± 0.017\n  - ID 402 (no-time, wd=0.0, BASE_SEED=123): 86.1 ± 0.013\n  - Prior seed 42 (no-time, wd=0.0): ID 394 → 85.7\n\n  Aggregated (no-time, wd=0.0 over seeds 42/7/123): mean ≈ 85.0\n\n  For time-injected:\n  - Seed 42: wd=0.0 → ID 395: 84.9; wd=1e-4 → ID 392: 84.2\n  - Seeds 7/123: wd=1e-4 → IDs 380/381: 85.3 / 85.2\n\n  Next (now submitted):\n  - Time-injected, wd=0.0, lr=4e-4 at BASE_SEED ∈ {7, 123} to isolate WD effect cleanly against IDs 380/381.\n\n  Plan:\n  - If time+wd=0.0 lifts both 7/123 above wd=1e-4 baselines, we’ll recommend AdamW wd=0.0 as default; then finalize a consolidated table across seeds for both time/no-time and close this addendum.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating experiment replicates**\n\nI’m looking at earlier replicates 380 and 381, which used a learning rate of 4e-4 and scored around 85.25. To assess the impact of weight decay (wd=0), I plan to keep the learning rate constant. I'll submit new replicates for seeds 7 and 123, maintaining that learning rate. Earlier, the best time was 5e-4, but for clarity with the past replicates, 4e-4 is more suitable. It seems no experiments are currently running, so I can proceed with submitting the new ones. Additionally, I should update the archive with wd0 results.**Planning experiment submissions**\n\nI see that token management indicates \"Pruning Actions Available,\" but since we just pruned and are on a cooldown, I can't prune again for now. After recent results, we’re at 32% tokens. My next steps should be: \n\nFirst, I'll submit two experiments focused on a time-injected architecture with weight_decay set to 0.0 at seeds 7 and 123. I need to import from double_step_time_core\
  \ to create the network and set _define_hyperparameters at a fixed learning rate of 4e-4, matching previous baselines. Next, I’ll update the Archive following submissions, confirming the double_step_time_core module is available for use.**Calculating averages across seeds**\n\nI’m thinking about computing the aggregated cross-seed mean for the no-time weight decay (wd=0) across seeds 42, 7, and 123. The scores are 85.7, 83.3, and 86.1, which gives a mean of 85.03 when calculated precisely. For the time+wd=1e-4 condition, I have scores of 84.2, 85.3, and 85.2, averaging 84.9. Currently, the average for no-time wd0 is 85.0, while the time conditions are at 84.9. If the time wd0 replicates yield around a score of 85.4, we might see a tie or improvement later.**Reviewing ablation IDs and YAML formatting**\n\nI need to consider head ablation ID 399, which shows a time/gap score of only 71.8. Earlier, I referenced ID 397 with a no-time gap score of 66.0, but it didn’t appear in the System Messages.\
  \ I think it's essential to mention IDs that actually exist, and even though 397 is likely created earlier, the output didn’t list it due to score sorting. Also, when crafting YAML, I must ensure correct quoting for entries with colons, whereas titles should include parentheses. It'll help to follow formatting standards properly!**Preparing to submit research actions**\n\nI need to ensure that the title includes a colon correctly, like in \"BASE_SEED=7 — d=6.\" However, there's no colon in the quoted part: \"Replicate (time, wd=0).\" It’s essential to quote any single-line YAML value if it contains a colon. Since the title itself doesn’t have a colon and includes a dash, it should be safe. I'll craft the two submissions, and for the YAML, I plan to include a title indicating the parameters accurately. After executing the necessary actions, I’ll report IDs 401 and 402 results and provide mean computations across seeds for wd0. Then, I’ll outline the plan for running time+wd0 replicates\
  \ for fairness!"
