thinking_content: "**Calculating weighted mean and learning rates**\n\nI’m calculating the weighted mean across seeds, which comes out to be approximately 85.0, consistent with earlier findings. Currently, I'm waiting for specific replicates to finish. There’s a thought about using a learning rate of 5e-4 for time variance since it performed well before. But, there’s some confusion regarding which learning rates were used in previous experiments, especially with conflicting results from different replicates. I need to clarify those details before proceeding!**Comparing learning rates and preparing updates**\n\nI’m comparing the results of time+wd=0 at 4e-4 with previous wd=1e-4, which seems promising. I’m also considering preparing a consolidated table in Private Memory or Archive once those results come in. We might write code for the results table, but I’m thinking it’s not strictly necessary right now. I can update the meta prompt to reflect my current plan, summarizing tasks and keeping\
  \ track of pruning tokens, which are currently at 35%. That’s manageable for now!**Organizing YAML and planning experiments**\n\nI need to ensure I’m using YAML appropriately and avoiding any special formatting. I’m considering running the d=3 experiments, but since d=6 performed better with scores around 85-86, I might not pursue d=3. I could also create code modules to unify \"double_step_time_core\" and \"double_step_notime_core\" for consistency, although they may already exist. For now, it seems we might just prepare a final reply in the Archive, but there aren’t any new results to add, so I could go to the Token Management Room to prune ticks!**Updating the meta prompt and token management**\n\nI’m planning to update the meta prompt to capture our nearly finished plan about finalizing the default settings for time injection versus no time based on specific replicates. I’ll keep token usage low by minimizing commentary and actions. I aim to set the meta prompt with instructions summarizing\
  \ what to await regarding results 407/408 while considering pruning earlier ticks later since we're currently at 35%. Optionally, I might prepare a note in Private Memory for the final table structure if needed!**Updating meta prompt and tracking experiments**\n\nI need to keep things concise. My plan is to issue the meta update and send a brief archive reply tracking the status of experiments 407 and 408, noting that they’re running and we won't queue more runs until results are in. Since we're already at the 2-run cap, I’ll prepare the meta update without adding anything else. \n\nI’ll summarize steps regarding the results and specify not to run new experiments until the current runs are complete. That should do it!"
