- text: "/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Final consolidation (PG-only, non-FE) — time vs no-time × weight decay across seeds 42/7/123\n\n  Per-seed results (mean solve rate; higher is better):\n  Seed 42\n  - Time, wd=1e-4: ID 392 → 84.2 (best lr=5e-4)\n  - Time, wd=0.0:  ID 395 → 84.9\n  - No-time, wd=1e-4: ID 393 → 85.6 (best lr=4e-4)\n  - No-time, wd=0.0:  ID 394 → 85.7\n\n  Seed 7\n  - Time, wd=1e-4: ID 380 → 85.3\n  - Time, wd=0.0:  ID 407 → 85.2\n  - No-time, wd=1e-4: ID 390 → 84.6\n  - No-time, wd=0.0:  ID 401 → 83.3\n\n  Seed 123\n  - Time, wd=1e-4: ID 381 → 85.2\n  - Time, wd=0.0:  ID 408 → 83.7\n  - No-time, wd=1e-4: ID 391 → 84.0\n  - No-time, wd=0.0:  ID 402 → 86.1\n\n  Cross-seed means (42/7/123):\n  - Time, wd=1e-4: ~84.9\n  - Time, wd=0.0:  ~84.6\n  - No-time, wd=1e-4: ~84.7\n  - No-time, wd=0.0:  ~85.0\n\n  Head ablation (confirming importance of attention pooling):\n  - No-time, GAP-only MLP: ID 397 → 66.0 ± 0.052\n  - Time,    GAP-only MLP: ID 399 → 71.8\
    \ ± 0.028\n  - Conclusion: Attn⊕GAP is essential (~+14–20 points).\n\n  Dilation summary (seed 42):\n  - d=6 Double-Step best-in-class; d=3 underperforms (ID 383 → 83.5), d=4 lower (ID 387 → 82.9).\n\n  Recommendation (PG default recipe):\n  - Backbone: Bottleneck-dilated CNN (32/64) with d=6, bottleneck_ratio=0.28.\n  - Recurrent core: Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (64 ch).\n  - Head: Attn⊕GAP.\n  - Optimizer: AdamW + clip_by_global_norm(1.0).\n  - Weight decay: 0.0 (wd=0.0) — slight cross-seed edge overall; note variance.\n  - Learning rate: 4e-4 for no-time; if using time injection at seed 42, 5e-4 was best (ID 392); at seeds 7/123, 4e-4 was used in our references.\n  - Time input: Small, seed-dependent effect. No-time + wd=0.0 has the highest tri-seed mean (~85.0) but with higher variance; time + wd=1e-4 is nearly tied (~84.9) and slightly more stable across 7/123. In practice, run both toggles if budget permits; otherwise default to no-time + wd=0.0 and fall back to time + wd=1e-4 if\
    \ early learning curves stagnate.\n\n  This concludes the addendum’s verification. All numbers above include evaluation IDs for reproducibility.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Calculating aggregated means**


  I’m looking at the scores for different seed IDs based on learning rates and weight decay settings. For example, seed 42 with a learning rate of 5e-4 scored 84.2, but adding weight decay improved it to 84.9. Conversely, seed 7 didn’t see an improvement and was down slightly from 85.3 to 85.2 without weight decay. Seed 123 showed a drop from 85.2 to 83.7 with the same settings as well. Overall, the results vary and show inconsistency across seeds.**Analyzing no-time variants**


  I’m diving into scores for no-time variants across different seeds. Seed 42 with no weight decay scored 85.7, which is a slight improvement. However, seed 7 dropped from 84.6 to 83.3 without weight decay, showing a decline of 1.3. Seed 123 improved significantly, rising from 84.0 to 86.1. So, it seems that no weight decay is beneficial for seed 123, slightly helps seed 42, but hurts seed 7. When averaging the results, the cross-seed mean remains around 85.03.**Evaluating seed performance**


  I’m comparing the means across seeds and it looks like the best performance is time with weight decay at 1e-4 averaging 84.9, while no-time with weight decay at 0 is slightly better at 85.03. However, varying learning rates complicate things. The best learning rate for seed 42 was 5e-4, while seeds 7 and 123 used 4e-4. I didn’t test 5e-4 for those. It''s tricky to recommend defaults since using no-time with weight decay at 0 might lead to a drop in score for seed 7.**Finalizing recommendations**


  I’m working on finalizing the addendum and creating a consolidated table. The goal is to show that both time and no-time approaches are viable, with no-time being slightly better at seeds 42 and 123 when weight decay is 0, but not for seed 7. My robust default recommendation is to use time-injected with weight decay at 1e-4 and learning rate of 4e-4 since the averages are close: 84.9 for time with weight decay compared to 85.0 for no-time. Next, I need to update Archive #10 with this table and conclusion.**Crafting response for Archive #10**


  I’m preparing to reply to Archive #10 with a concise summary and evaluation IDs. I plan to present a compact table format to keep things tidy. The key points include that using no-time with weight decay set to 0 is slightly better across certain seeds while time with weight decay at 1e-4 yields a comparable mean. I’ll provide a default recommendation preference for no-time due to simplicity and a less variable outcome. After that, I’ll update private memory and the meta to reflect our next steps.**Deciding on base seed and actions**


  I’m realizing that there''s no need to fix the base seed in the final recipe, so I can move forward without that. I’m also considering updating Private Memory, but that’s optional. It seems like streamlining our actions is a priority right now, so I’ll focus on producing the necessary steps instead of getting bogged down by extra updates. Let’s keep things efficient and concise as I move ahead!'
