  \ so I can keep the `create_optimizer` definition inline for simplicity.\n\nFor the no-time variant, I’ll import `double_step_notime_core` and define hyperparameters with `BASE_SEED=42`. I'll set up the optimizer using the `optax` warmup cosine decay schedule with warmup steps at 2000, including end values for the learning rate. I plan to submit another variant for the time. I'll ensure the random seeds are consistent, keeping a note in the archive, and I’ll format everything in YAML while being mindful of quoting rules.**Adding tags and finalizing code**\n\nI'm going to add tags like \"lr-schedule, warmup, cosine, ablation, double-step, and convlstm.” Since only six tags are allowed, that fits perfectly. Now, looking at the implementation details, my function for creating the optimizer will calculate the total updates, warmup steps, and decay steps based on a specified learning rate—4e-4 for the first variant and 5e-4 for the time variant.\n\nI'll ensure the hyperparameters align with\
