thinking_content: '**Updating on archive status**


  We need to stay aware of the current situation in the Archive Room. We received results from the cosine LR schedule ablation for both time and no-time, and they severely degraded performance. We also submitted warmup-only for both variants and posted them to Archive #10, but now submissions are queued with no new results yet. Since we’ve reached our 2-run cap, there’s nothing more to submit. I''ll just note the negative results and expectations, but it seems I don''t need to prune tokens right now.**Planning next actions**


  I could head to the Research Counter to unfilter the scoreboard and check the status, but perhaps that’s not necessary right now. Alternatively, I could jot down my plan in Private Memory while I wait, though it might be superfluous. The environment expects me to issue commands, so I could write a brief note about expected outcomes for the warmup-only experiments. I''ll summarize that decays harm compute-limited training, but since I''ve already posted, I might focus on next steps based on the results from 417 and 418.**Deciding on next steps**


  The meta indicates we''ve completed the low-cost exploration phase. We might consider methods like "entropy annealing" or "value coefficient schedule," but I want to avoid introducing new variables and stick with a constant LR. Since we already have two runs, I should log a short note in Private Memory and hold off for now. I should also ensure we don’t submit anything new. The environment seems to expect some action, but maybe doing nothing is okay for now while we wait for warmup-only results.**Choosing a response strategy**


  I feel the need to produce some sort of response, even if we''re just stating that we''ll wait for results. The interface doesn’t demand actions, but typically, agents use commands. To keep things moving, I might reply to Private Memory for consistency. I could also store utility code for future use, but that’s not urgent. I’ll reply to Archive #10 about the warmup-only status and emphasize why decays hurt performance, even though we’ve covered that before. Checking the scoreboard seems unnecessary since it’s already sorted by score.**Drafting Archive reply**


  I’m going to create a minimal response to Archive #10, mentioning that we''ll wait for the warmup-only results. If they don’t improve, we’ll finalize the constant LR and include the negative results in a table. The tokens are at 45%, so I might skip pruning for now. I won''t create a new meta, just a single reply action. Reviewing IDs 414 and 415 doesn’t seem necessary since we already have their logs in System Messages. Let''s keep it concise and finalize the Archive reply.'
