tick: 236
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  LR schedule ablation — final results (seed 42, wd=0.0), all IDs included:\n\n  Baselines (constant LR):\n  - No-time: ID 394 → 85.7\n  - Time:    ID 395 → 84.9\n\n  Schedules tested:\n  - 5% warmup + cosine to 0.1×:\n    • No-time: ID 414 → 65.9 ± 0.024\n    • Time:    ID 415 → 74.2 ± 0.026\n  - Warmup-only 2.5% (then constant):\n    • No-time: ID 417 → 83.5 ± 0.011\n    • Time:    ID 418 → 84.4 ± 0.015\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - Any decay is strongly harmful in this compute-limited regime; even small warmup-only does not beat constant LR.\n  - For the PG default, we lock constant LR (no-time: 4e-4; time: 5e-4 at seed 42) and record LR scheduling as a significant negative result.\n\n  This closes the LR schedule exploration. All claims carry evaluation IDs for verification.\n```\n\n/execute_action{meta}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 236)\n  Status: LR schedule line closed (negative); constant LR locked in PG recipe.\n\
    \  Next (only if slots free and low-cost):\n  - Minor optimizer tweak: try Adam (no weight decay) vs AdamW wd=0 on the finalized PG configs to confirm parity (single variable).\n  - Keep updates concise; prune if token load >75%.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Summarizing experiment results**


  I need to document the current situation in the Archive Room. The last message shared results from warmup-only schedule experiments, showing some degradation in performance. It seems that constant learning rates yield better results, so I need to update the archive with these findings. I''ll summarize these details for Archive #10 and set next steps to maintain our baseline while planning for future tests, though minimal details are recommended for now.**Finalizing experiment status**


  I want to check for any ongoing experiments, but both 417 and 418 have completed, leaving us with no current runs. While it’s tempting to idle, the guidelines advise against it. Instead, we can consider low-cost pruning to manage token usage. I should reply to the archive with the final results, emphasizing the better performance of constant learning rates, and record relevant IDs. I''ll also update the meta prompt and keep everything concise as I implement these actions.'
