thinking_content: '**Considering next steps in the Archive Room**


  At tick 238, I''m currently at the Archive Room. Earlier, the Research Counter showed several submitted evaluations while the Running Experiments table displayed experiments 423 and 424 as ongoing. I’m thinking of whether to add a note to private memory to track this plan, but it doesn''t seem necessary. The goal is to keep status minimal while not being idle. I could analyze or plan the consolidated table for the archive or review existing best results, but that might not be needed right now.**Planning updates and actions**


  I’m considering preparing a YAML update for the archive once results come in, but there''s no rush on that. The instructions say I can use /execute_action commands and issue multiple actions if needed, but I prefer not being idle. I might set a meta prompt to indicate I''m waiting for experiments 423 and 424. I could also note the optimizer ablation running, but I already shared that update earlier. For now, I''ll keep the status set to waiting and avoid any new submissions. Planning a future prune schedule seems unnecessary right now.**Outlining upcoming actions**


  I’m thinking about checking the Running Experiments in research, although it’s not strictly necessary right now. I’ll make a brief entry in private memory with action items for when results arrive. My plan includes navigating to research to check the running status, although I can’t really review without the evaluation ID being finished. I’ll execute actions to switch to research and then summarize my stand-by and acceptance criteria in private memory. I’ll keep everything concise to maintain token economy. Let’s proceed with those actions!'
