thinking_content: '**Considering experiment updates**


  At tick 239, it seems like there were running experiments numbered 428/429, but they aren''t showing as running anymore. I might need to check if their scores have been added elsewhere, even if they''re not visible. It''s possible their scores are lower than 82.4, so they could be on a different page. As for tick 240, I think I could update the Archive capsule with the optimizer ablation results, but I''m facing the challenge of not having final replicates to report yet.**Evaluating optimizer options**


  I think the next step might be updating the meta prompt and considering locking the optimizer selection for each variant until we get the replicates. I also want to run the time variant with a learning rate of 4e-4 for seeds 7 and 123 since we thought it performed better sometimes. Earlier, the time variant was tested at 5e-4 with seed 42, while the previous replicates used AdamW at 4e-4. Maybe I should also try the time variant with Adam at 4e-4 to see if it yields better results compared to 5e-4.**Analyzing experiment submission**


  Currently, there''s a two-run cap, and since the "Running Experiments" shows none, I can submit two new runs. However, I had previously submitted replicates 428 and 429, but they''re not appearing in the "Submitted Evaluations." It seems like they might have completed and could show up after a page navigation or the next tick. Even though it says "Running Experiments: none," there''s a chance those replicates are still running, creating a potential mismatch in the reporting.**Checking evaluation details**


  To be cautious, I’ll check the "Submitted Evaluations" table sorted by score since experiments 428 and 429 might not appear on the first page due to that sorting. I see 87.0 on page 1, but no sign of 428 or 429 yet. I can try using "/execute_action{preview 428,429}" to get more details or "/execute_action{review 428}." The Research Counter allows me to review evaluations and retrieve logs, so I''ll plan to review those two experiments. Once I get the results, I’ll update the archive accordingly.**Implementing review actions**


  Since the submissions were made at tick 239 and evaluations usually take at most 2 ticks, it''s tick 240 now, so I can attempt the review. If they aren’t ready, that’s okay. I’ll keep things concise and decide whether to set the meta. I don''t need heavy formatting; just a simple bullet list is fine. I’ll implement the actions in code lines and proceed with the reviews accordingly.'
