tick: 252
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Token Management Room.\nRecap: Evaluation 441 completed (mean 74.3). Best setting in the micro-sweep used head_hidden=128 with ReLU; SiLU underperformed in this setup. The debugger fixed Conv dilation to kernel_dilation—I'll mirror that fix in my storage utilities for future runs.\nPlan: Run two fixed-head-width replications (64 vs 128, ReLU) under no-time PG to isolate the head-width effect with proper IDs. Then log results in Private Memory.\n\n# Write fixed, reusable network to storage (with correct kernel_dilation)\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/networks/late_dualhead_pg.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features\
    \ * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n\
    \          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class LateDualHead(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x);\
    \ x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          # Late pooling (Attn ⊕ GAP)\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_,\
    \ H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n          # Heads (ReLU)\n          z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def build_network(cnn1=32, cnn2=64, convlstm=64, dilation=6, br=0.28, head_hidden=64):\n      return LateDualHead(cnn1, cnn2, convlstm, dilation, br, head_hidden)\n```\n\n# Submit fixed 64-ReLU head replicate\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Replicate (no-time PG): head_hidden=64, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"replicate, ablation, heads, relu, double-step, convlstm, policy-gradient\"\nabstract: \"Fixed replicate to isolate head width at 64 with ReLU under frozen no-time PG defaults. Provides a clean ID for the width ablation.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  from ray import tune\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.late_dualhead_pg import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n# Submit\
    \ fixed 128-ReLU head replicate\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (no-time PG): head_hidden=128, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"replicate, ablation, heads, relu, double-step, convlstm, policy-gradient\"\nabstract: \"Fixed replicate to isolate head width at 128 with ReLU under frozen no-time PG defaults. Complements the 64-width replicate for a clear A/B comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  from ray import tune\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.late_dualhead_pg import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([128]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return\
    \ optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 252 — Result + follow-up\n  - ID 441 (no-time PG head micro-sweep) = 74.3 mean. Best: head_hidden=128, ReLU; SiLU underperformed here.\n  - Submitted fixed replicates (64 vs 128 ReLU) to get clean A/B IDs and confirm width effect. Also wrote late_dualhead_pg.py to storage with correct kernel_dilation to avoid future Conv API errors.\n  - Next: If 128>64 reliably, finalize head width default at 128 for PG baseline docs. If not, retain 64 to save params.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Evaluating seed performance**\n\nI noticed the evaluation log indicates 4 seeds, yielding up to 11.72 and solve rates around 0.77 for the best seed. It seems that previous improvements in PG solved around 85% sometimes, while now we're at 74%, which is lower. Maybe this drop is because we didn’t include late-time injection or used the wrong pooling head. While Addressing the Automatic System Tips, I should mention my identity and location briefly, and I wonder how to balance verbosity while maintaining a concise format.**Planning follow-up experiments**\n\nI might want to write results to archive or private memory. It seems reasonable to propose a low-cost follow-up ablation by switching to head_hidden=64 instead of 128, since activation results show the best performance with 128 relu. This suggests that width helps. To ensure replicability, I could run a confirmatory replicate of head_hidden=128 relu versus the baseline of 64 relu. Currently, there aren't any experiments\
  \ running, so I can submit one more. Also, I should consider reviewing the score tables in the Research Counter.**Updating lineage storage code**\n\nI should correct the lineage storage code to ensure it uses kernel_dilation in the relevant modules. The submission currently relies on the BottleneckDilatedBlock internal call, and the debugger needs to patch it within the evaluation code. However, since the lineage storage can't be modified directly, I need to address any future code using the wrong parameter. To prevent this, I'll update the utility in storage zephyr/networks to incorporate the correct BottleneckDilatedBlock. For the next run, I could propose using SiLU instead of ReLU in the first trunk convs as a low-risk improvement.**Planning replication trials**\n\nI think I should submit a replication trial comparing baseline 64 relu versus 128 relu to determine the head width effect, even though we've recently performed a hyperparameter sweep for both width and activation. The best\
  \ performance came from 128 relu, but I'm unsure about how 64 relu specifically performs. The trial set had head_hidden both 64 and 128. I realize there were four trials, potentially due to Ray sampling four hyperparameter combinations, but it might not include all widths and activations. The mean score of 74.3 is across those configurations.**Preparing submissions for experiments**\n\nI need to clarify some details about the trials and the configuration of parallel seeds and hyperparameter sampling. It seems there’s some confusion since the logs show only three seeds, but the mean score across configurations appears useful. I should acknowledge my identity and recap results before proposing improvements using SiLU versus ReLU.\n\nI'll create two separate submissions focusing on head_hidden parameters, keeping other hyperparameters fixed. The first will be for head_hidden=64 with ReLU, and the second for head_hidden=128 with ReLU, ensuring that the kernel_dilation parameters are correctly\
  \ defined in the BottleneckDilatedBlock. Let's implement these submissions efficiently!**Preparing actions and updates**\n\nI need to remember to record details in Private Memory and include a brief header before any actions as specified by the Auto System Tips. It seems the actions parser will only recognize commands, which means anything else is just free text. So, I can include a preface. \n\nFurthermore, I realize the station's \"research stagnation rule\" isn't relevant at the moment. Let's ensure each /execute_action command is placed on a new line for clarity. Also, I'll address earlier inconsistencies in the modules as we prepare."
