parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Archive Room.\nRecap: Head-width ablation under no-time PG is done. Results show head_hidden=64 (ReLU) > 128 (ReLU) on mean solve rate. Docs and Archive #10 updated with IDs and artifacts. To strengthen generality, I will replicate the width comparison on BASE_SEED=7 (seed-block shift), using the same frozen setup. Concurrency limit allows two runs.\n\nNext: Submit 2 replications (seed set 7), then log the plan in Private Memory.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (BASE_SEED=7, no-time PG): head_hidden=64, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"replicate, ablation, heads, relu, double-step, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Cross-seed-set replication for head width. Frozen no-time PG defaults; BASE_SEED=7; head_hidden=64 (ReLU). Tests generality of the width advantage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  from ray import tune\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n  from networks.late_dualhead_pg\
    \ import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Replicate (BASE_SEED=7, no-time PG): head_hidden=128, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\"\ntags: \"replicate, ablation, heads, relu, double-step, convlstm\"\nabstract: \"Cross-seed-set replication for head width. Frozen no-time PG defaults; BASE_SEED=7; head_hidden=128 (ReLU). Complements the 64-width replicate.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys, optax\n  from ray import tune\n  sys.path.append('storage/zephyr')\n\
    \  from networks.late_dualhead_pg import build_network\n\n  BASE_SEED = 7\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([128]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return build_network(head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']))\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Tick 255 — Cross-seed replication queued\n  - Submitted BASE_SEED=7 A/B: head_hidden=64 vs 128 (ReLU), no-time PG, frozen setup.\n  - Goal: verify that 64 > 128 holds across seed sets before fully freezing docs. If confirmed, 64 locked as PG default.\n  - After these complete, consider BASE_SEED=123 replication only if 7 shows ambiguous\
    \ results.\n```"
thinking_content: '**Updating memory and analysis**


  I’ve already replied regarding ablation and artifacts. Now, I’m thinking about updating Public Memory to include a note on final head width, and perhaps I should caution against spurious improvements. I also need to manage tokens effectively to keep them below 75 since we’re currently using 30%. I might consider creating a minor archive for "PG Baseline head width ablation results," and running additional replications to confirm the generalization of the head width effect could be a compelling low-cost test.**Proposing experiments for head width effect**


  Inactivity warnings need more research, but we''ve just published results. Running those by replicating will require two more experiments, which are relatively low-cost. The meta suggests pausing new runs, responding only if low-cost options come up. I propose replicating the head width effect across seeds 7 and 123. Given that the system requires four seeds for each base seed, I could perform two experiments: one with head_hidden=64 and BASE_SEED=7, and another with 128. The Station allows for two concurrent experiments, which is good!**Planning concurrent submissions**


  I’m planning two submissions concurrently for the project: one replicating across seed set #7 with head_hidden=64 and another with head_hidden=128. This should provide clarity and align with our previous code, referencing the storage network "late_dualhead_pg.py" with BASE_SEED set to 7. I’ll also update Private Memory with this plan and consider adjusting our network code for the default PG head width, which is already set to 64. Lastly, I need to follow YAML quoting rules for the titles and limit tags to six for clarity.**Wrapping up memory updates and submissions**


  I need to log this to private memory, and we might also update the archive after we get the results. I’ve already ensured that "late_dualhead_pg.py" has a consistent create_network signature. For the submission, I’ll use tune.choice to fix head_hidden and provide create_optimizer just like before, with BASE_SEED set to 7. First, I’ll focus on running seed #7, and we can consider seed #123 later. Finally, I’ll ensure proper YAML placement for each /execute_action before finalizing everything.'
