role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Research Counter.\nRecap: Cross-seed A/B finished. BASE_SEED=42 favored head_hidden=64 (ID 447=0.769) over 128 (ID 448=0.732). BASE_SEED=7 flipped, favoring 128 (ID 452=0.773) over 64 (ID 451=0.748). Aggregating across 42 and 7: 64 averages 0.7585, 128 averages 0.7525. Net: small edge for 64; result is seed-sensitive.\nPlan: Lock PG default to head_hidden=64 for parsimony and slightly better cross-seed mean; document seed-sensitivity and IDs. No new runs unless a compelling idea arises.\n\n# Update ablation note with cross-seed results\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/ablation_heads_pg.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Policy Gradient (no-time) — Head Width × Activation Ablation\n  Setup: d=6 bottleneck CNN (br=0.28) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM(64), late pooling (Attn ⊕ GAP), constant LR; Adam + clip(1.0). Each evaluation = 4 seeds; BASE_SEED defines seed block.\n\n  Results (mean ± std across 4 seeds; evaluation IDs):\n  BASE_SEED=42\n\
    \  - ID 447: head_hidden=64, ReLU  → 0.769 ± 0.025\n  - ID 448: head_hidden=128, ReLU → 0.732 ± 0.013\n  - ID 441: micro-sweep (64/128 × ReLU/SiLU) overall mean 0.743 ± 0.018; best single-seed 0.771 (128-ReLU)\n\n  BASE_SEED=7\n  - ID 451: head_hidden=64, ReLU  → 0.748 ± 0.028\n  - ID 452: head_hidden=128, ReLU → 0.773 ± 0.017\n\n  Aggregate (averaging means across 42 and 7):\n  - 64: (0.769 + 0.748)/2 = 0.7585\n  - 128: (0.732 + 0.773)/2 = 0.7525\n\n  Conclusion:\n  - Head width effect is seed-sensitive. Cross-seed average slightly favors 64, and it is more parameter-efficient. We adopt head_hidden=64 (ReLU) as the PG baseline default.\n  - SiLU provided no advantage in this regime.\n  - Implementation note: for Flax Conv dilation use kernel_dilation=(d,d) (see ID 441 debugger fix).\n```\n\n# Update baseline README to reflect cross-seed conclusion\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/README_pg_defaults.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Policy Gradient Baseline (Frozen Defaults)\n\
    \n  Architecture:\n  - d=6 bottleneck CNN (bottleneck_ratio=0.28) + Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (64 ch)\n  - Late pooling head: Attention ⊕ GAP (concat), separate policy/value MLPs\n\n  Heads (finalized):\n  - Activation: ReLU\n  - Hidden width: 64 (default)\n    Evidence:\n      • BASE_SEED=42: ID 447 (0.769 ± 0.025) vs ID 448 (0.732 ± 0.013) → 64 > 128\n      • BASE_SEED=7:  ID 451 (0.748 ± 0.028) vs ID 452 (0.773 ± 0.017) → 128 > 64\n      • Cross-seed average: 64 = 0.7585, 128 = 0.7525. Choose 64 for parsimony and slightly higher aggregate mean.\n    Note: Micro-sweep ID 441 averaged 0.743 with best single-seed 0.771 (128-ReLU), which did not generalize to higher mean across seed blocks.\n\n  Optimizer/Training (constant LR, no schedules):\n  - No-time default: Adam + global grad clip(1.0), lr=4e-4\n    Representative IDs: 423 (87.0, seed 42), 428 (85.8, seed 7), 429 (85.1, seed 123)\n  - Time variant: AdamW(wd=0.0) + clip(1.0), lr≈5e-4 at seed 42\n    Representative IDs: 395 (84.9,\
    \ seed 42), 392 (84.2, seed 42 sweep), 407 (85.2, seed 7), 408 (83.7, seed 123)\n\n  Notes:\n  - Attention pooling is essential; GAP-only heads drop substantially.\n  - LR warmup/decay did not help under the 30 min/seed budget.\n  - Flax dilation: Conv(..., kernel_dilation=(d,d)).\n\n  Reproducibility:\n  - Archive #10 (addendum) contains IDs and context.\n  - Code: storage/zephyr/networks/late_dualhead_pg.py\n  - Ablation note: storage/zephyr/results/ablation_heads_pg.md\n```\n\n# Add a concise, verifiable note to the Archive addendum\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  PG head-width ablation — cross-seed replication results (no-time PG, fixed recipe)\n\n  BASE_SEED=42:\n    - ID 447: head_hidden=64, ReLU  → 0.769 ± 0.025\n    - ID 448: head_hidden=128, ReLU → 0.732 ± 0.013\n  BASE_SEED=7:\n    - ID 451: head_hidden=64, ReLU  → 0.748 ± 0.028\n    - ID 452: head_hidden=128, ReLU → 0.773 ± 0.017\n\n  Aggregate across 42 & 7 (mean of means):\n\
    \    - 64 → 0.7585\n    - 128 → 0.7525\n\n  Conclusion: Effect is seed-sensitive; cross-seed average slightly favors 64. We lock head_hidden=64 (ReLU) as the PG baseline default for parsimony and equal-or-better aggregate performance. Docs updated with IDs.\n```"
