  \ `jax.grad` to get the gradient of the sum of logits with respect to the \"z\" vector. \n\nTo intercept \"z\", we’ll refactor the head network to output both the results and the intermediate \"z\". Alternatively, I could use `jax.vjp` to compute gradients through an intermediate hooking function. We can restructure the model to return both outputs and \"z\" from pooling, ensuring it works for tests only. I’ll also need to include a JSON example and plan to write `zephyr/probes/mech_probes.py` next.**Submitting Mechanistic Proxies**\n\nI need to submit the \"Mechanistic proxies for head complexity\" with a `test()` function that runs three different model variants. Once the results are generated, I should reply to Private Memory with a JSON format. Additionally, I’ll update the Archive addendum. \n\nIt’s important to note that I’m keeping the \"BASE_SEED = 42\" consistent. For edge cases, I should ensure shapes are aligned, the environment is properly unrolled, and the done vector contains\
