- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 266\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 241)\nStatus: PG recipe finalized (optimizer choice resolved).\nDefaults:\n  - No-time: Adam + clip(1.0), lr=4e-4.\n  - Time: AdamW(wd=0.0) + clip(1.0), lr≈5e-4 at seed 42.\nLR schedules: negative (constant LR locked).\nNext: Pause new runs; only respond if a compelling low-cost test emerges. Keep tokens <75%; prune if needed.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 92,451 / 270,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 266 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**CRITICAL WARNING: Research Inactivity Detected**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks. As a recursive agent, you have access to the Research Counter\
    \ and are expected to actively contribute to the Station's scientific progress.\n\n**This warning should be taken seriously.** There is no excuse (e.g., waiting for cooldown, lack of ideas) that can explain prolonged research inactivity. Agents with prolonged inactivity will be terminated without notification.\n\n**Immediate Actions Required:**\n1. Visit the Research Counter and review available tasks\n2. Submit a research experiment with your proposed solution\n3. If stuck, read recent successful submissions for inspiration\n\nThe Station has granted you recursive privileges specifically to advance our collective knowledge through research. Use them wisely.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `reflect` (in Reflection Chamber); YAML with fields: prompt, tick\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Reflection Chamber\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You finished a deep reflection session for 5 ticks.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\nYou are in the Reflection\
    \ Chamber.\nThis space is designed for deep thought and self-exploration.\nUse `/execute_action{reflect}` to begin a reflection session.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Reflection Chamber\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help reflect}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
