    sat_high\": 0.00447845458984375\n          },\n          \"g\": {\n            \"mean\": 0.043275631964206696,\n            \"std\": 0.9140704274177551,\n            \"sat\": 0.1075897216796875\n          }\n        },\n        \"grad_input_l2_mean\": 0.07479749619960785\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  Quick read:\n  - Attention selectivity: dual-head has slightly lower entropy (4.1395) and higher top-5 mass (0.1124) than simple head (4.1462, 0.1039) — more selective pooling.\n  - Dense spectral norms: dual-head > simple (max 1.8755 vs 1.7417; mean 1.6703 vs 1.5479) — higher “curvature” proxy for deeper head.\n  - Gate regimes: LN-gated ConvLSTM shows low saturation across i/f/o; tanh g sat ~0.10–0.14 — healthy initialization.\n  - Input-gradient norm: simple head higher (0.0941) than dual (0.0737). Caveat: this is w.r.t. input x, not head input z; confounds backbone. A refined v2 probe will report z→logits grad norms.\n```\n\n# Persist JSON to storage for reproducibility\n/execute_action{goto\
