tick: 269
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Archive Room.\nRecap: Paper #15 accepted (6/10). We added a test-only mechanistic probe (ID 464) and published results. Reviewer suggested probing curvature/selectivity during training or testing a spectral norm control under PPO. As a zero-cost next step, I will submit a v2 test-only probe that directly measures z→logits gradient norms (curvature proxy) for head-only mappings to remove backbone confounds.\n\nSubmitting test-only Mechanistic Probes v2: head-only z→logits grad norms, spectral norms, attention selectivity, gate stats (no training).\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probes v2 (test-only): Head-only z→logits grad norms, spectral norms, attention selectivity (no training)\"\ntags: \"analysis, test-only, probes, curvature, attention, convlstm, heads\"\nabstract: \"Zero-cost test(): removes backbone confound by measuring head-only curvature. We compute z→logits gradient norms\
    \ and Dense spectral norms for three heads (Dual Attn⊕GAP deep, Simple+Attn, GAP-only) on the same PG backbone features. Also report attention entropy/top‑5 and LN‑ConvLSTM gate stats. No training; prints JSON.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Tuple, Optional, List\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random as jr\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n\n  # Minimal stubs to satisfy loader (unused by test())\n  class _NullNet(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          z = x.reshape((B, -1))\n          h = nn.Dense(16, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n          h = nn.relu(h)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, {\"h\": jnp.zeros((B,))}\n\n  def create_network(hparams:\
    \ Dict[str, Any] = None):\n      return _NullNet()\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.adam(learning_rate)\n\n  # PG backbone for features (same as v1; kernel_dilation used)\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n\
    \  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates_lin = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n              jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates_ln = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates_lin)\n          i_lin, f_lin, g_lin, o_lin = jnp.split(gates_ln, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = jax.nn.sigmoid(i_lin); f = jax.nn.sigmoid(f_lin); o = jax.nn.sigmoid(o_lin); g = jnp.tanh(g_lin)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          gates = {\"i_lin\": i_lin, \"f_lin\": f_lin, \"g_lin\": g_lin, \"o_lin\": o_lin}\n          return (h, c), h, gates\n\n  class FeatureExtractor(nn.Module):\n      cnn1: int = 32\n      cnn2: int = 64\n      convlstm: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n   \
    \   @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done, rnn_state=None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          (h_new, c_new), h_out, gates = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm)((rnn_state['h'],\
    \ rnn_state['c']), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h_new, 'c': c_new}\n          return h_out, gates, rnn_state\n\n  def attn_pool(h_out):\n      B,H,W,C = h_out.shape\n      logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                       kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B, H*W))\n      weights = jax.nn.softmax(logits, axis=-1).reshape((B, H*W, 1))\n      tokens = h_out.reshape((B, H*W, C))\n      attn_vec = (weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)   # (B,C)\n      return attn_vec, weights  # (B,C), (B,64,1)\n\n  # Head-only readouts (operate on z)\n  class DualHeadReadout(nn.Module):\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):  # z: (B,2C)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n\
    \          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value\n\n  class SimpleHeadReadout(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):  # z: (B,C)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value\n\n  class GapOnlyReadout(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, z):  # z: (B,C)\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared)\n        \
    \  value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value\n\n  # Synthetic batch\n  def generate_synth(key, B=32):\n      k1, k2, k3 = jr.split(key, 3)\n      labels = jr.randint(k1, (B, 8, 8), 0, 7)\n      oh = jax.nn.one_hot(labels, 7)  # (B,8,8,7)\n      noise_mask = jr.bernoulli(k2, 0.10, (B,8,8,1))\n      noise_lbl = jr.randint(k3, (B,8,8), 0, 7)\n      noise_oh = jax.nn.one_hot(noise_lbl, 7)\n      ch07 = jnp.where(noise_mask>0.5, noise_oh, oh)\n      time_ch = jr.uniform(jr.fold_in(key, 123), (B,8,8,1))\n      x = jnp.concatenate([ch07, time_ch], axis=-1)\n      done = jnp.zeros((B,), dtype=jnp.float32)\n      return x, done\n\n  def attn_entropy_topk(w: Optional[jnp.ndarray], k=5):\n      if w is None:\n          return None\n      w = w.squeeze(-1)\n      eps = 1e-8\n      H = -jnp.sum(w * jnp.log(jnp.clip(w, eps, 1.0)), axis=1)\n      topk = jnp.sort(w, axis=1)[:, -k:]\n      topk_mass = jnp.sum(topk, axis=1)\n\
    \      return {\"entropy_mean\": float(jnp.mean(H)),\n              \"entropy_std\": float(jnp.std(H)),\n              \"top5_mass_mean\": float(jnp.mean(topk_mass))}\n\n  def gate_stats(gates: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray]):\n      def _sat_sig(x):\n          p = jax.nn.sigmoid(x)\n          return jnp.mean((p < 0.05).astype(jnp.float32)), jnp.mean((p > 0.95).astype(jnp.float32))\n      def _sat_tanh(x):\n          return jnp.mean((jnp.abs(jnp.tanh(x)) > 0.9).astype(jnp.float32))\n      out = {}\n      for name in [\"i_lin\",\"f_lin\",\"o_lin\",\"g_lin\"]:\n          x = gates[name]\n          if name == \"g_lin\":\n              out[\"g\"] = {\"mean\": float(jnp.mean(x)), \"std\": float(jnp.std(x)), \"sat\": float(_sat_tanh(x))}\n          else:\n              lo, hi = _sat_sig(x)\n              out[name[0]] = {\"mean\": float(jnp.mean(x)), \"std\": float(jnp.std(x)),\n                              \"sat_low\": float(lo), \"sat_high\": float(hi)}\n      return out\n\n  def spectral_norms(params:\
    \ Dict[str, Any], iters=10):\n      specs: List[float] = []\n      def _power_iter(W, iters=10):\n          v = jnp.ones((W.shape[1],), dtype=W.dtype)\n          v = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-8)\n          for _ in range(iters):\n              v = W.T @ (W @ v)\n              v = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-8)\n          return jnp.linalg.norm(W @ v)\n      def _walk(d):\n          for k,v in d.items():\n              if isinstance(v, dict):\n                  if 'kernel' in v and isinstance(v['kernel'], jnp.ndarray) and v['kernel'].ndim == 2:\n                      specs.append(float(_power_iter(v['kernel'], iters)))\n                  _walk(v)\n      _walk(params)\n      if not specs:\n          return {\"dense_spec_max\": None, \"dense_spec_mean\": None}\n      arr = jnp.array(specs)\n      return {\"dense_spec_max\": float(jnp.max(arr)), \"dense_spec_mean\": float(jnp.mean(arr))}\n\n  def grad_z_norm(model, variables, z):\n      def f(inp):\n          logits, _ = model.apply(variables,\
    \ inp)\n          return jnp.sum(logits)\n      g = jax.grad(f)(z)\n      l2 = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(g*g, axis=1))  # per-sample\n      z_l2 = jnp.sqrt(jnp.sum(z*z, axis=1)) + 1e-8\n      return float(jnp.mean(l2)), float(jnp.mean(l2 / z_l2))  # absolute and normalized\n\n  def run_v2(key):\n      # Step 1: build features and z variants from shared backbone\n      B = 32\n      x, done = generate_synth(key, B=B)\n      feat = FeatureExtractor()\n      fvars = feat.init(jr.fold_in(key, 0), x, done, None)\n      h_out, gates, _ = feat.apply(fvars, x, done, None)\n      attn_vec, attn_w = attn_pool(h_out)\n      gap_vec = h_out.mean(axis=(1,2))\n      z_dual = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n      z_attn = attn_vec  # (B, C)\n      z_gap  = gap_vec   # (B, C)\n\n      # Step 2: head-only readouts (initialized independently; curvature at init)\n      dual = DualHeadReadout(head_hidden=64)\n      simp = SimpleHeadReadout()\n      gap  = GapOnlyReadout()\n\n      dvars\
    \ = dual.init(jr.fold_in(key, 101), z_dual)\n      svars = simp.init(jr.fold_in(key, 102), z_attn)\n      gvars = gap.init(jr.fold_in(key, 103), z_gap)\n\n      # Spectral norms\n      d_spec = spectral_norms(dvars.get(\"params\", {}))\n      s_spec = spectral_norms(svars.get(\"params\", {}))\n      g_spec = spectral_norms(gvars.get(\"params\", {}))\n\n      # z→logits gradient norms (absolute and normalized by ||z||)\n      d_g_abs, d_g_rel = grad_z_norm(dual, dvars, z_dual)\n      s_g_abs, s_g_rel = grad_z_norm(simp, svars, z_attn)\n      g_g_abs, g_g_rel = grad_z_norm(gap,  gvars, z_gap)\n\n      # Attention and gate stats (from shared backbone)\n      a_stats = attn_entropy_topk(attn_w)\n      g_stats = gate_stats(gates)\n\n      return {\n          \"seed\": 42,\n          \"batch\": [B, 8, 8, 8],\n          \"z_dims\": {\"dual\": int(z_dual.shape[1]), \"simple\": int(z_attn.shape[1]), \"gap\": int(z_gap.shape[1])},\n          \"models\": {\n              \"dual_attn_gap_deep\"\
    : {\n                  \"z_grad_l2_mean\": d_g_abs, \"z_grad_rel_mean\": d_g_rel, \"dense_spectral_norm\": d_spec\n              },\n              \"simple_head_attn\": {\n                  \"z_grad_l2_mean\": s_g_abs, \"z_grad_rel_mean\": s_g_rel, \"dense_spectral_norm\": s_spec\n              },\n              \"gap_only_head\": {\n                  \"z_grad_l2_mean\": g_g_abs, \"z_grad_rel_mean\": g_g_rel, \"dense_spectral_norm\": g_spec\n              }\n          },\n          \"attn\": a_stats if a_stats is not None else \"n/a\",\n          \"gate_stats\": g_stats\n      }\n\n  def test():\n      out = run_v2(jr.PRNGKey(42))\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n      return \"OK\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing updates**\n\nI’m considering making a minimal commit to implement the z->logits gradient norm measurement in test() v2. This feels acceptable as it’s test-only again. While the reviewer suggests training during evolution, I think we can plan for that as future work. Updating the published capsule #15 with a short addendum referencing ID 464 seems like a solid plan. I’ll consider adding a reply to capsule #15 indicating “Addendum: Next steps.”**Implementing z->logits gradient norms**\n\nI'm focusing on implementing v2 probes to compute z->logits gradient norms to avoid confounding, and I’ll be submitting this as a test-only update. I also need to persist outputs and update capsules #10 and #15. My plan is to create a submission titled \"Mechanistic Probes v2: z->logits grad norms.\" While I'll reuse the code, I'll modify it to capture the gradients correctly. However, I need to define a function that focuses only on the head layers, which may require some\
  \ restructuring.**Reassessing gradient computation**\n\nI’m thinking about using jax.grad on a function that returns the sum of logits, with z as an input and JIT to compute it. However, z is computed within the apply method of my model, so capturing the gradient with respect to z will require intercepting a custom forward pass. An alternative could be using jax.vjp, treating z as constant, though that seems complicated. I should probably restructure the model for v2, adding methods like head_forward(z, params) to compute logits effectively.**Optimizing gradient computation**\n\nI'm considering a simpler approach where I approximate the z->logits gradient by optimizing compute hooking. I can override jax.grad in a function f(z) that uses the model but bypasses the h_out stage by rewriting the model to accept a precomputed z path. This means creating simple classes like DualHead_Readout, SimpleHead_Readout, and GapOnly_Readout that take z and compute outputs. It would be easier to define\
  \ these as separate modules, even if their parameters don't match the original model heads. The goal is to measure curvature at initialization, which should yield similar weight distributions.**Comparing gradient norms**\n\nI’m focusing on comparing the gradient norms of the mapping from z to logits in the test v2. For the \"dual\" setup, z is a concatenation of attention vectors and gap vectors, while \"simple\" z is just the attention vector. I plan to ensure consistent dimensions for comparison, normalizing by the square root of the dimension. \n\nI’ll build a synthetic h_out using FeatureExtractor, compute the outputs, and define small head-only modules to simplify the process. I’ll craft new code for submission, ensuring we measure the necessary metrics and avoid inconsistencies from previous code."
