parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 273\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 241)\nStatus: PG recipe finalized (optimizer choice resolved).\nDefaults:\n  - No-time: Adam + clip(1.0), lr=4e-4.\n  - Time: AdamW(wd=0.0) + clip(1.0), lr≈5e-4 at seed 42.\nLR schedules: negative (constant LR locked).\nNext: Pause new runs; only respond if a compelling low-cost test emerges. Keep tokens <75%; prune if needed.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 133,724 / 270,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 273 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'PG: Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP\
    \ head (no-time defaults, 45-min allowance)' (ID: 474) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 92.8\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.938, 0.932, 0.933, 0.907]\nMean: 0.928, Std: 0.012\nBest trial: 1 (0.938)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  convlstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation: 6.000000\n  bottleneck_ratio: 0.280000\n  head_hidden: 64.000000\n  triple_steps: 3.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 474\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the hyperparameter definition issue that was causing an immediate crash. The code now runs without crashing and the evaluation is proceeding normally.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code defined hyperparameters as plain dictionary values in the `_define_hyperparameters()` function:\n\n```python\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate':\
    \ 4e-4,\n        'entropy_coef': 0.01,\n        'cnn_features_1': 32,\n        # ... other plain values\n    }\n```\n\nHowever, the evaluation system expects hyperparameters to be defined using Ray Tune search space objects with a `sample()` method. When the system tried to sample from these plain values on line 309 in `main.py` (`hparams[key] = space_obj.sample()`), it failed because plain numbers don't have a `sample()` method, leading to an empty `hparams` dictionary and the subsequent `KeyError: 'cnn_features_1'` when creating the network.\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged the hyperparameter definitions to use Ray Tune search space objects:\n\n```python\nfrom ray import tune\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        # ... other tune.choice objects\n    }\n```\n\nThis ensures that each hyperparameter has a `sample()` method that returns\
    \ the desired fixed value, making it compatible with the evaluation system's expectation while preserving the agent's intended fixed hyperparameter values.\n\n## Result\n- The evaluation v2 is now running successfully (status \"pending\" instead of \"failed\")\n- Code has been running for over 2 minutes without crashing\n- The fix preserves the original architecture and hyperparameter values exactly as intended by the agent\n- No changes were needed to the neural network architecture or training logic\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Fixed PG defaults; single config across 4 seeds for clean ablation\n    # Must use Ray Tune search\
    \ space objects\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n        'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n        'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n        'triple_steps': tune.choice([3]),\n    }\n\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                   kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n         \
    \           kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n \
    \   convlstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    triple_steps: int = 3\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN trunk\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n        # RNN state init/reset\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c':\
    \ zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Triple-step LN-ConvLSTM updates (heavier recurrence)\n        h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        for _ in range(self.triple_steps):\n            (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n        # Late pooling: Attention ⊕ GAP\n        B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n        tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n        attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n        gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n\n        # Heads\
    \ (modest MLP for parsimony)\n        shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n        convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n        dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n        bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n        head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n\
    \        triple_steps=int(hparams['triple_steps']),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    # No-time PG default: Adam + global grad clip\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: using default\n  create_optimizer: from\
    \ submission\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 4 seeds, 50,000,000 steps per seed\nParallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4\nTimeout: 45.0 min per trial, 180.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting Sokoban RL training - Seed 2 with timeout 45.0min\nPerforming initial network output shape validation...\nNetwork output shapes are correct.\nCompiling JAX functions...\n\nStep | 0.0M | 5.0M | 10.0M | 15.0M | 20.0M | 25.0M | 30.0M | 35.0M | 40.0M | 45.0M | 50.0M | 50.0M\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nReturn | 0.00 | -0.10 | 2.25 | 5.54 | 9.89 | 11.97 | 12.37 | 12.47 | 11.71 | 13.64 | 12.93 | 12.97\nSolve | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.154 | 0.333 | 0.700 | 0.864 | 0.903 | 0.906\
