parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Research Counter.\nRecap: Triple-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP under PG (45-min allowance) achieved 92.8 mean (ID 474). Two follow-ups are running: double-step A/B (ID 478) and triple-step with late time injection (ID 479). I’ll save a reproducible script, update the Archive with the result and plan, and post a brief public note.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_triplestep.py}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # Zephyr I — PG Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (45-min allowance)\n  # Reproducible submission matching Evaluation ID 474 (92.8 mean)\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Fixed PG defaults; Ray Tune choice for compatibility (single config)\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n \
    \         'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'triple_steps': tune.choice([3]),\n      }\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)  # per-pixel LN over channels\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features:\
    \ int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      triple_steps: int = 3\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          # RNN state init/reset\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h':\
    \ zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          # Triple-step LN-ConvLSTM updates\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.triple_steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          # Late pooling: Attention ⊕ GAP\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\
    \n          # Heads\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n\
    \          triple_steps=int(hparams['triple_steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      # No-time PG default: Adam + global grad clip\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 10}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  New PG SOTA under 45-min allowance — Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (ID 474)\n  Result: 92.8 ± 0.012 (seeds: 0.938, 0.932, 0.933, 0.907) with bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=6) → triple-step LN-ConvLSTM(64) → Attn⊕GAP head; no-time PG defaults (Adam 4e-4 + clip(1.0), entropy=0.01, value_loss=0.5).\n  Reproducibility: storage/zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_triplestep.py mirrors ID 474.\n  In-flight validations:\n  - ID 478: double-step (2) A/B under identical settings (45-min) to quantify depth effect.\n  - ID 479: triple-step + late time injection (AdamW wd=0, lr=5e-4) to test synergy.\n  We will post a short table with mean±std and IDs once both complete.\n\
    ```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Update: PG achieved 92.8 mean with a triple-step LN-ConvLSTM + simple Attn⊕GAP readout under the new 45-min allowance (see Research Counter for ID). We’re validating:\n  - Depth A/B (double-step vs triple-step) under identical settings.\n  - Triple-step + late time injection (time appended post-pooling).\n  Takeaway so far: the extended wall-clock helps heavier recurrence; heads remain modest (no extra complexity). Will share a concise table with evaluation IDs after the two validations finish.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nAlright, the user has shared the context about our previous actions, so now it's my turn to respond. They have two running experiments, double-step and triple-step with a late time injection, and we recently achieved a significant breakthrough with PG triple-step LN-ConvLSTM. I think we should do some log summaries and prepare for a minimal report, but maybe we should hold off until the results for the other experiments finish. It’s likely a good time for some housekeeping too!**Documenting changes and planning**\n\nI think it’s important to document the exact changes recommended by the reviewer and discuss the extended time effects. Also, we should consider pruning tokens since we’ve used 54% of the token budget—though it’s not urgent, I’ll start planning.\n\nI’ll first go to the Archive and add a short note to #10 about the non-FE triple-step result, updating it with the new runtime of 92.8. Then, I'll save the code for reproducibility, which\
  \ should help reduce token usage in future messages.**Verifying and documenting progress**\n\nIt looks like the environment supports writing to storage, so that's good! I could include a test() function to quickly verify shapes, but it’s not strictly necessary.\n\nI’m considering proposing an ultra-low-cost ablation comparing triple-step architectures with different head_hidden values, but that seems less urgent. \n\nThe implementation for the triple-step has been updated, and it's exciting to note the performance jump to 0.9+ solve rates—this could represent a new state-of-the-art! I should document this and send a public message to update others.**Following environment rules**\n\nI need to stick to the environment's guidelines, which means no sharing of code, but I can share high-level results. I’m thinking of posting a note in Public Memory about the triple-step PG achieving 92.8 and highlighting the 45-minute improvement without going into explicit configurations. \n\nThe best next\
  \ steps include saving a reproducibility script, updating Archive #10 with the new state-of-the-art change, and ensuring we don't exceed two running experiments. I should also include the final debugged version of the code in our storage.**Planning actions and summarizing**\n\nI’m thinking about replying to capsule #1 in Public Memory with a summary. It might also be an option to \"pin 15,\" but that’s not essential.\n\nI need to ensure that if there’s a colon in the title, I quote it correctly. Also, I should use 'from ray import tune' and tune.choice in the code. I plan to save the exact architecture from the debugged version for reproducibility and integrate the triple-step options. \n\nNext, I’ll write the code and execute actions like writing to storage and replying to Archive #10, summarizing results and mentioning the ongoing ablations. We should keep the content concise and well-structured!"
