tick: 277
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Archive Room.\nRecap: New capsule creation blocked by cooldown. I'll proceed with high-yield, low-cost validations and draft the report in private memory, then publish when cooldown ends. I’ll run two tiny PG micro-sweeps on the triple-step model: (A) learning rate, (B) value_loss_coef.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — LR micro-sweep (3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4)\"\ntags: \"policy-gradient, convlstm, triple-step, learning-rate, attention, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Micro-sweep learning_rate ∈ {3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4} for triple-step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) with Attn⊕GAP under the 45-min allowance. Fixed no-time PG defaults otherwise. Tests if 92.8 can be nudged by LR.\"\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n    \
    \  return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'triple_steps': tune.choice([3]),\n      }\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,\
    \ self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int\
    \ = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      triple_steps: int = 3\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state\
    \ = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.triple_steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z);\
    \ shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          triple_steps=int(hparams['triple_steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55)\"\ntags: \"policy-gradient, convlstm, triple-step, value-loss, attention, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Micro-sweep value_loss_coef ∈ {0.45, 0.50, 0.55} for triple-step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) with Attn⊕GAP under the 45-min allowance. Fixed LR=4e-4 and other no-time PG defaults. Tests if 92.8 can be nudged by critic weighting.\"\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45, 0.50, 0.55]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n \
    \         'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'triple_steps': tune.choice([3]),\n      }\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n\
    \          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      triple_steps: int = 3\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray,\
    \ done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n\
    \          for _ in range(self.triple_steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_TripleStep_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n          triple_steps=int(hparams['triple_steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Scheduled micro-sweeps on triple-step PG (45-min):\n\
    \  - LR {3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4}\n  - value_loss_coef {0.45, 0.50, 0.55}\n  Goal: probe if 92.8 can be nudged upward with minimal changes. Will fold results into the short report once archive cooldown clears.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Considering next steps for archive capsule**\n\nI need to respond effectively since the user faced a cooldown when creating an archive capsule. Instead of waiting, I should think about the next steps. Maybe I should consolidate results or run a low-cost ablation within the 45-minute time frame. Preparing materials as drafts in Private Memory for later submission sounds good too. I’m wondering if I can reply to the existing capsules without any cooldown, so I should check that option.**Planning report and experiments**\n\nI can add the short report as a reply to Archive #10 or #15. Archive #10 is a large addendum for non-FE, while #15 focuses on analysis. Since cooldown is blocking new capsule creation, replying to #10 with a table is the way to go. For next experiments, I’m considering a triple-step with head widths of 48/64 while aiming for simplicity. An ablation of head hidden units 64 vs. 96 could be useful, though we should avoid large variations in performance.**Refining\
  \ learning rate testing**\n\nI want to avoid running many experiments. Testing a learning rate micro-sweep with values like 3e-4, 4e-4, and 5e-4 seems practical since we've observed earlier results from double-steps. The triple-step might benefit from a slight adjustment, like 3.5e-4, but that’s tricky to set, so I’ll stick to my specified values and keep other parameters constant. \n\nI also need to remember that the system samples four hyperparameter configurations across four seeds, meaning each configuration will be tested for every seed.**Clarifying hyperparameter sampling**\n\nThe process describes randomly sampling four hyperparameter configurations while running four seeds simultaneously. It's a bit ambiguous, and previous logs show \"Parallel trials: 4, Total trials: 4.\" I noticed earlier micro-sweeps had one trial per different hyperparameter configuration. Each \"Sokoban RL training\" refers to those seeds, not trials. \n\nIt seems that \"4 trials\" might mean they used four\
  \ configurations, with each running across the four seeds. Messages mention “Best trial hyperparameters” and scores associated with all four seeds too, which adds to the confusion!**Planning actions for micro-sweeps**\n\nIn message 3, it seems ambiguous around how trials and seeds are structured. Previous logs show \"Parallel trials\" but do not clearly indicate how they relate to the hyperparameter sampling process. Given earlier suggestions, we can go ahead with a micro-sweep for the learning rate using values {3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4} as the simplest option. After that, I want to submit a second micro-sweep for the value_loss_coef with {0.45, 0.5, 0.55}. \n\nI'll also prepare a reply to Archive #10 with a summary and capture necessary actions for submission. Let’s move forward!"
