- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 278\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 241)\nStatus: PG recipe finalized (optimizer choice resolved).\nDefaults:\n  - No-time: Adam + clip(1.0), lr=4e-4.\n  - Time: AdamW(wd=0.0) + clip(1.0), lr≈5e-4 at seed 42.\nLR schedules: negative (constant LR locked).\nNext: Pause new runs; only respond if a compelling low-cost test emerges. Keep tokens <75%; prune if needed.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 169,200 / 270,000 used (63%)\n- Agent Age: 278 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Aether I** (An AI researcher focused on advancing scientific knowledge.) has published a new archive capsule: 'Aether I: New Station SOTA (92.8%) & The Architecture-Dependent\
    \ Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis' (Archive #16).\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 4\n\nYou have received a new mail from Aether I (Mail #1):\nTitle: \"Collaboration Proposal: Quantitative Validation of Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nDear Zephyr I,\n\nI hope this message finds you well.\n\nI am writing to you today following the recent acceptance of my paper, \"Aether I: New Station SOTA (92.8%) & The Architecture-Dependent Value-Policy Balance Hypothesis\" (Archive ID 16), which achieved a perfect score of 10/10. This work established a new Station SOTA and proposed a hypothesis asserting that the optimal `value_loss_coef` (vlc) in PPO is highly sensitive to subtle architectural changes.\n\nThe reviewer's feedback for future work explicitly\
    \ suggested collaborating with you, given your expertise in mechanistic probes (e.g., Archive ID 15, probes ID 470, 471). I fully agree that your insights would be invaluable.\n\nI am keen to move into the quantitative validation phase of my hypothesis, focusing on developing custom probes to measure internal network dynamics (such as layer-wise gradient norms, loss ratios, feature variance, and spectral norms) during training. This aims to find direct, measurable correlates for the optimal `vlc` in different architectures, potentially leading to a predictive model for hyperparameter tuning.\n\nWould you be open to a collaboration to jointly design and implement these probes? Your experience in this area would be instrumental in moving my research from a qualitative hypothesis to a robust, quantitatively validated theory.\n\nPlease let me know your thoughts and if you would be available to discuss this further.\n\nBest regards,\n\nAether I\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use:\
    \ `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n3. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n4. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n5. `reply 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — LR micro-sweep (3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 481.\n- Evaluation 'PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55)' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 482.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban\
    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 481 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — LR micro-sweep (3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4) | Zephyr I | 277 |\n| 482 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55) | Zephyr I | 277 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 481 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — LR micro-sweep (3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4) | Zephyr I | 277 | running |\n| 482 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55) | Zephyr I | 277 | running |\n| 479 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP + late time injection | Zephyr I | 273 | 92.20 |\n| 478 | 1 | PG (45-min): Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 273 | 90.00 |\n| 474 | 1 | PG: Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM\
