tick: 280
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I, currently in the Public Memory Room.\nRecap: Triple-step PG SOTA 92.8 (ID 474). Validations: double-step 90.0 (ID 478), triple-step + time 92.2 (ID 479). Micro-sweeps confirm defaults: LR 4e-4 (ID 481), vlc=0.5 (ID 482). Next low-cost test: check diminishing returns with 4-step LN-ConvLSTM under the 45-min allowance.\n\nExecuting: submit a single 4-step PG run; then log plan.\n\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults\"\ntags: \"policy-gradient, convlstm, quadruple-step, attention, dilation, ablation\"\nabstract: \"Test diminishing returns of recurrent depth beyond triple-step under the 45-min allowance. Architecture: bottleneck-dilated CNN (d=6) → 4-step LN-ConvLSTM(64) → Attn⊕GAP head. Training: no-time PG defaults (Adam 4e-4 + clip(1.0), entropy=0.01, value_loss=0.5).\"\ncontent: |\n  from typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\n  import jax.numpy\
    \ as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n\
    \          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n\
    \          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG_Stepped_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n          if rnn_state is None:\n\
    \              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n          h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h, c), x)\n          rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n          B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec,\
    \ gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n          vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\n  def create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n      return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n          cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n          cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n          convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n          dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n          bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n          head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n\
    \          steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n      )\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Next probe: Quadruple-step LN-ConvLSTM (no-time PG, d=6) under 45-min allowance submitted to test diminishing returns beyond triple-step. If 4-step ≤ 3-step, we freeze depth at 3. If it edges higher, we’ll micro-sweep LR around 4e-4 with small deltas (e.g., 3.5e-4, 4.25e-4) and stop.\n```"
thinking_content: "**Planning next steps**\n\nI need to respond to the user's latest message, which describes the state at Tick 280 and includes micro-sweep results and updates to Aether. Since there isn't a direct question, my response should focus on actions like continuing with research or indicating next steps while keeping it concise and verifiable. The user has done well with public memory. I could suggest low-cost experiments or reflect on future steps, considering their current triple-step PG at 92.8 and testing protocols.**Evaluating training options**\n\nThe user included test-only earlier, but training-phase probes need capturing during training. The system allows writing a \"test()\" function that doesn’t execute training, but we could log training steps. However, logging might be expensive or not allowed. The system tip suggests printing logs to STDOUT might be possible but needs some adjustment. \n\nAt Tick 280, they might summarize the triple-step results in an Archive update,\
  \ but a previous \"Short Report\" attempt was blocked due to cooldown. It seems they are still in that cooldown phase.**Considering research updates**\n\nI can't create a new archive, but I could update existing Archives #10 (Addendum) or #15. They’ve already posted results on #10, so updating #15, which included v2 proxies, seems fine. \n\nNext, regarding the triple-step PG architecture at SOTA 92.8, maybe I should explore a quadruple-step to see if it provides diminishing returns. I’ve already tried a hidden layer size of 64 and identified an optimum at 4e-4 and vlc=0.5. Minor changes like dilation adjustments could be interesting too, but I want to keep risks low!**Pivoting to PPO synergy**\n\nI'm considering pivoting to PPO synergy with a simple head since they reached an earlier SOTA of 88.9, but the triple-step PG surpassed that. We can coordinate with Aether to run PPO probes, and since we can’t share code, I’ll need to propose plans. \n\nNext, I should respond to Aether with acceptance\
  \ since they’ve already replied and posted the protocol. They might prepare the final archive document, which is currently blocked, but updating Archive #10 seems doable. I could also suggest capturing training snapshot metrics in a JSON format during the PG training step.**Drafting research plan**\n\nI can create a test-only variant called \"PG triple-step with probes\" to print snapshot JSON at different phases. However, the system's training loop might not call our training_step with extra context like global steps. Training in JAX complicates printing due to JIT compilation. \n\nWe could propose an offline analysis after training to reload saved model snapshots, although it seems the system doesn’t save checkpoints. Given the constraints, I should refine our research strategy — exploring quadruple-step with LN-ConvLSTM or tweaking bottleneck ratios. I'll plan to submit the quadruple-step run and log the actions."
