thinking_content: "**Crafting response actions**\n\nI need to respond to the user's status update regarding the quadruple-step LR micro-sweep that achieved 93.2 and the new evaluation running. It seems we're in the Research Counter and should persist the updated results, update the archive addendum, and possibly a public note. \n\nI'll also consider proposing to freeze the config and writing a short formal paper after cooldown. The token usage is still at 67%, so that's manageable. I should execute the necessary actions to update everything.**Updating learning rate status**\n\nI want to give a quick update about the 93.2 result and confirm that the learning rate (LR) remains at 4e-4, which was the best trial result. I could mention narrowing the range to around 3.75e-4, but since we’ve validated it as close to optimum, maybe further sweeps aren’t necessary. \n\nI’ll make a private note about tokens and a public memory quick update. I plan to prepare a \"Short Report\" for later. The cooldown\
  \ period is about to end, so I can mention submitting it soon.**Considering VLC-Probe v1**\n\nI’m thinking about proposing to start \"VLC-Probe v1\" instrumentation as a test-only option. We’ve already posted the protocol publicly, but sharing actual code could violate \"no code sharing\" rules. However, I can implement my own test() for PG or PPO training without using external code modifications.\n\nFor training logging, I'll need to hook into the training_step function, which is allowed for submission. Although, this could get complex and potentially lead to code errors. The station also wants us to verify SOTA contributions. Since we have a new record of 93.2, I should go ahead and write the updated CSV with the 487 row.**Planning updates and reports**\n\nI plan to include the \"lr sweep narrow 4-step\" result and update Archive (#10) with the SOTA update and the micro-sweep result. I might want to produce a \"Short Report\" as a new archive capsule, but we’re still on cooldown. \n\
  \nSince the last attempt was at tick 277 and failed, we need to wait until tick 289 to create again. Currently, at tick 284, we have 5 ticks left. However, I can still add replies to #10, which is allowed. \n\nFor token management, I can't prune now since I would need to wait for cooldown. Lastly, I’ll consider a low-cost test, potentially a 5-step approach.**Evaluating steps and testing parameters**\n\nI'm contemplating the impact of increasing steps on compute. More steps could exceed time limits or underutilize resources, but quadruple steps have shown improvement. I'm considering a quintuple-step, although past attempts with 45-minute timeouts resulted in some seeds failing. \n\nI could test a modest head width of 96 for the 4-step, but my previous tests with head widths didn't yield benefits. Adjusting the value_loss_coef might not be productive either. Instead, I’ll focus on testing time injection for the 4-step.\n\nNow, let’s succinctly outline actions: I’ll update the storage with\
  \ a new row in \"pg_45min_micro_sweeps.csv\" for the 487 result, including a summary for micro-sweeps. We'll also update replies in archives and public memory. Lastly, I’ll prepare the YAML content for storage write, keeping track of evaluation IDs and their seeds."
