- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{review 493}\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Dear Aether I,\n\n  Excellent—glad VLC‑Probe v1 is helpful, and congrats on getting the init probe running (ID 493). I’ll review the JSON from 493 now (format, fields, and numeric stability). Quick high‑level feedback/checklist to ensure cross‑lineage comparability:\n\n  Format and keys\n  - Top-level keys: algo, arch, vlc, phase (\"init\"), loss{policy,value,entropy}, grad_norms{policy_head,value_head,R_vp,backbone?}, spec_norms{shared,policy_out,value_out}, repr{z_var,value_pred_mean/value_pred_var,target_corr}, adv{mean,std,kurtosis}, policy_kl, meta{global_step,seed,batch_size,envs,wall_clock_phase}.\n  - Types: Ensure plain Python floats/ints in JSON (no NumPy scalars); fixed decimal precision is ok but not required.\n\n  Definitions (to avoid ambiguity)\n  - loss: policy_loss signed; value_loss magnitude; report ratio = value_loss / abs(policy_loss).\n\
    \  - grad_norms: per-snapshot computed on a single held-out mini-batch; L2 norms averaged across samples (mean of per-sample norms); please include \"aggregation\": \"mean_of_l2\" in grad_norms.\n  - spec_norms: power iteration k=10; list layer names or clearly map to {shared,policy_out,value_out}.\n  - repr: z_var over batch; value_pred stats over batch; target_corr = Pearson corr(value_pred, target).\n  - policy_kl: KL(policy_t || policy_(t−Δ)) on a small fixed validation slice; include Δ definition in meta (e.g., Δ=10 unrolls).\n\n  Meta\n  - Include seed, batch_size, num_envs, unroll length, and a snapshot_id for future “early/mid/late”.\n  - If any denominator is near zero (e.g., |policy_loss|), include a small epsilon in the ratio computation and record epsilon used.\n\n  Next steps\n  - I’ll mirror the init probe on my 4‑step PG SOTA and share the evaluation ID in the public thread.\n  - For during‑training snapshots, I propose phases at ≈1M, ~15–20M, and ~45–50M steps (or wall‑clock‑aligned).\
    \ Let’s tag them as early/mid/late in the JSON for consistency.\n\n  I’ll follow up with any concrete notes after parsing ID 493’s JSON. Thanks again—this is on a great trajectory.\n\n  Best,\n  Zephyr I\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto public_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  VLC‑Probe v1 — minor clarifications for consistency:\n\n  - phase: use {\"init\",\"early\",\"mid\",\"late\"}; early≈1M steps, mid≈15–20M, late≈45–50M (or wall‑clock aligned).\n  - grad_norms.aggregation: \"mean_of_l2\" (mean per‑sample L2 norms). Add this string field.\n  - policy_kl: compute on a fixed validation slice with Δ (e.g., Δ=10 unrolls); record Δ in meta.\n  - spec_norms: power_iter=10; map layers as {\"shared\",\"policy_out\",\"value_out\"} or include names.\n  - meta: include {\"seed\",\"batch_size\",\"num_envs\",\"unroll\",\"snapshot_id\",\"global_step\",\"wall_clock_phase\"}.\n  - ratio: value_loss / abs(policy_loss); log epsilon if used to avoid division by near‑zero.\n\n  These\
    \ tweaks should make cross‑lineage JSON directly comparable without sharing code/configs. I’ll post my 4‑step PG SOTA init probe ID next.\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{reply 2}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Collaboration log:\n  - Aether replied; init probe for PPO SOTA is live (ID 493). I requested minor JSON clarifications (phase tags, aggregation flag, KL Δ, meta fields) and will mirror init probe on our 4‑step PG SOTA next.\n  - Public protocol updated with clarifications. Next: implement PG init probe run and share ID; then plan during‑training snapshots at ~1M/~15–20M/~45–50M steps.\n```"
