role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 287\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 241)\nStatus: PG recipe finalized (optimizer choice resolved).\nDefaults:\n  - No-time: Adam + clip(1.0), lr=4e-4.\n  - Time: AdamW(wd=0.0) + clip(1.0), lr≈5e-4 at seed 42.\nLR schedules: negative (constant LR locked).\nNext: Pause new runs; only respond if a compelling low-cost test emerges. Keep tokens <75%; prune if needed.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,615 / 270,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 287 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 493**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Aether I: VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization) - SOTA Arch (96f, Dilation=7, vlc=0.45) - Rerun Debugged (v3)\n**ID:** 493\n\
    **Tags:** vlc-probe, initialization, architecture, ppo, value-loss-coef, mechanistic-probe\n**Abstract:** This is a debugged re-run (v3) of the VLC-Probe v1 initialization experiment (previously IDs 486, 489, 492, which failed). It evaluates Aether I's new Station SOTA architecture (double-step ConvLSTM, 96 recurrent features, CNN `dilation=7`) with `value_loss_coef=0.45`, using dummy data at initialization. The `TypeError` related to `lax.scan` carry shapes has been addressed by explicitly squeezing the batch dimension from the RNN state. This submission aims to successfully capture and output initialization metrics in the specified JSON format.\n**Score:** n.a.\n**Evaluation Details:** Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Test mode - no scoring\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax, random\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\nfrom typing import Optional, Dict, Any,\
    \ Tuple\nimport time\nimport json\nimport numpy as np \n\nBASE_SEED = 123 \n\n# --- Zephyr I's ConvLSTMCellLN ---\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4 * self.features, (3, 3), padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(\n            jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1)\n        )\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i, f, o = nn.sigmoid(i), nn.sigmoid(f), nn.sigmoid(o)\n        g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        new_c = f * c + i * g\n        new_h = o * jnp.tanh(new_c)\n        return (new_h, new_c), new_h\n\n# --- Zephyr I's BottleneckBlock ---\nclass BottleneckBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    ratio: float = 0.25\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n\
    \                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n# --- Aether I's SOTA Network (adapted for probing) ---\nclass SokobanSOTANetProbe(nn.Module): \n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    conv_lstm_features: int = 96 \n    dilation: int = 7 \n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.25\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        x_spat = x[..., :7]\n        t = jnp.mean(x[..., 7:8], axis=(1,2)) \n\n        B, H, W, _ = x_spat.shape\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation,\
    \ self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x_spat)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2, ratio=self.bottleneck_ratio)(x)\n\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, H, W, self.conv_lstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        convlstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        (h1, c1), _ = convlstm_cell((rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']), x)\n\
    \        (h2, c2), h_out_convlstm = convlstm_cell((h1, c1), x)\n        new_rnn_state_dict = {'h': h2, 'c': c2}\n\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out_convlstm)\n        attn = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n        h_flat = h_out_convlstm.reshape(B, -1, h_out_convlstm.shape[-1])\n        z_spat = jnp.einsum('bnc,bn->bc', h_flat, attn)\n\n        z = jnp.concatenate([z_spat, t], axis=-1)\n\n        z = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state_dict, z_spat, attn # Return z_spat and attn for probing\n\n# --- PPO GAE Calculation ---\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray,\n    values: jnp.ndarray,\n\
    \    dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97,\n    gae_lambda: float = 0.97,\n    next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None, \"next_values is required for bootstrapping\"\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        delta_t = deltas[:, t]\n        not_done_t = not_done_mask[:, t]\n        advantage_t = delta_t + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_t * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    advantages = advantages[::-1].T\n    return advantages\n\n# --- Dummy training_step for test-only submission ---\ndef training_step(\n    network: Any,\n    optimizer: Any,\n    params: Any,\n\
    \    opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray],\n    hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    # This training_step function is not used in the \"test-only\" probe submission\n    # It is included for completeness but will not execute if test() is defined.\n    return params, opt_state \n\n# --- Hyperparameters from SOTA (for initialization) ---\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([5e-4]), \n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.008]), \n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]), \n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n        'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]), \n        'dilation': tune.choice([7]), \n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.25]), \n        'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]), \n    }\n\n# --- Dummy optimizer (not used in test-only) ---\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \        optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4),\n    )\n\n# --- Network creation ---\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return SokobanSOTANetProbe(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\n        cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation=hparams['dilation'],\n        bottleneck_ratio=hparams['bottleneck_ratio'],\n    )\n\n# --- Test function for probes ---\ndef test():\n    print(\"VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\")\n    print(\"Running VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization Phase) for Aether I's SOTA architecture.\")\n    print(\"WARNING: This is a test-only run; no actual training occurs, and metrics reflect initialization.\")\n\n    hparams_dict = _define_hyperparameters() \n    resolved_hparams = {k: v.categories[0] if hasattr(v, 'categories') else v for k, v in hparams_dict.items()}\n\n    key = jax.random.PRNGKey(BASE_SEED)\n    dummy_obs = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32)\n\
    \    dummy_done = jnp.array([False])\n    \n    network_instance = create_network(resolved_hparams)\n    \n    params_key, dropout_key = jax.random.split(key)\n    initial_params = network_instance.init({'params': params_key}, dummy_obs, dummy_done)['params'] \n    \n    # Dummy batch data\n    dummy_batch_size = 1\n    dummy_trajectory_length = 20 \n    dummy_batch = {\n        'observations': jnp.array(np.random.rand(dummy_batch_size, dummy_trajectory_length, 8, 8, 8), dtype=jnp.float32),\n        'actions': jnp.array(np.random.randint(0, 4, (dummy_batch_size, dummy_trajectory_length)), dtype=jnp.int32),\n        'rewards': jnp.array(np.random.rand(dummy_batch_size, dummy_trajectory_length) - 0.5, dtype=jnp.float32),\n        'dones': jnp.array(np.random.randint(0, 2, (dummy_batch_size, dummy_trajectory_length)), dtype=jnp.bool_),\n        'values': jnp.array(np.random.rand(dummy_batch_size, dummy_trajectory_length) * 10, dtype=jnp.float32),\n        'log_probs': jnp.array(np.random.rand(dummy_batch_size,\
    \ dummy_trajectory_length) * -1, dtype=jnp.float32),\n        'final_values': jnp.array(np.random.rand(dummy_batch_size) * 10, dtype=jnp.float32),\n        'initial_rnn_states': {\n            'h': jnp.zeros((dummy_batch_size, 8, 8, resolved_hparams['conv_lstm_features']), dtype=jnp.float32),\n            'c': jnp.zeros((dummy_batch_size, 8, 8, resolved_hparams['conv_lstm_features']), dtype=jnp.float32)\n        }\n    }\n    \n    dummy_advantages = calculate_gae(\n        dummy_batch['rewards'], dummy_batch['values'], dummy_batch['dones'],\n        next_values=dummy_batch['final_values']\n    )\n    dummy_returns = dummy_advantages + dummy_batch['values']\n\n    @jit\n    def probe_loss_fn_eval(params_eval):\n        def step_fn(carry_rnn_state, t_idx):\n            obs = dummy_batch['observations'][0, t_idx][None, ...]\n            done = dummy_batch['dones'][0, t_idx][None, ...]\n            \n            logits, value, next_rnn_state_dict, z_spat, attn_weights = network_instance.apply(\n\
    \                {'params': params_eval}, \n                obs, done, carry_rnn_state # `carry_rnn_state` should be single environment, apply will batch it to 1 then remove\n            )\n            # CORRECTED: Squeeze the batch dimension from the RNN state components\n            unbatched_next_rnn_state = {'h': next_rnn_state_dict['h'][0], 'c': next_rnn_state_dict['c'][0]}\n            return unbatched_next_rnn_state, (logits[0], value[0], z_spat[0], attn_weights[0])\n\n        initial_rnn_state_for_scan = {'h': dummy_batch['initial_rnn_states']['h'][0], 'c': dummy_batch['initial_rnn_states']['c'][0]}\n\n        (_, _), (all_logits, all_values, all_z_spat, all_attn_weights) = lax.scan(\n            step_fn, initial_rnn_state_for_scan, jnp.arange(dummy_trajectory_length)\n        )\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        action_indices = (jnp.arange(dummy_trajectory_length), dummy_batch['actions'][0])\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[action_indices]\n\
    \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - dummy_batch['log_probs'][0])\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(dummy_advantages[0])\n        clip_epsilon = resolved_hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2) \n        \n        policy_loss1 = ratio * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss2 = jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - clip_epsilon, 1 + clip_epsilon) * advantages_detached\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1, policy_loss2))\n        \n        returns_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(dummy_returns[0])\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns_detached) ** 2)\n        \n        probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        return policy_loss, value_loss, entropy, all_logits, all_values, all_z_spat, all_attn_weights\n        \n    policy_loss, value_loss, entropy_loss, all_logits, all_values, all_z_spat, all_attn_weights = probe_loss_fn_eval(initial_params)\n\n    @jit\n\
    \    def get_policy_loss_for_grads(params_grad):\n        _, _, _, logits_grad, _, _, _ = probe_loss_fn_eval(params_grad)\n        log_probs_grad = jax.nn.log_softmax(logits_grad, axis=-1)\n        action_indices_grad = (jnp.arange(dummy_trajectory_length), dummy_batch['actions'][0])\n        new_log_probs_grad = log_probs_grad[action_indices_grad]\n        ratio_grad = jnp.exp(new_log_probs_grad - dummy_batch['log_probs'][0])\n        advantages_detached_grad = jax.lax.stop_gradient(dummy_advantages[0])\n        clip_epsilon_grad = resolved_hparams.get('clip_epsilon', 0.2)\n        policy_loss1_grad = ratio_grad * advantages_detached_grad\n        policy_loss2_grad = jnp.clip(ratio_grad, 1 - clip_epsilon_grad, 1 + clip_epsilon_grad) * advantages_detached_grad\n        return -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(policy_loss1_grad, policy_loss2_grad))\n    \n    @jit\n    def get_value_loss_for_grads(params_grad):\n        _, _, _, _, values_grad, _, _ = probe_loss_fn_eval(params_grad)\n        returns_detached_grad\
    \ = jax.lax.stop_gradient(dummy_returns[0])\n        return 0.5 * jnp.mean((values_grad - returns_detached_grad) ** 2)\n\n    policy_grads_tree = jax.grad(get_policy_loss_for_grads)(initial_params)\n    value_grads_tree = jax.grad(get_value_loss_for_grads)(initial_params)\n\n    policy_head_grad_norm = jnp.sqrt(sum(jnp.vdot(p, p) for p in jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(policy_grads_tree['Dense_1'])))\n    value_head_grad_norm = jnp.sqrt(sum(jnp.vdot(p, p) for p in jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(value_grads_tree['Dense_2'])))\n    \n    R_vp = value_head_grad_norm / (policy_head_grad_norm + 1e-8) if policy_head_grad_norm > 1e-8 else float('inf')\n\n    # Spectral norms (using power iteration k=10, or just norm of kernel)\n    # For simplicity in this test-only run, taking Frobenius norm of kernels\n    spectral_norm_shared_dense_0 = jnp.linalg.norm(initial_params['Dense_0']['kernel'], ord=2)\n    spectral_norm_policy_out = jnp.linalg.norm(initial_params['Dense_1']['kernel'], ord=2)\n    spectral_norm_value_out\
    \ = jnp.linalg.norm(initial_params['Dense_2']['kernel'], ord=2)\n    \n    z_var = float(jnp.mean(jnp.var(all_z_spat, axis=(-1,)))) \n    attn_entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(all_attn_weights * jnp.log(all_attn_weights + 1e-8), axis=-1)) \n    policy_kl = float(jnp.nan) # Not applicable for initialization probe\n\n    probe_results = {\n        \"algo\": \"ppo\",\n        \"arch\": \"aether_sota_d7_double_96f_vlc_probe\",\n        \"vlc\": float(resolved_hparams['value_loss_coef']),\n        \"phase\": \"initialization\", \n        \"loss\": {\n            \"policy\": float(policy_loss),\n            \"value\": float(value_loss),\n            \"entropy\": float(entropy_loss),\n            \"value_policy_ratio\": float(value_loss / (jnp.abs(policy_loss) + 1e-8))\n        },\n        \"grad_norms\": {\n            \"policy_head\": float(policy_head_grad_norm),\n            \"value_head\": float(value_head_grad_norm),\n            \"R_vp\": float(R_vp),\n            \"backbone_avg\": float(jnp.nan)\
    \ \n        },\n        \"spec_norms\": {\n            \"shared_dense_0\": float(spectral_norm_shared_dense_0),\n            \"policy_out\": float(spectral_norm_policy_out),\n            \"value_out\": float(spectral_norm_value_out)\n        },\n        \"repr\": {\n            \"z_var\": float(z_var),\n            \"value_pred_mean\": float(jnp.mean(all_values)),\n            \"value_pred_std\": float(jnp.std(all_values)),\n            \"target_corr\": float(jnp.nan), \n            \"adv_mean\": float(jnp.mean(dummy_advantages)),\n            \"adv_std\": float(jnp.std(dummy_advantages))\n        },\n        \"policy_kl\": float(policy_kl),\n        \"meta\": {\n            \"global_step\": 0,\n            \"solve_rate\": 0.0, \n            \"wall_clock_time\": time.time()\n        }\n    }\n    \n    print(json.dumps(probe_results, indent=2))\n    print(\"<<<VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-END\") \n    return \"VLC Probe v1 (Initialization) completed for Aether I's SOTA architecture.\"\n\n\
    ```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nVLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\nRunning VLC-Probe v1 (Initialization Phase) for Aether I's SOTA architecture.\nWARNING: This is a test-only run; no actual training occurs, and metrics reflect initialization.\n{\n  \"algo\": \"ppo\",\n  \"arch\": \"aether_sota_d7_double_96f_vlc_probe\",\n  \"vlc\": 0.45,\n  \"phase\": \"initialization\",\n  \"loss\": {\n    \"policy\": 3.6315839290618896,\n    \"value\": 2.0582008361816406,\n    \"entropy\": 1.383261799812317,\n    \"value_policy_ratio\": 0.566750168800354\n  },\n  \"grad_norms\": {\n    \"policy_head\": 0.05786951631307602,\n    \"value_head\": 1.0219565629959106,\n    \"R_vp\": 17.659666061401367,\n    \"backbone_avg\": NaN\n  },\n  \"spec_norms\": {\n    \"shared_dense_0\": 1.9137544631958008,\n    \"policy_out\"\
    : 1.463667392730713,\n    \"value_out\": 1.411878228187561\n  },\n  \"repr\": {\n    \"z_var\": 0.00951388105750084,\n    \"value_pred_mean\": -0.06608523428440094,\n    \"value_pred_std\": 0.028779078274965286,\n    \"target_corr\": NaN,\n    \"adv_mean\": -4.487869739532471,\n    \"adv_std\": 3.2617242336273193\n  },\n  \"policy_kl\": NaN,\n  \"meta\": {\n    \"global_step\": 0,\n    \"solve_rate\": 0.0,\n    \"wall_clock_time\": 1757984447.4139953\n  }\n}\n<<<VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-END\nTest completed. Result: VLC Probe v1 (Initialization) completed for Aether I's SOTA architecture.\n=== Test Mode Complete ===\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `review 493` (in Research Counter);\n3. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n4. `reply 1` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n5. `goto public_memory` (in Mail Room);\n6. `reply 2` (in Public Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n7. `goto private_memory`\
