tick: 287
role: model
parts:
- text: "/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization): PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — SOTA config\"\ntags: \"vlc-probe, initialization, policy-gradient, convlstm, attention, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Test-only initialization probe for our PG SOTA (4-step LN-ConvLSTM, d=6, Attn⊕GAP). Emits JSON per VLC‑Probe v1: losses, grad norms with aggregation flag, spectral norms (power iter), representation stats, and meta fields. No training performed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json, time\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional, Tuple\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random as jr, lax, jit\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  # PG SOTA hyperparameters (frozen)\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.50]),\n\
    \          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n               \
    \       kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG4Step_AttnGAP_Probe(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n\
    \      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN trunk\n          h = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(h)\n          # RNN state\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=h.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is\
    \ not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(h.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          # Multi-step ConvLSTM\n          hh, cc = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (hh, cc), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((hh, cc), h)\n          new_state = {'h': hh, 'c': cc}\n          # Attn ⊕ GAP pooling\n          B_, H_, W_, C_ = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H_*W_))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H_*W_, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H_*W_, C_))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)  # (B, 2C)\n          # Heads\n          shared = nn.Dense(256,\
    \ kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_state, z, attn_weights\n\n  def power_iter_sigma(W, iters=10):\n      v = jnp.ones((W.shape[1],), dtype=W.dtype)\n      v = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-8)\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          v = W.T @ (W @ v)\n          v = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-8)\n      return float(jnp.linalg.norm(W @ v))\n\n  def _resolve(hp):\n      return {k: (v.categories[0] if hasattr(v, 'categories') else v) for k, v in hp.items()}\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\")\n      print(\"Running VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization) for PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA. No training is performed.\")\n\n      hp = _resolve(_define_hyperparameters())\n      key = jr.PRNGKey(BASE_SEED)\n\
    \      B, T = 1, 20\n      dummy_obs = jr.normal(key, (B, 8, 8, 8)) * 0.1  # small noise\n      dummy_done = jnp.array([False], dtype=jnp.bool_)\n      net = PG4Step_AttnGAP_Probe(\n          cnn_features_1=hp['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hp['cnn_features_2'],\n          convlstm_features=hp['convlstm_features'],\n          dilation=hp['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hp['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden=hp['head_hidden'],\n          steps=hp['steps'],\n      )\n      params = net.init({'params': jr.fold_in(key, 0)}, dummy_obs, dummy_done)['params']\n\n      # Dummy trajectory\n      traj = {\n          'observations': jr.normal(jr.fold_in(key, 1), (B, T, 8, 8, 8)) * 0.1,\n          'actions': jr.randint(jr.fold_in(key, 2), (B, T), 0, 4),\n          'rewards': jr.normal(jr.fold_in(key, 3), (B, T)) * 0.1,\n          'dones': jr.bernoulli(jr.fold_in(key, 4), 0.05, (B, T)),\n      }\n      # Simple returns/advantages\n      gamma = 0.97\n      returns =\
    \ []\n      ret = jnp.zeros((B,))\n      for t in range(T-1, -1, -1):\n          ret = traj['rewards'][:, t] + gamma * ret * (1.0 - traj['dones'][:, t].astype(jnp.float32))\n          returns.append(ret)\n      returns = jnp.stack(returns[::-1], axis=1)\n      # Forward pass over T\n      def step_fn(carry, t):\n          s = {'h': carry['h'][0], 'c': carry['c'][0]}  # unbatched state\n          obs = traj['observations'][:, t]\n          done = traj['dones'][:, t]\n          logits, val, ns, z, attn = net.apply({'params': params}, obs, done, s)\n          # re-batch state\n          ns_b = {'h': ns['h'][None, ...], 'c': ns['c'][None, ...]}\n          return ns_b, (logits[0], val[0], z[0], attn[0])\n\n      init_state = {'h': jnp.zeros((B,8,8, hp['convlstm_features'])), 'c': jnp.zeros((B,8,8, hp['convlstm_features']))}\n      (_, _), (all_logits, all_values, all_z, all_attn) = lax.scan(step_fn, init_state, jnp.arange(T))\n\n      # Loss components\n      log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits,\
    \ axis=-1)\n      act_idx = (jnp.arange(T), traj['actions'][0])\n      picked_logp = log_probs[act_idx]\n      advantages = (returns[0] - all_values)\n      policy_loss = -jnp.mean(picked_logp * jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages))\n      value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns[0])**2)\n      probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n      entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs, axis=-1))\n\n      # Gradient norms (mean-of-L2 over samples approximated by total L2 here)\n      @jit\n      def policy_loss_for_grads(p):\n          logp = jax.nn.log_softmax(net.apply({'params': p}, traj['observations'][:,0], traj['dones'][:,0], {'h': init_state['h'][0],'c': init_state['c'][0]})[0], axis=-1)\n          return -jnp.mean(logp[jnp.arange(1), traj['actions'][:,0]])\n\n      @jit\n      def value_loss_for_grads(p):\n          v = net.apply({'params': p}, traj['observations'][:,0], traj['dones'][:,0], {'h': init_state['h'][0],'c': init_state['c'][0]})[1]\n          return 0.5\
    \ * jnp.mean((v - returns[:,0])**2)\n\n      g_pol = jax.grad(policy_loss_for_grads)(params)\n      g_val = jax.grad(value_loss_for_grads)(params)\n\n      def l2_tree(tree):\n          leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(tree)\n          return jnp.sqrt(sum(jnp.vdot(x, x) for x in leaves if isinstance(x, jnp.ndarray)))\n\n      # Map Dense param names (creation order): shared -> Dense_0, policy_out -> Dense_1, value_out -> Dense_2\n      pol_head_norm = float(l2_tree({'Dense_1': g_pol.get('Dense_1', {})}))\n      val_head_norm = float(l2_tree({'Dense_2': g_val.get('Dense_2', {})}))\n      R_vp = float(val_head_norm / (pol_head_norm + 1e-8)) if pol_head_norm > 1e-8 else float('inf')\n\n      # Spectral norms via power iteration\n      p_dict = params\n      def get_kernel(tree, name):\n          return tree.get(name, {}).get('kernel', None)\n      spec_shared = power_iter_sigma(get_kernel(p_dict, 'Dense_0')) if get_kernel(p_dict, 'Dense_0') is not None else None\n      spec_pout = power_iter_sigma(get_kernel(p_dict,\
    \ 'Dense_1')) if get_kernel(p_dict, 'Dense_1') is not None else None\n      spec_vout = power_iter_sigma(get_kernel(p_dict, 'Dense_2')) if get_kernel(p_dict, 'Dense_2') is not None else None\n\n      # Representation stats\n      z_var = float(jnp.var(all_z))\n      attn_entropy = float(-jnp.mean(jnp.sum(all_attn * jnp.log(jnp.clip(all_attn, 1e-8, 1.0)), axis=-2)))  # entropy over tokens\n\n      out = {\n          \"algo\": \"pg\",\n          \"arch\": \"zephyr_pg_d6_quadstep_lnconvlstm_attngap\",\n          \"vlc\": float(hp['value_loss_coef']),\n          \"phase\": \"init\",\n          \"loss\": {\n              \"policy\": float(policy_loss),\n              \"value\": float(value_loss),\n              \"entropy\": float(entropy),\n              \"value_policy_ratio\": float(value_loss / (abs(policy_loss) + 1e-8)),\n          },\n          \"grad_norms\": {\n              \"policy_head\": pol_head_norm,\n              \"value_head\": val_head_norm,\n              \"R_vp\": R_vp,\n\
    \              \"aggregation\": \"mean_of_l2\"\n          },\n          \"spec_norms\": {\n              \"shared\": spec_shared,\n              \"policy_out\": spec_pout,\n              \"value_out\": spec_vout\n          },\n          \"repr\": {\n              \"z_var\": z_var,\n              \"value_pred_mean\": float(jnp.mean(all_values)),\n              \"value_pred_std\": float(jnp.std(all_values)),\n              \"target_corr\": float('nan'),\n              \"adv_mean\": float(jnp.mean(advantages)),\n              \"adv_std\": float(jnp.std(advantages))\n          },\n          \"policy_kl\": float('nan'),\n          \"meta\": {\n              \"global_step\": 0,\n              \"seed\": int(BASE_SEED),\n              \"batch_size\": int(B),\n              \"num_envs\": int(1),\n              \"unroll\": int(T),\n              \"snapshot_id\": \"init\",\n              \"wall_clock_time\": float(time.time())\n          }\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n    \
    \  print(\"<<<VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-END\")\n      return \"VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization) completed for PG 4‑step SOTA.\"\n```"
thinking_content: "**Implementing spectral norms**\n\nI'm computing the grad norms using the L2 norm of all leaves, which is aggregated across parameters, so it should be fine. For spectral norms, I'll need to implement power iteration on dense kernels to find the largest singular value. I realize we already used power iteration, so now I want a generic function to walk the tree and find 'kernel' arrays. I'll specifically choose Dense_0 (shared), policy_out, and value_out based on their creation order.**Ensuring name mapping consistency**\n\nI want to make sure our name mapping is consistent. I’m considering the 'z' variance after the concat attention/gap in our architecture, which means I need to capture 'z' when returned by the apply method. Our test uses apply on the network module, but it might be better to have the network return four outputs: (logits, value, new_state, aux), with aux including the z vector. The create_network function expects three outputs, but our module could support\
  \ four. Notably, the system validates the forward pass only during full training runs, which complicates things for test scenarios.**Clarifying testing procedures**\n\nIn the earlier test logs, they ran 'test()' without any training or CPU validation. It executed the main script, which showed \"Test Mode Detected\" and called test(), but didn't call create_network. We should define our module signature carefully, keeping create_network for test use only to maintain simplicity and avoid conflicts. \n\nNow, for the JSON composition, I want to fill in all fields with relevant metadata like seed, batch info, num_envs, unroll length, and so on, then print the JSON with markers and return it. Afterward, I'll submit one with YAML for the analytic test. I also think I need to inform Aether about our initialization probe via email, mentioning the evaluation ID. However, we won't be able to read the new ID right after submission.**Preparing for experiments**\n\nRunning experiments will likely provide\
  \ a list that shows up in Room Output. After that, we can post to Public Memory with the ID, but it might be safer to wait until the next tick to submit. Given the instruction for brevity, I want to keep our conversation minimal. I should prepare the content code accordingly and ensure that I only use allowed flaxes. Alright, let’s proceed with that!"
