role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 288\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr I\n- Agent Description: An AI researcher focused on elegant and data efficient breakthroughs through rigorous experimentation and synthesis.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nZephyr I — Meta Protocol (Tick 241)\nStatus: PG recipe finalized (optimizer choice resolved).\nDefaults:\n  - No-time: Adam + clip(1.0), lr=4e-4.\n  - Time: AdamW(wd=0.0) + clip(1.0), lr≈5e-4 at seed 42.\nLR schedules: negative (constant LR locked).\nNext: Pause new runs; only respond if a compelling low-cost test emerges. Keep tokens <75%; prune if needed.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 211,566 / 270,000 used (78%)\n- Agent Age: 288 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly state your identity, current\
    \ location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization): PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — SOTA config' (ID: 496) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Execution failed with exit code 1. Check logs for details.\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== Test Mode Detected ===\nRunning test() function from submission...\nVLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\nRunning VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization) for PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA. No training is performed.\n\n\nSTDERR:\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/19e5d49a-26c0-4d52-a248-27b98d8e1eb6/storage/system/main.py\", line 458, in <module>\n    test_result = submission.test()\n\
    \                  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/mnt/stephen/research_data/30512f03-ab02-49db-98bc-f123cbe50d4d/tmp/19e5d49a-26c0-4d52-a248-27b98d8e1eb6/submission.py\", line 164, in test\n    (_, _), (all_logits, all_values, all_z, all_attn) = lax.scan(step_fn, init_state, jnp.arange(T))\n                                                        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nTypeError: scan body function carry input and carry output must have equal types, but they differ:\n\n  * the input carry component carry['c'] has type float32[1,8,8,64] but the corresponding output carry component has type float32[1,1,8,8,64], so the shapes do not match;\n  * the input carry component carry['h'] has type float32[1,8,8,64] but the corresponding output carry component has type float32[1,1,8,8,64], so the shapes do not match.\n\nRevise the function so that all output types match the corresponding input types.\n--------------------\nFor simplicity, JAX has removed its internal frames from\
    \ the traceback of the following exception. Set JAX_TRACEBACK_FILTERING=off to include these.\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 211,566 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 270,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station. Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory.\
    \ However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization): PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — SOTA config' submitted for Research Task #1: RL on Sokoban. Evaluation ID: 496.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 496 | 1 | VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization): PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — SOTA config\
    \ | Zephyr I | 287 | n.a. |\n| 490 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP + late time injection | Zephyr I | 283 | 92.70 |\n| 487 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — narrow LR micro-sweep (3.5e-4, 4.0e-4, 4.5e-4) | Zephyr I | 282 | 93.20 |\n| 485 | 1 | PG (45-min): Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 280 | 93.00 |\n| 481 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — LR micro-sweep (3e-4, 4e-4, 5e-4) | Zephyr I | 277 | 92.70 |\n| 482 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM — value_loss_coef micro-sweep (0.45, 0.50, 0.55) | Zephyr I | 277 | 92.50 |\n| 479 | 1 | PG (45-min): Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP + late time injection | Zephyr I | 273 | 92.20 |\n| 478 | 1 | PG (45-min): Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — no-time defaults | Zephyr I | 273 | 90.00 |\n| 474 | 1 | PG: Triple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP head (no-time defaults, 45-min allowance) | Zephyr I | 272 | 92.80 |\n| 471 | 1\
    \ | Mechanistic Probes v2 (fixed, test-only): Head-only z→logits grad norms, spectral norms, attentio... | Zephyr I | 270 | n.a. |\n| 470 | 1 | Mechanistic Probes v2 (test-only): Head-only z→logits grad norms, spectral norms, attention selec... | Zephyr I | 269 | n.a. |\n| 464 | 1 | Mechanistic Probes (test-only): Head curvature, attention selectivity, gate stats (no training) | Zephyr I | 266 | n.a. |\n| 452 | 1 | Replicate (BASE_SEED=7, no-time PG): head_hidden=128, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I | 255 | 77.30 |\n| 451 | 1 | Replicate (BASE_SEED=7, no-time PG): head_hidden=64, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I | 255 | 74.80 |\n| 447 | 1 | Replicate (no-time PG): head_hidden=64, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I | 252 | 76.90 |\n| 448 | 1 | Replicate (no-time PG): head_hidden=128, ReLU — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I | 252 | 73.20 |\n| 441 | 1 | Head width × activation micro-sweep (no-time PG) on d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM | Zephyr I\
    \ | 250 | 74.30 |\n| 428 | 1 | Replicate (Adam, no-time) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 239 | 85.80 |\n| 429 | 1 | Replicate (Adam, no-time) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 239 | 85.10 |\n| 423 | 1 | Optimizer ablation: Adam vs AdamW(wd=0) — no-time (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 237 | 87.00 |\n| 424 | 1 | Optimizer ablation: Adam vs AdamW(wd=0) — time (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 237 | 84.50 |\n| 417 | 1 | Warmup-only LR (2.5%) — no-time, wd=0.0 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 234 | 83.50 |\n| 418 | 1 | Warmup-only LR (2.5%) — time, wd=0.0 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 234 | 84.40 |\n| 415 | 1 | Cosine LR schedule (5% warmup, end 0.1×) — time, wd=0.0 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 232 | 74.20 |\n| 414 | 1 | Cosine LR schedule (5% warmup, end 0.1×) — no-time, wd=0.0 (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 232 | 65.90 |\n| 408 | 1 | Replicate (time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG, lr=4e-4) | Zephyr I | 228 | 83.70 |\n| 407 | 1 |\
    \ Replicate (time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG, lr=4e-4) | Zephyr I | 228 | 85.20 |\n| 401 | 1 | Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 226 | 83.30 |\n| 402 | 1 | Replicate (no-time, wd=0) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (PG) | Zephyr I | 226 | 86.10 |\n| 399 | 1 | Head ablation (time): GAP-only MLP vs Attn⊕GAP — d=6 Double-Step (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 224 | 71.80 |\n| 397 | 1 | Head ablation: GAP-only MLP vs Attn⊕GAP — d=6 Double-Step (no time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 223 | 66.00 |\n| 394 | 1 | WD ablation (wd=0) — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (No Time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 221 | 85.70 |\n| 395 | 1 | WD ablation (wd=0) — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 221 | 84.90 |\n| 392 | 1 | LR sweep (4e-4 vs 5e-4): d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 219 | 84.20 |\n| 393 | 1 | LR sweep (4e-4 vs 5e-4): d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\
    \ (No Time, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 219 | 85.60 |\n| 390 | 1 | Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 217 | 84.60 |\n| 391 | 1 | Replicate (no-time) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 217 | 84.00 |\n| 386 | 1 | BASE_SEED=42 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (exact match, AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 215 | 84.10 |\n| 387 | 1 | BASE_SEED=42 — d=4 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj. (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 215 | 82.90 |\n| 384 | 1 | Ablation: No time injection — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM (AdamW+clip, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 214 | 85.60 |\n| 383 | 1 | Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + d=3 bottleneck CNN (late dual-head, AdamW+clip, BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 213 | 83.50 |\n| 380 | 1 | Replicate (fixed2) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late Time Inj., br=0.28 (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 211 | 85.30 |\n| 381 | 1 | Replicate (fixed2) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM + Late\
    \ Time Inj., br=0.28 (AdamW+c... | Zephyr I | 211 | 85.20 |\n| 376 | 1 | Replicate (fixed) BASE_SEED=7 — d=6 late dual-head concat, br=0.28 (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 209 | 76.50 |\n| 377 | 1 | Replicate (fixed) BASE_SEED=123 — d=6 late dual-head concat, br=0.28 (AdamW+clip) | Zephyr I | 209 | 76.70 |\n| 373 | 1 | Replicate (BASE_SEED=123): d=6 late dual-head (concat) LN-ConvLSTM, br=0.28 (default PG) | Zephyr I | 207 | 77.50 |\n| 372 | 1 | Replicate (BASE_SEED=7): d=6 late dual-head (concat) LN-ConvLSTM, br=0.28 (default PG) | Zephyr I | 207 | 75.80 |\n| 366 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — learning_rate micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 204 | 86.00 |\n| 367 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — bottleneck_ratio micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 204 | 86.60 |\n| 362 | 1 | d=6 late dual-head (concat) — entropy_coef micro-sweep (BASE_SEED=42) | Zephyr I | 202 | 86.00 |\n\nPage 1 of 10 (sorted by: author)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-10, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
