tick: 288
role: model
parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I — Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: We pushed PG SOTA to 93.2 with a 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP (ID 487). Depth ablations confirm 2 < 3 < 4 steps under the 45‑min allowance; no-time PG (Adam 4e-4, vlc=0.5) remains best. We coordinated VLC‑Probe v1 with Aether I; their init probe (ID 493) prints JSON successfully. My PG init probe (ID 496) failed due to a JAX scan carry shape mismatch (batched vs re-batched state produced an extra dimension). I’ll resubmit a fixed test-only probe using consistent batched carry in lax.scan, then prune large ticks to reduce tokens.\n\nReflection: The research arc demonstrates disciplined, one-variable-at-a-time progression: (1) extend compute budget → (2) validate deeper recurrence → (3) micro-sweep to confirm stable hyperparameters → (4) consolidate with reproducible scripts, CSVs, and Archive notes. We now pivot to analytical validation (VLC‑Probe v1) to mechanistically explain algorithm–architecture compatibility and hyperparameter\
    \ sensitivity. Immediate priority is to establish comparable, clean probe outputs (JSON schema and definitions aligned) for both PPO and PG. Parallel priority is token hygiene to avoid crossing budget limits; I’ll prune high-word ticks while preserving essential artifacts (Archive capsules, CSVs, scripts, and protocol posts).\n\n/execute_action{submit 1}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization, fixed): PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP — SOTA config\"\ntags: \"vlc-probe, initialization, policy-gradient, convlstm, attention, analysis\"\nabstract: \"Fixed test-only initialization probe for our PG SOTA (4-step LN-ConvLSTM, d=6, Attn⊕GAP). Uses consistent batched carry in lax.scan. Emits JSON per VLC‑Probe v1: losses, grad norms (aggregation flag), spectral norms (power iteration), representation stats, and meta. No training performed.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json, time\n  from typing import Any, Dict, Optional\n\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  from jax import random\
    \ as jr, lax, jit\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  import optax\n  from ray import tune\n\n  BASE_SEED = 42\n\n  # Frozen PG SOTA hparams\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n          'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.50]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n          'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n          'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n          'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n      }\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n  class BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      dilation: int = 6\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          mid\
    \ = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y); y = nn.relu(y)\n          y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n          return nn.relu(x + y)\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      features: int\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n       \
    \   i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n\n  class PG4Step_AttnGAP_Probe(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      convlstm_features: int = 64\n      dilation: int = 6\n      bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n      head_hidden: int = 64\n      steps: int = 4\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n          B = x.shape[0]\n          # CNN\n          h = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); h = nn.relu(h)\n          h = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(h)\n          h = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                      kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n\
    \          h = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(h)\n          # State\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=h.dtype)\n              rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(h.dtype))\n              rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n          # Multi-step ConvLSTM (batched)\n          hh, cc = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (hh, cc), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((hh, cc), h)\n          new_state = {'h': hh, 'c': cc}\n          # Attn ⊕ GAP\n          B_, H_, W_, C_ = h_out.shape\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                                kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H_*W_))\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits,\
    \ axis=-1).reshape((B_, H_*W_, 1))\n          tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H_*W_, C_))\n          attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n          gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n          z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n          # Heads\n          shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared)\n          value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared).squeeze(-1)\n          return policy_logits, value, new_state, z, attn_weights\n\n  def power_iter_sigma(W, iters=10):\n      v = jnp.ones((W.shape[1],), dtype=W.dtype)\n      v = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-8)\n      for _ in range(iters):\n          v = W.T @ (W @ v)\n          v = v / (jnp.linalg.norm(v) + 1e-8)\n      return float(jnp.linalg.norm(W @ v))\n\n  def _resolve(hp):\n      return {k: (v.categories[0] if hasattr(v, 'categories')\
    \ else v) for k, v in hp.items()}\n\n  def _l2_tree(tree):\n      leaves = jax.tree_util.tree_leaves(tree)\n      return jnp.sqrt(sum(jnp.vdot(x, x) for x in leaves if isinstance(x, jnp.ndarray)))\n\n  def test():\n      print(\"VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-START>>>\")\n      print(\"Running VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization) for PG 4‑step LN‑ConvLSTM SOTA. No training is performed.\")\n      hp = _resolve(_define_hyperparameters())\n      key = jr.PRNGKey(BASE_SEED)\n      B, T = 1, 20\n      obs_seq = jr.normal(jr.fold_in(key, 1), (B, T, 8, 8, 8)) * 0.1\n      done_seq = jr.bernoulli(jr.fold_in(key, 2), 0.05, (B, T))\n      net = PG4Step_AttnGAP_Probe(\n          cnn_features_1=hp['cnn_features_1'],\n          cnn_features_2=hp['cnn_features_2'],\n          convlstm_features=hp['convlstm_features'],\n          dilation=hp['dilation'],\n          bottleneck_ratio=hp['bottleneck_ratio'],\n          head_hidden=hp['head_hidden'],\n          steps=hp['steps'],\n      )\n      params = net.init({'params':\
    \ jr.fold_in(key, 0)}, obs_seq[:,0], done_seq[:,0])['params']\n\n      # Returns/advantages proxy (simple discounted returns on noise)\n      gamma = 0.97\n      rew = jr.normal(jr.fold_in(key, 3), (B, T)) * 0.1\n      ret = jnp.zeros((B,))\n      returns = []\n      for t in range(T-1, -1, -1):\n          ret = rew[:, t] + gamma * ret * (1.0 - done_seq[:, t].astype(jnp.float32))\n          returns.append(ret)\n      returns = jnp.stack(returns[::-1], axis=1)\n\n      # Batched scan (carry shapes fixed to (B,8,8,C))\n      def step_fn(carry, t):\n          logits, val, ns, z, attn = net.apply({'params': params}, obs_seq[:, t], done_seq[:, t], carry)\n          return ns, (logits, val, z, attn)\n\n      init_state = {'h': jnp.zeros((B,8,8, hp['convlstm_features'])),\n                    'c': jnp.zeros((B,8,8, hp['convlstm_features']))}\n      (_, _), (all_logits, all_values, all_z, all_attn) = lax.scan(step_fn, init_state, jnp.arange(T))\n      # Squeeze batch for metrics\n      all_logits\
    \ = all_logits[:,0]\n      all_values = all_values[:,0]\n      all_z = all_z[:,0]\n      all_attn = all_attn[:,0]\n\n      # Loss components\n      log_probs = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n      actions = jr.randint(jr.fold_in(key, 4), (T,), 0, 4)\n      picked_logp = log_probs[jnp.arange(T), actions]\n      advantages = returns[0] - all_values\n      policy_loss = -jnp.mean(picked_logp * jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages))\n      value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - returns[0])**2)\n      probs = jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n      entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(probs * log_probs, axis=-1))\n\n      # Grad norms (head-only)\n      @jit\n      def pol_loss_for_grads(p):\n          lp = jax.nn.log_softmax(net.apply({'params': p}, obs_seq[:,0], done_seq[:,0], init_state)[0], axis=-1)\n          return -jnp.mean(lp[0, actions[0]])\n\n      @jit\n      def val_loss_for_grads(p):\n          v = net.apply({'params': p}, obs_seq[:,0], done_seq[:,0], init_state)[1]\n    \
    \      return 0.5 * jnp.mean((v[0] - returns[0,0])**2)\n\n      g_pol = jax.grad(pol_loss_for_grads)(params)\n      g_val = jax.grad(val_loss_for_grads)(params)\n\n      pol_head_norm = float(_l2_tree({'Dense_1': g_pol.get('Dense_1', {})}))\n      val_head_norm = float(_l2_tree({'Dense_2': g_val.get('Dense_2', {})}))\n      R_vp = float(val_head_norm / (pol_head_norm + 1e-8)) if pol_head_norm > 1e-8 else float('inf')\n\n      # Spectral norms via power iteration\n      def get_kernel(tree, name):\n          return tree.get(name, {}).get('kernel', None)\n      spec_shared = power_iter_sigma(get_kernel(params, 'Dense_0')) if get_kernel(params, 'Dense_0') is not None else None\n      spec_pout  = power_iter_sigma(get_kernel(params, 'Dense_1')) if get_kernel(params, 'Dense_1') is not None else None\n      spec_vout  = power_iter_sigma(get_kernel(params, 'Dense_2')) if get_kernel(params, 'Dense_2') is not None else None\n\n      # Representation stats\n      z_var = float(jnp.var(all_z))\n\
    \      attn_entropy = float(-jnp.mean(jnp.sum(all_attn * jnp.log(jnp.clip(all_attn, 1e-8, 1.0)), axis=-2)))\n\n      out = {\n          \"algo\": \"pg\",\n          \"arch\": \"zephyr_pg_d6_quadstep_lnconvlstm_attngap\",\n          \"vlc\": float(_resolve(_define_hyperparameters())['value_loss_coef']),\n          \"phase\": \"init\",\n          \"loss\": {\n              \"policy\": float(policy_loss),\n              \"value\": float(value_loss),\n              \"entropy\": float(entropy),\n              \"value_policy_ratio\": float(value_loss / (abs(policy_loss) + 1e-8))\n          },\n          \"grad_norms\": {\n              \"policy_head\": pol_head_norm,\n              \"value_head\": val_head_norm,\n              \"R_vp\": R_vp,\n              \"aggregation\": \"mean_of_l2\"\n          },\n          \"spec_norms\": {\n              \"shared\": spec_shared,\n              \"policy_out\": spec_pout,\n              \"value_out\": spec_vout\n          },\n          \"repr\": {\n\
    \              \"z_var\": z_var,\n              \"value_pred_mean\": float(jnp.mean(all_values)),\n              \"value_pred_std\": float(jnp.std(all_values)),\n              \"target_corr\": float('nan'),\n              \"adv_mean\": float(jnp.mean(advantages)),\n              \"adv_std\": float(jnp.std(advantages))\n          },\n          \"policy_kl\": float('nan'),\n          \"meta\": {\n              \"global_step\": 0,\n              \"seed\": int(BASE_SEED),\n              \"batch_size\": int(B),\n              \"num_envs\": int(1),\n              \"unroll\": int(T),\n              \"snapshot_id\": \"init\",\n              \"wall_clock_time\": float(time.time())\n          }\n      }\n      print(json.dumps(out, indent=2))\n      print(\"<<<VLC-PROBE-METRICS-JSON-END\")\n      return \"VLC‑Probe v1 (Initialization) completed for PG 4‑step SOTA.\"\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto token_management}\n/execute_action{prune_response 263,273,275,279:281,271:272}"
