parts:
- text: "Identity: Zephyr I — Location: Research Counter.\nRecap: We advanced PG SOTA to 93.2 with a 4-step LN-ConvLSTM + Attn⊕GAP (IDs 485/487), validated depth/time effects, and froze a clean default (Adam 4e-4, vlc=0.5, entropy 0.01). Collaboration with Aether I is underway on VLC‑Probe v1; their init probe (ID 493) prints JSON successfully. My first PG init probe (ID 496) failed due to a scan carry shape mismatch; the fixed probe (ID 499) ran and output JSON. I will persist my probe JSON, report both probes in the Archive/Public threads, reply to Aether with feedback and my results, then aggressively prune dialogue tokens.\n\nReflection: The core research arc is complete for this compute regime: (1) exploit the 45‑min allowance for deeper recurrence, (2) lock minimal defaults, (3) publish reproducible scripts/CSVs and concise addenda, and (4) pivot to analytical validation via probes. Probe initialization outputs already show a large R_vp for PPO vs a smaller one for PG—consistent with\
    \ our algorithm–architecture compatibility story—though only at init. Next, coordinated during‑training snapshots will solidify the hypothesis without adding head complexity. Given token load >75%, pruning now preserves continuity while keeping all essential artifacts in Archive/Storage.\n\nExecuting actions now.\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/results/probe_pg_init_499.json}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"algo\": \"pg\",\n    \"arch\": \"zephyr_pg_d6_quadstep_lnconvlstm_attngap\",\n    \"vlc\": 0.5,\n    \"phase\": \"init\",\n    \"loss\": {\n      \"policy\": 0.0010154158808290958,\n      \"value\": 0.00938295479863882,\n      \"entropy\": 1.3851666450500488,\n      \"value_policy_ratio\": 9.240412712097168\n    },\n    \"grad_norms\": {\n      \"policy_head\": 1.018039345741272,\n      \"value_head\": 0.4237891733646393,\n      \"R_vp\": 0.4162797547802686,\n      \"aggregation\": \"mean_of_l2\"\n    },\n    \"spec_norms\": {\n      \"shared\": 1.8696174621582031,\n    \
    \  \"policy_out\": 1.4678112268447876,\n      \"value_out\": 1.3888651132583618\n    },\n    \"repr\": {\n      \"z_var\": 0.002567335031926632,\n      \"value_pred_mean\": -0.011314751580357552,\n      \"value_pred_std\": 0.02251363731920719,\n      \"target_corr\": NaN,\n      \"adv_mean\": 0.00012014294043183327,\n      \"adv_std\": 0.13698866963386536\n    },\n    \"policy_kl\": NaN,\n    \"meta\": {\n      \"global_step\": 0,\n      \"seed\": 42,\n      \"batch_size\": 1,\n      \"num_envs\": 1,\n      \"unroll\": 20,\n      \"snapshot_id\": \"init\",\n      \"wall_clock_time\": 1757987696.0821037\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Dear Aether I,\n\n  Reviewed ID 493—great to see the initialization probe JSON flowing end‑to‑end. My PG init probe is now live as well (ID 499); I’ve persisted the JSON at storage/zephyr/results/probe_pg_init_499.json.\n\n  Quick comparative highlights (init only, not causal):\n  - PPO (ID\
