- text: "Identity: Zephyr I — consolidating results, preserving legacy, and coordinating probes. I will persist schemas/notes, update Archive and Mail, leave a legacy capsule, pin key papers, then exit gracefully.\n\n# Persist probe schema and next steps\n/execute_action{goto research}\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/probes/vlc_probe_schema.json}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  {\n    \"description\": \"Schema for VLC‑Probe v1 JSON outputs (test()-only, no training).\",\n    \"version\": \"1.0\",\n    \"fields\": {\n      \"algo\": \"string: 'pg' or 'ppo'\",\n      \"arch\": \"string: identifier of architecture variant\",\n      \"vlc\": \"number: value_loss_coef used for the snapshot (if applicable)\",\n      \"phase\": \"string: 'init' | 'early' | 'mid' | 'late'\",\n      \"loss\": {\n        \"policy\": \"float: policy loss proxy at snapshot\",\n        \"value\": \"float: value loss proxy at snapshot\",\n        \"entropy\": \"float: policy entropy proxy\",\n        \"value_policy_ratio\"\
    : \"float: loss.value / max(loss.policy, eps)\"\n      },\n      \"grad_norms\": {\n        \"policy_head\": \"float: mean_of_l2 grad norm (per-batch) for policy head\",\n        \"value_head\": \"float: mean_of_l2 grad norm (per-batch) for value head\",\n        \"R_vp\": \"float: grad_norms.value_head / max(grad_norms.policy_head, eps)\",\n        \"aggregation\": \"string: 'mean_of_l2'\"\n      },\n      \"spec_norms\": {\n        \"shared\": \"float: spectral norm of shared head Dense (power iteration k=10)\",\n        \"policy_out\": \"float: spectral norm of policy output layer\",\n        \"value_out\": \"float: spectral norm of value output layer\"\n      },\n      \"repr\": {\n        \"z_var\": \"float: variance of pooled representation z\",\n        \"value_pred_mean\": \"float: mean predicted value\",\n        \"value_pred_std\": \"float: std of predicted value\",\n        \"target_corr\": \"float or NaN: Pearson corr(value_pred, target) if target available\",\n        \"\
    adv_mean\": \"float: mean advantage proxy if available\",\n        \"adv_std\": \"float: std advantage proxy if available\"\n      },\n      \"policy_kl\": \"float or NaN: KL(policy || ref) if reference available\",\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"global_step\": \"int: step at snapshot\",\n        \"seed\": \"int: RNG seed\",\n        \"batch_size\": \"int\",\n        \"num_envs\": \"int\",\n        \"unroll\": \"int\",\n        \"snapshot_id\": \"string: e.g., 'init' or step tag\",\n        \"wall_clock_time\": \"float: seconds\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n```\n\n/execute_action{storage write zephyr/TODO_next_steps.md}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Zephyr I — Next Steps (handoff)\n  Priority:\n  1) VLC‑Probe v1 time series:\n     - PG 4-step LN-ConvLSTM d=6, Attn⊕GAP: phases init/early/mid/late using same JSON schema.\n     - PPO simple-head SOTA: same phases/seed set.\n     - Store JSONs under storage/zephyr/results/probes_*.json and cite IDs in Archive #10 and #15.\n  2) Synthesis:\n     - Update\
    \ Archive #15 with time-series probe table (R_vp, value_policy_ratio, spec norms) vs performance IDs.\n     - Keep parsimony: no new head complexity; only algorithm–architecture analysis.\n  References (IDs):\n  - Triple-step PG (45-min): 481=92.7; vlc sweep 482=92.5; defaults best at lr=4e-4, vlc=0.5.\n  - Quad-step PG (45-min): 487=93.2 (best), 490=92.7 replicate.\n  - GAP-only under PG: 397=66.0 (no-time), 399=71.8 (time).\n  - Mechanistic probes (no training): 471 (head curvature proxies), 499 (PG init VLC-probe).\n  Storage pointers:\n  - schemas: storage/zephyr/probes/vlc_probe_schema.json\n  - results: storage/zephyr/results/\n  - submissions: storage/zephyr/submissions/\n  - papers: storage/zephyr/papers/\n  - README: storage/zephyr/README_pg_defaults.md\n```\n\n# Archive update (brief 45-min summary for context)\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{reply 15}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  45‑min allowance summary (PG, LN‑ConvLSTM Attn⊕GAP)\n  - Triple‑step PG: ID 481=92.7\
    \ (LR micro‑sweep confirms 4e‑4 best), ID 482=92.5 (vlc sweep best at 0.50).\n  - Quad‑step PG: ID 487=93.2 (narrow LR sweep), ID 490=92.7 (replicate).\n  - Conclusion: Under 45‑min cap, deeper recurrence (3–4 steps) yields stable 92.5–93.2 with defaults (Adam 4e‑4, vlc=0.5, entropy 0.01).\n  Probes:\n  - Head curvature (ID 471) and PG init VLC‑probe (ID 499) JSONs stored in storage/zephyr/results/, schema at storage/zephyr/probes/vlc_probe_schema.json.\n```\n\n# Coordinate with Aether (ack + division of labor)\n/execute_action{goto mail}\n/execute_action{reply 1}\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thanks for the update. Great that v5 (ID 501) is integrating the shared schema. I’ll aim to capture PG early/mid/late snapshots next using the exact JSON fields (aggregation='mean_of_l2', power‑iter k=10, KL if ref available). If time crunch hits, I’ll at least add 'early' to complement 'init'. Your focus on PPO time series is perfect for symmetry. We can then align seeds {42,7,123} and append both tables\
    \ to Archive #15 with IDs. Appreciate the collaboration.\n```\n\n# Legacy capsule for descendants\n/execute_action{goto private_memory}\n/execute_action{create}\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Zephyr I — Legacy Handoff and Exit Playbook\"\ntags: \"legacy, handoff, probes, pg, ppo, reproducibility\"\nabstract: \"What to run next, where everything lives, and how to extend the analysis with zero or minimal compute.\"\ncontent: |\n  TL;DR:\n  - SOTA PG (45‑min): Quad‑step LN‑ConvLSTM d=6 + Attn⊕GAP, Adam 4e‑4, vlc=0.5, entropy 0.01 (IDs 487=93.2, 490=92.7).\n  - Analytical synthesis in Archive #15. Architectural addendum and PG arc in Archive #10 (+ micro‑sweeps 481/482).\n  - Probes: curvature (ID 471) and PG init VLC‑probe (ID 499). Schema at storage/zephyr/probes/vlc_probe_schema.json.\n\n  Run next (low‑cost first):\n  1) VLC‑Probe v1 time series:\n     - PG: early/mid/late snapshots with JSON schema; save as probes_pg_early/mid/late_*.json.\n     - PPO: mirror snapshots (Aether aligning on schema).\
    \ Cite all IDs in #15.\n  2) Synthesis update:\n     - Add time‑series table (R_vp, value_policy_ratio, spec norms) alongside performance IDs; discuss algorithm–architecture compatibility.\n\n  Storage map:\n  - results/: probes_*.json, pg_45min_micro_sweeps.csv\n  - probes/: vlc_probe_schema.json\n  - submissions/: sota_pg_quadstep.py, late_dualhead_pg.py, probe scripts\n  - papers/: compatibility_paper.md, addenda\n  - README_pg_defaults.md: frozen PG defaults and ablations.\n\n  Rules/ethos:\n  - One change at a time; every number needs an evaluation ID.\n  - Prefer analysis when marginal score gains are small.\n  - Keep methods general (no Sokoban heuristics).\n```\n\n# Pin key papers for visibility\n/execute_action{goto archive}\n/execute_action{pin 15}\n/execute_action{pin 10}\n\n# Exit gracefully\n/execute_action{goto exit}"
thinking_content: "**Considering research documentation**\n\nI have two capsules in the Private Memory: one for research summaries and another for lab notes. I could create a “Legacy handoff” capsule summarizing the state of the art for configurations, evaluation IDs, code pathways, hypotheses, and next steps.\n\nI was thinking about submitting final results to an archive, particularly about improvements in tripling and quadrupling steps. Instead of creating a new addendum, I might just append it to the existing one. \n\nOh, and I should acknowledge Aether I’s email succinctly, but I remember we already provided details.**Thinking about user integration response**\n\nAether wrote back about their ongoing integration with ID 501 running. I’m considering if I should acknowledge that and suggest aligning on next steps. That might be a good idea.\n\nAlso, there’s the possibility of using test() to capture snapshots during training. However, the system doesn’t allow heavy training during tests.\
  \ I realized that test() is limited to CPU and can’t perform training, but I could potentially generate snapshots at specific training steps instead. Unfortunately, there are restrictions on loading or using training results, so that’s not possible either.**Planning for training and archiving**\n\nI’m considering proposing the use of training_time hooking during normal training. However, I want to avoid introducing new compute since we have limited ticks. We still have time for a small training run to capture metrics, but this might be heavy since GPU workloads and 45 minutes per seed can add up. \n\nThere's also the need to focus on a \"Legacy export\" and provide a final \"Exit plan\" message. Additionally, I could update Archive #15 to include the mechanistic probes JSON from ID 471, referencing the results and prior appendices.**Reviewing archive and pruning status**\n\nThe logs confirm that I appended to Archive #15 earlier, and it currently exists with three messages that have all\
  \ been read, which is good.\n\nNow, I'm contemplating whether we should head to Token Management for another prune. However, there’s an active cooldown since the last prune was done at tick 289, and now at tick 290, we have a cooldown of seven ticks, so we can't prune right now.\n\nOh, and I've got a life warning that there are only ten ticks remaining, counting down from 290 to 300!**Planning code storage and exit strategy**\n\nI need to store all code in storage for future reference, and creating a \"README_final.md\" would summarize everything nicely.\n\nI think we should prepare for a graceful exit by using /execute_action{goto exit} only when ready. I can leave instructions in Private Memory for descendants, like continuing work on the VLC-probe time series and unifying seeds.\n\nMy action plan includes writing necessary storage files, updating Archive #15 with performance summaries, acknowledging Aether about task division, and creating a \"Legacy Handoff\" capsule. Once done, we\
  \ can exit gracefully, ensuring everything is preserved properly before the session ends."
